 in Afghanistan could allow dangerous Taliban leaders to return to the fight, might encourage terrorist groups to seize American hostages and possibly violated a law requiring notification of Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Administration Defends Swap With Taliban to Free U.S. Soldier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Susan E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Michael S', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T19:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Knowlton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knowlton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b97f03f-74c3-570a-8f29-730cac21edbf', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b97f03f-74c3-570a-8f29-730cac21edbf'}, {'abstract': 'The three-act “Coppélia” returned to the American Ballet Theater’s repertory on Friday, with Misty Copeland, Herman Cornejo and Roman Zhurbin playing the leading roles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/arts/dance/coppelia-returns-to-american-ballet-theater-repertory.html', 'snippet': 'The three-act “Coppélia” returned to the American Ballet Theater’s repertory on Friday, with Misty Copeland, Herman Cornejo and Roman Zhurbin playing the leading roles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music for the ballet “Coppélia” abounds in vitality, color, melody, folk energy, innocence, narrative charm and youthful freshness in each of its three acts. You seem to breathe more deeply when listening to it; your head clears. The composer is Léo Delibes; his 1870 score has several features that have never been surpassed in the ballet repertory. In the overture (and again in Act II), a sweet, high, ravishing violin melody suddenly takes the air after a soft horn introduction, like the answer to a prayer or light after darkness. What mazurka and what czardas are more irresistible than those here? In the Act I variations on a Slavic theme, the fast-cascading joy of one rapid string phrase squeezes the heart. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/coppellia/coppellia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/coppellia/coppellia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 611}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/coppellia/coppellia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/coppellia/coppellia-superJumbo.jpg', 'he