one, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/multimedia/bergdahl-parents/bergdahl-parents-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/multimedia/bergdahl-parents/bergdahl-parents-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/multimedia/bergdahl-parents/bergdahl-parents-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bergdahls’ News Conference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T20:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c77c4c32-df02-5a8b-a4b9-1091fc2a9a46', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c77c4c32-df02-5a8b-a4b9-1091fc2a9a46'}, {'abstract': 'The February announcement that Arsenio Hall’s syndicated late-night show would return for a second season turned out to be both premature and mistaken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/business/media/another-ending-for-arsenio-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The February announcement that Arsenio Hall’s syndicated late-night show would return for a second season turned out to be both premature and mistaken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The February announcement that Arsenio Hall’s syndicated late-night show would return for a second season turned out to be both premature and mistaken. CBS Television Distribution, which owns the show with Tribune Media, has announced a cancellation because of a ratings decline among the viewers most advertisers pay for in late night, people between the ages of 18 and 49. (The ratings leader in that group is Jimmy Fallon on NBC.) Mr. Hall, left, who had a hit syndicated late-night show in the early 1990s, revived the franchise with some fanfare in September, and he scored some early impressive ratings. But the late-night scene had become intensely crowded, with as many as 10 shows fighting for a shrinking number of viewers. The ratings drop set in motion a pattern of downgrades from a host of local television stations, which began relegating Mr. Hall’s show to little-watched hours of the night. In February, his old friend Jay Leno appeared on the show with a letter confirming a second year. The ratings slide forced CBS’s syndication division to rescind that decision.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Ending for Arsenio Hall', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Ending for Arsenio Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Arsenio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T21:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dad3f34-a3c0-55f5-94c9-a2ea7f7a77fb', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dad3f34-a3c0-55f5-94c9-a2ea7f7a77fb'}, {'abstract': 'Minnesota’s Phil Hughes, facing his former team for the first time, avoided becoming a hard-luck loser when the Yankees’ David Robertson blew a save opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/sports/baseball/yankees-robertson-fails-making-twins-hughes-a-winner.html', 'snippet': 'Minnesota’s Phil Hughes, facing his former team for the first time, avoided becoming a hard-luck loser when the Yankees’ David Robertson blew a save opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even though Phil Hughes was once an 18-game winner for the Yankees, had been an All-Star and had helped them win a World Series as an important relief pitcher, things could hardly have ended worse for him in the Bronx. A 4-14 record last season, including a 1-10 mark at home, made him the target of loud booing by fans who were only too happy to see him leave.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Robertson Fails, Making Twins’ Hughes a Winner', 'kicker': 'Twins 7, Yankees 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robertson Collapses, Making Hughes a Winner in His Return to the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, David (1985- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitley, Chase', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T21:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88258576-724a-5091-b66e-5d4ca28bb886', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88258576-724a-5091-b66e-5d4ca28bb886'}, {'abstract': '“Do Fathers Matter?” cites research that shows that fathers have an outsize effect on their children’s vocabulary, and that their presence can delay daughters’ puberty, among other findings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/books/do-fathers-matter-shows-why-they-do.html', 'snippet': '“Do Fathers Matter?” cites research that shows that fathers have an outsize effect on their children’s vocabulary, and that their presence can delay daughters’ puberty, among other findings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When our young daughters first decided to play on top of our Honda minivan, parked in our driveway, my wife was worried. But to me, it seemed no less safe than chasing a ball that frequently ended up in the street. And they loved the height, the novelty, the danger. So I let them stay. They never fell. And with the summer weather here, playing on the car is once again keeping them occupied for hours. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 567}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 894, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 894, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relevant? Nurturing? Well, So’s Your Old Man', 'kicker': 'Books Of the Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relevant? Nurturing? Well, So’s Your Old Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raeburn, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T21:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/70c8c716-1531-5f8d-865d-1a4abf6c6125', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70c8c716-1531-5f8d-865d-1a4abf6c6125'}, {'abstract': '“Light House,” by the choreographer Anne Zuerner, used fluorescent lights as part of an expression of dance and nature at Invisible Dog Art Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/arts/dance/light-house-keeps-dancers-and-audience-moving.html', 'snippet': '“Light House,” by the choreographer Anne Zuerner, used fluorescent lights as part of an expression of dance and nature at Invisible Dog Art Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The graceful sight of a lighthouse — preferably on a cliff with ocean waves crashing onto the rocks below — is more than a postcard symbol of summer. It’s a reminder of what happens when nature turns violent. In “Light House,” performed at the Invisible Dog Art Center on Friday, the choreographer Anne Zuerner drew on movements from the natural world, both calm and forceful. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/anne2/anne2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mermaids’ Flashlights, and Other Illuminations', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mermaids’ Flashlights, and Other Illuminations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuerner, Anne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Invisible Dog Art Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighthouses and Lightships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T21:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e131ec-a794-5342-8e0b-3dae9e7c061e', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e131ec-a794-5342-8e0b-3dae9e7c061e'}, {'abstract': 'Classic Shakespeare, Canadian acrobats and a GPS-led trek are among events planned for the 2014-15 season at the Skirball Center for the Performing Arts at New York University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/arts/skirball-announces-its-2014-15-season.html', 'snippet': 'Classic Shakespeare, Canadian acrobats and a GPS-led trek are among events planned for the 2014-15 season at the Skirball Center for the Performing Arts at New York University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classic Shakespeare, Canadian acrobats and a GPS-led trek are among events planned for the 2014-15 season at the Skirball Center for the Performing Arts at New York University. Highlights include “King Lear,” from Sept. 29 to Oct. 12, presented by Shakespeare’s Globe, the company behind Broadway’s recent productions of “Twelfth Night” and “Richard III”; Quebec’s high-flying troupe Cirque Alfonse (Oct. 13 to 19); and the Joshua Light Show Festival, a psychedelic mix of music, light, dance and projections (Oct. 23 to 25). Next spring, a three-week run of “Remote New York” is to guide participants through the city with GPS instructions delivered via headphones. More information: nyuskirball.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Skirball Announces  Its 2014-15 Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Skirball Announces Its 2014-15 Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skirball Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Shakespeare's Globe Theater", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-01T21:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4e05e4-bb2e-58b0-8ba7-8f91bdcf35f7', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4e05e4-bb2e-58b0-8ba7-8f91bdcf35f7'}, {'abstract': 'The NY Phil Biennial presented two compositions dedicated to manual labor on Friday at Avery Fisher Hall: Julia Wolfe’s “Anthracite Fields” and Steven Mackey’s “Dreamhouse.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/arts/music/ny-phil-biennial-offers-themes-of-mining-and-building.html', 'snippet': 'The NY Phil Biennial presented two compositions dedicated to manual labor on Friday at Avery Fisher Hall: Julia Wolfe’s “Anthracite Fields” and Steven Mackey’s “Dreamhouse.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The NY Phil Biennial presented a diptych of New York premieres dedicated to manual labor on Friday evening at Avery Fisher Hall. Julia Wolfe’s “Anthracite Fields” (2014) commemorates the Pennsylvania coal miners whose work fueled the industrial revolution. Steven Mackey’s “Dreamhouse” (2003) examines the process of building a house. Both works feature singers and an ensemble mixing acoustic and amplified instruments; both express unease with the American culture of comfort and consumption.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1261, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/BANG/BANG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Ensembles and Singers, a Night of Backbreaking Labor', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Ensembles and Singers, a Night of Backbreaking Labor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-