ts-went-unrealized.html', 'snippet': 'As an owner of the Nets when they were in New Jersey, Lewis Katz, who died Saturday in a plane crash, had a plan to help Newark, the state’s largest city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November 1999, Lewis Katz stood on a high school stage in New Jersey’s largest city and told an audience of students, local politicians and a smiling President Bill Clinton, “The New Jersey Nets are coming to Newark — remember that.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1117, 'width': 804, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/sports/CRASH/CRASH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lewis Katz’s Vision for the New Jersey Nets Went Unrealized', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vision for Nets and Newark Went Unrealized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Lewis R (1942-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T00:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb28591-7cb9-5d9e-a808-b038a5ea1af9', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb28591-7cb9-5d9e-a808-b038a5ea1af9'}, {'abstract': 'Congress must resist any push to weaken the lunch guidelines, and states must guard against accounting tricks used to snare a waiver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/opinion/bad-food-in-school-cafeterias.html', 'snippet': 'Congress must resist any push to weaken the lunch guidelines, and states must guard against accounting tricks used to snare a waiver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans on a powerful House committee have balked at requiring all schools to serve healthy lunches in the coming school year. The action drew a well-deserved rebuke from the first lady, Michelle Obama, who has focused public attention on combating obesity among young people through exercise and better nutrition. Let’s hope the Senate holds out against such inanity. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Food in School Cafeterias', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Food in School Cafeterias', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch and Breakfast Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T00:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc1ce9a-3b35-506f-a6a0-f42b5a11348f', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc1ce9a-3b35-506f-a6a0-f42b5a11348f'}, {'abstract': 'The State Senate should follow the Assembly’s lead and approve legislation that has wide support from medical groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/opinion/a-vote-on-medical-marijuana.html', 'snippet': 'The State Senate should follow the Assembly’s lead and approve legislation that has wide support from medical groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Assembly easily approved a law legalizing medical marijuana last Tuesday, and there appear to be enough votes to pass similar legislation in the State Senate if that chamber’s leaders agree to allow a vote. They ought to do so before the legislative session ends on June 19. The bills would make the drug available, under tight regulation, to patients who, in many cases, do not get relief from other medications. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vote on Medical Marijuana', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vote on Medical Marijuana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T00:52:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae6e309-40fb-569d-b14e-642519f91225', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae6e309-40fb-569d-b14e-642519f91225'}, {'abstract': 'After a vote by the Working Families Party to support Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, liberals were exulting in what they believed would be the start of a tectonic shift in New York politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/nyregion/tense-negotiations-between-left-and-cuomo-mark-wild-convention.html', 'snippet': 'After a vote by the Working Families Party to support Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, liberals were exulting in what they believed would be the start of a tectonic shift in New York politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLONIE, N.Y. — Weeks of intense negotiations between Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and an impatient, insurgent left resolved themselves shortly before midnight on Saturday in a stormy night of brinkmanship and shuttle diplomacy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ra