web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-june-2-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, June 2, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I tell people it’s like a funnel. You’re at the small end of the funnel for so long, and then suddenly the world opens up. It takes time to get used to it.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, June 2, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T04:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/0abc0be3-bb58-56a6-a915-e7e362a6f5a8', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0abc0be3-bb58-56a6-a915-e7e362a6f5a8'}, {'abstract': 'In 1989, a Chinese general refused to take part in violence against protesters, sending tremors through the Communist Party establishment, documents and interviews show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/world/asia/tiananmen-square-25-years-later-details-emerge-of-armys-chaos.html', 'snippet': 'In 1989, a Chinese general refused to take part in violence against protesters, sending tremors through the Communist Party establishment, documents and interviews show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — On a spring evening in 1989, with the student occupation of Tiananmen Square entering its second month and the Chinese leadership unnerved and divided, top army commanders were summoned to headquarters to pledge their support for the use of military force to quash the protests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/asia/TIANANMEN/TIANANMEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tales of Army Discord Show Tiananmen Square in a New Light', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tales of Army Discord Show Tiananmen Square in a New Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Liberation Army (China)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Qinxian', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Xiaoming', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T04:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs and Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97845e82-9378-5803-92d6-5fb82bdc3e41', 'word_count': 2534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97845e82-9378-5803-92d6-5fb82bdc3e41'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/arts/television/whats-on-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (TCM) A HARD DAY’S NIGHT (1964) When this film from the director Richard Lester had its debut, Bosley Crowther of The New York Times was astounded. “I wouldn’t believe it either, if I hadn’t seen it with my own astonished eyes,” he wrote of this first fiction film of the Beatles, adding that it “has so much good humor going for it that it is awfully hard to resist.” The film stars the Fab Four poking fun at Beatlemania in a plotline that takes viewers through the misadventures before a big show. “And all the way through the picture, there are frenzied episodes of the Beatles’ encounters with squealing fans and with reporters who ask silly questions, all in a facile, witty vein,” Mr. Crowther wrote. “But more than this, it’s a fine conglomeration of madcap clowning in the old Marx Brothers’ style, and it is done with such a dazzling use of camera that it tickles the intellect and electrifies the nerves.” Above, Mr. Lester at the train window with the Beatles. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T04:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ab0ee8-d0c6-5507-8ed2-482bdada428f', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ab0ee8-d0c6-5507-8ed2-482bdada428f'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 2, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/pageoneplus/corrections-june-2-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 2, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 2, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T05:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b5d0c96-2e2d-5d03-9ea0-b8bd657006b2', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b5d0c96-2e2d-5d03-9ea0-b8bd657006b2'}, {'abstract': 'Six people from a group known as the Church of the Almighty God were arrested in the killing of a woman at a McDonald’s restaurant in eastern china, but a cellphone video of the attack raised questions about whether witnesses should have intervened.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/anger-in-china-after-mcdonalds-patron-beaten-to-death/', 'snippet': 'Six people from a group known as the Church of the Almighty God were arrested in the killing of a woman at a McDonald’s restaurant in eastern china, but a cellphone video of the attack raised questions about whether witnesses should have intervene...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The beating death of a woman in a McDonald’s restaurant in eastern China has triggered widespread anger over the slow response of witnesses and condemnation of a fringe religious group that the police say influenced the attackers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anger in China After McDonald’s Patron Beaten to Death', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religious Cults', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Lidong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of Almighty God (Eastern Lighting)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Heilongjiang Province (China)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shandong Province (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T06:07:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy