ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The station, whose function is to check for smuggled goods, not to fight paramilitary forces, was under siege for more than 12 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — Several hundred separatist fighters mounted a coordinated assault against a border guard headquarters in the eastern city of Luhansk on Monday, holding it under siege for more than 12 hours in what appeared to be an attempt to eliminate the strategic control center for the region’s long and porous border with Russia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03ukraine01/03ukraine01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Separatists Attack a Border Guard Headquarters in Eastern Ukraine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Separatists Attack a Border Guard Headquarters in Eastern Ukraine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poroshenko, Petro Olekseyevich', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luhansk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T10:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d363ee66-b7f0-5a19-92b6-a48a409559cb', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d363ee66-b7f0-5a19-92b6-a48a409559cb'}, {'abstract': 'Chen Guang, one of the soldiers ordered to clear the protesters from Tiananmen Square in 1989, describes those days in an interview conducted before his detention by the Chinese authorities in the lead-up to the anniversary of the crackdown.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/q-a-chen-guang-on-the-soldiers-who-retook-tiananmen-square/', 'snippet': 'Chen Guang, one of the soldiers ordered to clear the protesters from Tiananmen Square in 1989, describes those days in an interview conducted before his detention by the Chinese authorities in the lead-up to the anniversary of the crackdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring of 1989, Chen Guang was a 17-year-old soldier with the 65th Group Army, which was instructed to clear student protesters from Tiananmen Square. The 65th Group Army, based north of Beijing in Hebei Province, made two attempts to enter the capital, the first on May 20 after the declaration of martial law. That attempt failed, after thousands of Beijing residents swarmed the streets and halted their convoy. The second, successful, attempt was on June 3, and Mr. Chen was among the first soldiers to make it past the blockades of protesters and enter the Great Hall of the People with thousands of weapons he had secretly transported on a public bus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/world/02sino-soldiers04/02sino-soldiers04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Chen Guang on the Soldiers Who Retook Tiananmen Square', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Martial Law', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen Guang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Military Commission (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Liberation Army (China)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hebei Province (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Henan Province (China)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T10:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a53a1ea-9ab7-54bc-b53a-39abcdac5fef', 'word_count': 2248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a53a1ea-9ab7-54bc-b53a-39abcdac5fef'}, {'abstract': 'The streets of Hyderabad were thronged by Telangana supporters as it became India’s 29th state on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/celebration-and-lingering-tensions-as-indias-29th-state-is-born/', 'snippet': 'The streets of Hyderabad were thronged by Telangana supporters as it became India’s 29th state on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HYDERABAD, India — On Monday, the southern Indian state of Andhra Pradesh officially split in two, and India’s 29th state, Telangana, was born. President’s rule — the interim government of united Andhra Pradesh — lifted in the new state, and the first popular government of Telangana came into power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebration, and Lingering Tensions, as India’s 29th State Is Born', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hyderabad (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Telangana (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T10:27:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sriram Karri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sriram', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da95a748-313b-5652-98ec-c255f3ae1438', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da95a748-313b-5652-98ec-c255f3ae1438'}, {'abstract': 'Evidence suggests that it’s partly because of a subtle change in a question in the 2010 census.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/upshot/pinpointing-another-reason-that-more-hispanics-are-identifying-as-white.html', 'snippet': 'Evidence suggests that it’s partly because of a subtle change in a question in the 2010 census.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, I wrote about new research that showed that a net 1.2 million Hispanics changed their racial identification from “some other race” to “white” between the 2000 and 2010 censuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-jumbo.gif', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/upshot/01up-hispanic/01up-hispanic-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pinpointing Another Reason That More Hispanics Are Identifying as White', 'kicker': 'Demographic Shift', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T10:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51e9cf8-3256-5d2f-aa50-747da2228972', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51e9cf8-3256-5d2f-aa50-747da2228972'}, {'abstract': 'Words matter. Putting a label on normal variations of physiology can cause needless worry, spending and even bodily harm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/upshot/calling-an-ordinary-health-problem-a-disease-leads-to-bigger-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Words matter. Putting a label on normal variations of physiology can cause needless worry, spending and even bodily harm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any parent knows, babies spit up. It’s gastroesophageal reflux, a pediatrician will explain — milk leaking backward from the stomach. When I was a pediatrics resident, my hospital constructed foam wedges for infants to sleep on. The thinking was that infants who were sleeping at an angle would be less likely to have milk come back up.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/upshot/02UP-disease/02UP-disease-articleLarge.jpg', 'height'