ed in April between the Palestine Liberation Organization, which is dominated by the mainstream Fatah faction, and its rival Hamas, the Islamic militant group that has controlled the Gaza Strip since 2007. As Ms. Rudoren reported, the development has alarmed Israel and could prompt reactions from the European Union and the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Questions About the New Palestinian Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Answers to Questions About the New Palestinian Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestine Liberation Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T12:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/dccf56ee-d07a-5fd8-8a99-d6c4ec863302', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dccf56ee-d07a-5fd8-8a99-d6c4ec863302'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration is set to announce an aggressive plan to slash 30 percent of carbon emissions from United States power plants by 2030, and critics are already questioning its impact.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/the-news-in-washington-critics-respond-to-carbon-emissions-plan/', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration is set to announce an aggressive plan to slash 30 percent of carbon emissions from United States power plants by 2030, and critics are already questioning its impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good\xa0Monday\xa0morning from sunny Washington on what wil