ine': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f87de1ad-ee1c-5cdc-bd17-7083c67a1826', 'word_count': 2300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f87de1ad-ee1c-5cdc-bd17-7083c67a1826'}, {'abstract': 'The band will make up its canceled performances at New York’s Beacon Theater in October, and said that two more concerts there will be its last.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/allman-brothers-band-announces-final-concerts/', 'snippet': 'The band will make up its canceled performances at New York’s Beacon Theater in October, and said that two more concerts there will be its last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Allman Brothers Band pulled into the Beacon Theater in March, it was set to play what it said was the last of its annual New York residencies at the hall. But when Gregg Allman, the band’s singer and keyboardist, fell ill toward the end of the run, the final week of sold-out concerts were canceled, with a promise that the band would make them up. The question was whether that would happen before the end of the year, when, word from around the group had it, the Allmans were planning to disband (something Mr. Allman denied in interviews).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/02artsbeat-allman/02artsbeat-allman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/02artsbeat-allman/02artsbeat-allman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/arts/02artsbeat-allman/02artsbeat-allman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran