e, 'lastname': 'WATKINS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d18f3e8a-4363-556a-a214-a599349e2768', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d18f3e8a-4363-556a-a214-a599349e2768'}, {'abstract': 'The most intense moments of the Hong Kong-based photojournalist Liu Heung Shing’s career came when he was a witness to the Tiananmen Square protests in 1989.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/q-a-liu-heung-shing-on-photographing-tiananmen/', 'snippet': 'The most intense moments of the Hong Kong-based photojournalist Liu Heung Shing’s career came when he was a witness to the Tiananmen Square protests in 1989.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hong Kong-born photojournalist Liu Heung Shing, who shared a 1992 Pulitzer Prize for documenting an attempted coup in Russia, now lives in Beijing, where he devotes most of his time to organizing photo exhibitions and editing books on historical photos of China. His own photos from China are themselves an archive of the country’s astounding changes since the death of Mao Zedong. His images for Time magazine and The Associated Press in China in the late 1970s and early 1980s have been collected in “China After Mao.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Liu Heung Shing on Photographing Tiananmen', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Widener, Jeff (1956- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhao Ziyang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing News, The', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time (Magazine)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Globe and Mail', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seoul (South Korea)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-02T22:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/843c9e02-f140-5e46-b927-0406f267ea48', 'word_count': 1682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/843c9e02-f140-5e46-b927-0406f267ea48'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Butler has just released the third album from his dance-music project. Here, he previews the first single — and curates an exclusive playlist for T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/listen-up-hercules-and-love-affair-makes-a-case-for-house-music/', 'snippet': 'Andy Butler has just released the third album from his dance-music project. Here, he previews the first single — and curates an exclusive playlist for T.', 'lead_paragraph': '“America has never fully had its house music moment,” says Andy Butler — better known by his moniker Hercules and Love Affair — via Skype while vacationing in Brussels. “In Europe, it’s another story. I feel it’s a rite of passage for people to go to the discotheque.” Butler is an American through and through (he got his start D.J.ing around Denver and attended Sarah Lawrence College), but you wouldn’t know it from Hercules and Love Affair’s distinctly Continental sound. “Audiences there have a tradition of integrating dance music in pop culture,” he explains. Indeed, Butler’s breakout hit, 2008’s “Blind,” had its biggest reception in Italy, and was received warmly in Britain as well. If there’s anyone in a position to get statesiders dancing, though, it’s Butler — thanks especially to his energetic third album, “The Feast of the Broken Heart,” just released on Big Beat/Atlantic Records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 1306, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/02/t-magazine/02hercules-ledonne-2/02hercules-ledonne-2-thumbStanda