 'byline': {'original': 'By Giuseppe Gallo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giuseppe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gallo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71376287-5ddf-563a-b3e2-d41410b60404', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71376287-5ddf-563a-b3e2-d41410b60404'}, {'abstract': 'The International Energy Agency said $40 trillion would be needed through 2025, but even that level of investment would not solve the industry’s problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/business/energy-environment/report-calls-for-huge-investment-in-energy-development.html', 'snippet': 'The International Energy Agency said $40 trillion would be needed through 2025, but even that level of investment would not solve the industry’s problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Enormous amounts of capital investment — up to $2.5 trillion a year — will be needed to supply the world’s energy needs through 2035, according to a report released Monday by the International Energy Agency, the intergovernmental organization based in Paris.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Calls for Huge Investment in Energy Development', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Projects Huge Investment in Energy Growth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Energy Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T00:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce20bb9a-3584-5db3-bc64-2c7dfd312449', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce20bb9a-3584-5db3-bc64-2c7dfd312449'}, {'abstract': 'This short documentary profiles residents of the Isle de Jean Charles in Louisiana, as they confront a future threatened by sinking shorelines and rising seas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/opinion/vanishing-island.html', 'snippet': 'This short documentary profiles residents of the Isle de Jean Charles in Louisiana, as they confront a future threatened by sinking shorelines and rising seas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although it’s only 80 miles from New Orleans, the Isle de Jean Charles feels much farther away. It’s literally at the end of the road, connected to the mainland by a little two-lane strip of asphalt with water lapping at its edges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Vanishing Island’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coast Erosion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Isle de Jean Charles (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T00:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmanuel Vaughan-Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmanuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vaughan-Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/68d0b0ee-006e-58be-804c-eef104e28143', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68d0b0ee-006e-58be-804c-eef104e28143'}, {'abstract': 'By positioning Michael Bradley as essentially a third forward, Jurgen Klinsmann is gambling that higher scoring will offset the possibility that more goals will be conceded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/sports/soccer/jurgen-klinsmann-gambles-on-michael-bradleys-scoring-prowess-for-us-soccer.html', 'snippet': 'By positioning Michael Bradley as essentially a third forward, Jurgen Klinsmann is gambling that higher scoring will offset the possibility that more goals will be conceded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.J. — Several times during the United States national team’s match Sunday against Turkey, midfielder Michael Bradley drifted so far forward that he was lined up with striker Jozy Altidore near the Turks’ penalty area. At that point, Bradley had almost stopped being a midfielder and was essentially a third forward.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-USSOCCER/CITY-USSOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-USSOCCER/CITY-USSOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-USSOCCER/CITY-USSOCCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-USSOCCER/CITY-USSOCCER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':