r adversaries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/world/the-hague-icc-politics-seen-undercutting-credibility-of-a-court.html', 'snippet': 'Critics cite The Hague’s complicated relationship with the United States and say it is sometimes a forum for nations to criticize their adversaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — The top American envoy to the United Nations, Samantha Power, recently made an impassioned case for the International Criminal Court, a tribunal based here that the United States had pilloried only a decade ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics Seen Undercutting Credibility of a Court', 'kicker': 'Memo From the Hague', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politics Seen Undercutting Credibility of a Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hague (Netherlands)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T00:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cb4d821-1123-5e3b-88d6-7cb662a561db', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cb4d821-1123-5e3b-88d6-7cb662a561db'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Cuomo confronts a perennial Democratic challenge: placating the left while holding the center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/opinion/bru