 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belmont Park', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Desormeaux, Kent', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durkin, Tom', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T01:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'Quynhanh Do', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quynhanh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Do', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/fc00d3c3-b6af-5d63-bf02-68982a835d83', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/fc00d3c3-b6af-5d63-bf02-68982a835d83'}, {'abstract': 'In a Virginia field, some 7,000 Union soldiers were killed or wounded in an hour – and the fighting raged for another week.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/02/the-crossroads-at-cold-harbor/', 'snippet': 'In a Virginia field, some 7,000 Union soldiers were killed or wounded in an hour – and the fighting raged for another week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By late spring 1864, Lt. Gen. Ulysses S. Grant was relentlessly pursuing his advance on the Confederate capital at Richmond, Va. With his recent appointment as commander of the Union armies, Grant had brought a new approach to the war – one of absolute and brutal attrition. Knowing that he could replace as many men as he lost, even as the rebel army suffered from a desperate shortage of manpower, he had bulldozed his way across Virginia in what was named the Overland Campaign, throwing tens of thousands of men against the Confederate wall. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crossroads at Cold Harbor', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T01:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Soodalter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soodalter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c460bce-1f6a-588d-b79f-77a459d4d3c2', 'word_count': 1455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c460bce-1f6a-588d-b79f-77a459d4d3c2'}, {'abstract': 'The Belmont track announcer Tom Durkin has called seven Triple Crown attempts and may still see a victorious effort before he retires later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/sports/voice-of-belmont-stakes-can-see-the-finish-line.html', 'snippet': 'The Belmont track announcer Tom Durkin has called seven Triple Crown attempts and may still see a victorious effort before he retires later this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His hypnotist was back on call, but Tom Durkin was in a state of anything but deep sleep. He was riffling through the more than 2,000 words in his notebook on Monday, trying to match words with images, poring over videotape of dozens of horse races and anticipating every imaginable outcome for the 146th running of the Belmont Stakes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/DURKIN1/DURKIN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Las