ions', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T03:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jorge Arangure Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jorge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arangure', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1543cde-691d-5f0b-97f8-94b2741ecf71', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1543cde-691d-5f0b-97f8-94b2741ecf71'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets and the Phillies managed to play a nine-inning game for a change, and the Mets scored 11 runs to make sure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/sports/baseball/mets-overcome-leadoff-concerns-to-win-in-nine.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets and the Phillies managed to play a nine-inning game for a change, and the Mets scored 11 runs to make sure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — The Mets had a handful of flaws at the start of the season. For one, they lacked a leadoff hitter. Eric Young Jr. had not established himself as an everyday player. And Juan Lagares was not exactly a true leadoff hitter. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-METS/CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-METS/CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/sports/CITY-METS/CITY-METS-jumbo.jpg', 'h