': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ace0fb3f-b591-5049-8238-f85966baaf01', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ace0fb3f-b591-5049-8238-f85966baaf01'}, {'abstract': 'Amid worries about a threat from radicalized Europeans who fight in Syria and then return, France is arresting would-be jihadis even before they leave the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/world/europe/france-intercepts-jihadis-bound-for-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Amid worries about a threat from radicalized Europeans who fight in Syria and then return, France is arresting would-be jihadis even before they leave the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The three young Frenchmen were arrested as they tried to make their way to Syria to wage jihad. They had not harmed anyone in France or made plans to do so, according to the evidence at their trial in January, but in France these days, seeking to fight in Syria is enough to bring a charge of plotting terrorism — and in this case sentences of three to five years in prison.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/JP-JIHADI/JP-JIHADI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/world/JP-JIHADI/JP-JIHADI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/JP-JIHADI/JP-JIHADI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/JP-JIHADI/JP-JIHADI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum