selves so enthusiastic that they had voted several times. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assad’s Win Is Assured, but Limits Are Exposed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Assad’s Win Is Assured, but Limits Are Exposed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T08:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a7cae89-fc11-5333-af67-75e2f1510067', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a7cae89-fc11-5333-af67-75e2f1510067'}, {'abstract': 'Become a cause célèbre. There’s never been a smoother path from anonymity to Wolf Blitzer’s greenroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/magazine/how-to-succeed-in-washington-without-really-trying.html', 'snippet': 'Become a cause célèbre. There’s never been a smoother path from anonymity to Wolf Blitzer’s greenroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We seem to be in the midst of several national conversations. Every day, in fact, on MSNBC or Fox News or NPR or Sarah Palin’s Facebook page or my brother in-law’s Twitter feed, new national conversations are being set aloft over something or other of great importance — cyberbullying, digital diets, “slut-shaming,” Benghazi and all that. But the only way to have your national conversation rise above the others is to have a “face” of that conversation — your very own Pussy Riot, Edward Snowden, Sandra Fluke, New York City carriage horses or “Duck Dynasty” guys. Or that cattle rancher from Nevada, what’s his name?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/08politics-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/08politics-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/08politics-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/08politics-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1201, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/mag-08Politics-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/mag-08Politics-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08politics/mag-08Politics-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_