as. | Valeant’s bid for Allergan raises a question about the role of drug companies. | Pilgrim’s Pride raises its bid for Hillshire Brands. | Trouble may be brewing at Sales...', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the prospect of a guilty plea in the United States looming, the French bank BNP Paribas has enlisted the support of a powerful ally: its own government, including top regulators and the French president, DealBook’s Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg write. President François Hollande recently reached out to the White House to raise concerns about a plea deal, injecting a political undercurrent into a law enforcement investigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: France’s Direct Appeal on Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T11:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61998bcc-4aca-59db-932f-1e00e69e95eb', 'word_count': 1861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61998bcc-4aca-59db-932f-1e00e69e95eb'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s best musical race is the most wide open since 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/tony-awards-predictions-best-musical/', 'snippet': 'This year’s best musical race is the most wide open since 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will the emotional punch of “Beautiful: The Carole King Musical” send that show soaring to victory on Sunday in the race for the best musical Tony Award? Will cleverness carry the day with a win for “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder”? Or will comic antics – as well as the lack of a clear favorite in this