ath/', 'snippet': 'Two former protest leaders who spent years in prison expressed understanding about a classmate who chose to sit out the 1989 pro-democracy demonstrations in Tiananmen Square — and is now immensely wealthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring of 1989, Wang Dan’s image, with his tousled hair and oversized, plastic-framed glasses, became known to millions around the world as he rallied students on Beijing’s Tiananmen Square. A history major at the elite Peking University, he chose the path of protest that led to imprisonment and, eventually, to exile following the crackdown on June 4 of that year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03sino-elite/03sino-elite-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03sino-elite/03sino-elite-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03sino-elite/03sino-elite-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03sino-elite/03sino-elite-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/world/03sino-elite/03sino-elite-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Exiled Students, Sympathy for One Who Chose Another Path', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 