alestinian government, signaling new strains in the often rocky relationship between Israel and the United States, two close and critical allies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Condemns Plan in Washington to Work With New Palestinian Alliance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Condemns Plan in Washington to Work With New Palestinian Alliance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T17:13:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6825f9-7859-5d5f-af79-55f48baccc38', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6825f9-7859-5d5f-af79-55f48baccc38'}, {'abstract': 'Six people were shot in a laundromat on the South Side of Chicago on Monday night, the latest outbreak in a wave of gun violence plaguing the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/us/illinois-six-are-shot-in-laundromat-in-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'Six people were shot in a laundromat on the South Side of Chicago on Monday night, the latest outbreak in a wave of gun violence plaguing the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six people were shot in a laundromat\xa0on the South Side of Chicago on Monday\xa0night, the latest outbreak in a wave of gun violence plaguing the city. The shootings happened shortly after\xa08 p.m.\xa0in a coin laundry in the 7900 block of South Colfax Avenue, a police spokesman said. The victims, described as two teenagers and four adults by police, were taken to hospitals. None of the injuries were believed to be life-threatening, the police said. Although the number of homicides in Chicago had dropped amid increased police efforts — there were more than 500 homicides in 2012 — violence has jumped in recent months. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Six are Shot in Laundromat in Chicago', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Six Are Shot in Laundromat in Chicago', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Nelson D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laundry and Laundromats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T17:23:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22ce1674-3e3b-555e-b293-688febc703da', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22ce1674-3e3b-555e-b293-688febc703da'}, {'abstract': 'The anger and confusion over Sergeant Bergdahl’s release seems like a fitting end to a messy and in