le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a176b64d-bb1c-5dbb-908c-bb0319984678', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a176b64d-bb1c-5dbb-908c-bb0319984678'}, {'abstract': 'This month, the buzzy young talent Erik Madigan Heck is debuting a series of fine-art photographs at Bosi Contemporary and curating an issue of Creem magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/photographer-erik-madigan-heck-the-absorbed-tradition-bosi-contemporary-gallery-creem-magazine/', 'snippet': 'This month, the buzzy young talent Erik Madigan Heck is debuting a series of fine-art photographs at Bosi Contemporary and curating an issue of Creem magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 30-year-old photographer and filmmaker Erik Madigan Heck has gained acclaim for hyper-real, richly colorful images that elevate fashion portraiture to fine art. A new series of 13 of his large-scale images, “The Absorbed Tradition,” debuts tomorrow at New York’s BOSI Contemporary gallery. They will also be featured as part of a special new Heck-curated and photographed issue of Creem magazine, out this month. “I decided that I needed to make a whole magazine that articulated a sort of remedy to the problem that I had created in my head,” Heck says of the Creem project, “which was that everything” in fashion image culture “resembled everything else.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03heck-bobb/03heck-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03heck-bobb/03heck-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03hec