 'nyt://article/3d09170b-6685-5f55-8f92-3bde01a1aab4'}, {'abstract': 'An opera based on the nine black students who enrolled at Central High School in Little Rock, Ark., is in the works, with music by Tania León and a libretto by Henry Louis Gates Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/an-opera-about-little-rock-integration-with-libretto-by-henry-louis-gates-jr/', 'snippet': 'An opera based on the nine black students who enrolled at Central High School in Little Rock, Ark., is in the works, with music by Tania León and a libretto by Henry Louis Gates Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since John Adams had his first operatic hit with “Nixon in China,” operas based on the headlines and recent history rather than mythological tales and literary adaptations have become plentiful. The University of Central Arkansas is hoping to add the story of the Little Rock Nine \xa0— nine black students who enrolled at what had been an all-white high school in Little Rock, Ark., in 1957 – to the operatic annals. The school is in the process of commissioning the composer Tania León and the scholar Henry Louis Gates Jr. to create a work about the incident, and hopes to present the premiere in September 2017, around the 60th anniversary of the events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/arts1/arts1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/arts1/arts1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 796}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/arts1/arts1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't