llowers of @TheCaucus Twitter account asked about a variety of issues, including the politics and timing of the rule, its effect on coal-producing states, the implications of the regulations for global negotiations on climate change, and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter Chat About New E.P.A. Carbon Pollution Regulations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davenport, Coral', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T21:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54bc91c2-4dc2-58bb-abb5-dde8d3c3dd2c', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54bc91c2-4dc2-58bb-abb5-dde8d3c3dd2c'}, {'abstract': 'Facing discontent over her government’s preparations for the World Cup, President Dilma Rousseff defended the funding of new stadiums and said Brazilians planning to shun the event were a “small minority.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/world/americas/brazilian-president-hits-back-at-critics-in-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Facing discontent over her government’s preparations for the World Cup, President Dilma Rousseff defended the funding of new stadiums and said Brazilians planning to shun the event were a “small minority.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRASÍLIA — The year was 1970. Agents of Brazil’s military dictatorship had arrested Dilma Rousseff, then a member of a fledgling urban guerrilla group, the Palmares Armed Revolutionary Vanguard. Inside the prison where she was being held in São Paulo, a debate raged among the inmates: Should they support Brazil in that year’s World Cup?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/world/BRAZIL/BRAZIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazilian President Rejects Criticism Over World Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazilian President Rejects Criticism Over World Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T21:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a68d09c-c82c-5cf9-9426-fa0aeeb28d05', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a68d09c-c82c-5cf9-9426-fa0aeeb28d05'}, {'abstract': 'No women are allowed at JF Men, the hairstylist Julien Farel’s new salon on the Upper East Side, and the services clients receive there (whether a facial or a salt-and-pepper camouflage) are nobody’s business but their own.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/03/julien-farel-jf-men-salon-restore-salon-and-spa/', 'snippet': 'No women are allowed at JF Men, the hairstylist Julien Farel’s new salon on the Upper East Side, and the services clients receive there (whether a facial or a salt-and-pepper camouflage) are nobody’s business but their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No man wants a woman to know when he’s gotten what the hairstylist Julien Farel calls a “salt-and-pepper camouflage” — where you blend your gray discreetly to get back to your natural color. And so what happens at JF Men — Farel’s new men’s-only salon, which opened below his new Restore Salon and Spa flagship at the Loews Regency Hotel on the Upper East Side of Manhattan — stays at JF Men. “It’s almost like Vegas,” Farel laughs. Indeed, the intimate space feels akin to a modern-day gentlemen’s club: a lounge for relaxing after a power lunch, a flat-screen TV, a bar cart — “We’re only missing the cigar,” Farel quips in a thick French accent. Need to get your shoes shined while you get a little taken off the back? No problem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/03/t-magazine/03julien-beddie/03julien-beddie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Groomed for Greatness | A Men’s Spa Where Discretion is Key', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regency Hotel (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-03T21:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47a9741e-1e83-58da-8a0b-7f2948361f25', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47a9741e-1e83-58da-8a0b-7f2948361f25'}, {'abstract': 'The life of the writer Jane Bowles in part forms the basis for Julia Jarcho’s play “Nomads.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/theater/nomads-at-the-incubator-arts-project.html', 'snippet': 'The life of the writer Jane Bowles in part forms the basis for Julia Jarcho’s play “Nomads.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The playwright Julia Jarcho and the director Alice Reagan share a fondness for strangeness, for edges that don’t quite line up. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/nomads/nomads-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlar