 Festival USA has seemed to be in more or less permanent reconstruction mode in recent years, thanks to the renovation of some of its main performance spaces: first the weather-beaten Memminger Auditorium (reopened in 2008), then the College of Charleston’s Sottile Theater (2009) and the historic Dock Street Theater (2010). Now the end is in sight, with work well along on a rebuilding and acoustical upgrade of the Gaillard Auditorium, which is scheduled to reopen next May.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1088, 'width': 1691, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/arts/04FESTIVAL/04FESTIVAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumb