able to afford costlier products, they drive the demand for organic, fair-trade and artisanal items.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/business/international/dairy-industrys-reputation-in-india-opens-door-for-upscale-farms.html', 'snippet': 'As more middle-class Indians are able to afford costlier products, they drive the demand for organic, fair-trade and artisanal items.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GURGAON, India — On a 26-acre farm a couple hours’ drive inland from Mumbai, hundreds of black-and-white Holstein-Friesian cows laze around, dining on seasonal greens and listening to a custom playlist of rap, pop, classical and even devotional music. They are treated to a routine medical checkup before heading to a “rotary milking parlor,” where their udders are gently squeezed, until the cows step away, at will.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upscale Dairies Grow in India, Promising Safer Milk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Upscale Dairies Grow in India, Promising Safer Milk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bearak, Max', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T00:17:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Max Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Max', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None},