N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T04:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julien Guyon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Guyon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3eb1ba9-2e21-5eb2-9127-a5b77ef74b7a', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3eb1ba9-2e21-5eb2-9127-a5b77ef74b7a'}, {'abstract': 'The Cubs made it 1-1 in the eighth on a home run, and won the game an inning later on a two-out single.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/sports/baseball/mets-lose-lead-in-8th-and-game-in-the-9th.html', 'snippet': 'The Cubs made it 1-1 in the eighth on a home run, and won the game an inning later on a two-out single.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — As the night wore on, and the Mets and the Cubs entered the eighth inning of a one-run game, the fans at Wrigley Field waited quietly. They had no reason to cheer, but no reason to leave. The game was still somehow anyone’s to win, because the Mets were just as inexplicable as their Cubs. Both teams were talented enough to get runners on base, and inept enough to strand most of them there. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 841}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1462, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/sports/METS/METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Lose Lead in 8th and Game in the 9th', 'kicker': 'Cubs 2, Mets 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Lose Lead in 8th and Game in the 9th', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'den Dekker, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coghlan, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T04:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8847476b-49d9-52ce-bcd6-2a717f2e2f84', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8847476b-49d9-52ce-bcd6-2a717f2e2f84'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:45 P.M. (Starz) WHITE HOUSE DOWN (2013) A police officer and former soldier (Channing Tatum) interviewing for a job with the Secret Service (he doesn’t get it) finds himself in the White House at the very moment it is overrun by a paramilitary group in this action-adventure directed by Roland Emmerich. Jamie Foxx (above right, with Mr. Tatum) plays the president, who needs saving — from the terrorists, and from big business — if only for his workable peace plan for the Middle East. And Maggie Gyllenhaal, James Woods, Richard Jenkins, Lance Reddick and Jason Clarke portray the administration’s team players. The film “is as demented and entertaining as promised, and a little less idiotic than feared,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. Mr. Emmerich “makes the opening siege unsettling enough to grab your attention and then, once he has it, begins folding in lighter moments — one-liners, cartoonish bits of business, laughably impossible situations and stunts — that ensure that at least this American collapse doesn’t end up feeling too heavy.” He “gives it the pow,” she added, “while Mr. Tatum provides the pulse.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T04:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/00eeca5a-d924-5bca-a925-7dece2e9b421', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00eeca5a-d924-5bca-a925-7dece2e9b421'}, {'abstract': 'Because of Shavuot, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Wednesday and Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/nyregion/special-parking-rules-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Because of Shavuot, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Wednesday and Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of Shavuot, alternate-side street-cleaning regulations will be suspended in New York City on Wednesday and Thursday. Other regulations remain in effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Special Parking Rules in New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parking Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T04:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce9f1cdf-fefc-536f-be56-f831dad22165', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce9f1cdf-fefc-536f-be56-f831dad22165'}, {'abstract': 'A wealthy insurance executive beat a perennial conservative candidate in the Republican primary in New Jersey’s Third Congressional District on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/nyregion/in-new-jersey-a-republican-nominee-will-try-to-hold-on-to-a-congressional-seat.html', 'snippet': 'A wealthy insurance executive beat a perennial conservative candidate in the Republican primary in New Jersey’s Third Congressional District on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A wealthy insurance executive beat a perennial conservative candida