-dream-in-mississippi-where-a-runoff-looms.html', 'snippet': 'A win by Chris McDaniel in the Republican primary would give Democrats hope in a polarized state, but the road to victory already seems blocked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a night of surprising regional shifts in voter turnout Tuesday, neither Thad Cochran, an incumbent Republican senator in Mississippi, nor Chris McDaniel, a state senator backed by Tea Party groups, appeared to reach the 50 percent necessary to avoid a runoff in Mississippi’s Republican Senate primary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 457}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1522, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/upshot/05UP-Primary/05UP-Primary-thu