ent/', 'snippet': 'A documentary on beauty pageant contestants and the women who see the contests as an affront to Indian culture will have its theatrical release in India on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Nisha Pahuja began filming the Miss India pageant in 2008, she envisioned the documentary as a portrait of India careening towards modernity through the lens of the pageant contestants.\xa0 But over time, Ms. Pahuja found herself drawn to another side of the story: India’s protest movement against these beauty contests, led largely by conservative religious groups here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Through Miss India and Its Critics, Two Approaches to Women’s Empowerment', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pahuja, Nisha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T09:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zahir Janmohamed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zahir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Janmohamed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8ba942f-2d71-5220-9580-747b6b9a8a66', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8ba942f-2d71-5220-9580-747b6b9a8a66'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/us/your-wednesday-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the Morning Briefing on NYT Now. (Download us for iPhone.)',