, '_id': 'nyt://article/3b239f5f-910e-566f-8197-0008e4322b85', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b239f5f-910e-566f-8197-0008e4322b85'}, {'abstract': 'I have come to understand that my company is not an e-commerce business; I am a retailer with a good website.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/why-im-rethinking-my-investment-in-e-commerce/', 'snippet': 'I have come to understand that my company is not an e-commerce business; I am a retailer with a good website.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been selling furniture and accessories online for about six years. Two years ago, we realized that we needed to upgrade our website if we wanted to keep up, so we went out and hired a company to rebuild it from scratch. We went with a developer that works with the popular Magento platform, and the site came out very well. As a matter of fact, it won an award from one of the magazines that give out awards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I’m Rethinking My Investment in E-Commerce', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 