{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Hudson's Bay Co", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nordstrom Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saks Fifth Avenue', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T11:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c49868a-5116-59f6-94f4-a0c62867f280', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c49868a-5116-59f6-94f4-a0c62867f280'}, {'abstract': 'BNP Paribas pinned its hopes on a legal memo. | Regulators may restrict BNP’s dollar-clearing operations. | The notion of legal education is colliding with the profit motive in Charleston, S.C. | Goldman’s new chief strategy officer will continue to expand the bank’s businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/morning-agenda-bnps-secret-weapon-misfired/', 'snippet': 'BNP Paribas pinned its hopes on a legal memo. | Regulators may restrict BNP’s dollar-clearing operations. | The notion of legal education is colliding with the profit motive in Charleston, S.C. | Goldman’s new chief strategy officer will continue ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BNP Paribas, under investigation for doing business with Sudan and other countries that the United States has blacklisted, is weeks away from having its parent company plead guilty to the crime. But several months ago, BNP thought it had a secret weapon to avoid that fate altogether, DealBook’s Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess write. BNP showed prosecutors a memo that the bank thought would explain and possibly mitigate its conduct.', 'source': 'The New York 