e.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/us/politics/hillary-clinton-says-she-has-moved-on-from-lewinsky-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Clinton, in an interview with People magazine released Wednesday, said, “I think everybody needs to look to the future.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton, in an interview with People magazine released Wednesday, said she had “moved on” from the Monica Lewinsky scandal that dominated her husband’s second term as president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton Says She Has ‘Moved On’ From Lewinsky Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewinsky, Monica S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vanity Fair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T11:53:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/838bdb65-6aae-5c08-9948-4ca1779d7a31', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/838bdb65-6aae-5c08-9948-4ca1779d7a31'}, {'abstract': '“Holler if Ya Hear Me,” a new musical that weaves songs and poetry from the rapper Tupac Shakur, is set to open on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/theater/holler-if-ya-hear-me-uses-songs-by-tupac-shakur.html', 'snippet': '“Holler if Ya Hear Me,” a new musical that weaves songs and poetry from the rapper Tupac Shakur, is set to open on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring of 2001, Todd Kreidler met his boss, the playwright August Wilson, for breakfast at the Cafe Edison, as was their custom. Mr. Kreidler was assisting Wilson as he brought his play “King Hedley II” to Broadway, but really he was there to learn whatever Wilson wanted to teach him. And that morning, the subject was Tupac Shakur.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08HOLLER1_SPAN/08HOLLER1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i