onald make history Sunday by winning her sixth Tony Award, the most ever in acting, for her performance as Billie Holliday in “Lady Day at Emerson’s Bar and Grill”? Or do you think LaTanya Richardson Jackson will prevail in the race for best actress in a play, for her star turn as Lena Younger in “A Raisin in the Sun”? And where does the intense competition in this category leave Cherry Jones, who delivered a much-discussed portrayal of Amanda in “The Glass Menagerie”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Award Predictions: Leading Actress in a Play', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daly, Tyne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Cherry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Audra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Jessie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Hara, Kelli", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T12:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126f7851-753f-53b9-be5b-8c54cd70599f', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126f7851-753f-53b9-be5b-8c54cd70599f'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve will release the Beige Book economic survey Wednesday, as it does eight times each year. It’s akin to asking your uncle about the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/upshot/no-need-to-read-th