mazon’s business practices, the prisoner-swap fallout, political polarization, Hillary Clinton and sentencing laws in Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/morning-views-4/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on Amazon’s business practices, the prisoner-swap fallout, political polarization, Hillary Clinton and sentencing laws in Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon’s running battle with the Hachette Book Group over e-book pricing has alarmed publishers. The online retail giant is blocking or slowing the sales of Hachette’s books — including the imprint Little, Brown. Amazon wants “to get the best deal for itself,”\xa0writes The New York Times editorial board, “while it squeezes publishers, annoys its customers and hurts authors by limiting their sales.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T12:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b6810f2-353e-5c04-b8ab-08971b6eaa69', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b6810f2-353e-5c04-b8ab-08971b6eaa69'}, {'abstract': 'As you pack for your summer vacation, Molly Wood tests out a new alternative to the small point-and-shoot cameras or the bulky high-end ones: the medium-size mirrorless camera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/personaltech/100000002918267/cameras-to-inspire-vacation-envy.html', 'snippet': 'As you pack for your summer vacation, Molly Wood tests out a new alternative to the small point-and-shoot cameras or the bulky high-end ones: the medium-size mirrorless