CAP Awards for Adventurous Programming. The awards are to be presented at a ceremony during the league’s national conference, which is being held in Seattle, Wednesday through Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bold Sounds: Orchestras Honored for ‘Adventurous Programming’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Augusta Read', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alabama Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Albany Symphony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN COMPOSERS ORCHESTRA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN SOCIETY OF COMPOSERS, AUTHORS AND PUBLISHERS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T13:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c104e0e3-a85a-5a3c-88ff-2a56bdbd75fc', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c104e0e3-a85a-5a3c-88ff-2a56bdbd75fc'}, {'abstract': 'The influential fashion critic Cathy Horyn chooses the most iconic images from a new book on the House of Dior.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/dior-legendary-images-book-cathy-horyn/', 'snippet': 'The influential fashion critic Cathy Horyn chooses the most iconic images from a new book on the House of Dior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The influential fashion critic Cathy Horyn chooses the most iconic images from a new book on the House of Dior.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gallery | No Filter', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Filter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T13:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fc082d0-e160-566a-af40-d0ea2f152753', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fc082d0-e160-566a-af40-d0ea2f152753'}, {'abstract': 'The two candidates were stuck at about 49 percent each, and campaign officials said that final results might not come until Thursday, as absentee and contested ballots remain to be counted.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/whats-news-in-washington-mississippi-primary-too-close-to-call/', 'snippet': 'The two candidates were stuck at about 49 percent each, and campaign officials said that final results might not come until Thursday, as absentee and contested ballots remain to be counted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good\xa0Wednesday\xa0morning from a sunny Washington. Eight states held primary elections last night, but most of the political excitement was concentrated in Mississippi, where votes are still being tallied in the Republican race between Senator Thad Cochran and his Tea Party-backed challenger, Chris McDaniel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s News in Washington: Mississippi Primary Too Close to Call', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_