4', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be02a711-ce59-50df-9c47-8039c8ffcc54'}, {'abstract': 'PAUL SMALERA introduces Op-Talk, a new service from The New York Times with a big mission: To bring you, our readers, the most interesting opinion and commentary from all over.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/introducing-op-talk/', 'snippet': 'PAUL SMALERA introduces Op-Talk, a new service from The New York Times with a big mission: To bring you, our readers, the most interesting opinion and commentary from all over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Op-Talk, a new service from The New York Times with a big mission: To bring you, our readers, the most interesting opinion and commentary from all over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing Op-Talk', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T13:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Smalera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smalera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39158717-5c5d-5e28-a975-6a2c8903cd92', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39158717-5c5d-5e28-a975-6a2c8903cd92'}, {'abstract': 'Penelope Skinner’s play “The Village Bike,” with Greta Gerwig, is making its American debut in an MCC Theater production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/theater/greta-gerwig-in-the-village-bike.html', 'snippet': 'Penelope Skinner’s play “The Village Bike,” with Greta Gerwig, is making its American debut in an MCC Theater production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is your Urban Dictionary lesson of the week: A “village bicycle” is slang for a local slut — everyone in town has ridden the bike, you see. The term has a double meaning, though, in Penelope Skinner’s play “The Village Bike,” making its American debut in an MCC Theater production. In the play, Becky (Greta Gerwig) is pregnant and hormonal and her sex drive is healthier than ever, but her husband seems to have completely lost interest in sex. Adventures ensue when she turns to pornography and then buys a used bike (an actual one) from a man known for his promiscuity. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE2/08GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Des