n initial public offering.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-articleLarge.png', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-jumbo.png', 'height': 762, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-superJumbo.png', 'height': 762, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/business/dbpix-travelport/dbpix-travelport-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Travelport, Backed by Blackstone, Files for an I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Public', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Travelport Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddeccc58-4c25-509f-bb3c-df314591add3', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddeccc58-4c25-509f-bb3c-df314591add3'}, {'abstract': 'Stockard Channing, F. Murray Abraham and Megan Mullally will join Nathan Lane and Matthew Broderick in a revised version of Terrence McNally’s 1980s comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/channing-abraham-and-mullally-to-join-its-only-a-play-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Stockard Channing, F. Murray Abraham and Megan Mullally will join Nathan Lane and Matthew Broderick in a revised version of Terrence McNally’s 1980s comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tony Award winner Stockard Channing, the Oscar winner F. Murray Abraham and the Emmy winner Megan Mullally will join Nathan Lane and Matthew Broderick on Broadway in a newly revised version of Terrence McNally’s 1980s comedy “It’s Only a Play,” the producers said on Wednesday. The show centers on an anxious playwright (Mr. Broderick); his best friend (Mr. Lane), who has left theater for television; the producer (Ms. Mullally) and a diva star (Ms. Channing) of the playwright’s new show; and a hypocritical drama critic (Mr. Abraham). The ensemble will also include Micah Stock as a coat check attendant; casting for the roles of the play’s director and a taxi driver will be announced later. The production, which reunites Mr. Lane and Mr. Broderick years after their starring roles in Broadway’s “The Producers” and the 2005 revival of “The Odd Couple,” will begin performances in late summer at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater and open on Oct. 9. Jack O’Brien will direct.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 795}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1916, 'width': 1446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/04artsbeat-stockard/04artsbeat-stockard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Channing, Abraham and Mullally to Join ‘It’s Only a Play’ on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Channing and Abraham To Join ‘It’s Only a Play’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNally, Terrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2800ae8-05d6-515f-87cb-f8536efa13f6', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2800ae8-05d6-515f-87cb-f8536efa13f6'}, {'abstract': 'Chrome, who won the Kentucky Derby and the Preakness Stakes, is the 3-5 morning-line favorite for Saturday’s race at Belmont Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/sports/california-chrome-draws-no-2-post-for-belmont-stakes.html', 'snippet': 'Chrome, who won the Kentucky Derby and the Preakness Stakes, is the 3-5 morning-line favorite for Saturday’s race at Belmont Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has always been a sense of destiny surrounding California Chrome — his owners called him their Kentucky Derby horse as soon as he hit the ground. They were right, and after the colt won the Preakness Stakes, too, the air of inevitably has only thickened.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/sports/SUB-05belmont/SUB-05belmont-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Decent Draw and Rising Hopes for California Chrome', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Decent Draw and Rising Hopes for Chrome', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'California Chrome (Race Horse)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04f1cb31-af62-5e1d-8ac9-41621e0dafb2', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04f1cb31-af62-5e1d-8ac9-41621e0dafb2'}, {'abstract': 'Zappos plans to replace traditional job listings with a social network, writes ANNA NORTH, and critics worry this could encourage other employers to encroach further into our personal lives.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/the-new-face-of-networking/', 'snippet': 'Zappos plans to replace traditional job listings with a social network, writes ANNA NORTH, and critics worry this could encourage other employers to encroach further into our personal lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The anemic labor market has forced the unemployed into various contortions in their efforts to get a job. The latest: joining a special social network so that maybe, someday, they can work for Zappos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Face of ‘Networking’', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f626065c-dfac-5b77-9580-f54e843db308', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f626065c-dfac-5b77-9580-f54e843db308'}, {'abstract': 'A number of companies are offering plans that effectively allow companies to reimburse employees for the individual insurance they buy. The problem is that the Internal Revenue Service may not approve — and the penalties could be big.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/would-you-try-this-health-insurance-strategy-with-your-company/', 'snippet': 'A number of companies are offering plans that effectively allow companies to reimburse employees for the individual insurance they buy. The problem is that the Internal Revenue Service may not approve — and the penalties could be big.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March, we interviewed Dr. Ezekiel J. Emanuel, a doctor who advised the Obama administration on the Affordable Care Act. Dr. Emanuel had just published a book in which he predicted that within a decade, private employers would largely abandon providing health insurance to employees. This, he said, would happen even though such coverage benefits from a big tax break.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Would You Try This Health Insurance Strategy With Your Company?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Ezekiel J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15111eaf-cde3-5424-96ba-5f5cc0ce1001', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15111eaf-cde3-5424-96ba-5f5cc0ce1001'}, {'abstract': 'The columnist takes a look at Mrs. Clinton’s recent media appearances, and the reasons behind them.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/hillary-speaks-but-oh-so-carefully/', 'snippet': 'The columnist takes a look at Mrs. Clinton’s recent media appearances, and the reasons behind them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And now we enter the Period of Parsing. What you are about to behold will make all prior textual analyses — of scripture, of scrolls — look like halfhearted child’s play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Speaks! But Oh So Carefully.', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df26ad16-5e79-5014-8709-336e614a338b', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df26ad16-5e79-5014-8709-336e614a338b'}, {'abstract': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s remarks were his first response to President Obama’s speech last week asserting that military force is not always the answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/world/middleeast/ayatollah-ali-khamenei-sees-change-in-west-point-speech.html', 'snippet': 'Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s remarks were his first response to President Obama’s speech last week asserting that military force is not always the answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Speaking from a stage decorated with a banner proclaiming “America cannot do a damn thing,” Iran’s supreme leader on Wednesday asserted that the Obama administration had taken the option of military intervention to resolve conflicts off the table.', 'print_section': 'A', 'prin