 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e5ebcaa-5ce6-5a56-8d16-a78b41620dc5', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e5ebcaa-5ce6-5a56-8d16-a78b41620dc5'}, {'abstract': 'The return of chandelier earrings; shorts suited for the workplace and more shopping news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/fashion/how-to-wear-shorts-in-the-workplace-the-return-of-chandelier-earrings-and-more-shopping-news.html', 'snippet': 'The return of chandelier earrings; shorts suited for the workplace and more shopping news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way the jewelry designer Lisa Salzer of Lulu Frost sees it, the return of chandelier earrings can be credited to the Céline fall runway, where they dangled solo in every single look. “Elongated, sculptural single earrings really signal a move away from delicate and dainty styles,” Ms. Salzer said. “My take is to do one long style with a simple stud on the opposite ear.” The designer Lizzie Fortunato is similarly inclined, citing the oversize earrings in Marni’s spring collection. “I’m a fan of merging the ‘statement’ and ‘delicate’ trends,” she said. These summer-friendly styles can ease you into the trend. They’ll look glamorous worn together, but for an added dose of cool, pair one with a bitty stud — lest you look as if you have lost one earring.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'