le/420ca6e4-db67-52a9-922a-defe132a66ee'}, {'abstract': 'The Vostok Battalion’s composition has raised questions about Russia’s role in eastern Ukraine. Its resolve could determine how long the fighting continues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/world/europe/in-ukraine-separatist-militia-with-russian-fighters-holds-a-key.html', 'snippet': 'The Vostok Battalion’s composition has raised questions about Russia’s role in eastern Ukraine. Its resolve could determine how long the fighting continues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — Surface-to-air missiles pilfered from army bases. Defectors from Ukraine’s elite special forces. Russian fighters who slipped across a porous border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Separatist Militia in Ukraine With Russian Fighters Holds a Key', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Separatist Militia in Ukraine With Russian Fighters Holds a Key', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:55:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/247f99f0-5fd7-5646-bc37-00dbe7d24302', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247f99f0-5fd7-5646-bc37-00dbe7d24302'}, {'abstract': 'As thousands elsewhere mark the 25th anniversary of the killings at Tiananmen Square, the the People’s Liberation Army Daily, the Chinese military newspaper, published an editorial calling for a stronger, more robust military posture.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/on-tiananmen-anniversary-chinas-military-touts-its-strength/', 'snippet': 'As thousands elsewhere mark the 25th anniversary of the killings at Tiananmen Square, the the People’s Liberation Army Daily, the Chinese military newspaper, published an editorial calling for a stronger, more robust military posture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times reported this week that there was discord throughout the People’s Liberation Army — even up to the ranks of the general staff — during the protests of 1989. Officers and soldiers argued over how to handle the demonstrations and what orders to obey. After soldiers carried out the massacre of civilians on June 3 and 4, 1989, killing hundreds, possibly thousands, of people, top military officers sought reassurances from Communist Party leaders that the army would never be deployed again for internal unrest. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Tiananmen Anniversary, China’s Military Touts Its Strength', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Liberation Army (China)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T15:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlenam