 the circumstances and decisions surrounding larger social injustices and then relate that back to their own experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Facing History School in New York City takes a unique approach to cyberbullying, based in part on its partnership with Facing History and Ourselves, a professional development organization that integrates the concepts of identity, community, responsibility, decision-making and participation into all aspects of its curriculum. By looking at case studies about social injustices, students try to understand the circumstances and decisions surrounding these events and then relate that back to their own experience and communities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Curriculum to Strengthen Students Against Cyberbullying', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facing History School (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T16:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c89746-34fb-5c31-8ded-dba9cc0d4275', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c89746-34fb-5c31-8ded-dba9cc0d4275'}, {'abstract': 'An investor consortium has bought back ALM Media from its current owners, Apax Partners and the Royal Bank of Scotland.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytime