e and cover star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WhoFrida Giannini, the creative director of Gucci, and Deborah Needleman, the editor in chief of T, hosted a sharply dressed crowd to fete the first anniversary of Gucci’s Chime for Change charity initiative. James Franco and Blake Lively, two faces of the brand, were in attendance, as were the writers Malcolm Gladwell and Marianne Pearl and the Russian street-style stars Miroslava Duma and Anya Ziourova. Attendees craned their necks and hoisted their smartphones to catch a glimpse of Solange Knowles, who was the D.J. for a portion of the festivities, and the evening’s guest of honor, none other than T’s new cover star, Beyoncé.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T Toasts Gucci’s Charity with Beyoncé', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Star Power: A Gift for Girls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/095ce2ec-9a25-5fbf-a6e1-98cccb3b0e08', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/095ce2ec-9a25-5fbf-a6e1-98cccb3b0e08'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco 49ers tight end said in an interview on Wednesday that the I.P.O. was about more than money. Instead, he said, it’s about helping him build his brand.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/vernon-davis-breaks-his-silence-over-fantex-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco 49ers tight end said in an interview on Wednesday that the I.P.O. was about more than money. Instead, he said, it’s about helping him build his brand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vernon Davis, a