nk': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguezmacedo Rivera, Jose Luis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro-Wright, Eduardo', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, H Lee Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Lynn E', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T17:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b958c2a3-b8da-5a9e-b190-967b4a267e87', 'word_count': 1565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b958c2a3-b8da-5a9e-b190-967b4a267e87'}, {'abstract': 'Hillshire Brands is facing two competing takeover bids, but its biggest decision may be whether to stick with its own acquisition strategy and remain independent, Steven M. Davidoff writes in the Deal Professor column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/04/hillshire-must-decide-whether-to-be-target-or-suitor/', 'snippet': 'Hillshire Brands is facing two competing takeover bids, but its biggest decision may be whether to stick with its own acquisition strategy and remain independent, Steven M. Davidoff writes in the Deal Professor column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone is asking how Hillshire Brands can get out of its acquisition of Pinnacle Foods in light of two competing bids for Hillshire for more than $6 billion. Instead, perhaps the question should be whether Hillshire even wants to exit the Pinnacle deal, and if so, what is the price it would have to pay Pinnacle for such relief. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':