rts', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb899811-194a-5b8b-8288-069f76f3bbad', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb899811-194a-5b8b-8288-069f76f3bbad'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Vacationers,” infidelity and other issues mar a family’s vacation in Mallorca, Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/books/in-the-vacationers-emma-straub-looks-at-infidelity.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Vacationers,” infidelity and other issues mar a family’s vacation in Mallorca, Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emma Straub’s bustling new novel is about a New York family’s two-week idyll in a house on the Spanish island of Mallorca. It’s also about a different kind of break: infidelity. The book is full of couples, and all of them have to cope with some kind of cheating during the course of the story. Even its youngest, most petulant character, a sharp-eyed teenager named Sylvia Post, has been betrayed by her high school boyfriend and rewarded with an Adonis of a Spanish tutor as compensation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/05BOOK/05BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/05BOOK/05BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 928}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/arts/05BOOK/05BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 662, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':