et', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T22:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0790493f-a7bc-5553-9174-4952aacb76f4', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0790493f-a7bc-5553-9174-4952aacb76f4'}, {'abstract': 'You can’t understand sexual violence in India without understanding caste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/opinion/indias-feudal-rapists.html', 'snippet': 'You can’t understand sexual violence in India without understanding caste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN a distressed father is reporting his daughter’s disappearance to a policeman in India, there are some questions he doesn’t want to hear. “What is your caste?” is one of them. Yet, the father, Sohan Lal, said this was the first thing the police asked him last Tuesday, when he begged them for help. After revealing his low-caste background as a Shakya, Mr. Lal said the officers mocked him and refused to lift a finger.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Feudal Rapists', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India’s Feudal Rapists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-04T22:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amana Fontanella-Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amana', 'middlename': None, '