destabilize Ukraine or aggressively extend Russia’s reach will not go unanswered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s decision to commit $1 billion to bolster security in Central and Eastern Europe sends important messages to both NATO allies and President Vladimir Putin of Russia. The crisis over Russia’s annexation of Crimea has calmed down a bit, and some Europeans, like France, seem eager to put it behind them. But Mr. Putin has shown he cannot be trusted. The alliance needs to be honest with itself and take full account of his ruthless unpredictability as it plans security arrangements for the future. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Standing Up to Mr. Putin', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Standing Up to Mr. Putin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastern Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T01:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://artic