g-views-5/', 'snippet': 'Morning Views', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of children crossing the border between Mexico and the United States illegally has doubled each year since 2011, with 60,000 more expected to arrive this year. This — The New York Times editorial board says — is not a security crisis, but a humanitarian one. “Young people are being pushed out of their homes, not pulled,” the board writes, citing increasing civil unrest in Mexico and parts of Central America. “They are fleeing for their lives.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T11:34:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5168198-c19d-5344-a24a-45ea59be87e8', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5168198-c19d-5344-a24a-45ea59be87e8'}, {'abstract': 'James W. Breyer will advise and invest alongside IDG Capital Partners, which is expected to make early stage investments in Chinese technology, media and telecommunication companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/accels-breyer-to-partner-with-v-c-firm-in-china/', 'snippet': 'James W. Breyer will advise and invest alongside IDG Capital Partners, which is expected to make early stage investments in Chinese technology, media and telecommunication companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI – James W. Breyer, the venture capitalist who made a fortune with an early bet on Facebook, is putting some of his winnings to work in China, partnering with Beijing-based venture capital firm to invest in Chinese technology sta