, is an expertly built machine for the mass production of tears. Directed by Josh Boone (“Stuck in Love”) with scrupulous respect for John Green’s best-selling young-adult novel, the film sets out to make you weep — not just sniffle or choke up a little, but sob until your nose runs and your face turns blotchy. It succeeds.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06FAULT_SPAN/06FAULT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Love, Complicated by Cancer', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love in the Time Remaining', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodley, Shailene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elgort, Ansel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Michael H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neustadter, Scott', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Fault in Our Stars (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Fault in Our Stars (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boone, Josh (1979- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T11:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2096f94-ee91-50bd-9e81-160ae844bb39', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2096f94-ee91-50bd-9e81-160ae844bb39'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrities and Times readers offer their Tony Award predictions.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/tony-award-predictions-readers-and-boldface-names-weigh-in/', 'snippet': 'Celebrities and Times readers offer their Tony Award predictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So said Anna Wintour, Condé Nast artistic director and editor-in-chief of Vogue, about the race for best actor in a musical as part of our Tony Award predictions series this week. At our invitation, Ms. Wintour, Oscar and Tony winner Liza Minne