ce yesterday.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/talking-rebranding-and-logos-with-loewes-jonathan-anderson/', 'snippet': 'The brand revealed its new logo and typeface yesterday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rebranding of heritage names has become something of a fashion trend recently, what with Hedi Slimane’s conversion of Yves Saint Laurent’s ready-to-wear to Saint Laurent Paris; Pinault-Printemps-Redoute’s transformation into Kering, complete with little owl pictogram: Celine’s new minimalism courtesy of Phoebe Philo, and so on. The latest entrant into this group is LVMH’s Loewe, under the creative directorship of Jonathan Anderson (aka J Anderson, iconoclastic Young British designer), which unveiled its new logo and typeface yesterday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Rebranding and Logos With Loewe’s Jonathan Anderson', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Jonathan William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kering SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T12:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f62880ca-a71f-5a13-af00-c9858c563bfa', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f62880ca-a71f-5a13-af00-c9858c563bfa'}, {'abstract': 'An educational intervention from a concern troll.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/energy-choices/', 'snippet': 'An educational intervention from a concern troll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nate Silver got a lot of grief when he chose Roger Pielke Jr., of all people, to write about environment for the new 538. Pielke is regarded among climate scientists as a concern troll – someone who pretends to be open-minded, but is actually committed to undermining the case for emissions limits any way he can. But is this fair?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Choices', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T12:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7467fda6-495d-5de4-adf9-e6d1193cd765', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7467fda6-495d-5de4-adf9-e6d1193cd765'}, {'abstract': 'The accused were convicted on charges including intentional murder, arson and participating in terrorist activities, with nine people sentenced to death. Three others received', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/world/asia/dozens-are-sentenced-on-terrorism-charges-in-xinjiang.html', 'snippet': 'The accused were convicted on charges including intentional murder, arson and participating in terrorist activities, with nine people sentenced to death. Three others received', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Chinese courts in the northwestern region of Xinjiang sentenced 81 people on terrorism and other charges on Thursday, according to the state broadcaster China Central Television. The sentences are part of a widening crackdown in the region after a spate of deadly violence in China for which the authorities have blamed foreign-backed Islamist separatists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Sentences Scores in Xinjiang for Acts of Terror', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Sentences Scores in Xinjiang for Acts of Terror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T12:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca5e50c5-a2c6-533e-873a-4cb2b4be95f7', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca5e50c5-a2c6-533e-873a-4cb2b4be95f7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is meeting with foreign leaders at the Group of 7 meetings in Brussels to discuss energy, climate change and, of course, the conflict between Russia and Ukraine that led to Russia’s exclusion from the meetings.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/whats-news-in-washington-obama-talks-climate-change-at-summit/', 'snippet': 'President Obama is meeting with foreign leaders at the Group of 7 meetings in Brussels to discuss energy, climate change and, of course, the conflict between Russia and Ukraine that led to Russia’s exclusion from the meetings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good\xa0Thursday\xa0morning. Political controversies over a\xa0prisoner swap\xa0with the Taliban and the\xa0scandal at the Department of Veterans Affairs\xa0are still swirling in Washington, but on this warm and gloomy day, President Obama has a busy agenda across the pond.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s News in Washington: Obama Talks Climate Change at Summit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T12:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4915a3e-0c88-57b3-9a6b-07fa646093f8', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4915a3e-0c88-57b3-9a6b-07fa646093f8'}, {'abstract': 'Israel said the proposal for about 1,500 units was a response to the creation of a unity Palestinian government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/world/middleeast/new-israeli-settlement-plans-draw-swift-condemnation.html', 'snippet': 'Israel said the proposal for about 1,500 units was a response to the creation of a unity Palestinian government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel says it is moving ahead with the planning and construction of hundreds of Jewish settlement homes as retaliation against the new Palestinian government, which has been accepted by the United States and much of the world even though it is supported by Hamas. The announcement enraged the Palestinians and flouted international opinion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 's