nifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08723818-409e-5315-be60-d3c208fec784', 'word_count': 4816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08723818-409e-5315-be60-d3c208fec784'}, {'abstract': 'Small, delicate pieces of jewelry, meant to be mixed and worn every day, are sentimental talismans of a particular moment in time.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/jewelry-report-necklaces-bracelets-rings-gucci-cartier-hermes-dior/', 'snippet': 'Small, delicate pieces of jewelry, meant to be mixed and worn every day, are sentimental talismans of a particular moment in time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Small, delicate pieces of jewelry, meant to be mixed and worn every day, are sentimental talismans of a particular moment in time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Something Special', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44e05f64-a9cf-5009-922c-9280ed6716a2', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44e05f64-a9cf-5009-922c-9280ed6716a2'}, {'abstract': 'In an internal investigation, the company cited bureaucratic problems and the failure of individual employees to deal with a fatal ignition flaw, and said 15 had been dismissed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/business/gm-ignition-switch-internal-recall-investigation-report.html', 'snippet': 'In an internal investigation, the company cited bureaucratic problems and the failure of individual employees to deal with a fatal ignition flaw, and said 15 had been dismissed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARREN, Mich. — A sweeping internal investigation of General Motors released on Thursday condemned the company for its decade-long failure to fix a deadly safety defect, one that led to “devastating consequences,” including at least 13 deaths. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/business/06motors2/06motors2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Inquiry Cites Years of Neglect Over Fatal Defect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Inquiry Cites Years of Neglect Over Fatal Defect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barra, Mary T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valukas, Anton R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T13:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229d4a96-03ca-53ac-ac14-9f111c98cede', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229d4a96-03ca-53ac-ac14-9f111c98cede'}, {'abstract': 'Sprint and T-Mobile have settled on the terms of a $32 billion deal. | A maverick judge leaves his mark. | Valeant’s opaque business model has been revealed. | Assessing the effects of a multibillion-dollar penalty on BNP’s capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/morning-agenda-sprint-and-t-mobile-near-a-deal-of-their-own/', 'snippet': 'Sprint and T-Mobile have settled on the terms of a $32 billion deal. | A maverick judge leaves his mark. | Valeant’s opaque business model has been revealed. | Assessing the effects of a multibillion-dollar penalty on BNP’s capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to a wave of consolidation in the telecommunications industry, the nation’s third- and fourth-largest wireless phone operators have agreed to a deal of their own. The operators, Sprint and T-Mobile, which have long contemplated a merger, finally settled on the terms of a $32 billion deal that is likely to be announced this summer, DealBook’s David Gelles and Michael J. de la Merced write. The merger would create a more formidable rival to the two largest wireless phone providers in the United States, Verizon and AT&T. Under the terms of the deal, Sprint, which is majority-owned by Japan’s SoftBank, would acquire T-Mobile for about $40 a share in cash and stock, a 17 percent premium to Wednesday’s price. Accounting for regulatory uncertainty, the early terms of the deal also include a breakup fee of more than $1 billion that Sprint would pay to T-Mobile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Sprint and T-Mobile Near a Deal of Their Own', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T13:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b93d03c-eb06-5cb3-9c55-9e6cd5671cd2', 'word_count': 1614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b93d03c-eb06-5cb3-9c55-9e6cd5671cd2'}, {'abstract': 'This poem, by Emma J., is one of the 11 winners of our fifth annual Found Poem Student Contest. It comes from a Travel article, “A Big Sur Bath by the Light of the Moon.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/found-poem-favorite-in-the-night/', 'snippet': 'This poem, by Emma J., is one of the 11 winners of our fifth annual Found Poem Student Contest. It comes from a Travel article, “A Big Sur Bath by the Light of the Moon.”', 'lead_parag