been much discussed recently, after a European court\xa0ruled\xa0last month that E.U. residents can force Google to remove certain embarrassing search results about them. Indeed, according to a Time magazine article published yesterday, Google is receiving 10,000 requests per day to be ‘forgotten’ in Europe. Neither the decision nor the volume of interest among Europeans in exercising this new “right” will affect Americans directly, but they may feed into a bigger conversation about memory and forgetting at a time when so much about our lives is recorded online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1980, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/opinion/nyto-forgotten/nyto-forgotten-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',