s may become anxious or withdrawn, may have trouble regulating their emotions or dealing with challenges, and may develop behavior problems or even become depressed themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 451, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 451, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-classroom/motherlode-classroom-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Teacher Is Depressed', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Annie Murphy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T16:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Murphy Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': 'Murphy', 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faded147-eb63-5261-9293-0c62a085c72c', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faded147-eb63-5261-9293-0c62a085c72c'}, {'abstract': 'The virus in a 44-year-old Saudi man who died in November was the same as that in an ailing camel he was tending, scientists report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/science/dna-test-indicates-camel-to-human-transmission-of-mers.html', 'snippet': 'The virus in a 44-year-old Saudi man who died in November was the same as that in an ailing camel he was tending, scientists report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the clearest evidence yet that the MERS virus can be passed directly from camels to humans, genetic sequencing has shown that a 44-year-old Saudi man who died of Middle East Respiratory Syndrome in November had a strain virtually identical to that in one of the camels in his herd, researchers said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DNA Test Indicates Camel-to-Human Transmission of MERS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke