ment.” Perversely, since in yoga we express aspirations as if they were already so, the sentence reminds me of people who congratulate me on being “cancer free.” Stable disease often goes unrecognized. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 793}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 775, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1550, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/31/health/31well_gubar/31well_gubar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With Cancer: Chronic, Not Cured', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Engelberg, Miriam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T16:26:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c7c221-a247-5583-ba7b-959492216006', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c7c221-a247-5583-ba7b-959492216006'}, {'abstract': 'The Oxford, England-based quartet — anointed by Paul Epworth, Adele’s producer — debuts a remix of “Pools,” the lead single from their new album, here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/glass-animals-interview-pools-song-remix/', 'snippet': 'The Oxford, England-based quartet — anointed by Paul Epworth, Adele’s producer — debuts a remix of “Pools,” the lead single from their new album, here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Bayley, the frontman for the quirky new Oxford, England-based band Glass Animals, says his original life plan was to become a doctor. In fact, Bayley insisted on finishing his degree in medicine at King’s College London before officially forming Glass Animals with three of his high school friends, Drew MacFarlane, Edmund Irwin-Singer and Joe Seaward, in 2012. It was a second beginning of sorts: Bayley had published some of the quartets demos on the Internet in 2010, but had removed them almost immediately when they proved too popular. “People started getting in touch,” says Bayley. “We didn’t know what it was like to be in a band. We didn’t know anyone in a band at all, so we freaked out and took everything off the Internet.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/t-magazine/05glass-safronova/05glass-safronova-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | The Smooth, Psychedelic Sounds of Glass Animals', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T16:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova'