'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile US Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T16:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0447149e-fc8a-518d-b9d7-777d37e069ec', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0447149e-fc8a-518d-b9d7-777d37e069ec'}, {'abstract': 'A classified report on the Army’s investigation into Sgt. Bowe Bergdahl’s disappearance in June 2009 says he had left assigned areas before and then returned, according to people briefed on it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/world/asia/bowe-bergdahl-walked-away-before-military-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'A classified report on the Army’s investigation into Sgt. Bowe Bergdahl’s disappearance in June 2009 says he had left assigned areas before and then returned, according to people briefed on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A classified military report detailing the Army’s investigation into the disappearance of Sgt. Bowe Bergdahl in June 2009 says that he had wandered away from assigned areas before — both at a training range in California and at his remote outpost in Afghanistan — and then returned, according to people briefed on it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bergdahl Is Said to Have History of Leaving Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bergdahl Is Said to Have History of Leaving Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T16:57:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e453bc2b-bf97-5e5e-8746-8db527b96ac6', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e453bc2b-bf97-5e5e-8746-8db527b96ac6'}, {'abstract': '“Jenny From the Block,” a.k.a. Jennifer Lopez, performed at Orchard Beach on Wednesday night to a hometown crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/arts/music/review-jennifer-lopez-back-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': '“Jenny From the Block,” a.k.a. Jennifer Lopez, performed at Orchard Beach on Wednesday night to a hometown crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As party tricks go, Jennifer Lopez has the best and most effective one: Regardless of her milieu, she comes off as if she’s slumming. Making records and having songs on the radio? That’s not something she appears interested in doing particularly often, even though she’s welcomed when she does. Making movies? Here and there, sure, but nothing notably great in years. Appearing on television? On “American Idol,” she had twice the wattage of anyone else around her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1267}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 485, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1812, 'width': 858, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/JENNIFER/JENNIFER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Homecoming Queen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Homecoming Queen in the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T17:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/57c78d9a-0b78-5d88-9625-38fb91e21fe2', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57c78d9a-0b78-5d88-9625-38fb91e21fe2'}, {'abstract': 'At Flinders Lane in the East Village, the chef grew up in Melbourne, but the most interesting dishes draw on flavors from across the Indian Ocean and the South China Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/dining/hungry-city-flinders-lane-in-the-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'At Flinders Lane in the East Village, the chef grew up in Melbourne, but the most interesting dishes draw on flavors from across the Indian Ocean and the South China Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is the choice: a bottle of brown HP sauce, with London’s Houses of Parliament in sky blue on the label and a secret recipe (tomatoes, tamarind, dates, molasses, malt vinegar, mysterious spices) dating from the late 19th century, or a ramekin of mayonnaise laced with a house-made sambal of bird’s-eye chiles, fish sauce and palm sugar.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/dining/11HUNGRY_395/11HUNGRY_395-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia Doesn’t Seem So Far Away', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Australia Isn’t So Far Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flinders Lane (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Melbourne (Australia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T17:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdd53d42-9568-54a4-8c95-fba909e372f3', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdd53d42-9568-54a4-8c95-fba909e372f3'}, {'abstract': 'Only 11 horses have won thoroughbred racing’s Triple Crown, the first, in 1919, and the last, in 1978. California Chrome will aim to become the 12th in Saturday’s Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/sports/the-triple-crown-eleven.html', 'snippet': 'Only 11 horses have won thoroughbred racing’s Triple Crown, the first, in 1919, and the last, in 1978. California Chrome will aim to become the 12th in Saturday’s Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Horse racing fans are used to the disappointment. Eleven times a horse has come into the Belmont Stakes having won the first two legs of the Triple Crown in the years since Affirmed captured the last one in 1978. Eleven times, it didn’t happen. Each came with such possibility, and each left with heartbreak. When Spectacular Bid was outgunned down the stretch by Coastal in 1979, no one knew the drumbeat of failure that was ahead, that would become the unofficial background music of the Belmont.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Triple Crown Eleven', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'California Chrome (Race Horse)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruguet, Jean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cauthen, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T17:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c104bc3a-8a65-5d89-bb40-1f5772c129ef', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c104bc3a-8a65-5d89-bb40-1f5772c129ef'}, {'abstract': 'The annual event, which runs Aug. 1 to 25, is scheduled to include almost 3,200 shows.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/scottish-independence-debate-will-reach-edinburgh-fringe-festival/', 'snippet': 'The annual event, which runs Aug. 1 to 25, is scheduled to include almost 3,200 shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Bowie was named best British male solo artist at the Brit Awards in February, his acceptance speech, read on his behalf by Kate Moss, included the plea “Scotland, stay with us,” and he thus entered the divisive public debate over Scottish independence, which will come to a vote in September. Mr. Bowie’s phrase is the inspiration for “All Back to Bowie’s,” a freewheeling and decidedly political presentation by a group of Scottish artists, including David Greig and Cora Bissett, that is planned for this summer at the annual Edinburgh Festival Fringe. The show will include poetry, music and more in a variety format that will be different at each performance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/SUBARTS-BRIEF3/SUBARTS-BRIEF3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/SUBARTS-BRIEF3/SUBARTS-BRIEF3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 795}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/SUBARTS-BRIEF3/SUBARTS-BRIEF3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 774, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam