, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kisselgoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f787d8fa-75ce-5274-85a0-441c8186ceb8', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f787d8fa-75ce-5274-85a0-441c8186ceb8'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Glaser’s concept for harnessing solar energy was deemed credible enough for the government to spend $20 million studying it, only to conclude it was too expensive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/us/peter-glaser-who-envisioned-space-solar-power-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Glaser’s concept for harnessing solar energy was deemed credible enough for the government to spend $20 million studying it, only to conclude it was too expensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Glaser, who in the late 1960s envisioned a way to harness limitless solar power in space and transmit it for use on Earth via invisible microwaves — a notion so intriguing that the government spent $20 million studying it, only to conclude that it was too complex and expensive — died on May 29 at his home in Lexington, Mass. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/us/GLASER-obit/GLASER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/04/us/GLASER-obit/GLASER-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/04/us/GLASER-obit/GLASER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima