ank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/057d08f9-e888-57af-b7f0-fc6ed8334c02', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/057d08f9-e888-57af-b7f0-fc6ed8334c02'}, {'abstract': 'The limits of what an individual can do in the face of well-financed opposition are shown throughout this documentary, which looks at the effects of the Citizens United Supreme Court case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/movies/a-documentary-on-the-koch-brothers-influence-on-elections.html', 'snippet': 'The limits of what an individual can do in the face of well-financed opposition are shown throughout this documentary, which looks at the effects of the Citizens United Supreme Court case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of the impact of “Citizen Koch” comes from juxtaposing average Americans with the moneyed interests that grip today’s political process. When we see a Republican in Wisconsin weighing her dissatisfaction with her party and her stance on abortion, it’s an inspiring sight of a citizen at work, grappling in good faith with the situation at hand. It’s a world away from the documentary’s portrayal of Americans for Prosperity, the conservative advocacy group funded by the billionaires David and Charles Koch.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06CITIZEN/06CITIZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06CITIZEN/06CITIZEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06CITIZEN/06CITIZEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c