tion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/141d4d33-0e7c-5bdf-997e-f3346c9ab296', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/141d4d33-0e7c-5bdf-997e-f3346c9ab296'}, {'abstract': 'While most races in this year’s Tony Awards are fiercely competitive, interviews with 40 of 800 voters yield some informed predictions of who will triumph Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/theater/theaterspecial/shoo-ins-are-few-in-heated-tony-race.html', 'snippet': 'While most races in this year’s Tony Awards are fiercely competitive, interviews with 40 of 800 voters yield some informed predictions of who will triumph Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a departure from recent Tony Awards seasons, when popular musicals like “The Book of Mormon,” “Once,” and “Kinky Boots” were dominant, voters for Sunday’s prizes are likely to spread them around. But among which shows? Which performers and artists? Making predictions is unusually difficult this year, with few clear-cut favorites, more wild cards than usual and some fierce races involving Hollywood stars, veteran stage actors and past Tony winners.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TONYS1/06TONYS1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 945, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TONYS1/06TONYS1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 945}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TONYS1/06TONYS1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TONYS1/06TONYS1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'wid