ct', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wrestling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Wrestling Entertainment Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVERTISING COUNCIL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T22:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane L. Levere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Levere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46c6d90b-90f6-5765-98c4-88316c82bdc3', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46c6d90b-90f6-5765-98c4-88316c82bdc3'}, {'abstract': 'Janelle Monáe held court in her free show of retro-futurist R&B to kick off the 36th Celebrate Brooklyn! series, with an enormous overflow audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/arts/music/janelle-monae-kicks-off-celebrate-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Janelle Monáe held court in her free show of retro-futurist R&B to kick off the 36th Celebrate Brooklyn! series, with an enormous overflow audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every narrative needs a tension, and in the kinetic, fantastical saga of Janelle Monáe’s career, it boils down to the tug-of-war between abandon and control. At the Prospect Park Bandshell on Wednesday night, she was wheeled onstage in a straitjacket, her posture and pompadour briefly evoking the Bride of Frankenstein. Breaking free, she headed straight into “Givin Em What They Love,” a prowling funk processional whose title refrain lands somewhere between a boast and a pledge. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Regent of Retro and Future', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Regent of Retro and Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monae, Janelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrate Brooklyn (Festival)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-05T22:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8108bdd-2235-51c2-a95b-132209cfa7dc', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8108bdd-2235-51c2-a95b-132209cfa7dc'}, {'abstract': 'In Alex van Warmerdam’s malevolent adult fairy tale, “Borgman,” an enigmatic, beady-eyed drifter intrudes on the lives of a rich suburban family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/movies/borgman-alex-van-warmerdams-adult-fairy-tale.html', 'snippet': 'In Alex van Warmerdam’s malevolent adult fairy tale, “Borgman,” an enigmatic, beady-eyed drifter intrudes on the lives of a rich suburban family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no one who resembles a sleeping princess, a fairy godmother or a dashing romantic savior in the Dutch filmmaker Alex van Warmerdam’s malevolent adult fairy tale, “Borgman.” The story’s magic is black, its perfidy driven by evil spirits.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06BORGMAN/BORGMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06