lark Gregg, stars Mr. Gregg as a scuffling, obsequious agent specializing in child actors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/movies/trust-me-stars-clark-gregg-as-a-hollywood-agent.html', 'snippet': '“Trust Me,” written and directed by Clark Gregg, stars Mr. Gregg as a scuffling, obsequious agent specializing in child actors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until it disintegrates in an explosion of sentimentality, “Trust Me” qualifies for what could be called “The Day of the Locust” award. That imaginary honor, named for the Nathanael West novel, would be bestowed on the year’s nastiest, most stomach-turning movie about no-holds-barred Hollywood wheeling and dealing. Such films are usually box office poison, but they still are made, perhaps because they give their creators a chance to vent. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TRUST/06TRUST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TRUST/06TRUST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TRUST/06TRUST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TRUST/06TRUST-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/arts/06TRUST/06TRUST-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'i