l': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eec3927-c714-5605-b6f2-d3fc3676335c', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eec3927-c714-5605-b6f2-d3fc3676335c'}, {'abstract': 'A crunchy and fun debut by Kameron Austin Collins.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/05/language-originally-known-as-mocha/', 'snippet': 'A crunchy and fun debut by Kameron Austin Collins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Every now and then, people write to me asking for advice on constructing and, although I sadly no longer have time to actually collaborate with constructors, I always enjoy discussing the aspects of construction. Once in a while, among those who write to me, there emerges a truly nice person with charmingly good manners, who is not only smart but loves the process of learning and furthermore, puts it to good use. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Language Originally Known As Mocha', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T02:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/059852b6-b749-595d-ac01-dfe095ed0009', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059852b6-b749-595d-ac01-dfe095ed0009'}, {'abstract': 'The Houston Astros selected Brady Aiken, a left-handed pitcher, with the first pick in the 2014 draft, the first time in more than two decades a high school pitcher was selected with the top pick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/sports/baseball/picking-high-school-pitcher-at-no-1-astros-end-trend.html', 'snippet': 'The Houston Astros selected Brady Aiken, a left-handed pitcher, with the first pick in the 2014 draft, the first time in more than two decades a high school pitcher was selected with the top pick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECAUCUS, N.J. — In 1991, the Yankees selected Brien Taylor, a high school left-hander, with the first overall pick in baseball’s amateur draft. His failure to make the majors scared teams away from showing similar faith in a prep pitcher in the 22 drafts that followed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1905, 'width': 1497, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/CITY-DRAFT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/sports/CITY-DRAFT-1/C