', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Paul E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T09:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7666501-93b8-5c9a-afcf-8ba3f0a1ef9b', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7666501-93b8-5c9a-afcf-8ba3f0a1ef9b'}, {'abstract': 'June 6, 1944, has long since taken on the aura of myth, and the commemorations retell stories of heroism and sacrifice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/world/europe/memories-of-d-day-replayed-on-the-normandy-coast.html', 'snippet': 'June 6, 1944, has long since taken on the aura of myth, and the commemorations retell stories of heroism and sacrifice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VIERVILLE-SUR-MER, France — At Camp Dog Green, recreated just a few miles inland from where combat raged on and around the Normandy beaches in June 1944, soldiers in American uniforms and nurses with the Red Cross insignia on their breast pockets mill among the drab green tents, tuning their tinny radios to the music of Glenn Miller. They appear to be just waiting for orders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/world/DDAY/DDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/world/DDAY/DDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio