onomic growth and carbon emissions were once closely linked. The results in nine states show they no longer necessarily are.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/upshot/best-of-both-worlds-northeast-cut-emissions-and-enjoyed-growth.html', 'snippet': 'Economic growth and carbon emissions were once closely linked. The results in nine states show they no longer necessarily are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some critics of the Environmental Protection Agency’s new requirements for power plants argue that forcing emissions reduction will curtail economic growth. But the recent experience of states that already cap carbon emissions reveals that emissions and economic growth are no longer tightly tied together.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best of Both Worlds? Northeast Cut Emissions and Enjoyed Growth', 'kicker': 'Environmental Ingenuity', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best of Both Worlds in Cutting Emissions?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairfield, Hannah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Fairfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fairfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf652dc8-7863-5d09-ab34-1e1cc29d31d1', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf652dc8-7863-5d09-ab34-1e1cc29d31d1'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia met with Petro O. Poroshenko of Ukraine, and Mr. Putin also had an informal conversation with President Obama at the D-Day commemoration ceremony in France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/world/europe/obama-honors-moment-of-liberation-in-normandy.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia met with Petro O. Poroshenko of Ukraine, and Mr. Putin also had an informal conversation with President Obama at the D-Day commemoration ceremony in France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BÉNOUVILLE, France — As President Obama wrapped up a four-day European trip on Friday, the violent conflict over Ukraine seemed to move toward a new phase of diplomacy, but it remained unclear whether the Russian president, Vladimir V. Putin, was genuinely willing or able to call off a pro-Russian uprising across his border.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/world/PREXY/PREXY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/world/PREXY/PREXY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 747}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/world/PREXY/PREXY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/world/PRE