into an election cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/upshot/its-not-too-soon-to-pay-attention-to-senate-polling.html', 'snippet': 'An analysis of Senate contests suggests polls are as accurate as so-called fundamentals this far into an election cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just five months until November’s midterm elections and already early polling results have countered some expectations. In Arkansas, the Democrat Mark Pryor is showing surprising strength in a red state, and in North Carolina, Kay Hagan is trailing as an incumbent in a battleground state. We won’t know how accurate polling is until after the election, so for now, the very relevant question is, How much should we care about early polls?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1523, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Polls/07UP-Polls-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not Too Soon to Pay Attention to Senate Polling', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn and Josh Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6c4bbf1-c164-574e-b4d2-8b6f63c021cd', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6c4bbf1-c164-574e-b4d2-8b6f63c021cd'}, {'abstract': 'Morning Views', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/morning-views-6/', 'snippet': 'Morning Views', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s opponents have pounced on the decision to trade five Taliban leaders in exchange for the release of Sgt. Bowe Bergdahl. This is yet another example of the hypocrisy which “now pervades the Republican party and the conservative movement,” The New York Times editorial board writes. “The critics seeking political advantage don’t care about the life or mental state of a particular soldier, or of a principle of loyalty that should provide comfort to any soldier in danger of capture. They live only for the attack.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T11:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3628a2a-fe9f-5691-8beb-280bcd1afb78', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3628a2a-fe9f-5691-8beb-280bcd1afb78'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. has called for changes to govern fast trading. | Telecommunication bankers are running out of deals to pitch. | A rally in the bond market has banks worried. | A hedge fund manager sets goats grazing in Detroit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/morning-agenda-s-e-c-takes-on-high-speed-trading/', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. has called for changes to govern fast trading. | Telecommunication bankers are running out of deals to pitch. | A rally in the bond market has banks worried. | A hedge fund manager sets goats grazing in Detroit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'S.E.C. TAKES ON HIGH-SPEED TRADING \xa0|\xa0 Regulators have been slow to react to changes in the stock market, which in the last decade has evolved into a place dominated by high-speed traders. Now, the Securities and Exchange Commission is seeking to update the market’s rules for the new era, DealBook’s William Alden writes. On Thursday, Mary Jo White, the chairwoman of the S.E.C., unveiled a sweeping package of recommendations for new rules and other changes geared toward strengthening the structure of the market and improving disclosures for investors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: S.E.C. Takes on High-Speed Trading', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T11:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a881784-ce0b-5b1a-b9b2-6a1544822f5c', 'word_count': 1656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a881784-ce0b-5b1a-b9b2-6a1544822f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Skills honed during decades spent in one career can be relevant to strikingly different positions, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/your-money/for-retirees-a-second-career.html', 'snippet': 'Skills honed during decades spent in one career can be relevant to strikingly different positions, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEVER in a million years did Cheryl Delaney expect to spend her retirement working with the elderly. Her entire career had been in the financial sector — as a bank officer and loan administrator, in collections and finally as an office manager at Fidelity Investments in Boston. Changing bedpans was not on her bucket list.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, '