ing the beginning of the end of the last World War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s News in Washington: D-Day Remembrance', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Archives and Records Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Normandy (France)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Phoenix (Ariz)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T12:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c01f8309-ce7d-53ae-8329-6a2872f3d162', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c01f8309-ce7d-53ae-8329-6a2872f3d162'}, {'abstract': 'Good news in an economic report is also a reminder of how long it has taken to recover from the downturn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/upshot/in-jobs-report-two-milestones.html', 'snippet': 'Good news in an economic report is also a reminder of how long it has taken to recover from the downturn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This morning’s jobs report has two important labor market milestones. First, the total number of nonfarm jobs has finally climbed back above its pre-recession level. This comes fully six years and four months after employment last peaked, meaning that it has taken longer to recover from this recession than in any previous post-World War II downturn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Jobs Report, Two Milestones', 'kicker': 'Everyday Economics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T12:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15a01a37-e749-5758-8b5d-1666b9e0e68e', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15a01a37-e749-5758-8b5d-1666b9e0e68e'}, {'abstract': 'Guy Pearce stars as a former military man in “The Rover,” which is set in a future Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/movies/guy-pearce-stars-in-the-rover.html', 'snippet': 'Guy Pearce stars as a former military man in “The Rover,” which is set in a future Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years ago, the Australian actor Guy Pearce played an unusual but crucial role in “The Hurt Locker,” Kathryn Bigelow’s Academy Award-winning Iraq drama. Appearing at the beginning of the film, Mr. Pearce was a bomb expert who seemed set to be a primary character. As it turned out, his performance was limited to a single scene, but its impact set up the film’s high-stakes authenticity.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1683, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08PEARCE1/08PEARCE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vanishing Into the Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vanishing Into the Role', 'name': None, 'seo