cy to write dreck. His darkly comic debut thriller (already a blockbuster in Europe!) is unimpeachably terrific.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Publish or Perish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Publish or Perish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dicker, Joel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:46:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Cain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/24583982-d5ed-54c9-8294-98e22b03f4ed', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24583982-d5ed-54c9-8294-98e22b03f4ed'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Levitas discusses the process of creating his first picture, “Lullaby,” which stars the likes of Amy Adams and Terrence Howard, and his future in film.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/talking-talent-an-artists-directorial-debut/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Levitas discusses the process of creating his first picture, “Lullaby,” which stars the likes of Amy Adams and Terrence Howard, and his future in film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Levitas has the Midas touch. The 36-year-old artist, one of only a handful of American painters to ever study at the prestigious Société Nationale des Beaux-Arts in Paris, had never made a movie before he cast Garrett Hedlund and a whole slew of Oscar darlings (Amy Adams, Jennifer Hudson, Richard Jenkins, Terrence Howard) in his directorial debut, “Lullaby.” On June 13, his semi-autobiographical film about family and mortality will prove that the New York-based multihyphenate can write and direct the way he paints — with the confidence of a seasoned veteran and the vulnerability of a true artist.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/t-magazine/06levitas-tabach/06levitas-tabach-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | An Artist’s Directorial Debut', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art, Multiplied', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:47:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa09920f-6c72-5b87-a2e8-37068c460d81', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa09920f-6c72-5b87-a2e8-37068c460d81'}, {'abstract': 'In Georgian London, a tale of seduction, sex, love, death and the pianoforte.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/books/review/sedition-by-katharine-grant.html', 'snippet': 'In Georgian London, a tale of seduction, sex, love, death and the pianoforte.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s 1794 in London. In the dark Virginia & Baltick coffeehouse, huddling in the pungent shadow of tallow candles, four rich men are hatching a plan to marry off their daughters. Risen from the underbelly of the city, wheeling and dealing, they’ve made their fortunes in cloth, fur and timber. They’re successful and wealthy, but now they want sons-in-law with titles who will produce “grandchildren of a certain kind.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1019, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/0608-bks-WULF/0608-bks-WULF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Settling Scores', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Settling Scores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Katharine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Wulf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wulf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8065af1-45fd-5b39-9561-4f1d63310203', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8065af1-45fd-5b39-9561-4f1d63310203'}, {'abstract': 'Ward Just’s novel, set largely before the American escalation in Vietnam, evokes “Lord Jim” and other works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/books/review/american-romantic-by-ward-just.html', 'snippet': 'Ward Just’s novel, set largely before the American escalation in Vietnam, evokes “Lord Jim” and other works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ward Just is both a writer’s writer and an astute tracker of human souls under duplicity and duress. He writes incisively, with striking imagery and with deep knowledge of how people in power behave, from ambassadors coping with the world’s hot spots to Midwestern community leaders suppressing a local crime. Like many distinguished novelists, Just was a journalist first, covering Washington, London and Saigon before the release of his first novel in 1970. “American Romantic,” his 18th, is one of his finest. It has all the qualities Just’s regular readers look forward to, yet it’s an equally good place to be introduced to his work.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 728}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 845, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1689, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08bksCrime2/0608-bks-Crime-1401205501932-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Conrad in Vietnam', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conrad in Vietnam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Just, Ward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Godwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/570bcf61-ad45-5858-8641-72f5f90ae7af', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/570bcf61-ad45-5858-8641-72f5f90ae7af'}, {'abstract': 'Some courts in California offer a program that allows couples without lawyers to dissolve their marriages in hours. The concept could spread to more states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/your-money/court-aided-one-day-divorces-may-be-wave-of-the-future.html', 'snippet': 'Some courts in California offer a program that allows couples without lawyers to dissolve their marriages in hours. The concept could spread to more states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARISSA YORK, a real estate broker in Manhattan, used a $50 online do-it-yourself divorce kit when she and her husband of more than nine years decided to part ways. Their breakup was relatively amicable, she said, so she figured they could save money by avoiding lawyers. “We didn’t want to drag it out over months or years,” she said.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/business/subAdviser/subAdviser-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California Pioneers the Court-Aided One-Day Divorce', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Pioneers the Court-Aided One-Day Divorce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halfens, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Diego (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sacramento (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:50:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3f0d712-4b00-5f4a-9774-cd1e4a9fb30f', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3f0d712-4b00-5f4a-9774-cd1e4a9fb30f'}, {'abstract': 'A novelist recalls a post-college year working for an old-fashioned literary agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/books/review/my-salinger-year-by-joanna-rakoff.html', 'snippet': 'A novelist recalls a post-college year working for an old-fashioned literary agency.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My Salinger Year,” Joanna Rakoff’s breezy memoir of being a “bright young assistant” in the mid-1990s, opens with her decision to leave graduate school, desert her nice college boyfriend and move to New York to write poetry. Almost immediately, she falls for an overbearing aspiring novelist, takes a poorly paid job at a famous literary agency and lands in an unheated apartment in Williamsburg. “I wanted to be extraordinary,” she admits. Instead, she joins a legion of “girls” from comfortable backgrounds determined to live uncomfortably, at least briefly, in vague pursuit of Art.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 1195, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08BERNE/08BERNE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bright Young Assistants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bright Young Assistants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'va