ank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitroeff, Natalie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T14:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Kitroeff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitroeff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a953094-59be-539c-893e-5f992c980c4d', 'word_count': 1729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a953094-59be-539c-893e-5f992c980c4d'}, {'abstract': 'The political journey of the first African-American in major league baseball mirrored the movement of black voters to the Democratic party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/upshot/jackie-robinson-and-nixon-life-and-death-of-a-political-friendship.html', 'snippet': 'The political journey of the first African-American in major league baseball mirrored the movement of black voters to the Democratic party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here in Yankee Stadium’s locker room after Game 5 of the 1952 World Series, Senator Richard Nixon of California, Republican nominee for vice president, congratulates Jackie Robinson on the Brooklyn Dodgers’ 6-5 win over the Yankees. (The Dodgers ultimately lost in seven games.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1610, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/upshot/07UP-Jackie/07UP-Jackie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jackie Robinson and Nixon: Life and Death of a Political Friendship', 'kicker': 'HistorySource', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Life and Death of a Political Friendship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beschloss, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jackie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T15:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Beschloss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beschloss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e4315e-fc0e-510d-a036-9999873ab927', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e4315e-fc0e-510d-a036-9999873ab927'}, {'abstract': 'The “Glee” star Lea Michele, whose “Brunette Ambition” is No. 13 on the advice, how-to and miscellaneous list, once tried to cover up acne using a strategy she’d seen on “Sex and the City.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'The “Glee” star Lea Michele, whose “Brunette Ambition” is No. 13 on the advice, how-to and miscellaneous list, once tried to cover up acne using a strategy she’d seen on “Sex and the City.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spotted: The actress and singer Lea Michele, who plays Rachel Berry on “Glee,” has a book on the advice, how-to and miscellaneous list: “Brunette Ambition,” her breezily memoiristic style guide and advice manual for women, is No. 13 in its second week. Among other things, Michele reveals she once tried to cover up an outbreak of acne using a strategy she’d seen on TV. It didn’t go well: “Hilariously,” she writes, “I thought I had picked up a great concealing trick from ‘Sex and the City,’ when Carrie uses a black eyeliner to turn a zit into a beauty mark. Brilliant, except my skin was so bad I needed about 16 beauty marks. I went out with my girlfriends with black dots all over my face thinking I had the world fooled. They took one look at me and asked, ‘What . . . did you do to your face?’ ” These days, Michele more often opts for a homemade facial mask and the services of a professional dermatologist to keep her skin clear. She also goes without makeup if possible. “Whenever I can, I give my skin a vacation,” she says. “It’s nice to remember what I actually look like.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08michele/08michele-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08michele/08michele-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 456, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08michele/08michele-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08michele/08michele-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/books/review/08michele/08michele-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T15:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc1474f-4b84-5efd-8d49-be8fd9aace33', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc1474f-4b84-5efd-8d49-be8fd9aace33'}, {'abstract': 'Diane von Furstenberg is in the midst of filming her own series, “The DVF Project” for E!, signifying the first embrace of the pop-culture phenomenon by an establishment name since Michael Kors took on “Project Runway” in 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/fashions-embrace-of-reality-tv/', 'snippet': 'Diane von Furstenberg is in the midst of filming her own series, “The DVF Project” for E!, signifying the first embrace of the pop-culture phenomenon by an establishment name since Michael Kors took on “Project Runway” in 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fashion/reality TV love affair is still going strong', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion’s Embrace of Reality TV', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Furstenberg, Diane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Fashion Designers of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E! Entertainment Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Project Runway (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T15:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/629a1889-153b-5fdd-b0c2-aa2cf9010958', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/629a1889-153b-5fdd-b0c2-aa2cf9010958'}, {'abstract': '64 years after the devastating 1950 World Cup, Maracanã stadium will host another final. Can the home team erase the memory of what happened there the last time?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/magazine/this-is-what-a-cursed-soccer-stadium-looks-like.html', 'snippet': '64 years after the devastating 1950 World Cup, Maracanã stadium will host another final. Can the home team erase the memory of what happened there the last time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The place was built for a coronation, a colossal theater where hundreds of thousands could bear witness and celebrate. When Maracanã opened in 1950, in the heart of Rio, it was the world’s largest stadium, the site of what Brazil was certain would be its first World Cup championship. And things started well enough: The host country breezed through to the final match, where, because of tournament rules at the time, it needed only a draw against Uruguay to win the whole event. With little more than 10 minutes to go, the score was 1-1, and the fans were on edge. Then the Uruguayan winger Alcides Ghiggia put them over with a sudden strike. “Only three people have, with just one motion, silenced the Maracanã,” he famously said later. “Frank Sinatra, Pope John Paul II and me.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1568, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/magazine/08stadium/08stadium-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is What a Cursed Soccer Stadium Looks Like', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pitch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghiggia, Alcides (1926-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T15:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'ar