eave the children alone when you must and then really be with them when you can. Or, to put it slightly differently: Alternate fully engaging with fully ignoring them. There is, of course, an implied “instead of” here — instead of half paying attention to them all the time (cough smartphone cough).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-articleLarge.png', 'height': 333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 333}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-jumbo.png', 'height': 568, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1947, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/06/us/motherlode-ben-music-box/motherlode-ben-music-box-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Give Kids Your Undivided Attention — or No Attention At All', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T15:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47951330-db9c-53f4-9152-4e9eb917b9b8', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47951330-db9c-53f4-9152-4e9eb917b9b8'}, {'abstract': 'The new Securities and Exchange Commission inquiry into high frequency trading and so-called dark pools is long overdue.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/thoughts-on-dark-pools-and-michael-lewis/', 'snippet': 'The new Securities and Exchange Commission inquiry into high frequency trading and so-called dark pools is long overdue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Securities and Exchange Commission inquiry into high frequency trading and so-called dark pools — as announced yesterday by Chairwoman Mary Jo White\xa0— is long overdue. As speed has become the most important factor in getting the absolute best price, high-frequency traders have gained advantages over other investors that are undeniable. Some of these firms almost never have down days anymore. More and more, the average investor has to feel that the game is rigged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thoughts on Dark Pools and Michael Lewis', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw