_paragraph': 'My gateway drug to serious Anglophilia was horses — the British Pony Club Manual of Horsemanship, my English saddle made by Barnsby — but the addiction was truly about words. What, for example, could “Hounds, gentlemen, please” possibly mean? This was a sign along the roadside near the stable where we kept my horse outside St. Louis. I turned it over in my mind for months before I understood that drivers were being asked to slow down if foxhounds were in the vicinity.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08ENGLAND/08ENGLAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in Time in England’s Northeast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost in Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durham (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gateshead (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newcastle-on-Tyne (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jarrow (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Holy Island (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T19:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Smiley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smiley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ea19831-27b5-5513-9cb4-e3577ab63b0a', 'word_count': 2339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ea19831-27b5-5513-9cb4-e3577ab63b0a'}, {'abstract': 'A mountain winery and the only museum in the world solely dedicated to the artist James Turrell combine at Colomé.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/travel/in-argentina-wine-art-and-altitude.html', 'snippet': 'A mountain winery and the only museum in the world solely dedicated to the artist James Turrell combine at Colomé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our friends love modern art but don’t really drink; my companion and I are closer to the reverse. So as we researched places where we could travel and all come away happy, Colomé, in northwest Argentina, stood out. It’s a mountain winery with a contemporary art museum and sounded like the perfect two-couple compromise — a little bit high culture, a little bit grand cru.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/travel/08-cultured-top/08-cultured-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Argentina, Wine, Art and Altitude', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wine, Art and Altitude: Stir Well', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turrell, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salta (Argentina)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hess, Donald', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T19:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/098ddd2a-f686-5247-9ff2-5a725f17d823', 'word_count': 1922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/098ddd2a-f686-5247-9ff2-5a725f17d823'}, {'abstract': 'Jeeps from World War II are ubiquitous at military vehicle shows, and they are a starting point for many people getting into the collecting hobby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/automobiles/collectibles/world-war-ii-jeeps-have-become-collectibles.html', 'snippet': 'Jeeps from World War II are ubiquitous at military vehicle shows, and they are a starting point for many people getting into the collecting hobby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Army, it was known simply as the G503 or the quarter-ton, but to millions of soldiers it quickly became the jeep, a coinage generally linked to a character from the Popeye cartoon strip, Eugene the Jeep. Today, wartime jeeps are ubiquitous at military vehicle shows, and they are starting point for most people getting into the collecting hobby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u