k: under fire from Republicans for statements she made about a murky sequence of events involving Americans in a distant land.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Aide Defends Remarks on Bergdahl’s ‘Honor’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Aide Defends Remarks on Bergdahl’s ‘Honor’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Susan E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T19:49:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55131217-b50e-5cea-b235-370f11ea3858', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55131217-b50e-5cea-b235-370f11ea3858'}, {'abstract': 'Why don’t they exist? Because nature’s fundamental forces remain a mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/opinion/sunday/i-was-promised-flying-cars.html', 'snippet': 'Why don’t they exist? Because nature’s fundamental forces remain a mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS an astronomy-obsessed kid in the 1970s, I subsisted on a steady diet of science fiction. It promised a future filled with technological wonders: talking computers, bionic limbs, flying cars. Forty years later, though much of that future has arrived, it’s still missing what I consider its most important ingredient. Sure, we’ve got the iPhone’s Siri, and the Food and Drug Administration just approved a prosthetic arm controlled by signals from the brain — but where are our smooth-gliding flying machines, our Landspeeders (“Star Wars”) and airborne DeLoreans (“Back to the Future”)?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sunday-review/0608GRAY/0608GRAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline'