Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T20:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeb5d4f7-4bac-5a44-932d-4813bd0ca3c2', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeb5d4f7-4bac-5a44-932d-4813bd0ca3c2'}, {'abstract': 'A three-bedroom apartment in the popular A-line of the 90-story One57 tower was the most expensive sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/big-ticket-30-4-million-for-a-midtown-three-bedroom/', 'snippet': 'A three-bedroom apartment in the popular A-line of the 90-story One57 tower was the most expensive sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another of the glassy three-bedroom aeries in the popular A line at the Extell Development Company’s 90-story Midtown tower, One57, sold for $30,449,175 and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. For now, the monthly carrying costs for the 4,483-square-foot condominium, No. 61A, are a mere $7,545, thanks to a tax abatement.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/realestate/08TICKET/08TICKET-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/realestate/08TICKET/08TICKET-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 643}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/realestate/08TICKET/08TICKET-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 