ation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T21:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d045fff4-bf84-532b-af8d-c8431198fc72', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d045fff4-bf84-532b-af8d-c8431198fc72'}, {'abstract': 'A series of questions was posed to 2,880 investors in the first quarter of 2014 in 16 countries globally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/06/06/your-money/07wealth-doc.html', 'snippet': 'A series of questions was posed to 2,880 investors in the first quarter of 2014 in 16 countries globally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A series of questions was posed to 2,880 investors in the first quarter of 2014 in 16 countries globally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-articleLarge.png', 'height': 727, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 727}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1141, 'width': 942, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/your-money/07wealth-doc-pic/07wealth-doc-pic-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'State Street Financial Literacy Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T21:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Your Money', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/805a007f-f2d4-57df-9d5d-ad908e27c078', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/805a007f-f2d4-57df-9d5d-ad908e27c078'}, {'abstract': 'The omnivorous curator discusses “A Stroll Through a Fun Palace,” his exhibition that explores the connections between two late-20th-century architectural thinkers: the architect Cedric Price and the political economist Lucius Burckhardt.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/06/hans-ulrich-obrist-venice-architecture-biennale-swiss-pavilion/', 'snippet': 'The omnivorous curator discusses “A Stroll Through a Fun Palace,” his exhibition that explores the connections between two late-20th-century architectural thinkers: the architect Cedric Price and the political economist Lucius Burckhardt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if summer travelers needed any more incentive to descend on the sinking city of Venice, tomorrow the 14th International Architecture Exhibition of the Venice Biennale opens to the public. This year’s edition, directed by Rem Koolhaas, gets back to the basics of modern architecture, with dozens of exhibitions at national pavilions that delve into formative moments of the 20th century. The Swiss Pavilion is headed by Hans-Ulrich Obrist, the omnivorous curator and co-director of exhibitions and programs at the Serpentine Galleries in London. In it, Obrist has brought together two 20th-century figures whose research has influenced architectural thinking in their own time and since: the Swiss political economist Lucius Burckhardt and the English architect Cedric Price. Here, Obrist walks through the genesis of the pavilion’s exhibition “A Stroll Through a Fun Palace,” whose title refers to Price’s great unrealized construction, “Fun Palace,” and Burckhardt’s concept of “Strollology.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A. | Hans-Ulrich Obrist on Curating the Swiss Pavilion at the Venice Architecture Biennale', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice Architecture Biennale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T21:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7344dead-fa64-5c2b-bc25-9b85597e1635', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7344dead-fa64-5c2b-bc25-9b85597e1635'}, {'abstract': 'Russian prosecutors released the ship, the Arctic Sunrise, nearly nine months after seizing it following a protest at the first offshore oil platform in the Arctic, Greenpeace announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/world/europe/russia-releases-greenpeace-ship.html', 'snippet': 'Russian prosecutors released the ship, the Arctic Sunrise, nearly nine months after seizing it following a protest at the first offshore oil platform in the Arctic, Greenpeace announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russian prosecutors released a Greenpeace International ship nearly nine months after seizing it following a high-seas protest at the first offshore oil platform in the Arctic, the organization announced Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Releases Greenpeace Ship', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T21:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67b2a74d-7da2-5242-af78-0efa106eb3a3', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67b2a74d-7da2-5242-af78-0efa106eb3a3'}, {'abstract': 'Mackenzie Davis, 27, of “Halt and Catch Fire” on AMC, has philosophical conviction and a macabre pastime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/arts/television/mackenzie-davis-of-halt-and-catch-fire-on-amc.html', 'snippet': 'Mackenzie Davis, 27, of “Halt and Catch Fire” on AMC, has philosophical conviction and a macabre pastime.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love seeing the insides of things,” Mackenzie Davis said, tucking her bleached bob behind her ears, a giraffe’s neck expanse above her slashed and safety-pinned Bart Simpson T-shirt. “It just fascinates me and always has.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1063, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1063}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 579, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1157, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08SNAPHOT/08SNAPHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hacking Into Prime Time With Attitude', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hacking Into Prime Time With Attitude', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Halt and Catch Fire (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Mackenzie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T21:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f8e38ab-4bd0-5e0b-826a-7c9bdd9a75fd', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f8e38ab-4bd0-5e0b-826a-7c9bdd9a75fd'}, {'abstract': 'Frederick Ashton’s “Cinderella,” which enters the repertory of American Ballet Theater on Monday at the Metropolitan Opera House, is the only staging of Prokofiev’s score to stand the test of time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/arts/dance/cinderella-to-join-american-ballet-theater-repertory.html', 'snippet': 'Frederick Ashton’s “Cinderella,” which enters the repertory of American Ballet Theater on Monday at the Metropolitan Opera House, is the only staging of Prokofiev’s score to stand the test of time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your world is not the only world: That’s the lesson of Romantic ballet. And when a grown woman moves from one world to another, she herself is transformed. In Prokofiev’s “Cinderella,” not only does the title character’s dream come true, but she becomes her dream version of herself.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08CINDERELLA1/08CINDERELLA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': '