 as a misdemeanor Ms. Walters, with Ms. Gruelle’s encouragement, filed kidnapping charges. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE6/08GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unflinching View at a Festival', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unflinching View at a Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T22:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3fadd21-bef2-59d3-9053-adb1eec6c38c', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3fadd21-bef2-59d3-9053-adb1eec6c38c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s just another four nights in Brooklyn, only more so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/arts/music/northside-festival-booms-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'It’s just another four nights in Brooklyn, only more so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s just another four nights in Brooklyn, only more so. Clubs are full of local bands and selected visitors; there’s more music than anyone could possibly attend. The sixth annual Northside Festival, expanding each year, promises some 400 bands playing in Williamsburg and Greenpoint from Thursday through Sunday. There are free but ticketed shows (with an online R.S.V.P. to the festival) at McCarren Park, to be headlined, on Saturday, by Thee Oh Sees, playing typically brief, frenzied sets of manic garage rock, and on Sunday by Chvrches with their gleaming synth-pop conundrums. Music badges, for $80, encourage club hopping, but are subject to capacity limits; strategic fans may want to choose particular shows. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/arts/08GUIDE4/08GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image