on/is-softball-sexist.html', 'snippet': 'Women played baseball before they could vote — and they still should.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OVER the next three weeks, baseball players from around the country will compete in three regional tryouts for a chance to make it onto the United States baseball team. These are among the most elite, dedicated and talented athletes in their sport, and the best of them will go on to play against teams from Japan, Australia, Canada, Hong Kong, Venezuela and Taiwan in the World Cup tournament held in September in Miyazaki, Japan. But the team receives almost no attention, and many of its members weren’t even able to play their sport in high school. These baseball players are women.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/opinion/0607OPEDclarke/0607OPEDclarke-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Softball Sexist?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Softball Sexist?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Span, Emma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Softball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Little League Baseball and Softball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Title IX (Gender Discrimination Legislation)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T23:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2627ff0-186f-51d6-aa59-0add2d850c9e', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2627ff0-186f-51d6-aa59-0add2d850c9e'}, {'abstract': 'Meet the 12 horses who have come oh-so-close since 1978, winning the Kentucky Derby and the Preakness but failing in the Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/sports/belmont-stakes-twelve-triple-crown-contenders.html', 'snippet': 'Meet the 12 horses who have come oh-so-close since 1978, winning the Kentucky Derby and the Preakness but failing in the Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a chestnut colt named Affirmed won the Triple Crown in 1978, he was the third horse to do so in six years, and it seemed that achieving the holy grail of horse racing was no longer so arduous a quest.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12 Contenders Who Just Missed Out on a Triple Crown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bid for Crown, Take 13', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bearak, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'California Chrome (Race Horse)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Big Brown (Race Horse)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T23:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0cf6b19-e5b2-5693-975f-7e24d851cf4f', 'word_count': 1915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0cf6b19-e5b2-5693-975f-7e24d851cf4f'}, {'abstract': 'To follow horse racing is to become a connoisseur of bad luck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/opinion/hard-lessons-from-belmont.html', 'snippet': 'To follow horse racing is to become a connoisseur of bad luck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE been fooled by the Belmont Stakes before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard Lessons From Belmont', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard Lessons From Belmont', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T23:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Banks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Banks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/edc3ff39-aad1-5117-a169-03116fd0d351', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edc3ff39-aad1-5117-a169-03116fd0d351'}, {'abstract': 'The supply of safe water in Syria is now one-third of the level it was before March 2011 when the civil war began, Unicef officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/world/middleeast/syria-unicef-says-drought-adds-to-safe-water-woes.html', 'snippet': 'The supply of safe water in Syria is now one-third of the level it was before March 2011 when the civil war began, Unicef officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The supply of safe water in Syria is now one-third of the level it was before March 2011 when the civil war began, Unicef said Friday in a report that warns of new levels of suffering because of a worsening regional drought. The report said the 9.6 million Syrians affected by the conflict, half of them children, are at increased risk of disease because the water scarcity has compounded problems caused by damage to water and sewage systems. Parts of Syria have received the lowest levels of rainfall in more than half a century, the report said, and most parts of the country have only received half the average rainfall of a normal year. The drought also threatens to put new pressures on Jordan, Lebanon and Iraq, where Syrian refugees are already straining the water supply. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Drought Adds to Woes, U.N. Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Drought Adds to Woes, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United Nations Children's Fund", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-06T23:56:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2195b43-3509-5d4f-8e05-881e0392c8c1', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2195b43-3509-5d4f-8e05-881e0392c8c1'}, {'abstract': 'While conservative evangelicals are prominent on television, the liberal wings of Christian churches have their own leading preachers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/us/festival-draws-stars-of-christian-preaching-not-as-seen-on-television.htm