rmer Senator Sam Nunn and Moon Landrieu, a former New Orleans mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Still relatively early in the 2014 election cycle, candidates are trying to introduce themselves — or reintroduce, as the case may be — to voters. And amid a panoply of negative spots, image mavens and ad wizards have found a way to try to help their politicians cut through the clutter: family, family, family. A look at some of the latest ads that feature kin (appealing parents, cute children) in supporting roles.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1278, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/HOTSPOTS/HOTSPOTS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subTyp