p in New York City, where immigrants in every ethnic enclave are preparing to cheer on their home countries. Here are some city spots to watch with the faithful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a gloriously sunny afternoon recently, Lunasa, an East Village pub, was packed seven deep at the bar, as three TVs showed the day’s big games. Soccer games, that is, in Germany, Portugal and England.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/nyregion/08CUP/08CUP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching the World’s Game, in the World’s City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World’s Game, in the World’s City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T04:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2361851f-df4a-58d2-bdbf-91062f0154ea', 'word_count': 2877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2361851f-df4a-58d2-bdbf-91062f0154ea'}, {'abstract': 'The Fire Department said no one was seriously injured in the three-alarm blaze and that the cause is being investigated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/nyregion/fire-breaks-out-at-tgi-fridays-near-rockefeller-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Fire Department said no one was seriously injured in the three-alarm blaze and that the cause is being investigated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fast-moving fire at a restaurant near Rockefeller Center on Friday night sent flames and smoke shooting into the night sky as diners ran for the exits and dozens of firefighters rushed to extinguish the blaze, the authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Breaks Out at TGI Friday’s Near Rockefeller Center', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fire Breaks Out at TGI Friday’s Near Rockefeller Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tgi Friday', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T04:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f69b517-797d-5630-a215-cd62c34d08e0', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f69b517-797d-5630-a215-cd62c34d08e0'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) ENOUGH SAID (2013) Julia Louis-Dreyfus, in a Golden Globe-nominated role, plays Eva, a divorced massage therapist in Los Angeles who finds her life emptying out as her daughter (Tracey Fairaway) prepares to leave for Sarah Lawrence College. Then she meets Albert (James Gandolfini, above, with Ms. Louis-Dreyfus), another divorced parent of a college-bound girl, and although he isn’t her usual type, Eva suddenly finds herself falling for this funny, tender and sexy slob. Enter Marianne (Catherine Keener), a glamorous bohemian poet and Eva’s new client — who, Eva finds out a little too late, also happens to be Albert’s former wife. And so Eva listens to Marianne’s complaints about her ex — he’s a bore and a loser, clumsy in bed and unable to take care of himself — and surreptitiously tries to correct the faults in Albert that caused their marriage to disintegrate. “The real genius of ‘Enough Said’ is that it takes this entirely plausible anecdotal circumstance and unlocks both its farcical potential and its latent profundity,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this “small miracle of a movie” written and directed by Nicole Holofcener. “This movie will make you laugh and leave you in tears. Some of the pathos is the accidental byproduct of seeing Mr. Gandolfini, so playful and alive, in one of his final major movie roles and feeling once again the loss of his remarkable gift. There is also the pang of the empty nest, that mixture of grief and pride that is the special anguish of modern parents. But there is also something deeper. The ache that ‘Enough Said’ leaves behind comes from the blunt force of truth.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a09ca3-6e2b-56fc-96ce-f3b767920874', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a09ca3-6e2b-56fc-96ce-f3b767920874'}, {'abstract': 'Most tables at Space Billiards in Koreatown are the standard six-pocket variety, but those without holes are for four-ball billiards, a preferred game in South Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/nyregion/no-pockets-no-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Most tables at Space Billiards in Koreatown are the standard six-pocket variety, but those without holes are for four-ball billiards, a preferred game in South Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Space Billiards is a pool hall of the sort that feels nocturnal on even a bright day. But it is not a dour place, and it isn’t filled with unsavory hustlers. In its slightly manic, neon-noir way, it exudes a quirky sense of cheer. Simple strobe lights jitter across walls. A seemingly endless string of dance hits plays. The wall behind the red couch is covered with small mirrors. At some tables you’ll find cheap American beer; at other tables, bottles of OB Lager and soju, the beer and liquor of South Korea. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Pockets, No Problem', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Pockets, No Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vadukul, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Billiards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Space Billiards (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T05:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Vadukul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vadukul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c544833f-a4b3-530c-9d75-57887d2212cd', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c544833f-a4b3-530c-9d75-57887d2212cd'}, {'abstract': '“American Odyssey: Photos From the Detroit Photographic Company, 1888-1924,” which opens with a sampling of New York vistas, contains color photochroms, as they were called, that the authors say were “the first color photographs of the North American continent.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/nyregion/the-oz-moment.html', 'snippet': '“American Odyssey: Photos From the Detroit Photographic Company, 1888-1924,” which opens with a sampling of New York vistas, contains color photochroms, as they were called, that the authors say were “the first color photographs of the North Ameri...', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ll never forget eyeballing Ebbets Field for the first time. I had seen photographs in the sports pages, and grainy images on TV. And I had seen grass before, even growing up in Brooklyn. Still, I was totally unprepared for what the verdant playing field looked like in person in what, in a few years, the NBC peacock would introduce as living color.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Oz’ Moment', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The ‘Oz’ Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walter, Marc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arque, Sabine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T05:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'or