ekend at the Berkshire International Film Festival in western Massachusetts, and I want to recommend two terrific law-related documentary films I saw there. One is directly law-related: “The Case Against 8,” the story of the federal court case that led to the invalidation of California’s Proposition 8 and to the arrival of marriage equality there. The film, by Ben Cotner and Ryan White, is now playing commercially in New York and Los Angeles, will soon open elsewhere, and will be shown on HBO on June 23 (disclosure: I had a tiny consulting role in the making of the film, actually a discussion of Supreme Court procedure over a cup of coffee with the filmmakers.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two New Legal-Themed Documentaries', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8214053d-a7c4-5e11-ad9b-21f4ceecb262', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8214053d-a7c4-5e11-ad9b-21f4ceecb262'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/sports/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Sports Editor:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Sports Editor', 'kicker': 'Inbox', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the N.B.A., Salary ‘Crumbs’ Amount to a Feast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmer, Don', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T15:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/017fabc0-5d35-53d5-8577-1242783e3c68', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/017fabc0-5d35-53d5-8577-1242783e3c68'}, {'abstract': 'An attack on a 12-year-old, brought on, perhaps, by an obsession with the fictional Internet figure Slender Man, has forced an urgent self-examination in Waukesha, Wis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/us/milwaukee-suburb-tries-to-cope-with-slender-man-stabbing.html', 'snippet': 'An attack on a 12-year-old, brought on, perhaps, by an obsession with the fictional Internet figure Slender Man, has forced an urgent self-examination in Waukesha, Wis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WAUKESHA, Wis. — At Horning Middle School last week, some girls painted cat whiskers on their faces with liquid eyeliner, in tribute to a fellow sixth grader who loved cats but who lay in a hospital recovering from 19 stab wounds that the authorities say were inflicted by two friends who had lured her into a park to kill her.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/us/STABBING4/STABBING4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 4