 been five since 1997, if you count this one), and we haven’t seen one since 2006. But if you wait long enough, I’m told, everything comes back into style, and Arthur Schulman, who created the first four, has a new vowel-less crossword for us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Vowel-less Crossword Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T16:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/213b5c6e-ab00-5bde-a53d-e116b0b054c8', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/213b5c6e-ab00-5bde-a53d-e116b0b054c8'}, {'abstract': 'L.G.B.T. pride month is now observed not just with parades and parties, but also with travel promotions.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/gay-pride-promotions/', 'snippet': 'L.G.B.T. pride month is now observed not just with parades and parties, but also with travel promotions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Companies such as\xa0Hilton,\xa0Kimpton\xa0and\xa0American Airlines\xa0have long marketed to the gay community. This month in a most public display of affection,\xa0Marriott International, a company with conservative Mormon roots, is wrapping three of its Washington, D.C., hotels in photo banners, including Jason Collins, the N.B.A.’s first openly gay basketball player, and Geena Rocero, a transgender model. The campaign urges travelers to share photos on Instagram under #LoveTravels @MarriottIntl.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Pride Promotions', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gay Pride Promotions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marriott International Inc.', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T16:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daaf51e0-055a-5b4a-8976-3a5a1dba2f46', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daaf51e0-055a-5b4a-8976-3a5a1dba2f46'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive at General Motors, Mary T. Barra, wants to ensure that deadly failures never happen again, but old habits are hard to change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/business/gretchen-morgenson-on-the-problems-at-gm.html', 'snippet': 'The chief executive at General Motors, Mary T. Barra, wants to ensure that deadly failures never happen again, but old habits are hard to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the release last Thursday of the internal report on General Motors’ failure to recall thousands of defective cars for more than a decade, Mary T. Barra, the chief executive, addressed the company’s employees. In her remarks, Ms. Barra projected an earnest and urgent desire to reform the company’s culture, which she said was permeated by “bureaucratic processes that avoided accountability.” That culture meant no one took responsibility for faulty ignition switches in Chevrolet Cobalts and other cars that were ultimately responsible for at least 13 deaths. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 982, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1635, 'width': 1567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/business/08-GRET-JP/08-GRET-JP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vow to End Hollow Nods and Salutes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vow to End Hollow Nods and Salutes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None