Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c1cda43-a7ec-5616-b429-da7e3811ded6', 'word_count': 1856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c1cda43-a7ec-5616-b429-da7e3811ded6'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s young people face limited job opportunities and increasing hardship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/opinion/sunday/starting-out-behind.html', 'snippet': 'Today’s young people face limited job opportunities and increasing hardship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s young people, ages 18 to 24, should have been the lucky ones. They were preteens or teenagers when the recession hit in late 2007, with high school and college still ahead. Unlike those who had to enter the work force in the depths of the downturn, they had time, or so it seemed, to wait out the weak economy. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starting Out Behind', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting Out Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T18:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/120a18de-6c2e-5580-9ae9-e0b1798fbcff', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120a18de-6c2e-5580-9ae9-e0b1798fbcff'}, {'abstract': 'And technology won.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/the-war-on-coal-already-happened/', 'snippet': 'And technology won.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m trying to pull together some thoughts about interests and ideology in the fight over climate policies, and found myself wondering what exactly is at stake in the supposed “war on coal”. And the answer is, surprisingly little — at least as far as jobs are concerned. Here’s total employment in coal mining (the earlier numbers are from Historical Statistics of the United States, Millennial Edition; the later from the FRED database):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The War on Coal Already Happened', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T18:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29a91fb0-b6d6-5ea8-b207-6f597c9616b8', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29a91fb0-b6d6-5ea8-b207-6f597c9616b8'}, {'abstract': 'Apple’s new family sharing program will come too late for those embroiled in disastrous situations because of inadvertently shared private messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/your-money/when-a-shared-id-leads-to-a-grim-predicament.html', 'snippet': 'Apple’s new family sharing program will come too late for those embroiled in disastrous situations because of inadvertently shared private messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live, it has been said many times, in the era of oversharing. Sometimes this produces awkward situations. Other times, it produces something much worse.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ra