}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d38a393-9345-5195-a48f-e2382244f222', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d38a393-9345-5195-a48f-e2382244f222'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about Clinton’s legacy as Secretary of State', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/what-hillary-rodham-clinton-did/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about Clinton’s legacy as Secretary of State', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column takes aim at the commonly heard narrative that Hillary Clinton as Secretary of State was glamorous but didn’t really achieve much or leave any legacy. I think that’s completely wrong, and that she did have a significant impact–just not the usual kind. I think this is an issue that is going to spark more debate this week following publication of Clinton’s book on Tuesday and as the presidential campaign approaches. So let me know if you agree, or where you think she did–or didn’t–have impact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Hillary Rodham Clinton Did', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T20:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2896cc5-bc2b-5672-8302-90ae02c17f88', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2896cc5-bc2b-5672-8302-90ae02c17f88'}, {'abstract': 'To measure the amounts that chief executives were paid last year, Sunday Business asked Equilar Inc., an executive compensation data firm, to compile and analyze pay data from corporate filings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/bu