 it out and admires it. The ring motivates him. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/08/sports/pagan/pagan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Series Gives Mets Another Look at What They Lost in Pagan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Get Another Look at What They Lost in Pagan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pagan, Angel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-07T22:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea556fd5-0dda-59e8-ad6f-61f7cabb8f36', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea556fd5-0dda-59e8-ad6f-61f7cabb8f36'}, {'abstract': 'In the World Cup, you can choose to root for your ancestors or, if you want, a team that speaks to you, and not your patriotic pride. If that’s your chosen course, this is a chart for you.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/07/behind-the-slightly-better-than-a-dartboard-guide-to-choosing-a-team/', 'snippet': 'In the World Cup, you can choose to root for your ancestors or, if you want, a team that speaks to you, and not your patriotic pride. If that’s your chosen course, this is a chart for you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a nation of immigrants, Americans tend to have more choices than most when it comes to rooting for a team in the World Cup. You get the United States — that’s your safety school, so to speak. Unfortunately, the U.S. national team never figures to go very deep into the tournament. So you can choose to root for your ancestors or, if you want, a team that speaks to you, and not your national or ethnic pride. If that’s your chosen course, this is a chart for you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/07/nyregion/07cupchartcrop/07cupchartcrop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 259, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge