 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackman, Hugh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-08T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15857742-b24f-5a91-bceb-e7a8f7337cf2', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15857742-b24f-5a91-bceb-e7a8f7337cf2'}, {'abstract': 'When I was a child playing soccer, there weren’t that many women who’d grown up playing the game. Now there are, but they’re still not represented on the sidelines, and that’s not the way this is supposed to work.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/a-plea-to-the-daughters-of-title-ix-why-dont-more-women-coach/', 'snippet': 'When I was a child playing soccer, there weren’t that many women who’d grown up playing the game. Now there are, but they’re still not represented on the sidelines, and that’s not the way this is supposed to work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first registered my daughter, Lily, for soccer five years ago, I made a conscious decision to take a back seat. I wouldn’t volunteer to be the head coach. Instead, I would take a role as an assistant/orange-slice dispenser. The plan was for me to lend support, but not loom too large over my daughter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-soccer-victory/motherlode-soccer-victory-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/05/us/motherlode-soccer-victory/motherlode-soccer-victory-articleLarge.jp