n to comic strips last week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/08/calvin-and-hobbes-creator-returns-briefly/', 'snippet': 'After nearly two decades, Bill Watterson, the creator of “Calvin and Hobbes,” made a surprising return to comic strips last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Watterson, the creator of “Calvin and Hobbes” who retired in 1995 and withdrew from the public eye for almost two decades, has finally returned to drawing comic strips, if only for a brief moment. Last week, Mr. Watterson was the ghost artist for a handful of panels on Stephan Pastis’s “Pearls Before Swine” for a storyline in which Mr. Pastis is replaced as the artist of the strip by a second grader named Libby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Calvin and Hobbes’ Creator Returns, Briefly', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watterson, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-08T18:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72267dd2-7beb-5bc2-b5b2-84709088c986', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72267dd2-7beb-5bc2-b5b2-84709088c986'}, {'abstract': 'A dispute over how to combat the threat of homegrown Islamic extremism in British schools has provoked a political crisis, prompting a public apology and a resignation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/world/europe/rift-deepens-over-claims-of-infiltration-by-islamic-extremists-in-british-schools.html', 'snippet': 'A dispute over how to 