/article/386ee391-64d9-57d2-8523-df4ba94e3031'}, {'abstract': 'Eyehategod performs old and new songs in a Brooklyn club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/arts/music/eyehategod-maintains-hopelessness-and-rage-in-lyrics.html', 'snippet': 'Eyehategod performs old and new songs in a Brooklyn club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There must be a positive lesson to be extracted from the story of Eyehategod. This band from New Orleans has endured 26 years — through opiates, hurricanes, homelessness, jail and probation. It has survived a name that has never gotten any less puerile; the recent death of a drummer, Joey LaCaze, who helped define its angry and sensuous sound; touring whenever possible; recording a lot less often; and a kind of artfully antisocial behavior.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 268, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 268}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 914, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/09/arts/eyehate/eyehate-thumbSta