ica.html', 'snippet': 'Nations afflicted by the epidemic, as well as their neighbors, will need to redouble efforts to contain the virus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Health Organization warned last Wednesday that the epidemic caused by the deadly Ebola virus in West Africa, which had seemed to be waning, has recently taken a turn for the worse. The afflicted nations and their neighbors will need to redouble their efforts to contain a virus for which there is neither a cure nor a vaccine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola Gets Worse in West Africa ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ebola Gets Worse in West Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T00:46:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fa718e4-698f-5859-b17b-09cfd2978003', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fa718e4-698f-5859-b17b-09cfd2978003'}, {'abstract': 'The Pinehurst No. 2 course, recently returned to its original appearance with irregular sand and native vegetation, will host the United States Open and the United States Women’s Open in the coming weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/sports/golf/pinehurst-course-back-to-its-original-shaggy-self-is-set-for-close-up.html', 'snippet': 'The Pinehurst No. 2 course, recently returned to its original appearance with irregular sand and native vegetation, will host the United States Open and the United States Women’s Open in the coming weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PINEHURST, N.C. — As one of the country’s first golf resorts, Pinehurst has long been viewed as an American cradle of the sport. The resort’s showcase golf course, known as Pinehurst No. 2, hosted its first major event more than 100 years ago and evolved into a masterpiece of the nation’s best-known golf architect, Donald Ross.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1470, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/09/sports/jpPINEHURST/jpPINEHURST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r