': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5c56649-4edc-52e4-bc72-bdaad6e33899', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5c56649-4edc-52e4-bc72-bdaad6e33899'}, {'abstract': 'China’s top antigraft body actually used the Chinese word for adultery last week while announcing the expulsion of a party member, rather than oft-used euphemisms like “moral corruption.”', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/in-communist-party-parlance-adultery-has-many-names/', 'snippet': 'China’s top antigraft body actually used the Chinese word for adultery last week while announcing the expulsion of a party member, rather than oft-used euphemisms like “moral corruption.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Communist Party regularly employs a variety of muffled euphemisms for sexual misdeeds: moral corruption, dissolute lifestyle and the like. But in a rare display of lucidity, China’s top antigraft body actually used the Chinese word for adultery — tongjian (通奸) — last week while announcing the expulsion of a party member.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/9sino-adultery2/9sino-adultery2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 328, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/world/9sino-adultery2/9sino-adultery2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 328}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/9sino-adultery2/9sino-adultery2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/9sino-adultery2/9sino-adultery2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1093, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail',