'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd681ad-4e68-5d07-a359-98950dae674d', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd681ad-4e68-5d07-a359-98950dae674d'}, {'abstract': 'Morning Views', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/morning-views-8/', 'snippet': 'Morning Views', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times editorial board supports a settlement in a lawsuit between the Justice Department and the State of Ohio over care in juvenile correctional facilities. “Ohio will sharply reduce and eventually end solitary confinement,” the board writes, citing statistics indicating higher likelihood of mental problems and suicidal behavior in youngsters forced to endure it. “The Justice Department’s settlement with Ohio puts states on notice that solitary policies need to change. If adopted nationally, the principles in that settlement would go a long way toward humanizing juvenile detention.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T04:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d3028cf-654e-5950-a58d-2b6d397eec67', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d3028cf-654e-5950-a58d-2b6d397eec67'}, {'abstract': 'The world’s best golfers will compete for the U.S. Open at Pinehurst. The resort’s landmark cour