 their Chinese operations.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/the-challenges-of-enforcing-customer-service-policies/', 'snippet': 'The challenges become even greater when Western companies try to introduce established customer-service procedures into their Chinese operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A gate agent stopped me recently as I was boarding a flight to Dallas. After inspecting my carry-on bag, she asked me if it would fit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Challenges of Enforcing Customer Service Policies', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T11:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weidenhamer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225610bc-6061-5cab-8082-871e3a1ed5a3', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225610bc-6061-5cab-8082-871e3a1ed5a3'}, {'abstract': 'Plans could compete based on the types of treatments they cover, which would give consumers a far clearer choice than they have now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/upshot/how-to-pay-for-only-the-health-care-you-want.html', 'snippet': 'Plans could compete based on the types of treatments they cover, which would give consumers a far clearer choice than they have now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One reason health insurance is expensive is that most plans cover just about every medical technology — not just the ones that work, or the ones that are worth the price. This not only drives up costs, but also forces many Americans into purchasing coverage for therapies they may not value. But there’s no reason things couldn’t be different, and better for consumers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10healthillo/10healthillo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge',