t', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jared Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jared', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34a5052a-74d7-5497-b0f2-98b335a8e60c', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34a5052a-74d7-5497-b0f2-98b335a8e60c'}, {'abstract': 'The sentences were the toughest punishment to date in the long-running investigation into Anna Politkovskaya’s death, but it is still unclear who paid for and ordered the killing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/world/europe/moscow-court-sentences-5-to-prison-for-contract-killing-of-anna-politkovskaya.html', 'snippet': 'The sentences were the toughest punishment to date in the long-running investigation into Anna Politkovskaya’s death, but it is still unclear who paid for and ordered the killing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Moscow’s highest criminal court on Monday sentenced five men to prison, including two to life sentences, for the 2006 murder of the investigative journalist Anna Politkovskaya, but left unsolved the question of who ordered the killing, the highest-profile attack on a Russian journalist of the last decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/world/10-Politkovskaya/10-Politkovskaya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/world/10-Politkovskaya/10-Politkovskaya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 918}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/world/10-Politkovskaya/10-Politkovskaya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'cr