sing-industry.html', 'snippet': 'HanesBrands picks Elevate Studios of Chicago to be its first digital agency of record, and Heineken chooses Droga5’s Sydney office to create campaigns for Tiger beer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lee Allan joined Gage, Minneapolis, as the agency’s design director. She succeeds Kenny Friedman, who left to join Flor, Chicago, as executive creative director. Ms. Allan had most recently been creative director at Go East Design, St. Paul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T13:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09550c78-a065-5a30-8373-7c14fb15edd8', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09550c78-a065-5a30-8373-7c14fb15edd8'}, {'abstract': 'A geologist who is documenting the degradation of China’s waterways discusses what he has learned and how rapid development affects people living along these waterways.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/q-and-a-yang-yong-on-documenting-the-damage-to-chinas-rivers/', 'snippet': 'A geologist who is documenting the degradation of China’s waterways discusses what he has learned and how rapid development affects people living along these waterways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a geologist for a state-owned company, Yang Yong saw firsthand both the beauty of China’s rivers and the damage done to them by the country’s rapid development. In 1992, he set out to document the degradation of China’s waterways on his own, and has since widely explored rivers across China, particularly in the south and west of the country. His photographs of the Jinsha River, the Yangtze River’s upper reach, which flows through Qinghai, Sichuan and Yunnan Provinces, show vividly how that critical waterway has been harmed by the development of mining and hydropower. In an interview, he discussed what led him to this line of research, what his exploration of China’s rivers has revealed and how rapid development affects people living along these waterways.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/09/world/09sino-river01/09sino-river01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumb