: [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538cbdc6-5056-51df-8135-2fbc0ee075f6', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538cbdc6-5056-51df-8135-2fbc0ee075f6'}, {'abstract': 'An increase in the black share of the electorate isn’t the likeliest outcome, but it has happened before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/upshot/how-black-turnout-could-decide-senate-control.html', 'snippet': 'An increase in the black share of the electorate isn’t the likeliest outcome, but it has happened before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Black voters will play an outsize role in this year’s fight for control of the Senate. Mississippi, Louisiana and Georgia are the three states where African-Americans represent the largest share of the population, and North Carolina isn’t too far behind, at seventh on the list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/upshot/10UP-Black/10UP-Black-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Black Turnout Could Decide Senate Control', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77d9526-dcec-5ec3-8fc3-bf81b4f4c975', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77d9526-dcec-5ec3-8fc3-bf81b4f4c975'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Reitzell — the force behind many of the film world’s most innovative soundtracks and scores — premieres his first-ever solo album, “Auto Music,” streaming here exclusively for T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/brian-reitzell-exclusive-stream-auto-music-sofia-coppola/', 'snippet': 'Brian Reitzell — the force behind many of the film world’s most innovative soundtracks and scores — premieres his first-ever solo album, “Auto Music,” streaming here exclusively for T.', 'lead_paragraph': "“That’s the ‘Blade Runner synth,'” Brian Reitzell notes, pointing to the hulking ’70s-era Yamaha CS-80 keyboard in a corner of his L.A. recording studio. “And this is the ‘Terry Riley organ,'” he continues, brushing the keys on another vintage Yamaha, the YC-45-D, before moving on to a sleek ’80s-era PPG Wave 2.2. “I remember being 12 years old and playing a chord on this at Guitar Center in San Francisco, and feeling like I was being transported to heaven on Mars,” he says. These three machines are but a few of the vintage instruments crammed into the room where Reitzell – one of today’s pre-eminent film and TV soundtrack composers and music supervisors – creates his evocative scores. “This is only a fraction of the things that I have,” Reitzell adds. “And there’s nothing in here that’s new!”", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1889, 'width': 1888, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09reitzell-diehl1/09reitzell-diehl1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | Sofia Coppola’s Music Man Strikes Out on his Own', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coppola, Sofia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT DIEHL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DIEHL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d64109ff-780b-58dd-a3ea-70989d8276b9', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d64109ff-780b-58dd-a3ea-70989d8276b9'}, {'abstract': 'In a statement issued on Monday, a Walmart spokeswoman emphasized that the company believed their driver “was operating within the federal hours of service regulations.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/nyregion/driver-charged-in-tracy-morgan-crash-had-not-slept-in-24-hours-prosecutors-say.html', 'snippet': 'In a statement issued on Monday, a Walmart spokeswoman emphasized that the company believed their driver “was operating within the federal hours of service regulations.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Walmart driver whose truck collided with a van carrying the comedian Tracy Morgan and other performers had not slept for more than 24 hours before the crash, New Jersey prosecutors said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driver Charged in Crash Involving Tracy Morgan Had Not Slept in 24 Hours, Prosecutors Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Driver Charged in Fatal Crash Had Not Slept in 24 Hours, Prosecutors Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Tracy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roper, Kevin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNair, James (1952-2014)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driver Distraction and Fatigue', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4838cbed-f35e-505d-947e-e4288894609f', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4838cbed-f35e-505d-947e-e4288894609f'}, {'abstract': 'Drug and food deals are being done at huge premiums. And still shareholders are bidding up the shares of buyers. They may regret it, contend Robert Cyran and Kevin Allison of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/merger-market-shows-signs-of-froth/', 'snippet': 'Drug and food deals are being done at huge premiums. And still shareholders are bidding up the shares of buyers. They may regret it, contend Robert Cyran and Kevin Allison of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The merger market is showing symptoms of overheating. Global deal volume is up sharply this year – up 63 percent according to Bernstein research and 71 percent by Thomson Reuters’ tally. Monday’s announcements, meanwhile, hint at “toppiness.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/business/dbpix-merck-breakingviews/dbpix-merck-breakingviews-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merger Market Shows Signs of Froth', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hillshire Brands Co.', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hittite Microwave Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Pilgrim's Pride Corp", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tyson Foods Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6709991c-45c6-5c46-8be0-37961fa96040', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6709991c-45c6-5c46-8be0-37961fa96040'}, {'abstract': '“Do you think it makes sense for the president of the United States to be negotiating with terrorists?” he asked.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/bobby-jindals-berdahl-questions-answered/', 'snippet': '“Do you think it makes sense for the president of the United States to be negotiating with terrorists?” he asked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Bobby Jindal of Louisiana, one of a long list of Republican politicians who yearn for national office and who grab the national spotlight by pandering to the far right, received applause from fellow Republicans on Friday by attacking President Obama over the decision to trade five Taliban prisoners for Sgt. Bowe Bergdahl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bobby Jindal’s Bergdahl Questions, Answered', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergdahl, Bowe R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:06:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/706bb3ff-a897-5edd-9004-a7ba9cb14982', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/706bb3ff-a897-5edd-9004-a7ba9cb14982'}, {'abstract': 'Reading The New York Times’s reviews of Ms. McDonald, who has won a Tony in each of the four performing categories.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/how-audra-mcdonald-won-six-tony-awards/', 'snippet': 'Reading The New York Times’s reviews of Ms. McDonald, who has won a Tony in each of the four performing categories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday night, Audra McDonald won her sixth Tony Award for acting, more than any other performer. Her achievement is all the more remarkable in that she has worked in just nine Broadway productions since she first appeared in “The Secret Garden” two decades ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 980, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 980}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1254, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/09artsbeat-audra3/09artsbeat-audra3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Audra McDonald Won Six Tony Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Audra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c806d0b-e9c1-5736-a0ba-6b19ebde9e05', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c806d0b-e9c1-5736-a0ba-6b19ebde9e05'}, {'abstract': 'In a time when the writing life feels more precarious than ever, just sticking with it is becoming its own art form, writes ANNA NORTH.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/with-stay-lit-writers-persevere-in-a-hostile-world/', 'snippet': 'In a time when the writing life feels more precarious than ever, just sticking with it is becoming its own art form, writes ANNA NORTH.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing is scary. It is especially scary now, as advances shrink, publishers\xa0fight with Amazon, and the\xa0death of the novel\xa0is forecast with ever-increasing frequency. It’s a time when it would make a lot of sense to quit — and a time when simply not quitting is becoming its own art form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With ‘Stay Lit,’ Writers Persevere in a Hostile World', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T18:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organi