'snippet': 'The designer shares behind-the-scenes shots of the making of her Resort 2015 look book at the Pollock-Krasner House and Studio in the Hamptons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, Rosetta Getty will present her sophomore collection to a host of fashion editors at the Chelsea Arts Tower in Manhattan. It’s fitting that the designer chose the art gallery condominium to set the scene for her resort 2015 outing: this season, like last, she sourced inspiration from one artist and one artistic muse. The personal style of Betty Parsons —\xa0the gallerist, artist and proponent of the Abstract Expressionist movement —\xa0infuses the set of sensible and effortless separates. And the palette of Jackson Pollock — specifically, his “Mural” painting, originally commissioned by Peggy Guggenheim in 1943 —\xa0informed Getty’s mostly chartreuse, black and white color choices for the season. Even Pollock’s relaxed, fluid brush strokes come into play in the L.A.-based designer’s laid-back silhouettes.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosetta Getty’s Art-Inspired Sophomore Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Verge: Her Own Muses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T19:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8e6a39b-dcf8-547f-8838-c9126c9ad970', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8e6a39b-dcf8-547f-8838-c9126c9ad970'}, {'abstract': 'For some, buying a burial space near the final resting place of a person they admire is a different kind of hero worship, and puts a new twist on the real estate cliché “location, location, location.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/nyregion/prime-real-estate-at-the-cemetery-is-a-plot-next-to-an-idol.html', 'snippet': 'For some, buying a burial space near the final resting place of a person they admire is a different kind of hero worship, and puts a new twist on the real estate cliché “location, location, location.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a break in a concert in the Bronx, Victor Goines, a jazz saxophonist and clarinetist, realized that he wanted to spend more time in that very place — a lot more time. Being there would put him close to people he idolized, like Duke Ellington, so he decided to spend $25,000 to buy the land behind the stage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/nyregion/CEMETERYweb1/CEMETERYweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/nyregion/CEMETERYweb1/CEMETERYweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/nyregion/CEMETERYweb1/CEMETERYweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/nyregion/CEMETERYweb1/CEMETERYweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/nyregion/CEMETERYweb1/CEMETERYweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTy