act': 'In “The Antiquarian,” the narrator’s best friend, confined to a psychiatric ward after the murder of his fiancée, admits to the deed yet drops hints that the truth might be more complex.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/books/the-antiquarian-by-gustavo-faveron-patriau.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Antiquarian,” the narrator’s best friend, confined to a psychiatric ward after the murder of his fiancée, admits to the deed yet drops hints that the truth might be more complex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news from college friends tends to be the stuff of weddings, children and jobs. In “The Antiquarian,” the delightfully macabre first novel by the Peruvian writer Gustavo Faverón Patriau, the narrator, Gustavo, receives a rather more alarming update: His closest friend from his university days, Daniel, has murdered his fiancée, Juliana, by stabbing her 36 times, attempting to burn her body and leaving her in the trunk of his car while trying to kill himself with a gunshot to the head. He fails and lands in a psychiatric ward.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/book/book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 936, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 936, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'c