: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/arts/music/jack-white-and-vampire-weekend-at-governors-ball.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s Governors Ball was about hometown New York City pride, but also about guitar heat versus electronic cool, strong female songwriters and the many ways to make people dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every well-planned festival holds a skein of tangled story lines. This year’s Governors Ball — the fourth annual event, presented Friday through Sunday with 68 acts on four stages on Randalls Island — was, first of all, about hometown New York City pride. It had a headlining set on Sunday by Vampire Weekend and a much-anticipated, fully rewarding set on Saturday by the Strokes, as well as a lineup dotted with other New York City bands, notably a recharged TV on the Radio.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Festival With a New York Heart', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Festival With a New York Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors Ball Music Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Randalls Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vampire Weekend (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Jack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-09T22:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8a6c787-39a6-51e1-ae99-8f6c8331ecc0', 'word_count': 1286,