tion Pictures, scheduled to open in 2017, is still figuring out its mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — In the dim light of a gutted department store, through the dust of nearby construction, Kerry Brougher sees a flickering movie future filled with “hundreds of different cinemas.” For tiny screens. Vast ones. Theaters yet to be conceived. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/arts/10BROUGHER1/10BROUGHER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Museum Devoted to Movies Is Still Writing Its Own Script', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Museum Devoted to Movies Is Still Writing Its Own Script', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brougher, Kerry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Academy Museum of Motion Pictures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T01:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229f43ad-7076-5eeb-8368-fefe2c356ca9', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229f43ad-7076-5eeb-8368-fefe2c356ca9'}, {'abstract': 'A bidding war for the maker of Jimmy Dean sausages ended in a $7.7 billion offer by Tyson Foods, reflecting a trend of consolidation among food producers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/09/after-a-short-furious-battle-a-rich-offer-for-hillshire/', 'snippet': 'A bidding war for the maker of Jimmy Dean sausages ended in a $7.7 billion offer by Tyson Foods, reflecting a trend of consolidation among food producers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just over three weeks ago, Hillshire Brands was focusing on shoring up support for its planned takeover of Pinnacle Foods despite vocal shareholder opposition.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'