acle Foods Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tyson Foods Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T01:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb44689c-ef58-560f-9235-36f8562a4ce7', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb44689c-ef58-560f-9235-36f8562a4ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Advancements include Medicare covering gender reassignment surgery, an evaluation of the military’s senseless ban on transgender service and Maryland’s law extending civil rights protections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/opinion/progress-on-transgender-rights-and-health.html', 'snippet': 'Advancements include Medicare covering gender reassignment surgery, an evaluation of the military’s senseless ban on transgender service and Maryland’s law extending civil rights protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Progress on civil rights typically comes in incremental steps that discard old policies for new approaches advancing fair treatment. The Obama administration recently took such a step by reversing a 1981 policy that excluded gender reassignment surgery from coverage under Medicare. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Progress on Transgender Rights and Health', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Progress on Transgender Rights and Health', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '