rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Daniel (1985- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T03:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08167bc9-aa7e-5e54-936a-d7a184c45905', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08167bc9-aa7e-5e54-936a-d7a184c45905'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration announced Monday that it had set new safety standards for infant formula.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/us/new-safety-standards-set-for-baby-food.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration announced Monday that it had set new safety standards for infant formula.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration announced Monday that it had set new safety standards for infant formula. The rules require manufacturers to screen products for salmonella, which can cause fever and diarrhea, and cronobacter, a potentially lethal germ that thrives in very dry places, like powdered milk and baby formula. The F.D.A. said that companies must also test products for nutrient content and demonstrate that they support “normal physical growth.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Safety Standards Set for Baby Food', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Safety Standards Set for Baby Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infant Formulas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmonella (Bacteria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Foods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T03:26:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eb28f4b-cca5-5b98-a26b-633d12773973', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eb28f4b-cca5-5b98-a26b-633d12773973'}, {'abstract': 'Immigration and health authorities will open a shelter at Fort Sill, an Army base in Lawton, for unaccompanied minors caught crossing the border illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/us/oklahoma-another-base-to-house-young-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'Immigration and health authorities will open a shelter at Fort Sill, an Army base in Lawton, for unaccompanied minors caught crossing the border illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immigration and health authorities will open a shelter at Fort Sill, an Army base in Lawton, for unaccompanied minors caught crossing the southwest border illegally, Obama administration officials said Monday. About 600 youths will be sent there in the coming days, with the number expected to grow to 1,200. About 1,200 minors who were apprehended without parents are in a shelter at Lackland Air Force Base in San Antonio, and 575 are at Naval Base Ventura County near Oxnard, Calif. The authorities also set up temporary holding cells in Nogales, Ariz., to process the youths for deportation proceedings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oklahoma: Another Base to House Young Immigrants', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Plains', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oklahoma: Another Base to House Young Immigrants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Sill (Okla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T03:26:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0da322-2d8d-5cd9-809f-69399f62c0bd', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0da322-2d8d-5cd9-809f-69399f62c0bd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ambrose was President Richard M. Nixon’s first drug czar, but resigned before he could take the helm of the new government arm he had helped shepherd into being, the Drug Enforcement Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/us/myles-j-ambrose-87-deas-midwife-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ambrose was President Richard M. Nixon’s first drug czar, but resigned before he could take the helm of the new government arm he had helped shepherd into being, the Drug Enforcement Administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Myles J. Ambrose, who was President Richard M. Nixon’s first drug czar, but who resigned before he could take the helm of the new government arm he had helped shepherd into being, the Drug Enforcement Administration, died on June 3 in Leesburg, Va. He was 87. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/us/AMBROSE-obit/AMBROSE-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Myles J. Ambrose, Nixon Drug Czar, D.E.A. Midwife, Dies a