 neck injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'USA Hockey, the sport’s governing body in the United States, announced Monday that it had permitted use of the Look-Up Line, an orange warning track painted on the ice designed to reduce paralyzing neck injuries that could result from collisions into the boards. However, the measure fell short of mandating its use in American ice rinks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'USA Hockey Permits Use of Safety Feature Resembling Warning Track', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'USA Hockey Backs Warning Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Hockey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T03:51:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a27f7b78-9cf2-5a0f-aa50-be8c0cf29107', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a27f7b78-9cf2-5a0f-aa50-be8c0cf29107'}, {'abstract': 'The Americans are making themselves at home at a São Paulo facility in preparation for their opening match with Ghana.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/sports/worldcup/us-team-hits-practice-field-soon-after-touching-down-in-brazil.html', 'snippet': 'The Americans are making themselves at home at a São Paulo facility in preparation for their opening match with Ghana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — The United States national team arrived in Brazil early Monday morning, and the players were on the field for their first training session by that afternoon. If that seems like a quick turnaround after a 12-hour, two-leg, overnight travel itinerary that began in Jacksonville, Fla., consider that Tim Howard, the starting goalkeeper, actually was surprised at how long it took for the team to get to work. “With Jurgen, I’m surprised we weren’t out here earlier,” Howard said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Team Hits Practice Field Soon After Touching Down in Brazil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Team Hits Practice Field Soon After Touching Down in Brazil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T03:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'World Cup', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47cc172d-e70d-54f3-81bd-37515ed02022', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47cc172d-e70d-54f3-81bd-37515ed02022'}, {'abstract': 'Hailed as the 21st century’s answer to Proust for his controversial six-volume autobiographical work, “My Struggle,” Karl Ove Knausgaard responds to his sudden celebrity with this essay on his tortured relationship with fame — its intense lure, its perils and the Scandinavian culture that condemns its pursuit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/t-magazine/karl-ove-knausgaard-on-fame-my-struggle.html', 'snippet': 'Hailed as the 21st century’s answer to Proust for his controversial six-volume autobiographical work, “My Struggle,” Karl Ove Knausgaard responds to his sudden celebrity with this essay on his tortured relationship with fame — its intense lure, it...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hailed as the 21st century’s answer to Proust for his controversial six-volume autobiographical work, “My Struggle,” Karl Ove Knausgaard responds to his sudden celebrity with this essay on his tortured relationship with fame — its intense lure, its perils and the Scandinavian culture that condemns its pursuit. Translated by Ingvild Burkey.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '94', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-knausgaard-1/15culture-well-knausgaard-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-knausgaard-1/15culture-well-knausgaard-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-knausgaard-1/15culture-well-knausgaard-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-knausgaard-1/15culture-well-knausgaard-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15