thers who run the textile house Fortuny have curated a massive home-accessories sale debuting tomorrow on the flash-sale site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Design enthusiasts who weren’t fortunate enough to visit Venice this week for the opening of the Architecture Biennale (and might be suffering from a touch of Instagram envy), can at least fake the experience via an upcoming sale on One Kings Lane. Mickey and Maury Riad, the two brothers who run the century-old Venetian textile house Fortuny, were invited by the site to shop the town’s various islands to assemble a massive home-accessories sale of over 200 items, which begins tomorrow. A tag sale of the brothers’ own personal collection will also debut on the same day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10fortuny-rubinstein/10fortuny-rubinstein-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10fortuny-rubinstein/10fortuny-rubinstein-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10fortuny-rubinstein/10fortuny-rubinstein-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10fortuny-rubinstein/10fortuny-rubinstein-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10fortuny-rubinstein/10fortuny-rubinstein-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'lega