 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aa8eb1a-e45c-58f0-aa11-a485abb89b4c', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aa8eb1a-e45c-58f0-aa11-a485abb89b4c'}, {'abstract': 'Important opinions on the Pakistan bombing, protecting journalists, safe roads, Arizona water and Andy Murray’s coach.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/morning-views-9/', 'snippet': 'Important opinions on the Pakistan bombing, protecting journalists, safe roads, Arizona water and Andy Murray’s coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times editorial board condemns the “brazen assault” carried out by Taliban militants on the international airport in Karachi, Pakistan, this weekend. “One has to assume the militants will stop at nothing until the state is utterly destabilized and they have taken control,” the board writes, calling on Pakistani political and military leaders to recognize the Taliban threat and quickly devise a strategy to protect the nation’s people. “Time to find a solution is fast running out.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T10:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45fc171c-7f50-5beb-8e5e-1bed347d55ef', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45fc171c-7f50-5beb-8e5e-1bed347d55ef'}, {'abstract': 'The report, by CrowdStrike, a security company, ties a hacker group in Shanghai to attacks on governments, contractors and research companies.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/daily-report-report-implicate