g others, as well as the third annual Live Ideas mini-festival, to be programmed by the composer Laurie Anderson, are among the highlights of the 2014-15 season at New York Live Arts, the Chelsea dance theater directed by the choreographer Bill T. Jones. The season, which Mr. Jones announced Tuesday, will include 71 performances by more than 22 artists and ensembles, including the Bill T. Jones/Arnie Zane Dance Company.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Works and Programming by Laurie Anderson to Highlight New York Live Arts Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Live Arts to Feature New Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abraham, Kyle (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, LAURIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Bill T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Rashaun', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jones, Bill T/Arnie Zane Dance Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T15:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b47b9568-9e0e-526f-a4fd-0a519b2797bd', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b47b9568-9e0e-526f-a4fd-0a519b2797bd'}, {'abstract': 'Why Democrats shouldn’t assume that the president’s poll numbers won’t weigh them down in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/does-obamas-unpopularity-matter/', 'snippet': 'Why Democrats shouldn’t assume that the president’s poll numbers won’t weigh them down in 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My last post\xa0offered 1400 words in response to a Jonathan Chait tweet; now let me offer a few more in response to his actual rebuttal to\xa0my recent column\xa0on why the Democrats need Hillary Clinton to hold their presidential majority together. Here, from\xa0his latest post, is a two-part argument that I’m overstating the significance of President Obama’s stuck-in-the-40s approval ratings for his party’s fortunes in 2016. First, because of the Republicans:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Obama’s Unpopularity Matter?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chait, Jonathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T15:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca1219f6-cd80-5c25-913a-a52f8243e739', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca1219f6-cd80-5c25-913a-a52f8243e739'}, {'abstract': 'A controversial message on yogurt lids has people talking about anti-science sentiment in America, and the power of social media to change it, ANNA NORTH writes.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/chobanis-science-lesson/', 'snippet': 'A controversial message on yogurt lids has people talking about anti-science sentiment in America, and the power of social media to change it, ANNA NORTH writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Greek yogurt company Chobani raised hackles last week with a message under some of its lids that read, “Nature got us to 100 calories, not scientists. #howmatters.” The company has\xa0apologized, but some scientists say the controversy suggests something bigger about anti-science sentiment in America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chobani’s Science Lesson', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T15:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf111c95-6ad0-5292-9bcd-5ffdb125c690', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf111c95-6ad0-5292-9bcd-5ffdb125c690'}, {'abstract': 'Tumult in Ukraine has ensured that there is no shortage of labor on Spitsbergen, a Norwegian island where a Russian company mines coal and Moscow heavily subsidizes aspects of daily life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/world/europe/ukrainians-find-jobs-and-a-slice-of-russia-in-arctic-norway.html', 'snippet': 'Tumult in Ukraine has ensured that there is no shortage of labor on Spitsbergen, a Norwegian island where a Russian company mines coal and Moscow heavily subsidizes aspects of daily life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARENTSBURG, Norway — While scientists up here in the high Arctic monitor global warming by studying the movement of polar bears, ice floes and glaciers, Nikolai Mikitenko tracks the meltdown in Ukraine, the land of his birth more than 2,000 miles away, through the migration of desperate coal miners.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/world/11ARCTIC1/11ARCTIC1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'