.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/hong-kong-rebel-loses-his-trademark-long-hair/', 'snippet': 'Leung Kwok-hung’s unkempt mane had been a constant in his decade as one of the city’s most animated legislators. That was, until his hair was cut short on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what he did to the laws — making them as a legislator in the somber wooden chamber of Hong Kong’s Legislative Council, or breaking them when he burst into a room to disrupt a public forum — Leung Kwok-hung’s long unkempt hair had been a constant in his decade as one of the city’s most animated legislators. That was, until his hair was cut short on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Rebel Loses His Trademark Long Hair', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Kwok-hung', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APPLE DAILY', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T15:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1145dbfc-4092-5b3d-ba91-182853cc5a47', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1145dbfc-4092-5b3d-ba91-182853cc5a47'}, {'abstract': 'This Thursday, the downtown designer with a cult following opens the doors to her first brick and mortar outpost, a cheeky yet refined shop located just under her own apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/rachel-comey-new-soho-flagship/', 'snippet': 'This Thursday, the downtown designer with a cult following opens the doors to her first brick and mortar outpost, a cheeky yet refined shop located just under her own apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is fitting that Rachel Comey, who hosts intimate dinner parties rather than runway shows during fashion week, has chosen to open her first brick-and-mortar outpost just downstairs from her own SoHo apartment next door. The downtown designer with a cult following has a knack for keeping things personal — and for not taking fashion too seriously. “It’s important for the store to be a tad funny,” she says. Indeed, the buzz surrounding the shop — which her most ardent followers have been hoping and wishing for for the past 13 years — has been on overdrive since Comey released a photo of a cheeky flag, painted with the help of her good friend Leanne Shapton, hanging outside the then-raw space on Crosby Street. It poked fun at the storefront’s mainstream-Manhattan neighbors: SoulCycle, Jamba Juice and Duane Reade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09comey-bobb/09comey-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09comey-bobb/09comey-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/09/t-magazine/09comey-bobb/09comey-bobb-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre