est donors to educational causes and a strong backer of the academic guidelines known as the Common Core, has called for a two-year moratorium on states or school districts making any high-stakes decisions based on tests aligned with the new standards.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delay Urged on Actions Tied to Tests by Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delay Urged on Actions Tied to Tests by Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Chief State School Officers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Governors Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Vicki (1958- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-10T19:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b98a979-011b-592f-95c3-8107e9ce39f5', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b98a979-011b-592f-95c3-8107e9ce39f5'}, {'abstract': 'The smoky-voiced chanteuse sounds off on her festival style, taking calls from inmates and her Fiona Apple obsession.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/singer-banks-goddess-album-drowning-video/', 'snippet': 'The smoky-voiced chanteuse sounds off on her festival style, taking calls from inmates and her Fiona Apple obsession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early press on Jillian Banks, the 25-year-old songstress who goes simply by Banks, focused largely on how little was actually known about her. The Los Angeles native seemed to appear out of nowhere, dropping a song, “Before I Ever Met You,” on Soundcloud in early 2013 to huge acclaim, and appearing in only a handful of photos in which her dark, searching eyes and model-like cheekbones were hidden in shadow or behind her long brown hair. At a time when many of her peers were blasting out songs about their famous exes and tipping off TMZ to their whereabouts, Banks was — quite literally — shrouded in obscurity. (Appropriately, the singer showed up for her interview with T clad in head-to-toe black, hair hanging over her face.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10bank-oloizia/10bank-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10bank-oloizia/10bank-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10bank-oloizia/10bank-oloizia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/10/t-magazine/10bank-oloizia/10bank-oloizia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr