ption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/HYER-obit/HYER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/HYER-obit/HYER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/HYER-obit/HYER-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Martha Hyer, Oscar-Nominated Actress, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Martha Hyer, 89, Oscar-Nominated Actress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyer, Martha (1924-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T00:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a50772c8-be7c-54de-8582-46716a6563c0', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a50772c8-be7c-54de-8582-46716a6563c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Internal Revenue Service on Tuesday unveiled a Taxpayer Bill of Rights that is intended to ensure the rights to privacy, confidentiality and a fair appeals process with the agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/us/irs-publishes-guide-it-says-will-help-ensure-taxpayer-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The Internal Revenue Service on Tuesday unveiled a Taxpayer Bill of Rights that is intended to ensure the rights to privacy, confidentiality and a fair appeals process with the agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internal Revenue Service on Tuesday unveiled a Taxpayer Bill of Rights that is intended to ensure the rights to privacy, confidentiality and a fair appeals process in dealings with the agency. “This reinforces for the average taxpayer the fairness of the system,” the agency’s commissioner, John Koskinen, said. He said the timing had nothing to do with the investigations that the I.R.S. is facing after being accused of giving improper scrutiny to conservative groups while reviewing their applications for tax-exempt status. He said that the decision was meant to “help taxpayers’ comfort level with the I.R.S.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S. Publishes Guide It Says Will Help Ensure Taxpayer Rights', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.R.S. Publishes Guide It Says Will Help Ensure Taxpayer Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d87051e-93e0-5506-bcca-67608f886a29', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d87051e-93e0-5506-bcca-67608f886a29'}, {'abstract': 'After Gov. Terry McAuliffe lost his battle with the legislature over Medicaid expansion, he is thought to be studying how to press the issue by executive action — a legally and politically uncertain course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/us/virginia-governor-may-try-to-expand-medicaid-on-his-own.html', 'snippet': 'After Gov. Terry McAuliffe lost his battle with the legislature over Medicaid expansion, he is thought to be studying how to press the issue by executive action — a legally and politically uncertain course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHMOND, Va. — Gov. Terry McAuliffe has lost his battle with the legislature over Medicaid expansion, an enormous retreat from the high expectations he set for a liberal agenda. However, he is thought to be studying how to press the issue by executive action — a legally and politically uncertain course.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/us/VIRGINIA/VIRGINIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/us/VIRGINIA/VIRGINIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/us/VIRGINIA/VIRGINIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/us/VIRGINIA/VIRGINIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 977, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption':