//www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/upshot/why-did-cantor-lose-not-easy-to-explain.html', 'snippet': 'The House majority leader outspent his opponent, had defeated a challenger in a more favorable year for the Tea Party and was said to have led in polls. But he lost anyway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, lost his primary on Tuesday night in one of the most stunning electoral upsets in recent memory. It is not easy to explain his defeat, or the extent to which his campaign apparently underestimated the severity of the threat posed by David Brat, a Tea Party-backed economics professor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/upshot/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor/SUB-3-11UP-Cantor-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Did Cantor Lose? Not Easy to Explain', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brat, David A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0bfcfd-c70c-5d1c-93f2-98709596cb8a', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0bfcfd-c70c-5d1c-93f2-98709596cb8a'}, {'abstract': 'The trustees of Union Theological Seminary, a liberal Protestant organization in New York City, voted on Tuesday to divest the school’s $108.4 million endowment from fossil fuel companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/us/campaigning-for-environment-seminary-to-divest-some-holdings.html', 'snippet': 'The trustees of Union Theological Seminary, a liberal Protestant organization in New York City, voted on Tuesday to divest the school’s $108.4 million endowment from fossil fuel companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trustees of Union Theological Seminary, a historic cradle of liberal Protestantism in New York City, voted unanimously\xa0on Tuesday to divest the school’s $108.4 million endowment from fossil fuel companies. Union is said to be the first seminary to take up the divestment tactic in a campaign by environmentalists to combat climate change. Last month, Stanford University announced it would divest, but only from coal companies. The president of Union, Serene Jones, said, “Climate change poses a catastrophic threat, and as stewards of God’s creation we simply must act.” The seminary had already divested from tobacco and liquor companies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaigning for Environment, Seminary to Divest Some Holdings', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campaigning for Environment, Seminary to Divest Some Holdings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union Theological Seminary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endowments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:12:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/80641840-1685-5e1e-885f-472223bb1782', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80641840-1685-5e1e-885f-472223bb1782'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio is reviving a rezoning plan around Grand Central Terminal with a wiser approach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/opinion/smart-growth-on-the-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio is reviving a rezoning plan around Grand Central Terminal with a wiser approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the sun setting on his final term, Mayor Michael Bloomberg tried last fall to push through a grand rezoning plan for East Midtown that would have brought many more office towers and a flood of workers to a 73-block area around Grand Central Terminal. He said it met an urgent need to keep the city competitive, with up-to-date buildings and improved transportation above and below ground. The plan died in the City Council, under criticism from community members and elected officials who said it was too drastic and too complicated to wave through. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smart Growth on the East Side', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smart Growth on the East Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SL Green Realty Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:12:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7adadb8c-2a08-5c37-9140-d43b8f7e8321', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7adadb8c-2a08-5c37-9140-d43b8f7e8321'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s order providing relief to millions with loans and a pending loan refinancing bill speak to a grave problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/opinion/student-borrowers-and-the-economy.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s order providing relief to millions with loans and a pending loan refinancing bill speak to a grave problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama took an important step this week when he signed an executive order providing relief to millions of struggling student loan borrowers and urged Congress to pass a student loan refinancing bill that is scheduled for a vote in the Senate on Wednesday. Both the executive order and the refinancing bill speak to a grave problem that has trapped recent college graduates and threatens the long-term health of the economy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Borrowers and the Economy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Student Borrowers and the Economy ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d6798ba-5187-5a95-b525-8b4e8c4c6ab6', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d6798ba-5187-5a95-b525-8b4e8c4c6ab6'}, {'abstract': 'The bank made its final multibillion-dollar settlement offer Monday, but it was said to be short of what the Justice Dep