en Over by a Develope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dufresne, Wylie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordinier, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WD-50 (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10944ab4-40ba-540c-b165-2ad90d59494e', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10944ab4-40ba-540c-b165-2ad90d59494e'}, {'abstract': 'The indiscriminate use of noncompete clauses hurts workers by limiting their ability to seek better jobs in their chosen professions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/opinion/clauses-that-hurt-workers.html', 'snippet': 'The indiscriminate use of noncompete clauses hurts workers by limiting their ability to seek better jobs in their chosen professions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many businesses have long required that executives and other important employees agree not to work for a competitor for a year or two after they leave. Now some employers are unfairly imposing that requirement on all kinds of workers, including lower-wage employees like camp counselors, interns and yoga instructors, The Times has found. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clauses That Hurt Workers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clauses That Hurt Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T01:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a3b144-8244-5955-88c0-4563651659d5', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a3b144-8244-5955-88c0-4563651659d5'}, {'abstract': 'The religious extremists and the committed environmentalists both want a Middle East without borders, but for very different reasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/opinion/friedman-the-real-war-of-ideas.html', 'snippet': 'The religious extremists and the committed environmentalists both want a Middle East without borders, but for very different reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The takeover Tuesday of the Iraqi city of Mosul by Sunni extremists who spilled over the Syrian border underscores the clash of world views that is underway in the whole Eastern Mediterranean, which I saw close up during my visit to Kurdistan a few days ago. And it’s not what you think. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima