': 'nyt://article/f7c8c317-5a53-5ca8-a0e3-8ff616d6f586', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c8c317-5a53-5ca8-a0e3-8ff616d6f586'}, {'abstract': 'A standoff between the Justice Department and an elected county attorney in Montana ended with an agreement under which local prosecutors promised to improve their response to sexual assault cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/us/montana-prosecutors-agree-to-improve-sex-assault-response.html', 'snippet': 'A standoff between the Justice Department and an elected county attorney in Montana ended with an agreement under which local prosecutors promised to improve their response to sexual assault cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A standoff between the Justice Department and an elected county attorney in western Montana ended\xa0on Tuesday\xa0with an agreement under which local prosecutors promised to improve their response to sexual assault cases. The agreement came months after a lacerating report by federal authorities accused the Missoula County attorney’s office of gender bias in handling sexual assault cases. The county attorney, Fred Van Valkenburg, sued federal judiciary officials, arguing they had no right to investigate his office. Under the deal, that challenge is being dropped, and the attorney’s office has promised to set up new policies and training for sexual assault cases and to communicate better with victims and the police. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Montana: Prosecutors Agree to Improve Sex Assault Response', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Montana: Prosecutors Agree to Improve Sex Assault Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'ra