news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/55547173-a365-59fe-ace0-02b37d66bc23', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55547173-a365-59fe-ace0-02b37d66bc23'}, {'abstract': 'Ian Livengood waves proudly at us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/10/athenas-counterpart/', 'snippet': 'Ian Livengood waves proudly at us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — There is absolutely nothing wrong with this puzzle. It is a light-hearted and amusing tribute to June 14’s Flag Day holiday, and Ian Livengood’s puzzle offers us a chance to identify the prominent features of the flags of four countries. So far, so good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Athena’s Counterpart', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T02:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a81b945-13e1-5085-9e7c-2017f6df4b45', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a81b945-13e1-5085-9e7c-2017f6df4b45'}, {'abstract': 'Robert S. Ford, who resigned in February, said more weapons to the moderate Syrian rebels would increase the opposition’s leverage in peace talks and combat the rise of extremist groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/world/middleeast/former-ambassador-to-syria-urges-increasing-arms-supply-to-moderate-rebels.html', 'snippet': 'Robert S. Ford, who resigned in February, said more weapons to the moderate Syrian rebels would increase the opposition’s leverage in peace talks and combat the rise of extremist groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Robert S. Ford’s misgivings about the Obama administration’s policy toward Syria became so great last summer that he sought to leave his post as the senior United States envoy for Syria.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/world/FORD/FORD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Ambassador to Syria Urges Increasing Arms Supply to Moderate Rebels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Ambassador to Syria Urges Increasing Arms Supply to Moderate Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T02:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f11bf5b2-f4df-5597-95ab-aad55909a833', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f11bf5b2-f4df-5597-95ab-aad55909a833'}, {'abstract': '“The Village Bike,” Penelope Skinner’s play at the Lucille Lortel Theater, centers on a lonely pregnant woman whose growing obsession with sex takes her and other characters to dark places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/theater/the-village-bike-stars-greta-gerwig-as-a-woman-obsessed.html', 'snippet': '“The Village Bike,” Penelope Skinner’s play at the Lucille Lortel Theater, centers on a lonely pregnant woman whose growing obsession with sex takes her and other characters to dark places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greta Gerwig turns out to be the perfect person to ride right over the edge of a cliff with. Now don’t say you haven’t been warned. Because over the cliff is where this surprising actress will have taken you by the end of “The Village Bike,” the genuinely daring new play by Penelope Skinner that opened on Tuesday night at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1588, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/arts/11VILLAGE/11VILLAGE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Careening Into a Bottomless Vortex', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Careening Into a Bottomless Vortex', 'na