/morning-views-10/', 'snippet': 'Morning Views', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noncompete clauses are harmful to both employees and “the economy as a whole,” writes The New York Times editorial board. While the board recognizes these policies have reasonable utility in deterring upper management from defecting to competitors, the restrictions can be needlessly hampering to lower-wage employees who statistically earn more money over the years the more professional freedom they enjoy. More broadly, The Times points to studies showing that gratuitously stringent noncompete policies stifle entrepreneurship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T06:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dcb9190-10b6-542a-844f-39409fbb1ab3', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dcb9190-10b6-542a-844f-39409fbb1ab3'}, {'abstract': 'The student was arrested after she posted a Twitter message suggesting that a method for sending spam text messages might also be used to rally public awareness of the Tiananmen anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/beijing-police-detain-student-over-tiananmen-tweet/', 'snippet': 'The student was arrested after she posted a Twitter message suggesting that a method for sending spam text messages might also be used to rally public awareness of the Tiananmen anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Beijing authorities have detained a woman linked with a Twitter posting suggesting that a method for sending spam text messag