rticle', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae8fdf46-3622-5d39-81f0-a10993a133b8', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae8fdf46-3622-5d39-81f0-a10993a133b8'}, {'abstract': 'Randy Crath was most recently at Scotia Waterous, the oil and gas arm of the Canadian financial firm Scotiabank. At Evercore, he will advise oil and gas companies on acquisitions or sales of international exploration and production assets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/evercore-hires-senior-banker-for-energy-deals/', 'snippet': 'Randy Crath was most recently at Scotia Waterous, the oil and gas arm of the Canadian financial firm Scotiabank. At Evercore, he will advise oil and gas companies on acquisitions or sales of international exploration and production assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The investment bank Evercore Partners has hired a senior banker to advise oil and gas companies on deals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evercore Hires Senior Banker for Energy Deals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Banker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crath, Randy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evercore Partners Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T13:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c6e394-bab4-587e-bfce-11ded5568535', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c6e394-bab4-587e-bfce-11ded5568535'}, {'abstract': 'Some fund managers are skeptical about fossil fuel companies as long-term investments as nations move toward tougher rules on emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/business/international/weighing-the-risks-of-investing-in-energy-companies.html', 'snippet': 'Some fund managers are skeptical about fossil fuel companies as long-term investments as nations move toward tougher rules on emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Norway’s economy is highly dependent on oil and gas production, yet the Nordic country’s largest private pension fund manager, Storebrand, worries about the risks of investing in companies that extract fossil fuels. Figuring that tighter regulations on carbon emissions will emerge in the coming years in an effort to combat climate change, Storebrand has decided not to invest in businesses that it believes will be hurt most by those new rules: coal companies and large producers of oil from tar sands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/12green-pic/12green-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/business/12green-pic/12green-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/12green-pic/12green-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ