nal': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c00d6d6b-61e7-51a5-8486-e63c1b5c3356', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c00d6d6b-61e7-51a5-8486-e63c1b5c3356'}, {'abstract': 'The revival of “A Raisin in the Sun,” which won three Tony Awards, has recouped its entire $4.25 million capitalization.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/broadway-raisin-recoups/', 'snippet': 'The revival of “A Raisin in the Sun,” which won three Tony Awards, has recouped its entire $4.25 million capitalization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway revival of “A Raisin in the Sun,” the biggest box-office hit play of the spring theater season, has recouped its entire $4.25 million capitalization. The producers made the announcement on Tuesday, two days after Lorraine Hansberry’s classic reaped success at the 2014 Tony Awards. “Raisin” won for best play revival, best director of a play (Kenny Leon), and best featured actress in a play (Sophie Okonedo); its three Tonys were the most for any play in the 2013-14 season. The critically acclaimed production, which stars Denzel Washington and LaTanya Richardson Jackson, is scheduled to end its run on Sunday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/arts3/arts3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/arts3/arts3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/arts3/arts3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',