688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e734b04f-a948-5a8b-9f79-980f90751afe'}, {'abstract': 'The writer talks about where he first went to learn about the Mediterranean city and names some of his favorite spots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/travel/peter-mayles-marseille.html', 'snippet': 'The writer talks about where he first went to learn about the Mediterranean city and names some of his favorite spots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Provence, that languid, lavender-covered stretch of France along the Mediterranean, is the region most fans associate with Peter Mayle. His 1989 memoir, “A Year in Provence,” about restoring an 18th-century farmhouse in the Luberon, became such a blockbuster it spawned a veritable franchise of Provençal travelogues, food guides and novels. Indeed, Mr. Mayle said he and his wife had to leave the region for several years just to take a break from eager fans turning up at his doorstep (and from his detractors grumbling about those tourists disturbing the area’s tranquillity).', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15QNA1/15QNA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15QNA1/15QNA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15QNA1/15QNA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15QNA1/15QNA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None