at', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T18:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f193a659-ca43-598d-9396-38826dc06d98', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f193a659-ca43-598d-9396-38826dc06d98'}, {'abstract': 'With coverage of Hillary Clinton continuing nonstop, The Times was among those who missed the clues on Cantor.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/why-didnt-the-data-driven-media-see-eric-cantors-defeat-coming/', 'snippet': 'With coverage of Hillary Clinton continuing nonstop, The Times was among those who missed the clues on Cantor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Was the coverage – or lack thereof – of Eric Cantor’s doomed campaign an epic fail by the media?\xa0Or was Mr. Cantor’s defeat just one of those inevitable surprises that keeps political junkies coming back for more?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Didn’t the Data-Driven Media See Eric Cantor’s 