partner Brad Anderson have created an aesthetically pleasing range of boards that blend old-school materials and craftsmanship with modern shapes and techniques.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/t-magazine/11surf-donnelly/11surf-donnelly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Sustainable Surfboards Made in Maine, or in Your Own Garage', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Forest to the Sea ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T19:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Donnelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donnelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/168b3c78-4ae4-5e92-bae0-34da423d7eb2', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/168b3c78-4ae4-5e92-bae0-34da423d7eb2'}, {'abstract': 'Lauren Stovall prefers comfortable, out-of-the-ordinary items for her retro style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/fashion/style-in-eastern-market-detroit-michigan.html', 'snippet': 'Lauren Stovall prefers comfortable, out-of-the-ordinary items for her retro style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sporting a vintage jumpsuit and her dad’s throwback frames, Lauren Stovall was channeling an era when Motown music ruled Detroit. Ms. Stovall was recently passing time in the city’s Eastern Market neighborhood, a diverse area with rich history that she finds inspirational. She is a self-proclaimed ’70s girl, a hippie at heart, and says comfort is her main approach to style. “Heels, I mean, yeah, they’re cool, but I just love like some unique flats,” Ms. Stovall said.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Industry, Eclectic Styles in Eastern Market, Detroit', 'kicker': 'Intersection | Video', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Industry, Eclectic Styles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T19:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhod Family', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Family', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68fdf04b-4bb8-58f0-bede-42c4710711b4', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68fdf04b-4bb8-58f0-bede-42c4710711b4'}, {'abstract': 'Dexter Filkins on the American exit and its consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/how-we-left-iraq/', 'snippet': 'Dexter Filkins on the American exit and its consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a backgrounder on today’s grim news from Iraq\xa0— the most important news of the day, with apologies to David Brat\xa0—\xa0I’m just going to quote, without comment, from\xa0Dexter Filkins’ New Yorker piece today\xa0on the reasons the country has slid back into chaos and civil war:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Left Iraq', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filkins, Dexter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T19:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2b7ac81-391a-5069-90e8-a6b2759a806b', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2b7ac81-391a-5069-90e8-a6b2759a806b'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Cohen, upon re-reading Saul Bellow’s “Herzog,” elaborates on the idea that some books may be read at the wrong time in one’s life, and suggests timings for the reading of a few classics.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/roger-cohen-when-to-read-what-ive-read/', 'snippet': 'Roger Cohen, upon re-reading Saul Bellow’s “Herzog,” elaborates on the idea that some books may be read at the wrong time in one’s life, and suggests timings for the reading of a few classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent column, Roger Cohen wrote about re-reading Saul Bellow’s “Herzog,” 50 years after the book’s initial publication. He mentioned the idea that some books may be read too soon or too late in life. We asked him to elaborate:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roger Cohen: When to Read What I’ve Read', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T19:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/610db5c6-8ed2-56a1-8294-7d3ef0299399', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/610db5c6-8ed2-56a1-8294-7d3ef0299399'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Martin on the reasons behind Eric Cantor’s surprise defeat in Virginia. Was he just a weak candidate?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000002934016/what-went-wrong-for-eric-cantor.html', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Martin on the reasons behind Eric Cantor’s surprise defeat in Virginia. Was he just a weak candidate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Martin on the reasons behind Eric Cantor’s surprise defeat in Virginia. Was he just a weak candidate?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/11/multime