pacific-northwest-ballet-offers-a-multilayered-giselle.html', 'snippet': 'A staging of Peter Boal’s “Giselle” by the Pacific Northwest Ballet has new designs by Jérôme Kaplan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Peter Boal, artistic director of Pacific Northwest Ballet, staged a revelatory “Giselle” for that company here in 2011. Yet “Giselle” is danced everywhere. So what needed to be revealed? \xa0In truth, the basic text of this central work is in a terrible state all ’round the world. (The same is true for most 19th-century ballet classics, alas. No classic play, opera or concert work is presented today laden with anachronistic and showy changes that are standard for the 19th-century ballets.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 1498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/GISELLE/GISELLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Work Sheds Mythic Aura as It Dons New Clothes', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Work Sheds Mythic Aura as It Dons New Clothes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Giselle (Ballet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boal, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwest Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Jerome', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T21:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f33ab85f-c493-5045-83d5-0533f9730c79', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f33ab85f-c493-5045-83d5-0533f9730c79'}, {'abstract': 'Designers cannot agree on what the five-week pre-spring season is, or even what to call it. Resort? Cruise? Pre-Collection?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/fashion/fashions-identity-crisis-over-a-season-in-flux.html', 'snippet': 'Designers cannot agree on what the five-week pre-spring season is, or even what to call it. Resort? Cruise? Pre-Collection?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So we come to the end of that interminable, puzzling, ill-defined women’s wear season that is known as pre-spring — or almost the end, to be absolutely accurate; there are a few more shows dribbling out after the men’s wear spring 2015 collections begin in London this weekend. But you have to draw a line somewhere. And having drawn it, we are left with ... what exactly?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/fashion/12zRESORT/12zRESORT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Season That Defies Its Own Description', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Season That Def