without an Internet connection is preparation.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/11/with-a-bit-of-planning-keep-the-cloud-with-you-always-even-offline/', 'snippet': 'The key to using your cloud services without an Internet connection is preparation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cloud computing may seem incompatible with being offline, but there are ways to live in the cloud even when you don’t have an Internet connection. The most common situation occurs when you are actually in the clouds — stuck on a plane with no Wi-Fi, or, more likely, Wi-Fi so slow it might as well be nonexistent.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Bit of Planning, Keep the Cloud With You Always —\xa0Even Offline', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With a Bit of Planning, Keep the Cloud With You Always', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beats Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dropbox Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T22:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Wood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1994b279-fe00-5290-a16a-0b0517a47ed8', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1994b279-fe00-5290-a16a-0b0517a47ed8'}, {'abstract': 'The singer and comedian Emily Bergl applies a sarcastic edge to some happy standards during her show at 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/arts/music/emily-bergl-performs-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'The singer and comedian Emily Bergl applies a sarcastic edge to some happy standards during her show at 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarcasm is the weapon of choice for the singer and comedian Emily Bergl, who opened at 54 Below on Tuesday evening. And oh, how bracing it feels! Just listen to this supersmart, platinum-haired spitfire sing tainted renditions of the Rodgers and Hammerstein standards “People Will Say We’re in Love” and “I Have Confidence.” Inflected with notes of doubt, cynicism and contempt, they curdle from happy, life-affirming ditties into objects of suspicion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1877, 'width': 1351, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/12EMILY/12EMILY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cynics Need Love, Too', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cynics Need Love, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergl, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T22:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7e581e3-d4df-522b-95ca-718410773968', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7e581e3-d4df-522b-95ca-718410773968'}, {'abstract': '“Breakthrough Weekend” is a New York shaggy-dog story that involves an unusual private detective and his protégé, who take on three increasingly bizarre cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/movies/breakthrough-weekend-follows-a-gumshoe-through-new-york.html', 'snippet': '“Breakthrough Weekend” is a New York shaggy-dog story that involves an unusual private detective and his protégé, who take on three increasingly bizarre cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The closing credits of “Breakthrough Weekend” list a technical crew of five. That figure doesn’t count the producing team, which consists of two of the actors and the director, or the composer, whose personal website is advertised below his name. This New York shaggy-dog story from Sujewa Ekanayake is an example of extreme-makeshift filmmaking — but not, unfortunately, a successful one.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/arts/breakthrough-image/breakthrough-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Detective Who Is More Softy Than Hard-Boiled', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breakthrough Weekend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Breakthrough Weekend (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ekanayake, Sujewa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-11T22:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ac48b4-009e-519e-9b28-4cfd6c9c1708', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ac48b4-009e-519e-9b28-4cfd6c9c1708'}, {'abstract': 'In Southampton, Club Monaco adds vintage and contemporary housewares to its mix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/garden/moving-beyond-clothing-with-collections-for-the-home.html', 'snippet': 'In Southampton, Club Monaco adds vintage and contemporary housewares to its mix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Club Monaco’s shop in Southampton, N.Y., which opened Memorial Day weekend, has the expected clothing and accessories. But it also has home furnishings, and mostly vintage ones at that. Crossing the threshold, one comes upon a table full of hotel silver to the right and old-fashioned mirrors. Other collections throughout the 3,000-square-foot space include vintage glass bottles, silver cocktail shakers and ironstone dishes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/garden/12DECOR/12DECOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/garden/12DECOR/12DECOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge