'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef0da36-cd5a-59d8-bd57-5e34ca8b7e3c', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef0da36-cd5a-59d8-bd57-5e34ca8b7e3c'}, {'abstract': 'Loud prints work well on bikinis; a global fashion website focuses on Brazil during the World Cup; a tote features a rescue dog helping other pups in need; and more shopping news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/fashion/Prints-Bikinis-Tote-That-Helps-Rescue-Puppies-Clyde-visor-Shop-Latitude-.html', 'snippet': 'Loud prints work well on bikinis; a global fashion website focuses on Brazil during the World Cup; a tote features a rescue dog helping other pups in need; and more shopping news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given the season’s giddy profusion of prints — the tribal patterns, the splashy botanicals, the retro blooms — it follows that they would feel right for swimwear as well. Gabby Sabharwal, the designer of the swimwear label Giejo, a collection made with vintage fabrics, worked with a brush-stroke print after seeing the painterly inspirations on the spring runways. Yodit Eklund, who designs the African surf and beach label Bantu, developed the prints for her collaboration with J. Crew from traditional West African wax cloth patterns. Her color palette was based on 1970s funk and high-life album covers from Africa. Kenzo swimsuits echo the popular fish motifs in its spring collection. And as Ms. Eklund points out, a swimsuit is an easy way to pull off ... well, loud prints. “The surface area of a swimsuit is naturally small, so swimwear is a great opportunity to play with print without a head-to-toe look that might be overwhelming.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':