s will no longer send female adult migrants with children to a makeshift detention center in Nogales and then release them in Arizona, the Homeland security secretary said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/us/policy-will-change-on-young-migrants.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities will no longer send female adult migrants with children to a makeshift detention center in Nogales and then release them in Arizona, the Homeland security secretary said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The border authorities will no longer send female migrants with children to a makeshift detention center in Nogales, Ariz., and then release them in the state, Homeland Security Secretary Jeh Johnson said Wednesday at a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing.\xa0 As of June 1, Mr. Johnson said, unaccompanied children caught crossing the border illegally are being sent to the Nogales center for initial immigration processing, and they will not be released in the state. Gov. Jan Brewer of Arizona had said that she was “disturbed and outraged” when hundreds of women and children were sent by immigration officials on buses to Phoenix and released with no assistance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan Will Change on Young Migrants', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Policy Will Change on Young Border Crossers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeh C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nogales (Ariz)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Secu