inal': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa3f3971-33ec-5702-a64b-5468d37148ea', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa3f3971-33ec-5702-a64b-5468d37148ea'}, {'abstract': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac agreed to resist any speculative deal that would turn the complex into a luxury enclave, Senator Charles E. Schumer said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/nyregion/lenders-enlisted-in-effort-to-preserve-stuyvesant-town-for-the-middle-class.html', 'snippet': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac agreed to resist any speculative deal that would turn the complex into a luxury enclave, Senator Charles E. Schumer said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One month after word circulated that Stuyvesant Town-Peter Cooper Village was for sale, the battle is fully engaged to preserve this increasingly rare oasis for middle-class families in Manhattan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lenders Enlisted in Effort to Preserve Stuyvesant Town for the Middle Class', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lenders Enlisted in Effort to Preserve Stuyvesant Town for the Middle Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stuyvesant Town (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peter Cooper Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Capital Management', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'n