offs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Trophy Is the Biggest Star', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Trophy Is the Biggest Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T02:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/935b3f96-531d-5cc4-9e04-274c57a4ecfa', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/935b3f96-531d-5cc4-9e04-274c57a4ecfa'}, {'abstract': 'The board of Detroit’s general retirement system voted Wednesday to endorse the city’s bankruptcy plan, becoming the latest retiree group to support a so-called grand bargain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/us/michigan-another-retiree-group-agrees-to-pension-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'The board of Detroit’s general retirement system voted Wednesday to endorse the city’s bankruptcy plan, becoming the latest retiree group to support a so-called grand bargain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board of Detroit’s general retirement system voted Wednesday to endorse the city’s bankruptcy plan, becoming the latest retiree group to support a so-called grand bargain that includes outside funding and base pension cuts of 4.5 percent for former municipal workers. Pensioners must vote on the proposal by July 11 and could face steeper reductions if they reject the debt-slimming plan, which is subject to a federal judge’s approval. As part of the bargain, which would also keep a city-owned art collection off the auction block, two national foundations committed a combined $13 million to the Detroit Institute of Arts, the museum announced Wednesday. This week, automakers made a $26 million pledge. The artwork has been targeted by some creditors as a source of cash. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Another Retiree Group Agrees to Pension Cuts', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Another Retiree Group Agrees to Cuts to Pensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T02:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/527f0829-634f-5154-afb7-7d13ae4fafb0', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/527f0829-634f-5154-afb7-7d13ae4fafb0'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court in Atlanta on Wednesday ruled that the Fourth Amendment protects information about people’s locations based on the cell towers their mobile phones are using.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/us/court-requires-warrants-for-tracking-locations-by-cellphone.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court in Atlanta on Wednesday ruled that the Fourth Amendment protects information about people’s locations based on the cell towers their mobile phones are using.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a groundbreaking case, a federal appeals court in Atlanta on Wednesday ruled that the Fourth Amendment protects information about people’s locations based on the cell towers their mobile phones are using. The ruling means investigators must get judicial warrants to obtain cell site data about someone. It builds on a ruling by the Supreme Court in 2012 finding that the police needed a warrant to attach a GPS device to a suspect’s car. While the court held that investigators should have obtained a warrant to get his locational data, it declined to overturn his conviction because the legal principle was not yet clear at the time of the investigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Requires Warrants for Tracking Locations by Cellphone', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Requires Warrants for Tracking Locations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T02:45:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2379a82c-4e25-530e-ae0b-21623360b14c', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2379a82c-4e25-530e-ae0b-21623360b14c'}, {'abstract': 'The moves are in reaction to the accidental revelation last month of the Central Intelligence Agency’s top spy in Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/world/white-house-outlines-steps-to-protect-covert-identities.html', 'snippet': 'The moves are in reaction to the accidental revelation last month of the Central Intelligence Agency’s top spy in Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House on Wednesday outlined the steps it would take to prevent the disclosure of covert officials’ identities when the president is traveling abroad. The moves are in reaction to the accidental revelation last month of the Central Intelligence Agency’s top spy in Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Outlines Steps to Protect Covert Identities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White House Outlines Steps to Protect Covert Identities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T02:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7755ca4-e16f-572f-89c4-5ab82181f280', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7755ca4-e16f-572f-89c4-5ab82181f280'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, who is accused in last year’s marathon bombings, filed court documents on Wednesday saying that they want their client’s trial moved out of Boston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/us/massachusetts-venue-change-is-sought-in-marathon-case.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, who is accused in last year’s marathon bombings, filed court documents on Wednesday saying that they want their client’s trial moved out of Boston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, who is accused in last year’s marathon bombings, filed court documents on Wednesday saying that they want their client’s trial moved out of Boston. The lawyers did not say why they were seeking a new location, but indicated that they were trying to spare Mr. Tsarnaev the death penalty. In early court filings, Mr. Tsarnaev’s lawyers have referred to Boston’s news media coverage of the bombings, suggesting that the pretrial publicity there would prevent Mr. Tsarnaev from receiving a fair trial. If the court grants the move, the trial could still be held in Massachusetts, avoiding the intense feelings in Boston while benefiting from the state’s general anti-death-penalty tilt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Venue Change Is Sought in Marathon Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Venue Change Is Sought in Marathon Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T02:57:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dc5f54b-0977-5fba-b5a4-0a2020fa7017', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dc5f54b-0977-5fba-b5a4-0a2020fa7017'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob deGrom, the Mets’ rookie starting pitcher, pitched six innings in his third loss of the season, with the Mets managing just two hits over the final four innings against the Brewers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/sports/baseball/familiar-course-to-defeat-for-jacob-degrom.html', 'snippet': 'Jacob deGrom, the Mets’ rookie starting pitcher, pitched six innings in his third loss of the season, with the Mets managing just two hits over the final four innings against the Brewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season, when Matt Harvey pitched a brilliant game and was ultimately let down by his offense, he often recited the same message. He said that his job was to pitch as well as he could, to give his offense a chance, and that he could do nothing more than that. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/sports/12mets1/12mets1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro