tless attack on Wednesday, Los Angeles was denied the Stanley Cup in its first opportunity to close out the Rangers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/sports/hockey/kings-head-home-empty-handed-but-hoping-for-redemption.html', 'snippet': 'Despite its relentless attack on Wednesday, Los Angeles was denied the Stanley Cup in its first opportunity to close out the Rangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Kings entered Madison Square Garden on Wednesday night needing one victory to clinch their second Stanley Cup in three years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kings Head Home Empty-Handed but Hoping for Redemption', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kings Head Home Empty-Handed but Hoping for Redemption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kopitar, Anze', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Dustin (Ice Hockey)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T05:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kreda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96d7fe65-500c-5aa8-aa9f-9e9002ecfef1', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96d7fe65-500c-5aa8-aa9f-9e9002ecfef1'}, {'abstract': 'A new report says that President Xi Jinping is torn between ambitions to have China exert power over Asia and a desire for peace in the region so he can focus on domestic priorities.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/xi-of-two-minds-be-a-good-neighbor-or-assert-chinas-power/', 'snippet': 'A new report says that President Xi Jinping is torn between ambitions to have China exert power over Asia and a desire for peace in the region so he can focus on domestic priorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re sometimes discombobulated by China’s foreign policy gyrations, there may be some consolation in knowing that so, apparently, is President Xi Jinping. A new report argues that China’s external strategy under him remains an unstable compound of impulses: swelling ambitions that China will use its growing economic and military power to subdue rivals versus a longstanding desire for a stable, benign regional setting so that the ruling Communist Party can tend to domestic priorities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/world/12sino-FOREIGN/12sino-FOREIGN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Xi of Two Minds: Be a Good Neighbor, or Assert China’s Power?', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Strategic and International Studies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Confucius Institutes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T05:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':