ing players financially.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAKLAND, Calif. — Three days into a federal antitrust trial involving the N.C.A.A., the key witness has been Roger Noll, a 74-year-old economics professor emeritus at Stanford. His studies and theories form much of the basis for the allegation that the N.C.A.A. has engaged in price fixing by systematically depriving players a piece of lucrative broadcast and video-game contracts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Testimony Against N.C.A.A., Economics Professor Suggests Players Should Be Paid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Testimony Against N.C.A.A., Economics Professor Suggests Players Should Be Paid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T06:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6776d07-166b-5e98-bab1-614347e809b3', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6776d07-166b-5e98-bab1-614347e809b3'}, {'abstract': 'Masahiro Tanaka pitched a complete game, lowering his earned run average to 2.02, the fourth-best mark in the majors, and Mark Teixeira supported him with a three-run homer.', 'web_url': '