one calls, taxpayer-funded campaigns, sex-trafficking laws and Middle East militants.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The forces of political nihilism not only remain alive and well within the Republican Party, but they are on the rise,” writes The New York Times editorial board. The Times finds the defeat of Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, by David Brat, an upstart “of the distant extremes,” to be both regrettable and disconcerting. For the Republicans of Virginia’s Seventh Congressional District, even Mr. Cantor, “who had been one of the most implacable opponents to the reform of immigration, health care and taxation,” was apparently too moderate. “His crime (in addition to complacent campaigning)? He was occasionally obliged, as a leader, to take a few minimalist steps toward governing, like raising the debt ceiling and ending a ruinous shutdown.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T10:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4c917c-7e13-5e7d-917e-632a24941c01', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4c917c-7e13-5e7d-917e-632a24941c01'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Adams talks about her life in the restaurant business and the impact of meeting Julia Child.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/women-who-belong-in-the-kitchen-jody-adams/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Adams talks about her life in the restaurant business and the impact of meeting Julia Child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jody Adams remembers her first job as a 25-year-old cook, working directly on the hot line. “I cut myself. I burned myself. I was a mess; I cried,” she said. “But I survived.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Who Belong in the Kitchen: Jody Adams', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Jody', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Child, Julia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T11:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colleen DeBaise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeBaise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cac95fb-3370-5142-83b9-946d20f95a97', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cac95fb-3370-5142-83b9-946d20f95a97'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers often put too much stock in arbitrary thresholds like zero growth, and sometimes adjust their spending accordingly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/upshot/the-economic-damage-of-recession-news.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers often put too much stock in arbitrary thresholds like zero growth, and sometimes adjust their spending accordingly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Real gross domestic product (G.D.P.) in the United States shrank by 1 percent in the first quarter of the year. What made this announcement seem so significant?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Economic Damage of Recession News', 'kicker': 'Everyday Economics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T11:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brendan Nyhan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brendan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nyhan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79efffec-8dd2-543d-961d-aee6e17a838b', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79efffec-8dd2-543d-961d-aee6e17a838b'}, {'abstract': 'The financing round in the start-up, which offers cloud-based software on a subscription basis, is being led by Tiger Global Management and includes Google Capital and Accel Partners.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/freshdesk-raises-31-million-for-customer-support-software/', 'snippet': 'The financing round in the start-up, which offers cloud-based software on a subscription basis, is being led by Tiger Global Management and includes Google Capital and Accel Partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stock market investors have rallied around Zendesk, a customer service software company that went public last month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freshdesk Raises $31 Million for Customer Support Software', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':