ite saying that his doctors have advised him to slow down, and that he will therefore give up his directorship of the Munich Philharmonic. He also said he would not take any professional engagements during the 2014-15 season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maazel to Slow Down, on Doctors’ Orders', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maazel to Slow Down On Doctors’ Orders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maazel, Lorin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T15:23:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72f1b3a-fbd7-5cee-906b-5e1427a73298', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72f1b3a-fbd7-5cee-906b-5e1427a73298'}, {'abstract': 'The Interval, opening this month in the Fort Mason Center, features a library, an ambient soundtrack created by Brian Eno and, later this year, two robots.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/interval-robot-bar-san-francisco-brian-eno/', 'snippet': 'The Interval, opening this month in the Fort Mason Center, features a library, an ambient soundtrack created by Brian Eno and, later this year, two robots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since merriment sometimes just isn’t enough, the Interval, a Mensa-courting bar that opens this month in the Fort Mason Center, also offers a library stacked with 1,000 literary masterworks and reference books, an ambient soundtrack created by Brian Eno and, later this year, two robots: One will make drinks, while the other will write predictions about the future on the space’s massive chalkboard. Conceived by the San Francisco-based collective the Long Now Foundation — whose board of directors includes Eno and the Whole Earth Catalog creator Stewart Brand — the Interval will also host regular salons for cerebral scenesters. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-look-interval2/15culture-look-interval2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-look-interval2/15culture-look-interval2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-look-interval2/15culture-look-interval2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-look-interval2/15culture-look-interval2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-look-interval2/15culture-look-interval2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | A Techno-Utopian Bar in San Francisco for Those Who Like to Think While They Drink', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Now Booking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eno, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Long Now Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T15:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Freeman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96f35c18-f8d0-54f1-ac3e-3531298e8a76', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96f35c18-f8d0-54f1-ac3e-3531298e8a76'}, {'abstract': 'As colleges come under intense pressure to curb sexual assault, binge drinking and hazing, they are increasingly looking at their fraternities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/education/fraternities-are-focus-of-measures-to-reduce-assaults-and-misconduct.html', 'snippet': 'As colleges come under intense pressure to curb sexual assault, binge drinking and hazing, they are increasingly looking at their fraternities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVANSTON, Ill. — At the University of Tennessee this year, some fraternity pledges had hot sauce poured on their genitals. At Emory in Atlanta, pledges were required to consume items “not typical for eating” and to engage in fistfights. And at Wesleyan in Connecticut, a few months after the university reached a settlement with a woman who said she was raped at a fraternity house, another woman said that she was raped at a different fraternity house.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/SUB-FRATERNITIES/SUB-FRATERNITIES-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Efforts by Colleges to Curb Assaults Focus on Fraternities ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Efforts by Colleges to Curb Assaults Focus on Fraternities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fraternities and Sororities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's