7'}, {'abstract': 'The direct damage looks manageable, but confidence in the country’s giant credit system has eroded, writes John Foley of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/missing-collateral-a-sign-of-weakness-in-chinas-financing-chains/', 'snippet': 'The direct damage looks manageable, but confidence in the country’s giant credit system has eroded, writes John Foley of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Faith in metal-backed lending in China is corroding – and so is confidence in the country’s giant credit system. Authorities and banks, including Standard Chartered and Citic, are investigating whether traders at Qingdao port used the same lot of copper and aluminum to back multiple loans. Vanishing collateral isn’t a new problem, but could prove to be China’s weakest link.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/dbpix-commodities3/dbpix-commodities3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/business/dbpix-commodities3/dbpix-commodities3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/dbpix-commodities3/dbpix-commodities3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/dbpix-commodities3/dbpix-commodities3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/business/dbpix-commodities3/dbpix-commodities3-thumbStandard.jpg', '