l Over Juice Claim, Court Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pomegranates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pom Wonderful', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T16:21:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3cc4932-3b63-5471-8585-552a22c3afb8', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3cc4932-3b63-5471-8585-552a22c3afb8'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of the 10 funniest, cleverest, most caustic zingers written by the late fashion icon during her lifetime.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/in-her-words-elizabeth-hawes-on-fashion-and-style/', 'snippet': 'A selection of the 10 funniest, cleverest, most caustic zingers written by the late fashion icon during her lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For T’s culture issue, out this Sunday, Alice Gregory wrote about “The Most Brilliant American Fashion Designer”: Elizabeth Hawes, the writer, designer and feminist who passed away in 1971. Throughout her career, Hawes offered an honest, often funny appraisal of the fashion world as it was and as she thought it should be. She was a proponent of using style to get what you want (and, essentially, to become who you want to be), and a wicked critic. While researching the piece, Gregory amassed a collection of Hawes’s wittiest one-liners from her nine books. Here, she lists her 10 favorite quips from the most important woman in fashion you’ve never heard of.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 209, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 209}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/t-magazine/15culture-well-hawes-books/15culture-well-hawes-books-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Her Words | Elizabeth Hawes on Fa