screen/', 'snippet': 'Cathy Lang Ho, who is putting on an exhibition about citizen-initiated use of public space, is the motivating force behind giving soccer fans the chance to watch games in that outdoor setting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In New York City, there is no shortage of places to catch a World Cup match. In addition to the bars and saloons where soccer fans gather on a regular basis, hotels are opening rooftops for viewings; big screens are being erected in Dumbo, Brooklyn, and on 46th Street in Manhattan’s Little Brazil; and normally staid restaurants are being converted into arenas for the faithful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Cup Comes to Governors Island, via the Big Screen', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ho, Cathy Lang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Governors Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T17:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b20fe7b-c81c-5dcc-9bee-e84921d64afe', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b20fe7b-c81c-5dcc-9bee-e84921d64afe'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Vásquez, a Colombian novelist, is the first South American writer to win the lucrative award.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/juan-gabriel-vasquez-wins-international-impac-dublin-literary-award/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Vásquez, a Colombian novelist, is the first South American writer to win the lucrative award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Colombian novelist Juan Gabriel Vásquez on Thursday became the first South American writer to win the lucrative International Impac Dublin Literary Award, for “The Sound of Things Falling” (Riverhead Books).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 891}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1379, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/books/12vasquez/12vasquez-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juan