ne}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d09bc31c-a494-5b3f-9f12-cc5ce0c4962d', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d09bc31c-a494-5b3f-9f12-cc5ce0c4962d'}, {'abstract': 'The most uplifting moment in one woman’s life collides with the most wrenching time in another family’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/a-wedding-and-a-funeral/', 'snippet': 'The most uplifting moment in one woman’s life collides with the most wrenching time in another family’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tears spill from the eyes of Maung Tin May. This is supposed to be the happiest day of her life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wedding and a Funeral', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T18:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Sganga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sganga', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b844ed9-78ec-52c6-b800-a1233bc7533d', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b844ed9-78ec-52c6-b800-a1233bc7533d'}, {'abstract': 'I think of summer as a happy time of year—which is why I’m annually blindsided by the small sorrows of graduations and change.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/kids-and-parents-happy-to-move-up-sad-to-say-goodbye/', 'snippet': 'I think of summer as a happy time of year—which is why I’m annually blindsided by the small sorrows of graduations and change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This morning was the “step-up” ceremony at my children’s school. It’s the fifth time I’ve attended this same event (it’s a K-8 school) and it always follows the same leisurely pattern: acknowledging the teachers; various presentations; songs from each of the different music classes; speeches from the fifth graders who are moving on to middle school; and a class gift from the graduating eighth grade (that had a separate graduation ceremony the day before). There is no pomp and circumstance, there are no flat hats. It’s a pleasant, charming way of acknowledging the passing of another year and the inevitable forward movement of children. And the first time I attended, I felt like chewing my own arm off to escape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 997, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/us/motherlode-cartwheels/motherlode-cartwheels-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids and Parents: Happy to Move Up, Sad to Say Goodbye', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T19:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b2966ec-54e4-592a-8ce0-5b63cb0219ba', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b2966ec-54e4-592a-8ce0-5b63cb0219ba'}, {'abstract': 'In the end, it’s the result that everyone expected, but not before Croatia scared Brazilian fans everywhere with a shock 1-0 lead.', 'web_url': 'https://sports.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/brazil-vs-croatia-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'In the end, it’s the result that everyone expected, but not before Croatia scared Brazilian fans everywhere with a shock 1-0 lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, it’s the result that everyone expected, but not before Croatia scared Brazilian fans everywhere with a shock 1-0 lead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/sports/12BC2/12BC2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/sports/12BC2/12BC2-article