 '_id': 'nyt://article/5a8e9d96-7329-5b2c-a93b-1023d16518ab', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a8e9d96-7329-5b2c-a93b-1023d16518ab'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters in Brazil accused the police of using excessive force against a demonstration in São Paulo on Thursday, ahead of the World Cup kickoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/world/americas/police-tactics-under-increased-scrutiny-at-world-cup.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters in Brazil accused the police of using excessive force against a demonstration in São Paulo on Thursday, ahead of the World Cup kickoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protesters in Brazil accused the police of using excessive force to prevent a small group of demonstrators opposed to what they call lavish spending on the World Cup from reaching the stadium in São Paulo where the tournament began on Thursday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Tactics Under Increased Scrutiny at World Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T20:23:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74256336-94cc-585f-9eab-7af2f2b4a47a', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74256336-94cc-585f-9eab-7af2f2b4a47a'}, {'abstract': 'Some readers argue that calling some books good and others merely fun oversimplifies the joys of reading, ANNA NORTH writes.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/defending-guilty-pleasures/', 'snippet': 'Some readers argue that calling some books good and others merely fun oversimplifies the joys of reading, ANNA NORTH writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Should we feel bad about reading for fun? A Slate critique of young-adult fiction last week had readers answering mostly in the negative. But beyond any specific genre, there may be a larger conversation to be had about which books are good, which books are fun, and whether there needs to be a difference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending ‘Guilty Pleasures’', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T20:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d852578c-e3bc-59b0-96f0-6c2f2e0c399e', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d852578c-e3bc-59b0-96f0-6c2f2e0c399e'}, {'abstract': 'The online-only basics brand is opening a temporary store, which will host food-oriented events and provide detailed information about the origins of its products.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/in-store-everlane-pops-up-in-soho/', 'snippet': 'The online-only basics brand is opening a temporary store, which will host food-oriented events and provide detailed information about the origins of its products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2011, the online-only basics brand Everlane\xa0has, with its motto of “radical transparency,” encouraged consumers to ask where and how their clothes are made — and how much they are marked up\xa0(which in Everlane’s case is a fraction of the usual amount).\xa0Starting tomorrow, shoppers will have the chance to sample the brand’s understated (and, compared to similar offerings, underpriced) staples in person at a SoHo pop-up. And though it’s not Everlane’s first appearance in New York, it’s by far its largest and most social outing. Called “Open House,” the space, which operates through June 28, will host catered events with other transparency-minded organizations from the food world, such as Gather Journal and Edible Schoolyard NYC. Every garment and accessory sold in the store — whose perforated-plywood interiors come courtesy of the Isa restauranteur Taavo Somer’s creative agency, Friends and Family —\xa0will be sold alongside an infographic detailing its origin story.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/12/t-magazine/12everlane-ortved/12everlane-ortved-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | Everlane Pops Up in SoHo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where It Starts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T20:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Ortved', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ortved', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9852bb42-19ba-5561-8648-50412f81e674', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9852bb42-19ba-5561-8648-50412f81e674'}, {'abstract': 'As he winds his way to the World Cup, the Frugal Traveler stops in Suriname, where he travels in the interior by boat, and experiences a chaotic slice of the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/12/travel/getting-to-the-heart-of-suriname.html', 'snippet': 'As he winds his way to the World Cup, the Frugal Traveler stops in Suriname, where he travels in the interior by boat, and experiences a chaotic slice of the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Tiapoe pointed out two mature trees just a few feet apart amid the dense jungle vegetation. “When you see 