ests won out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/realestate/the-vanderbilts-and-their-battle-over-fifth-avenue.html', 'snippet': 'The Vanderbilts tried to keep their section of Fifth Avenue residential, but commercial interests won out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dowdy loft building at the northeast corner of Fifth Avenue and 52nd Street is about as blank as a building can get, just limestone and windows. But it sent the Vanderbilt family over the edge, the symbol of their defeat after years of attempts to preserve the residential sanctity of this stretch of New York’s most famous address. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/realestate/15SCAPES/15SCAPES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'