ce is sinking — literally under rising sea levels, and figuratively beneath the weight of day-tripping tourists. But these obstacles have not hindered this beguiling city from establishing itself over the past decade as the pre-eminent place in Italy for contemporary art. More recently, a wave of high-end hotels has opened along the Grand Canal, and back alleys have been set abuzz with new nightspots and a revived restaurant scene. So leave the famous sights to the crowds and instead drink up the less overt charms of this watery wonderland.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1836, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/travel/15-hours-top-sf/15-hours-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Venice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Venice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Ingrid K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-12T23:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ingrid K. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingrid', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a327dbc-3a28-5d87-8fe0-1fcb2518de0d', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a327dbc-3a28-5d87-8fe0-1fcb2518de0d'}, {'abstract': '“Test,” a drama centering on a dancer in San Francisco, recalls a period of intense anxiety in the mid-1980s as gay men waited to learn whether they were H.I.V. positive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/movies/test-set-in-the-year-hiv-screening-arrived.html', 'snippet': '“Test,” a drama centering on a dancer in San Francisco, recalls a period of intense anxiety in the mid-1980s as gay men waited to learn whether they were H.I.V. positive.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Test,” set in San Francisco in 1985, captures with extraordinary precision and sensitivity the moment when an H.I.V. test became available, and the city’s gay men faced the daunting prospect of finding out their status. In those scary days, there was no pharmaceutical regimen that could arrest the disease. And as one man, looking ahead to a future of sexual self-discipline, puts it, “