n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f191496-87ca-5d78-90e3-f4a564fdb13f', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f191496-87ca-5d78-90e3-f4a564fdb13f'}, {'abstract': 'The new expansion plan isn’t right for the small museum in a mansion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/opinion/david-masello-save-the-frick-collection.html', 'snippet': 'The new expansion plan isn’t right for the small museum in a mansion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICA has few mansions built by a family with an art collection they meant to share with the public. So when word came this week that the Frick Collection, on the Upper East Side of Manhattan, was planning to\xa0expand and build a six-story addition where there is now a discreet garden and a splashing fountain with lily pads — one of those few places in the cityscape where we are allowed to stop and breathe — I felt blunt disappointment, as well as betrayal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/opinion/0613OPEDbiskup/0613OPEDbiskup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1786, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/opinion/0613OPEDbiskup/0613OPEDbiskup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1786}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/opinion/0613OPEDbiskup/0613OPEDbiskup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 344, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/opinion/0613OPEDbiskup/0613OPEDbiskup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ