p if it is taken away from Qatar.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Denies Talk on 2022 World Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Denies Talk on ’22 World Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2022 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulati, Sunil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7a0c1b9-3092-50c1-960f-7917f225447a', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7a0c1b9-3092-50c1-960f-7917f225447a'}, {'abstract': 'Cellphone tracking cannot be allowed to trample the Fourth Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/opinion/cellphone-tracking-cannot-trample-the-fourth-amendment.html', 'snippet': 'Cellphone tracking cannot be allowed to trample the Fourth Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The capacity of cellphones to track people’s movements and provide a vivid picture of their private lives poses a substantial and growing threat to privacy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Good Ruling on Privacy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Good Ruling on Privacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce77dabf-17a2-5e22-8463-50792266c9a7', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce77dabf-17a2-5e22-8463-50792266c9a7'}, {'abstract': 'A deal to save the struggling city of Bayonne, N.J., was a good deal for Gov. Chris Christie, but not for the bistate authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/opinion/saving-bayonne-was-a-good-deal-for-chris-christie.html', 'snippet': 'A deal to save the struggling city of Bayonne, N.J., was a good deal for Gov. Chris Christie, but not for the bistate authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The purchase of 131 acres along the waterfront of Bayonne, N.J., in 2010 was a fabulous bargain for the seller, the struggling city of Bayonne, and a windfall for New Jersey’s governor, Chris Christie. It was not such a good deal for the buyer — the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Port Authority Is Fooled Again', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Port Authority Is Fooled Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bayonne (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a7e2f24-f2da-5b03-92eb-fabb955e5a4d', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a7e2f24-f2da-5b03-92eb-fabb955e5a4d'}, {'abstract': 'It is up to Iraq to show leadership in the face of recent insurgent victories. The United States cannot be sucked into another round of war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/opinion/prime-minister-maliki-panics-as-insurgents-gain.html', 'snippet': 'It is up to Iraq to show leadership in the face of recent insurgent victories. The United States cannot be sucked into another round of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s happening in Iraq is a disaster and it is astonishing that the Iraqis and the Americans, who have been sharing intelligence, seem to have been caught flat-footed by the speed of the insurgent victories and the army defections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq in Peril', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq in Peril', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4deb2c54-848c-5197-a36e-1671f274a328', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4deb2c54-848c-5197-a36e-1671f274a328'}, {'abstract': 'Unpredictability was expected at Pinehurst, which had been restored to look as it did in the 1930s, but some of the results of Thursday’s first round looked overly retro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/sports/golf/us-open-players-struggle-to-adjust-to-pinehursts-different-look.html', 'snippet': 'Unpredictability was expected at Pinehurst, which had been restored to look as it did in the 1930s, but some of the results of Thursday’s first round looked overly retro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PINEHURST, N.C. — Matt Kuchar’s second shot at the 18th hole rolled through the green, sped down an embankment and did not stop until it was in the clubhouse. A Brandt Snedeker bunker shot ricocheted behind him and settled in the woods. Justin Rose came within an inch of a hole in one, but after his ball flirted with the cup, it ended up so far from the hole Rose chose a wood to play his next shot. In a flash, a near ace became a bogey.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/sports/Y-OPEN/Y-OPEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Lot of Oops Moments,’ but the Scores at the U.S. Open Aren’t Too Shabby', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘A Lot of Oops Moments,’ but the Scores Aren’t Too Shabby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinehurst Resort and Country Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Players Championship (Golf)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PGA Championship', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuchar, Matt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDowell, Graeme', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snedeker, Brandt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaymer, Martin', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:16:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b186a6-e5e6-5e70-bf1c-4c34ab6acf98', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b186a6-e5e6-5e70-bf1c-4c34ab6acf98'}, {'abstract': 'The daughter of the screenwriter Roger Towne directs, writes and stars in her own film, “I Am I.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/movies/i-am-i-stars-jocelyn-towne-and-kevin-tighe.html', 'snippet': 'The daughter of the screenwriter Roger Towne directs, writes and stars in her own film, “I Am I.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the mini-trend in films about aging parents in decline (“Amour,” “Away From Her,” the recent “Grand Départ”), add “I Am I,” a wispy vanity project for the writer-director-actress Jocelyn Towne. Rachael (Ms. Towne) is at her mother’s funeral when she encounters Gene (Kevin Tighe), her father, who left shortly after Rachael was born. Gene, his memory dimming, has been in a retirement home. When he meets Rachael, he falls under the delusion that she is her mother, for whom he still carries a torch. Rachael, to know him better, eventually decides to play along.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/IAMI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/IAMI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/IAMI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/IAMI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/13IAMI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/13IAMI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13IAMI/13IAMI-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman Is Courted, but the Suitor Is Her Father', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Am I', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tighe, Kevin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'I Am I (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Towne, Jocelyn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T01:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed854bbf-9883-58ef-9483-b507c94002d3', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed854bbf-9883-58ef-9483-b507c94002d3'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Eric Cantor and President Obama never got along, but Mr. Cantor’s primary defeat this week may also mean the defeat for what remains of Mr. Obama’s legislative agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/us/obamas-odds-with-congress-bad-to-worse.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Eric Cantor and President Obama never got along, but Mr. Cantor’s primary defeat this week may also mean the defeat for what remains of Mr. Obama’s legislative agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One day in April, President Obama called Representative Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, to wish him a happy Passover. However the call started, it went downhill from there. By day’s end, both sides were arguing about what was said and taking shots at the other for not getting along.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/us/JP-OBAMA/JP-OBAMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge',