a sale. | Hostile deal-making is back. | Oppenheimer’s emerging markets fund has outperformed its peers since 2010. | Sycamore takes aim at Express.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/morning-agenda-univisions-sale-talks/', 'snippet': 'Univision’s owners are considering a sale. | Hostile deal-making is back. | Oppenheimer’s emerging markets fund has outperformed its peers since 2010. | Sycamore takes aim at Express.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIVISION OWNERS SAID TO WEIGH A SALE \xa0|\xa0 The owners of Univision Communications, the biggest Spanish-language broadcaster in the United States, are said to have held preliminary talks about a potential sale with media companies in recent weeks, including CBS, Time Warner and Viacom, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. The talks were at a very early stage and no sales process is underway at the moment. Should Univision’s owners ‒ a consortium led by the billionaire Haim Saban ‒ pursue a sale, they will probably expect bids to top at least $20 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Univision’s Sale Talks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T11:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76ee3f5-6af7-5d7e-bcfc-aa8f42c6be51', 'word_count': 1711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76ee3f5-6af7-5d7e-bcfc-aa8f42c6be51'}, {'abstract': 'Jan Troell’s latest film, “The Last Sentence,” is a portrait of Torgny Segerstedt, a Swedish newspaper editor who was an early, ferocious and persistent critic of Hitler.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/movies/jan-troell8217s-film-8216the-last-sentence8217-looks-at-a-swedish-editor-who-defied-nazi-threats.html', 'snippet': 'Jan Troell’s latest film, “The Last Sentence,” is a portrait of Torgny Segerstedt, a Swedish newspaper editor who was an early, ferocious and persistent critic of Hitler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From “High Noon” to “Silkwood” and “The Insider,” the courageous loner who stands up to evil at great personal risk is a familiar film figure. Now the Swedish master Jan Troell has added to that gallery with “The Last Sentence,” his portrait of Torgny Segerstedt, a Swedish newspaper editor who was an early, ferocious and persistent critic of Hitler, defying both Nazi threats and his own government’s pleas not to undermine its neutral stance.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15TROELL1/15TROELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15TROELL1/15TROELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15TROELL1/15TROELL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15TROELL1/15TROELL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15TROELL1/15TROELL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014