15-277e-524b-9530-3ea35051c893'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since 2009, the number of short-term unemployed workers has surpassed the number of long-term unemployed workers — a sign of demand in the job market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/business/economy/Growth-in-US-Job-Market.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time since 2009, the number of short-term unemployed workers has surpassed the number of long-term unemployed workers — a sign of demand in the job market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR more than 60 years, unemployment in the United States was largely a short-term problem. The level of unemployment went up and down, but most of the unemployed found work relatively quickly. Few remained out of work for as long as 15 weeks. Long-term unemployment was always a lesser problem.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indications of Growth in U.S. Job Market', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Handful of Indicators Showing Growth on the Jobs Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T12:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed61fb27-8349-58a8-826c-f8b822e282c5', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed61fb27-8349-58a8-826c-f8b822e282c5'}, {'abstract': 'Remarks by Britain’s chancellor of the Exchequer, George Osborne, on addressing market manipulation in currency trading gives greater clarity to the banking sector, write two Nasdaq OMX executives.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/a-step-forward-for-foreign-exchange-oversight/', 'snippet': 'Remarks by Britain’s chancellor of the Exchequer, George Osborne, on addressing market manipulation in currency trading gives greater clarity to the banking sector, write two Nasdaq OMX executives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael O’Brien and Bill Nosal are senior executives with Nasdaq OMX’s SMARTS market surveillance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Regulator Osborne Takes a Step Forward for Foreign Exchange Oversight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T12:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': "By Michael O'Brien and Bill Nosal", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nosal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93fee2ea-471b-5ae5-99a3-1b9792a8e37d', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93fee2ea-471b-5ae5-99a3-1b9792a8e37d'}, {'abstract': 'David Greig’s play about the aftermath of a mass shooting, “The Events,” will use local choirs in its American debut this month in New Haven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/theater/david-greigs-the-events-is-coming-to-new-haven.html', 'snippet': 'David Greig’s play about the aftermath of a mass shooting, “The Events,” will use local choirs in its American debut this month in New Haven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Scottish playwright David Greig was hard to pin down while traveling in the highlands of his homeland recently, so it turned out to be eerily coincidental that we finally spoke the day after Elliot O. Rodger went on a murderous rampage in Isla Vista, Calif. Efforts to understand what motivated the young man were popping up all over the Internet as Mr. Greig discussed “The Events,” his 2013 play about the anguished aftermath of a deadly shooting. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15events3/15events3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {