s Saturday in the city’s Midtown district.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/willys-detroit-new-multibrand-concept-boutique/', 'snippet': 'Willys, a new lifestyle store featuring four U.S.-based, made-largely-in-America brands — Steven Alan, Filson, Clare V. and Mollusk — opens Saturday in the city’s Midtown district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the most visible new success story in the ongoing effort to revitalize Detroit’s economy is Shinola\xa0—\xa0the three-year-old leather goods and lifestyle brand which employs more than 130 people at its bicycle and watch manufacturing facilities there (and some 130 more in its offices and retail operations). Now, a couple of doors down from its store in the city’s emerging Midtown district, the company is spawning what might be Detroit’s first multibrand concept boutique. Willys, which opens to the public on Saturday, takes its name from the Willys Overland Motor Company, which invented the first jeep in 1941 and was for a time during the 1910s the second-largest car manufacturer in the U.S.; the 2,900-square-foot space is housed in the former service bay of the company’s old headquarters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13willys-hartman/13willys-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | A New Multibrand Concept Boutique in Detroit', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T15:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1558315d-f8c2-5163-b569-7295650e3e7c', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1558315d-f8c2-5163-b569-7295650e3e7c'}, {'abstract': 'In Thursday’s Game 4 of the N.B.A. finals, the Heat’s offense was dispirited and disorganized, and their defense invariably left open a member of the Spurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/sports/basketball/the-miami-heat-dispirited-and-disorganized-in-loss-to-san-antonio-spurs.html', 'snippet': 'In Thursday’s Game 4 of the N.B.A. finals, the Heat’s offense was dispirited and disorganized, and their defense invariably left open a member of the Spurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Toward the end of the third quarter of Game 4 of the N.B.A. finals Thursday, an intensely generic D.J. began exhorting the crowd in the Miami Heat’s arena to get loud. In the stands, a few women with bare midriffs stood up and randomly started shaking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 549, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 549}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1169, 'width': 1277, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/sports/CITY-POWELL-1/CITY-POWELL-1-