4-06-13T15:29:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellery Washington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Washington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a04d42d1-a8c6-5f89-b728-066b04ac36b2', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a04d42d1-a8c6-5f89-b728-066b04ac36b2'}, {'abstract': 'In Michel Déon’s 1975 bildungsroman, a young Frenchman sets off to discover the Continent between the two world wars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/books/review/the-foundling-boy-by-michel-deon.html', 'snippet': 'In Michel Déon’s 1975 bildungsroman, a young Frenchman sets off to discover the Continent between the two world wars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michel Déon’s 1975 novel “The Foundling Boy” (in French “Le Jeune Homme Vert,” or “The Green Young Man”) is a bildungsroman, an account of a naïve young person’s education and the formation of his character, in this case inspired by Henry Fielding’s 18th-century novel “Tom Jones,” about a similarly clueless but likable character making his way on the road of life. As witty as its English forebear but with French savoir-faire, “The Foundling Boy” may win new readers for books translated from French, of which too few are published. English PEN and Arts Council England have supported Julian Evans’s translation, evidently in hopes of broadening our reading of these classics.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 494}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 991, 'width': 1204, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/books/review/15JOHNSON/15JOHNSON-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Pastoral', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Pastoral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Diane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deon, Michel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Julian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T15:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qual