ure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T16:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/41a0f5cd-87f8-5d85-bc9a-637164ac5a19', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/41a0f5cd-87f8-5d85-bc9a-637164ac5a19'}, {'abstract': 'Entertainment options for almost everyone.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/five-things-to-do-this-weekend/', 'snippet': 'Entertainment options for almost everyone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are a lot of cultural options out there. Too many to choose from? Perhaps. So below we’ve winnowed them all down to a few, for brows of all kinds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1278, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/arts/13SPAREKIDS2/13SPAREKIDS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Things to Do This Weekend', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T16:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01a0bc72-77b9-5bad-8bb3-ce508c38687f', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01a0bc72-77b9-5bad-8bb3-ce508c38687f'}, {'abstract': 'The actress Zosia Mamet strikes a pose – a whole lot of them, in fact – while recreating images from fashion catalogs and magazines.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/zosia-mamet-poses-leanne-shapton-women-in-clothes-book/', 'snippet': 'The actress Zosia Mamet strikes a pose – a whole lot of them, in fact – while recreating images from fashion catalogs and magazines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after the Canadian-born artist Leanne Shapton ordered a nightgown from the Vermont Country Store last year, she began to receive mail-order catalogs from National (their tagline: “Living the comfortable life since 1952″) and Woman Within. Struck by the models’ demure stances, she cut out certain images, before turning to her own fashion magazines and other periodicals. Last September, she asked Zosia Mamet to imitate the poses she had collected; the photographer Gus Powell shot. “Posturing” — inspired by the grids of the German artist Hans-Peter Feldmann, illustrated workouts and 1970s yoga manuals (hence the unitard) — is one of the many projects in “Women in Clothes,” out this fall. Edited by Sheila Heti, Heidi Julavits and Shapton, the book explores the issues women face when they get dressed. According to Shapton, the photo series evokes the energetic, experimental spirit of the publication, which features over 600 contributors. “We wanted the reader to do exercises,” Shapton said. “Exercises for the critical eye.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '118', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Document | Act Natural', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Act Natural', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heti, Sheila', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, Zosia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shapton, Leanne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T16:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Stokes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stokes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbde9219-70ed-5f6d-92e6-f81b39df59bc', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbde9219-70ed-5f6d-92e6-f81b39df59bc'}, {'abstract': 'It’s no fun leading a caucus that resembles a raucous playground.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/kevin-mccarthy-wont-enjoy-being-majority-leader/', 'snippet': 'It’s no fun leading a caucus that resembles a raucous playground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin McCarthy of California, the House Republican Whip, is running hard to win Eric Cantor’s post as Majority Leader, and claims he has the votes locked up. But except for the big office — and the security detail, and the power and the glory — it’s hard to know why he really wants the job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kevin McCarthy Won’t Enjoy Being Majority Leader', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Control Act (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Kevin (1965- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T16:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46dcc491-577c-5bc0-8a32-2facb718f345', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46dcc491-577c-5bc0-8a32-2facb718f345'}, {'abstract': 'Because of low inventory in many markets, buyers will need to be strategic in how they present their offers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/realestate/winning-a-real-estate-bidding-war.html', 'snippet': 'Because of low inventory in many markets, buyers will need to be strategic in how they present their offers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The low supply of homes for sale in many markets means buyers must be prepared for bidding wars. Buyers should be strategic in how they present thei