s of normal life happening despite it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/nyregion/stayin-alive.html', 'snippet': 'Meryl Meisler wasn’t interested in capturing the urban decay of Bushwick, Brooklyn, in the 1980s so much as she was the signs of normal life happening despite it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meryl Meisler couldn’t believe the sight that greeted her when she emerged from the subway in Bushwick, Brooklyn, for the first time, in 1981. “It looked like the photographs that I had seen of Beirut,” she recalled of the cityscape of bombed-out buildings.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stayin’ Alive', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stayin’ Alive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bushwick (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meisler, Meryl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T17:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Mahler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11289ec0-f086-5f86-ab17-4514d915d32c', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11289ec0-f086-5f86-ab17-4514d915d32c'}, {'abstract': '“Third Person,” a new film written and directed by Paul Haggis, follows several relationships as the examine questions of trust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/movies/paul-haggis-prepares-his-film-third-person-for-release.html', 'snippet': '“Third Person,” a new film written and directed by Paul Haggis, follows several relationships as the examine questions of trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the conclusion of a 2011 New Yorker article on the Church of Scientology, the writer-director Paul Haggis made a prediction regarding his very public break with that institution.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/arts/15HAGGIS1/15HAGGIS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Never Happened, but It’s Still True', 'kicker': None, 'conte