rld will now “pause for a month,” to follow the action in Brazil.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/enter-the-world-cup/', 'snippet': 'The Op-Ed columnist handicaps the national teams as the world will now “pause for a month,” to follow the action in Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world will now pause for a month. It’s the World Cup. Coups and annexations, meltdowns and earthquakes will have to take a back seat to the beautiful game. No other global obsession even comes close. I have been at the last two in South Africa and Germany and came away with glorious memories. Love of the game usually wins out in the end whatever the pretournament grumbling and ugly moments (like Zinedine Zidane’s head butt in the 2006 final).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enter the World Cup', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T17:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7468181-c947-5cd6-9eff-d7cf17bf7e17', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7468181-c947-5cd6-9eff-d7cf17bf7e17'}, {'abstract': 'As Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, exits the scene, several candidates are vying for leadership positions, which may force a change in Republican party politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000002937283/who-to-watch-in-the-gop-shuffle.html', 'snippet': 'As Eric Cantor, the House majority leader, exits the scene, several candidates are vying for leadership positions, which may force a change in Republican party politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Eric Cantor, th