/', 'snippet': 'As President Obama weighs intervention in Iraq, analysts debate the country’s options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As President Obama weighs whether to help defend the Iraqi government against insurgents, analysts around the world are offering their prescriptions (and their sometimes-dire predictions) for a country in the throes of worsening conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq’s Uncertain Future', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T18:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73f4455a-0e16-5123-b9e6-4138703fe5fe', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73f4455a-0e16-5123-b9e6-4138703fe5fe'}, {'abstract': '“I Like You Just The Way I Am: Stories About Me and Some Other People,” the actor’s collection of hilarious autobiographical tales, all started with a handful of online essays that she wrote for Playboy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/jenny-mollen-new-book-of-laughs-talking-talent/', 'snippet': '“I Like You Just The Way I Am: Stories About Me and Some Other People,” the actor’s collection of hilarious autobiographical tales, all started with a handful of online essays that she wrote for Playboy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honest and often painfully embarrassing, Jenny Mollen’s debut book, “I Like You Just The Way I Am: Stories About Me and Some Other People” (St. Martin’s Press), hits bookstores on Tuesday and is poised to be one of the season’s funniest reads. The 35-year-old wife of the actor Jason Biggs and mother to their newborn son, Sid, spent over a decade appearing in barely-there parts on film and television, but found her true calling when she decided to put pen to paper to chronicle her every phobia, sexual encounter and misadventure while stalking her future husband’s exes. With over 125,000 Twitter followers who hang on her acerbic pearls of wisdom — “It’s 10:40, He’s not calling to make plans!” — Mollen, who looks more like a Maxim pinup than a raunchy comedienne, is amassing a devoted legion of fans, one selfie at a time.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/13/t-magazine/13mollen-tabach-1/13mollen-tabach-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 