can ground troops back into the country.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/13/avoiding-another-iraq-quagmire/', 'snippet': 'President Obama on Friday ruled out sending American ground troops back into the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given that he built a political career on opposition to the Iraq war, it was a relief but no surprise when President Obama on Friday ruled out sending American ground troops back into the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avoiding Another Iraq Quagmire', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T20:05:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50b4661b-f455-503a-bde0-2936a7b51b1a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50b4661b-f455-503a-bde0-2936a7b51b1a'}, {'abstract': 'The store’s books — 4,000, perhaps — are organized by subject: bread, sauce, breakfast, etiquette. But Ms. Slotnick also stocks biographies, memoirs and even manuscripts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/nyregion/at-bonnie-slotnick-cookbooks-recipes-to-feed-your-mind-and-body.html', 'snippet': 'The store’s books — 4,000, perhaps — are organized by subject: bread, sauce, breakfast, etiquette. But Ms. Slotnick also stocks biographies, memoirs and even manuscripts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s always a slight sense of dread as you approach West 10th\xa0Street, just off Seventh\xa0Avenue, that you might find Bonnie Slotnick’s vintage cookbook shop closed that day. But if the chipped wooden “Open” sign (she painted it herself) peeks out from the brownstone’s stoop, you’re in luck. Shove open the rickety door and a string of bells will herald your arrival.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Bonnie Slotnick Cookbooks, Recipes to Feed Your Mind and Body', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Recipe Repository', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slotnick, Bonnie J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Slotnick, Bonnie, Cookbooks (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T20:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvie Bigar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bigar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5167eac-9e2e-5c88-88cc-28087041d9ad', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5167eac-9e2e-5c88-88cc-28087041d9ad'}, {'abstract': 'For Mr. Jones, 69, original lead guitarist of the band Foreigner, Sundays can be for soccer, family and probably some shopping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/nyregion/mick-jones-a-quiet-day-for-a-juke-box-hero.html', 'snippet': 'For Mr. Jones, 69, original lead guitarist of the band Foreigner, Sundays can be for soccer, family and probably some shopping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is an amusement of New York life that rock stars live among us, picking up dry cleaning or going to the dentist just like everybody else. And it is a quirk of contemporary rock stardom that its constituents now come in all vintages, with hairstyles and heydays stretching back for decades. So it is that Mick Jones, 69, original lead guitarist of the band Foreigner, has been living near Central Park since the ’70s, long enough that he can say, in the accent of Somerset, England, “I’m really a native New Yorker.” These days he is sometimes eclipsed by his stepchildren and children, who include: the D.J., singer and producer Mark Ronson, 38; the fashion designer Charlotte Ronson, 36; the singer and D.J. Samantha Ronson, 36; and the actress Annabelle Dexter-Jones, 27. Foreigner will perform with Styx and Don Felder at Jones Beach on Long Island on June 28.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mick Jones: A Quiet Day, for a Juke Box Hero', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Quiet Day, for a Juke Box Hero', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Mick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreigner (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-13T20:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07021e23-e84e-51cc-8f18-945d559aab63', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07021e23-e84e-51cc-8f18-945d559aab63'}, {'abstract': 'Frutti di mare rice salad is summer cooking at its best, meant to be enjoyed outside with friends and a bottle of wine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/dining/the-mediterranean-seafood-salad-of-your-dreams.html', 'snippet': 'Frutti di mare rice salad is summer cooking at its best, meant to be enjoyed outside with friends and a bottle of wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer appetites are different, and so is summer cooking. In the morning one craves fresh fruit and little more, but by midday a voracious hun