age of omnipresent monitoring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/arts/dance/surveillance-a-dance-work-at-new-york-live-arts.html', 'snippet': '“Surveillance,” performed by ZviDance at New York Live Arts, considers what remains of intimacy in the age of omnipresent monitoring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who’s watching whom and to what purpose? “Surveillance” — a new 60-minute piece by ZviDance at New York Live Arts this week — is a shrewd collage, both appealing and disconcerting, of the Orwellian Big Brother society, aspects of sexuality and dancing to rock music. It’s the urban world we know, deconstructed and reassembled. In a society in which people need to film or photograph everything, what intimacy is left? Zvi Gotheiner’s choreography suggests that he is as much sociologist as dance-maker.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/arts/14SURVEILLANCE/14SURVEILLANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/14/arts/14SURVEILLANCE/14SURVEILLANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/arts/14SURVEILLANCE/14SURVEILLANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/arts/14SURVEILLANCE/14SURVEILLANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/arts/14SURVEILLANCE/14SURVEILLANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu