: 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/cd1817c8-5347-531a-a596-d55334bf54d1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/cd1817c8-5347-531a-a596-d55334bf54d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Beinecke Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Yale has acquired the papers of the writer and gardener Vita Sackville-West and her husband, Harold Nicolson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/books/beinecke-library-gets-sackville-west-papers.html', 'snippet': 'The Beinecke Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Yale has acquired the papers of the writer and gardener Vita Sackville-West and her husband, Harold Nicolson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Beinecke Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Yale has acquired the papers of the writer and gardener Vita Sackville-West and her husband, Harold Nicolson, a diplomat, novelist and historian. The couple featured prominently in Britain’s literary and political life in the first half of the 20th century and provided their son, Nigel Nicolson, with the subject of his best-selling 1973 biography, “Portrait of a Marriage.” The archives include drafts of lectures, broadcasts and articles (including a manuscript of her 1942 novel, “Grand Canyon”); letters from her parents; letters from close friends and lovers, including Rosamund Grosvenor, Pat Dansey, Geoffrey Scott, Hilda Matheson, Christopher St. John and Gwen St. Aubyn; and diaries and garden journals dating from 1930 to 1962.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beinecke Library Gets Sackville-West Papers', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beinecke Library Gets Sackville-West Papers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript 