ey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3255bca-a2c3-57b4-bb4f-c5327e832475', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3255bca-a2c3-57b4-bb4f-c5327e832475'}, {'abstract': 'Iraq may see the possibility of significant aid from Iran as a means of pressuring the United States to come to Iraq’s defense with aid of its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/world/middleeast/beleaguered-iraqis-court-iranian-mastermind-of-the-shiites-who-fought-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'Iraq may see the possibility of significant aid from Iran as a means of pressuring the United States to come to Iraq’s defense with aid of its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Gen. Qassim Suleimani, the shadowy commander of Iran’s paramilitary Quds Force, flew to Iraq this week with dozens of his officers to advise the country’s beleaguered leadership about how to blunt the advance of militant forces on Baghdad, American officials said Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beleaguered Iraqis Court Iranian Mastermind of the Shiites Who Fought the U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beleaguered Iraqis Court Iranian Mastermind of the Shiites Who Fought the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suleimani, Qassim', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T01:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt, Mark Mazzetti and Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abbd91c5-59b8-53e0-b090-e14fc2b36381', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abbd91c5-59b8-53e0-b090-e14fc2b36381'}, {'abstract': 'A new report lays out a clear road map for preserving order without suspending or expelling students under “zero tolerance” policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/opinion/zero-tolerance-policies-need-to-be-tamed.html', 'snippet': 'A new report lays out a clear road map for preserving order without suspending or expelling students under “zero tolerance” policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “zero tolerance” disciplinary policies that swept through the country’s schools beginning in the 1990s have led to millions of children each year being suspended, expelled and even arrested, mainly for minor misbehavior that would once have been dealt with at the principal’s office. Federal civil rights officials warned this year that these tactics are often used in a discriminatory fashion against black and Latino children, who are at greater risk of being thrown out of school and denied an education. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Approach to School Discipline', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Better Approach to School Discipline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of State Governments Justice Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T01:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e52ece0-cae8-5f5c-94d7-a61586c1e6f0', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e52ece0-cae8-5f5c-94d7-a61586c1e6f0'}, {'abstract': 'All sides bear some of the responsibility for the deteriorating crisis in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/opinion/sunday/nicholas-kristof-the-blame-for-iraq-is-shared.html', 'snippet': 'All sides bear some of the responsibility for the deteriorating crisis in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE debacle in Iraq isn’t President Obama’s fault. It’s not the Republicans’ fault. Both bear some responsibility, but, overwhelmingly, it’s the fault of the Iraqi prime minister, Nuri Kamal al-Maliki.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/kristof-circular