. Yet federal law does not allow abortion coverage in the volunteers’ health care program, even in cases of rape or incest, or when a pregnancy endangers a woman’s life. Next week, subcommittees in both the House and the Senate will begin work on a Peace Corps budget for the next fiscal year. The lawmakers should repeal this unfair prohibition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peace Corps Volunteers Deserve Fairness', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peace Corps Volunteers Deserve Fairness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peace Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowey, Nita M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaheen, Jeanne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T02:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca15a746-3e64-59fa-8a46-c8be2c1fcae5', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca15a746-3e64-59fa-8a46-c8be2c1fcae5'}, {'abstract': 'Sunni militants in Iraq are rounding up former government workers, allowing some to repent and live while executing others, residents and a United Nations official said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/world/middleeast/reprisal-killings-reported-in-iraqs-militant-held-areas.html', 'snippet': 'Sunni militants in Iraq are rounding up former government workers, allowing some to repent and live while executing others, residents and a United Nations official said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ERBIL, Iraq — While still largely refraining from terrorizing the population inside Mosul, militants, working from a list they have obtained, have begun seeking out citizens who worked for the government, offering some a chance to repent and live under their authority, and in other cases executing them on the spot, according to accounts of residents and a top United Nations official.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/14/world/14mosul2/14mosul2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb