1-d75b-5cf8-95ac-c765ec609c56'}, {'abstract': 'Tommy Roy, the lead producer for NBC and the Golf Channel, is at his 20th U.S. Open, an event he has covered like a conductor orchestrating a symphony of words and pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/sports/golf/21-flat-screen-tvs-18-holes-one-pair-of-eyes.html', 'snippet': 'Tommy Roy, the lead producer for NBC and the Golf Channel, is at his 20th U.S. Open, an event he has covered like a conductor orchestrating a symphony of words and pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PINEHURST, N.C. — It was the first round of his 20th United States Open telecast, and the Golf Channel and NBC producer Tommy Roy had a meaty morsel of information for the on-air host Dan Hicks, who could not decipher what Roy was shouting into his earpiece.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-JP-GOLF/DOG-JP-GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '21 Flat-Screen TVs, 18 Holes, One Pair of Eyes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '21 TVs for Two Eyes to Scour 18 Holes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golf Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roy, Tommy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T17:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/719b02e1-6771-5c9e-9be8-b0eb91768553', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/719b02e1-6771-5c9e-9be8-b0eb91768553'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway musical “After Midnight,” a revue of song-and-dance numbers from the Cotton Club era of the 1920s, will close on June 29 after more than eight months of performances, a spokesman for the show confirmed on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/after-midnight-to-close-after-8-months/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway musical “After Midnight,” a revue of song-and-dance numbers from the Cotton Club era of the 1920s, will close on June 29 after more than eight months of performances, a spokesman for the show confirmed on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Broadway musical “After Midnight,” a revue of song-and-dance numbers from the Cotton Club era of the 1920s, will close on June 29 after more than eight months of performances, a spokesman for the show confirmed on Saturday. The producers of “After Midnight” were hoping to boost their modest ticket sales by winning the Tony Award for best musical last Sunday, but another nominee, “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder,” took the prize. “After Midnight,” which was capitalized at about $7 million, will close at a financial loss. Investors may recoup some money if a national tour of the show – now in discussions – comes together and proves successful.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15after/15after-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15after/15after-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 468}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15after/15after-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15after/15after-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1597, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/theater/15after/15after-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201