els-contention.html', 'snippet': 'After stumbling early in the season the last two years, the Los Angeles Angels are entering the summer in the thick of the race in the A.L. West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first two seasons as general manager of the Los Angeles Angels, Jerry Dipoto watched his team all but disappear from contention in the early-season quicksand. In 2012, the Angels doomed themselves with a 6-14 start. Last year, they lost 22 of their first 33.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/15/sports/DOG-BASES-1/DOG-BASES-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Position for Angels: Contention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Position for Angels: Contention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEAGUE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T17:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/000c63ab-5140-5827-bc88-86a563cf6615', 'word_count': 1416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/000c63ab-5140-5827-bc88-86a563cf6615'}, {'abstract': 'At a time when gun issues are volatile nationally and sales are increasing, many minority gun owners are trying to balance the pros and cons of ownership with the N.R.A.’s unyielding stances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/us/minority-gun-owners-face-balancing-act-weighing-isolation-and-stigma-of-violence.html', 'snippet': 'At a time when gun issues are volatile nationally and sales are increasing, many minority gun owners are trying to balance the pros and cons of ownership with the N.R.A.’s unyielding stances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — Standing in a small booth surrounded by displays for rifles, pistols, holsters and other firearm accouterments, the Rev. Kenn Blanchard signed copies of his book “Black Man With a Gun: Reloaded.” Amid the sea of thousands of white faces that descended on this city for the National Rifle Association convention in late April, Mr. Blanchard, an N.R.A. member since 1991, offered his reasoning for why he was one of the few black visitors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minority Gun Owners Face Balancing Act, Weighing Isolation and Stigma of Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Minority Gun Owners Face Balancing Act, Weighing Isolation and Stigma of Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vega, Tanzina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T18:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a30699c7-72e2-55fa-8407-f4d7cd6bf4b6', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a30699c7-72e2-55fa-8407-f4d7cd6bf4b6'}, {'abstract': 'The Big City Book Club’s hot-summer reading selection is Richard Price’s best-selling 2008 novel, “Lush Life.” Join us for the live discussion of the book on Tuesday, July 15, at 6:30 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/nyregion/big-city-book-club.html', 'snippet': 'The Big City Book Club’s hot-summer reading selection is Richard Price’s best-selling 2008 novel, “Lush Life.” Join us for the live discussion of the book on Tuesday, July 15, at 6:30 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Big City Book Club’s hot-summer reading selection is Richard Price’s best-selling 2008 novel, “Lush Life.” The book is both an evocation of decades of life on the Lower East Side of Manhattan and the tale of a violent crime whose effects ripple. One of the witnesses of the murder is initially considered a suspect, and even when he is exonerated, the trauma of the event stays long with him. Join us for the live discussion of the book on Tuesday, July 15, at 6:30 p.m. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big City Book Club', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Clubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Richard (1949- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lush Life (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T18:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1fbf92-e6b5-5b72-b525-bddeeaf872be', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1fbf92-e6b5-5b72-b525-bddeeaf872be'}, {'abstract': 'After falling behind 1-0, Costa Rica scores three goals to defeat Uruguay in one of the first upsets of the World Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://sports.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/14/uruguay-vs-costa-rica-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'After falling behind 1-0, Costa Rica scores three 