: 'Like diamonds, plastics are forever. The tons dumped into the ocean float around, swirling on currents, breaking into smaller bits, never going away. Scientists have identified huge gyres of plastic in the Pacific. There is an Eastern Garbage Patch, between Hawaii and California; a Western Garbage Patch, off Japan, and a patch between them called the Subtropical Convergence Zone, north of Hawaii.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Plasticene Epoch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Notes From the Plasticene Epoch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-14T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6645e46-1ea7-5f98-9cfb-27c25add40b8', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6645e46-1ea7-5f98-9cfb-27c25add40b8'}, {'abstract': 'A corporate tax holiday was disastrous in 2005. It would be disastrous again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/opinion/sunday/corporate-tax-holiday-wont-cure-highway-fund-woes.html', 'snippet': 'A corporate tax holiday was disastrous in 2005. It would be disastrous again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It should surprise no one that the federal Highway Trust Fund is on the brink of insolvency. 