'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, June 15, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-15T04:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c606e2-95a3-51c9-a9b9-e78b7c5b9a16', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c606e2-95a3-51c9-a9b9-e78b7c5b9a16'}, {'abstract': 'Quarterback Vince Young, who has not played in the N.F.L. since 2011, told NFL.com that he had retired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/sports/young-former-titans-quarterback-retires.html', 'snippet': 'Quarterback Vince Young, who has not played in the N.F.L. since 2011, told NFL.com that he had retired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quarterback Vince Young, who has not played in the N.F.L. since 2011, told NFL.com that he had retired. Young, the No. 3 overall pick in 2006 by the Tennessee Titans, was released in 2011 after a falling-out with Jeff Fisher, then the Titans’ coach. Young participated in the Cleveland Browns’ minicamp before signing with the team May 1, but the team cut him four days after drafting Johnny Manziel. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young, Former Titans Quarterback, Retires', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young, Former Titans Quarterback, Retires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Vince', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Titans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014