dia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a2db0fc7-72bd-5411-8d1d-2d33687eac9c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a2db0fc7-72bd-5411-8d1d-2d33687eac9c'}, {'abstract': 'Pining for Mitt Romney, too.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/15/the-corporates-and-the-crazies/', 'snippet': 'Pining for Mitt Romney, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeremy Peters and Shaila Dewan write about corporate shock over the sudden fall of Eric Cantor; it’s further confirmation of the story I told in my last column. Corporations and plutocrats had a good deal going: they bankrolled politicians who talked cultural populism during campaigns, but more or less ignored all that and focused on tax cuts and deregulation after the polls closed. And Cantor fit that profile perfectly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Corporates and the Crazies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-15T13:37:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae5c60d7-83d6-51f9-ac40-837945dbc09b', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae5c60d7-83d6-51f9-ac40-837945dbc09b'}, {'abstract': 'American players do not fake injuries or exaggerate contact nearly as much as others do, perhaps putting the squad at a strategic disadvantage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/sports/worldcup/for-us-soccer-team-honesty-may-not-be-the-best-policy.h