n-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Smithsonian) SHARK GIRL “My family and morals have made me the person I am today,” Madison Stewart, above, says, before adding what might give some viewers pause: “When I speak of family, I speak of sharks.” The 20-year-old Ms. Stewart, who was 2 when she began crisscrossing the Great Barrier Reef off the coast of Australia on a boat with her parents, goes where few others dare. Since the age of 12, she has been diving with sharks, without the protection of a cage but armed with the video camera she uses as a media weapon to fight the misconceptions circling these creatures. This documentary follows Ms. Stewart as she travels from Australia to Mexico, Palau and the Bahamas to commune with tiger sharks, Caribbean reef sharks and silky sharks — and in the process debunks myths and alleviates fears by demonstrating how these predators help keep the entire ocean ecosystem in balance.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-15T16:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9875f57-0036-5482-873f-446080715fe5', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9875f57-0036-5482-873f-446080715fe5'}, {'abstract': 'London', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/06/15/fashion/runway-mens/man-spring-2015-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'London', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'source': 'The N