fuddled and bemused by Bruce Haight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — There’s a revealer here in Bruce Haight’s grid, but you might have to look for it. It’s at 11 Down, not a place where you might normally expect to find the punchline of the puzzle. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subs', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-15T22:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc949f51-39db-5c7a-9d20-3ce2922ac09d', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc949f51-39db-5c7a-9d20-3ce2922ac09d'}, {'abstract': 'A farmworkers’ trailer park east of Palm Springs celebrates a precious amenity, a community focal point and public space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/arts/design/out-of-desert-dust-a-miracle-on-a-shoestring.html', 'snippet': 'A farmworkers’ trailer park east of Palm Springs celebrates a precious amenity, a community focal point and public space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MECCA, Calif. — About an hour east of Palm Springs, past the Tesla and Maserati dealers and the poodle and labradoodle walkers, lies St. Anthony’s Trailer Park, in the eastern Coachella Valley. It is a vast psychic and economic distance from the annual spring hipster music festival. This Coachella is a place where farmworkers live in dilapidated mobile home parks improbably named after saints. These are communities where clean drinking water and reliable electricity are never givens, and where, during the rainy season, children wrap plastic bags around their sneakers to stay dry while parched desert turns to mud.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/arts/COACHELLA/COACHELLA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Desert Dust, a Miracle on a Shoestring', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of Desert Dust, a Miracle on a Shoestring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Patricia Leigh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning 