}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/business/AMAZON/AMAZON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With an Amazon Smartphone, the Retailer Seeks a Tether to Consumers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Phone, Amazon Seeks Tether to Shoppers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streitfeld, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T00:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/944406ab-4dd1-56bc-a5e8-c9ff34d08285', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/944406ab-4dd1-56bc-a5e8-c9ff34d08285'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Kagan has called for the president to resist a popular pull toward making the United States a nation without larger responsibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/us/politics/historians-critique-of-obama-foreign-policy-is-brought-alive-by-events-in-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Kagan has called for the president to resist a popular pull toward making the United States a nation without larger responsibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McLEAN, Va. — In a much-discussed essay, the historian Robert Kagan recently depicted President Obama as presiding over an inward turn by the United States that threatened the global order and broke with more than 70 years of American presidents and precedence. He called for Mr. Obama to resist a popular pull toward making the United States a nation without larger responsibilities, and to reassume the more muscular approach to the world out of vogue in Washington since the war in Iraq drained the country of its appetite for intervention. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/us/KAGAN-sub/KAGAN-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Events in Iraq Open Door for Interventionist Revival, Historian Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Historian’s Critique of Obama Foreign Policy Is Brought Alive by Events in Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kagan, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T00:31:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Horowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7048dc11-86dd-5dcc-a216-16f0889f21b8', 'word_count': 1657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7048dc11-86dd-5dcc-a216-16f0889f21b8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Roth was the scion of the Matson Navigation Company but served as the chief negotiator for the U.S. in a historic trade pact; ran for governor of California; and restored Ghirardelli Square in San Francisco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/business/william-m-roth-shipping-heir-who-became-lifelong-public-servant-dies-at-97.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Roth was the scion of the Matson Navigation Company but served as the chief negotiator for the U.S. in a historic trade pact; ran for governor of California; and restored Ghirardelli Square in San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the scion of a shipping empire, William Matson Roth grew up in a 43-room home with 16 acres of formal gardens. When his twin sisters made their debut at a ball there in 1939, The San Francisco Chronicle said they were “launched like luxury liners.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi