illing to pay seems likely to rise as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Confidence Likely to Bring Pricier Deals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN APPRAISAL ASSOCIATES INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T01:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a1c853-7e99-550b-9412-14760e46e692', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a1c853-7e99-550b-9412-14760e46e692'}, {'abstract': 'A deeply flawed appeals court ruling could severely limit enforcement against foreign cartels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/opinion/the-motorola-mobility-ruling-and-antitrust-enforcement.html', 'snippet': 'A deeply flawed appeals court ruling could severely limit enforcement against foreign cartels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American antitrust laws have protected consumers against monopolies and cartels for more than a century. But a recent appeals court decision could severely limit the enforcement of those laws against foreign cartels that supply critical components used in cellphones, computers and other products Americans buy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cramped View of Antitrust Laws', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cramped View of Antitrust Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyword