maintain traditions despite the challenges of encroaching development.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/echoes-of-africa-along-the-carolina-coast/', 'snippet': 'Pete Marovich has been documenting the Gullah communities he first encountered as a teenager in South Carolina, which maintain traditions despite the challenges of encroaching development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Africa endures in the language and customs of the Gullah people, descendants of slaves who have lived along the Carolina coast for generations, sustaining themselves through the land and water.  Pete Marovich, who grew up in South Carolina aware of this distinctive culture, wanted to photograph these communities, so about a decade ago he pitched the idea to a magazine editor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/blogs/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/13/blogs/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/blogs/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/blogs/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/13/blogs/20140613-lens-gullah-slide-BTCU/201