 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/morning-views-15/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on global counterterrorism, Saudi health safety, Wisconsin equality and British biodiversity.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If all goes according to President Obama’s plan, the United States will soon be making a major new investment of $5 billion so that other countries can help in the fight against extremists,” writes The New York Times editorial board. The goal is to scale back American involvement in combatting terrorism by funding and equipping foreign counterterrorism operations. The Times is skeptical: “As Iraq demonstrates, just training troops to shoot and providing generals with expensive weapons will not address the threat.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T11:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24fc4dc2-9314-5665-87dc-b07e84bc186d', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24fc4dc2-9314-5665-87dc-b07e84bc186d'}, {'abstract': 'The investment in WeLab Holdings, an Internet finance start-up in Hong Kong, highlights the strong demand among investors for the Chinese Internet sector.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/welab-raises-14-million-from-li-ka-shing-and-sequoia-capital/', 'snippet': 'The investment in WeLab Holdings, an Internet finance start-up in Hong Kong, highlights the strong demand among investors for the Chinese Internet sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG – WeLab Holdings, an Internet finance start-up in Hong Kong, said