7729170ef5a'}, {'abstract': 'Alibaba unveils the 27 individuals in its controlling partnership. | A rival offer is expected to challenge G.E.’s bid for Alstom. | A bank account screening tool is under regulatory scrutiny. | Medtronic has agreed to buy Covidien.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/morning-agenda-alibabas-inner-circle-revealed/', 'snippet': 'Alibaba unveils the 27 individuals in its controlling partnership. | A rival offer is expected to challenge G.E.’s bid for Alstom. | A bank account screening tool is under regulatory scrutiny. | Medtronic has agreed to buy Covidien.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese e-commerce giant Alibaba Group on Monday publicly disclosed the names of all 27 individuals who will make up the company’s select inner circle in an amended initial public offering prospectus, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. The individuals, led by a company founder, Jack Ma, will essentially control the online market operator through their ability to nominate a majority of directors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Alibaba’s Inner Circle Revealed', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T12:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/872cc434-bed5-53f0-bba7-77164acb92bf', 'word_count': 1961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/872cc434-bed5-53f0-bba7-77164acb92bf'}, {'abstract': 'The takeover would add to the size of Level 3 Communications, already one of the country’s biggest providers of back-end Internet services.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.