 1,700 Iraqi soldiers being executed by Sunni Islamist militants and two bombs going off in Baghdad.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/whats-news-in-washington-situation-in-iraq-worsens/', 'snippet': 'The weekend brought no calm to the violent situation in Iraq. Instead, it got worse, with reports of 1,700 Iraqi soldiers being executed by Sunni Islamist militants and two bombs going off in Baghdad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good\xa0Monday\xa0morning. President Obama is returning from Southern California today to a Washington heat wave and a Middle East crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s News in Washington: Situation in Iraq Worsens', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T13:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a050640-9528-5bb8-8a88-f16cef1c28a1', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a050640-9528-5bb8-8a88-f16cef1c28a1'}, {'abstract': 'The newly elected prime minister concluded his first foreign visit to the neighboring country of Bhutan on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/modi-underscores-ties-to-bhutan-in-first-foreign-visit/', 'snippet': 'The newly elected prime minister concluded his first foreign visit to the neighboring country of Bhutan on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The Indian prime minister Narendra Modi concluded a two-day visit to Bhutan on Monday afternoon, making the tiny landlocked country nestled toward the eastern end of the Himalayas his first stop on his