197-a7a113908c88', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5f36e2c-bbbe-5dc2-b197-a7a113908c88'}, {'abstract': 'The Internet has made it easier than ever before for foul-mouthed, often sexist haters to air their grievances without consequence, writes JAKE FLANAGIN.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/rise-of-the-internet-hate-machine/', 'snippet': 'The Internet has made it easier than ever before for foul-mouthed, often sexist haters to air their grievances without consequence, writes JAKE FLANAGIN.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the age of Internet hate, when “it’s never been easier to send an anonymous death threat,” writes Jack Shafer for Reuters. “As with so many of life’s labors, advanced technology has removed most of the work and hazard from sending cowardly messages to people to frighten them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rise of the Internet Hate Machine', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T15:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cffc894-0fce-568a-8abe-2d65f169950e', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cffc894-0fce-568a-8abe-2d65f169950e'}, {'abstract': 'Cutting broccoli stalks into two-inch julienne is almost like adding yet another vegetable to this quick stir-fry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/health/stir-fried-broccoli-stalks-and-flowers-red-peppers-peanuts-and-tofu.html', 'snippet': 'Cutting broccoli stalks into two-inch julienne is almost like adding yet another vegetable to this quick stir-fry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Probably most of you have used broccoli time and again in stir-fries. In this version I cut the stalks into 2-inch julienne, which is almost like adding a separate vegetable to the mix of broccoli flowers and red pepper (also cut in julienne). There’s a lot of texture at play here – crisp-tender vegetables, crunchy peanuts and soft tofu. You can add a little spice if you want, but I’ve made the chili flakes optional.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/16recipehealth/16recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stir-fried Broccoli Stalks and Flowers, Red Peppers, Peanuts and Tofu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Broccoli', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T15:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8132acd-6fce-5581-9602-f1c390620e41', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8132acd-6fce-5581-9602-f1c390620e41'}, {'abstract': 'A swift way to turn broccoli into an irresistible snack or side dish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/health/pan-fried-broccoli-stems.html', 'snippet': 'A swift way to turn broccoli into an irresistible snack or side dish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was an experiment and now it is a keeper. Peel broccoli stems, slice them thin, and pan-fry in hot oil just until the slices are charred on the edges, then flip over and brown for just a little bit of time on the other side. If you do this just right, the medallions will have edges that are slightly crispy with that wonderful fried flavor, and tender interiors. With a little salt (or even without) they are irresistible. One stem’s worth of medallions will disappear quickly, so count on 1 per person (at least!). Although you will use a fair amount of oil for frying, it doesn’t all get absorbed by the broccoli stems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17recipehealth/17recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pan-Fried Broccoli Stems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Broccoli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T15:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4958c03-9063-5c32-8790-aa6ca0b6c180', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4958c03-9063-5c32-8790-aa6ca0b6c180'}, {'abstract': 'Uncooked, paper-thin broccoli keeps its shape and color, but absorbs a dressing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/health/pre-summer-greek-salad-with-shaved-broccoli-and-peppers-or-beets.html', 'snippet': 'Uncooked, paper-thin broccoli keeps its shape and color, but absorbs a dressing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classic Greek salad is a summer dish in my house; impossible to make if tomatoes are not in season and wonderful. But other vegetables take to the same treatment – a simple dressing with a high ratio of acid (in this case a combination of lemon juice and vinegar with olive oil), feta cheese and lots of mint and parsley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/science/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 