ce64326', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/0a4c405b-9e65-5f41-a16e-b3a03ce64326'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Botanical Garden will present “Frida Kahlo’s Garden” starting next May.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/frida-kahlos-garden-to-sprout-in-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'The New York Botanical Garden will present “Frida Kahlo’s Garden” starting next May.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I paint flowers so they will not die,” Frida Kahlo once said, and in her paintings as well as her life, flora of many varieties – flowers, trees, roots, tendrils, watermelon, cactus fruit – took on an almost supernatural presence. Next year the New York Botanical Garden will explore her obsession with the vegetable world in “Frida Kahlo’s Garden,” an exhibition that will include not only rarely seen paintings by Kahlo but also a re-creation of her studio and garden at Casa Azul in the Coyoacán neighborhood of Mexico City, where she lived for many years and where she died in 1954.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/KAHLO/KAHLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/KAHLO/KAHLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/KAHLO/KAHLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/KAHLO/KAHLO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1598, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/KAHLO/KAHLO-thumbSta