g attention.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/popcast-jimmy-giuffre-and-eric-dolphy-rediscovered-jazz-innovators/', 'snippet': 'Ben Ratliff and Nate Chinen discuss two jazz players who were perhaps underappreciated in their own time but are again attracting attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The saxophonist Jimmy Giuffre, who died in 2008 at the age of 86, was often out of step with jazz, even after he wrote the swing anthem “Four Brothers” for Woody Herman’s band in 1947 and led the Jimmy Giuffre 3, a late-’50s, drummer-less group that created cultural weight out of light-toned music. He started new groups that got away from swing rhythm and other conventions of jazz; his searches made him fall out of favor with audiences, and after the 1962 album “Free Fall,” he released no new records for 10 years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/guiffre/guiffre-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Jimmy Giuffre and Eric Dolphy, Rediscovered Jazz Innovators', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolphy, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuffre, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T18:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e80d5680-17f4-5a95-a610-7f387afda163', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e80d5680-17f4-5a95-a610-7f387afda163'}, {'abstract': 'The best school dress codes aren’t about students and sexuality, but about placing school on the list of places where there are standards, and where the freedom to do whatever we want, whenever we want shouldn’t and doesn’t apply.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/whose-dress-code-is-it-and-why/', 'snippet': 'The best school dress codes aren’t about students and sexuality, but about placing school on the list of places where there are standards, and where the freedom to do whatever we want, whenever we want shouldn’t and doesn’t apply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dress code — for girls, at least — has become a complicated issue. Is it intended to protect the girls against unwanted advances, or the boys against temptation? If the intent is to foster an atmosphere conducive to learning, why would spaghetti straps interfere with an understanding of algebraic equations? Does demanding that young women disregard the siren song of advertising and the media and leave the midriff-baring tops on the racks teach them that they are worth more than their appearance, or that their appearance is the measure of who they are? Is sexy strong, or is sexy dangerous? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-articleLarge.png', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-jumbo.png', 'height': 471, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-superJumbo.png', 'height': 471, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-dress-code/motherlode-dress-code-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whose Dress Code Is It, and Why?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T18:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c65d6e0-bd8b-52c3-8a43-b73160e60425', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c65d6e0-bd8b-52c3-8a43-b73160e60425'}, {'abstract': 'European researchers are testing designs for a small, easily piloted helicopter that could one day help shorten commutes and ease traffic congestion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/science/a-helicopter-of-ones-own.html', 'snippet': 'European researchers are testing designs for a small, easily piloted helicopter that could one day help shorten commutes and ease traffic congestion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIVERPOOL, England — You know what would be cool? ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17COPT/17COPT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/science/