web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/science/sounds-of-frog-lust-made-even-sexier.html', 'snippet': 'Male Mientien tree frogs are using storm drains to enhance their mating calls, researchers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tiny frogs in Taiwan are making the most of urban development by using storm drains to amplify their mating calls and impress females, researchers say. Open concrete drains are common in Taiwan, and male\xa0 Mientien tree frogs (above, one in its more usual setting) like to perch inside when courting. Writing in The Journal of Zoology, researchers reported that the drains enhanced the volume and duration of calls. \xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/science/17FLOA/17FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit