curities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Permanent Subcommittee on Investigations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T21:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2084bd92-b547-5f58-9cd6-688483031770', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2084bd92-b547-5f58-9cd6-688483031770'}, {'abstract': '“A Gentleman’s Guide for Love & Murder,” which won the Tony Award for best musical, hit a new high in ticket sales last week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/best-week-yet-for-gentlemans-guide-after-tony-win/', 'snippet': '“A Gentleman’s Guide for Love & Murder,” which won the Tony Award for best musical, hit a new high in ticket sales last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week was the best yet at the box office for the Broadway musical “A Gentleman’s Guide to Love & Murder,” following the show winning the Tony Award for best musical on June 8. “Gentleman’s Guide,” one of the most modest-selling musicals of the 2013-14 season until it became a front-runner for the Tony last month, grossed $851,262 for eight performances last week; its previous high was $816,932 for nine performances during Christmas week last year. The average paid ticket price was $121.89, up nearly $22 from the week before – a big jump that reflects theatergoers’ buying more premium-price tickets, a goal of the show’s producers as they try to leverage the Tony into making the show a commercial hit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u