oncerned about social issues have struggled to make their voices heard.', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/as-brazil-cheers-on-world-cup-squad-protesters-struggle-to-be-heard/', 'snippet': 'With Brazilians loudly rallying behind their national team in the World Cup, activists concerned about social issues have struggled to make their voices heard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twelve months after hundreds of thousands of protesters took to Brazil’s streets to complain of lavish public spending on stadiums for the World Cup, the tournament organizers have been relieved to see just hundreds attend scattered demonstrations as the first round of games got underway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Brazil Cheers, Protesters Struggle to Be Heard', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronaldo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Folha de Sao Paulo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T22:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad226a4-2929-5dda-b4ae-6fc2bee1e97b', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad226a4-2929-5dda-b4ae-6fc2bee1e97b'}, {'abstract': 'Disrupt this!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/creative-destruction-yada-yada/', 'snippet': 'Disrupt this!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jill Lepore has a great article in the New Yorker debunking the hyping of “disruptive innovation” as the key to success in business and everything else. It’s not a bah-humbug piece; it is instead a careful takedown, in which she goes back to the case studies supposedly showing the overwhelming importance of upstart innovators, and shows that what actually happened didn’t fit the script. Specifically, many of the “upstarts” were actually long-established firms, and more often than not the big payoffs went not to disruptive innovators but to firms that focused on incremental change and ordinary forms of efficiency and quality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creative Destruction Yada Yada', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-16T22:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee529cec-ab29-56b8-96a9-ddf022716164', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee529cec-ab29-56b8-96a9-ddf022716164'}, {'abstract': 'The creative team had described the production as the first open commercial run of a Spanish-language play Off Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/spanish-language-vagina-monologues-closes-after-short-run/', 'snippet': 'The creative team had described the production as the first open commercial run of a Spanish-language play Off Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spanish-speaking audienc