ed results, and I’m so impressed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Video of Modern-Day Concentration Camps', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T00:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d873b2b0-4f38-5734-8b1d-450172570e85', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d873b2b0-4f38-5734-8b1d-450172570e85'}, {'abstract': 'Abdullah Elshamy, an Al Jazeera reporter, had been detained without charges since last August.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/world/middleeast/egypt-to-free-ill-journalist-abdullah-elshamy-who-staged-hunger-strike.html', 'snippet': 'Abdullah Elshamy, an Al Jazeera reporter, had been detained without charges since last August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Prosecutors will release a hunger-striking journalist, Abdullah Elshamy, because of his deteriorating health, the Egyptian state news media said on Monday, offering a concession on the treatment of one of more than 16,000 prisoners detained since the military takeover last summer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt to Free Ill Journalist Who Staged Hunger Strike', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt to Free Ill Journalist Who Staged Hunger Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizati