ct': 'A community and an event for women experiencing maternal mental illness, those who have passed through it, and their family and friends.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/16/climbing-out-of-the-darkness-of-maternal-mental-illness/', 'snippet': 'A community and an event for women experiencing maternal mental illness, those who have passed through it, and their family and friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two articles in the Health section, “Thinking of Ways to Harm Her” and “After Baby, an Unraveling,” shed new light on the timing and range of maternal mental Illness. New studies and research suggest that maternal mental illness can appear during pregnancy, or can appear not only in the first few weeks after birth but in later months. In the year after giving birth, studies suggest, as many as one in five and at least one in eight women develop symptoms of mental illness, including not just depression, but anxiety, bipolar disorder, obsessive-compulsive disorder or a combination as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-maternal-illness/motherlode-maternal-illness-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-maternal-illness/motherlode-maternal-illness-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-maternal-illness/motherlode-maternal-illness-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/16/us/motherlode-maternal-illness/motherlode-maternal-illness-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType':