almart and Costco, joined in the deal with New York’s attorney general. But there was one holdout, Amazon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/business/big-retailers-agree-to-list-unit-prices-on-websites.html', 'snippet': 'Six major stores, including Walmart and Costco, joined in the deal with New York’s attorney general. But there was one holdout, Amazon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is that television-size box of graham crackers at Costco really a better deal than a standard box at Walmart? Soon, online customers won’t have to do the math to figure it out.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Retailers Agree to List Unit Prices on Websites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Retailers Agree to List Unit Prices on Websites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T02:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c146294a-0a95-5bba-a5b5-bd148f24a878', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c146294a-0a95-5bba-a5b5-bd148f24a878'}, {'abstract': 'Religious beliefs and contemporary life rub up against each other in Ayad Akhtar’s new play, “The Who & The What.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/theater/the-who-the-what-examines-faith-and-family.html', 'snippet': 'Religious beliefs and contemporary life rub up against each other in Ayad Akhtar’s new play, “The Who & The What.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matters of faith and family, gender and culture are stirred together into a fiery-flavored stew in “The Who & the What,” the probing new play by Ayad Akhtar that opened on Monday at the Claire Tow Theater at Lincoln Center. Like Mr. Akhtar’s “Disgraced,” which won the 2013 Pulitzer Prize and will be seen on Broadway this fall, this new work considers the itchy frictions that emerge when religious belief and contemporary life rub up against each other, as they do for the family at the center of the play, a Pakistani immigrant and his two grown daughters. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/17WHO/17WHO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/17WHO/17WHO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/17WHO/17WHO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/17WHO/17WHO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1164, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/17WHO/17WHO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'l