e treated more solemnly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/arts/television/watching-the-season-4-finale-of-louie.html', 'snippet': 'The fourth season of Louis C. K.’s “Louie” on FX was more serious and sober than in the past, and although the topics were familiar, they were treated more solemnly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the 20-month hiatus between Seasons 3 and 4 of “Louie,” the show’s creator, writer, director and star, Louis C. K., said he needed “a little breathing room” to gather his ideas and take the series — one of the smartest and funniest comedies on television — in a new direction.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1912, 'width': 1502, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE/LOUIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/LOUIE