 of a series of electronic “handshakes” between the missing Flight 370 and a satellite in the hours after the Boeing 777-200 vanished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANBERRA, Australia — Australia plans to resume searching for Malaysia Airlines’ missing Flight 370 to the southwest of the area in the Indian Ocean where the seafloor was scanned in detail last month, Australian officials say.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Search for Missing Malaysia Airlines Jet to Move Southwest, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Australia to Revisit Area of Indian Ocean in Search for Missing Jet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 370', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indian Ocean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inmarsat PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houston, Angus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T10:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d2f5e49-990b-5c63-8c9b-8666884f8f81', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d2f5e49-990b-5c63-8c9b-8666884f8f81'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike Mr. Scott’s usual fan base, the actress was in place and on time for his Moschino show in London.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/lindsay-lohan-cheerleads-for-jeremy-scott/', 'snippet': 'Unlike Mr. Scott’s usual fan base, the actress was in place and on time for his Moschino show in London.', 'lead_paragraph': ' LONDON — Jeremy Scott’s fashion shows are infamous for their celebrity contingents, an audience bloc with a history of delaying proceedings past even the fashion world’s usual loose interpretation of timeliness. (At his Moschino debut in Milan in February, Rita Ora and Katy Perry were so delayed that their arrivals were greeted by boos from the photographers’ pit.) So it was all the more a surprise to see, at his debut men’s show for Moschino here Monday, a famous friend perched quietly\xa0— and punctually\xa0— front row.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/fashion/17runway-A/17runway-A-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lindsay Lohan Cheerleads for Jeremy Scott', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohan, Lindsay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moschino', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T10:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e31fe29-098b-518b-8d6a-5fcc6f3f4ca8', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e31fe29-098b-518b-8d6a-5fcc6f3f4ca8'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on gun-violence research, workplace equality, genetically modified bananas, Iraqi compromise and casual-rents rules.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/morning-views-16/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on gun-violence research, workplace equality, genetically modified bananas, Iraqi compromise and casual-rents rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times reports dozens of school shootings have occurred in the 18 months since the massacre at Sandy Hook Elementary School in Newtown, Conn., and the public-health community still lacks necessary information on how to prevent gun violence. “And if pro-gun members of Congress have their way, it will stay that way,” the editorial board writes. Representative Jack Kingston, Republican of Georgia and head of the House subcommittee that sets the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention budget, has labeled efforts to understand the socio-psychological causes of gun violence as “propaganda” for “gun-grabbing initiatives.” The price of ignorance “is measured in tens of thousands of preventable deaths and avoidable injuries from guns, year in and year out,” the board notes. “Compared with that, $10 million for the C.D.C. to study the problem and propose solutions would be a small price to pay.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T10:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a55679-2094-5db7-85fd-cf315748031e', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a55679-2094-5db7-85fd-cf315748031e'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Das, an assistant sports editor, gave us an update from Brazil on how the World Cup coverage is going so far.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/06/17/adjusting-coverage-to-a-changing-world-cup/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Das, an assistant sports editor, gave us an update from Brazil on how the World Cup coverage is going so far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Das, an assistant sports editor, gave us an update from Brazil on how the World Cup coverage is going so fa