ectu...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Monday handed two major defeats to the government of Argentina, which has been fighting with New York hedge funds over bonds that the country defaulted on in 2001. Along with putting Argentina at risk of another default, the setbacks could also make it harder in the future for a financially troubled country to cut a deal with its creditors to reduce its debt load, DealBook’s Peter Eavis writes. Argentina had asked the Supreme Court to overturn a lower court’s ruling that had required the country to pay back defaulted bonds held by the litigating hedge funds, known as holdouts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Argentina’s Court Loss Buoys Creditors', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T11:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4948876f-904c-568a-8b4d-b7ab673956d8', 'word_count': 2065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4948876f-904c-568a-8b4d-b7ab673956d8'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Howorth, an owner of the beloved Square Books in Oxford, Miss., draws from a family tragedy to write her first novel, “Flying Shoes.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/books/a-bookstore-owner-taps-a-wound-to-write-a-first-novel.html', 'snippet': 'Lisa Howorth, an owner of the beloved Square Books in Oxford, Miss., draws from a family tragedy to write her first novel, “Flying Shoes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the opening pages of Lisa Howorth’s novel, “Flying Shoes,” her heroine, Mary Byrd Thornton, gets a phone call from a police detective. He has news: The unsolved 30-year-old murder of her brother is being reinvestigated. She picks up a glass-laminate dish, advertised as indestructible, and shatters it on the kitchen floor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 780}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/arts/howorth/howorth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bookstore Owner Taps a Wound to Write a First Novel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opening an Old Wound to Find a First Novel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howorth, Lisa', 'rank': 