ddlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/133e1e25-d3c9-52d2-ab93-fe1f35c74584', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/133e1e25-d3c9-52d2-ab93-fe1f35c74584'}, {'abstract': 'The onslaught of Sunni militants in Iraq will have violent repercussions in Syria and could bring wider war in the Middle East, the panel said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/world/middleeast/extremist-groups-in-iraq-threaten-regional-war-un-panel-warns.html', 'snippet': 'The onslaught of Sunni militants in Iraq will have violent repercussions in Syria and could bring wider war in the Middle East, the panel said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The onslaught of extremist Sunni militants in Iraq will have violent repercussions in Syria and could bring wider war in the Middle East, a United Nations panel warned on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extremist Groups in Iraq Threaten Regional War, U.N. Panel Warns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extremist Groups in Iraq Threaten Regional War, U.N. Panel Warns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T12:53:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ffda89f-7591-550c-83af-8c21f5489bc6', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ffda89f-7591-550c-83af-8c21f5489bc6'}, {'abstract': 'The cult downtown eyewear brand is launching a customize-it-yourself option for three of its frames today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/illesteva-sunglasses-custom-diy/', 'snippet': 'The cult downtown eyewear brand is launching a customize-it-yourself option for three of its frames today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the four years of its existence, the New York-based eyewear and accessories brand Illesteva has made some noise with its collaborations, including House of Waris, the Webster boutique and Lou Reed. Lou Reed! How to follow up a partnership with the man who helped invent punk? Perhaps the only thing more punk than punk is the ethos of D.I.Y., and so today, the line — whose colorful, unisex shades have been sported by Beyoncé, Lady Gaga and Cara Delevingne — is unveiling a new custom sunglasses service. Using Illesteva’s website, users can select one of three frame styles, then choose from up to eight colors for the fronts and sides and match them up with one of up to nine lens varieties, including a polarized option. Like all of the brand’s offerings, the shades will be made in Italy or France. “I’ve never seen this offered in sunglasses before. I’m interested to see what color ways people will come up with,” says Daniel Silberman, the brand’s co-owner and designer. His decision to hand control over to his customers comes down to one of punk’s main tenets: self-expression. “Everyone wants to feel like they have something unique,” he says, “something that someone else doesn’t have.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17Illesteva/17Illesteva-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling For | Illesteva Shades You Design Yourself', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Waris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Illesteva', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T13:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {