}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7159ddb5-231b-5f37-acef-3f3d62d1ae16', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7159ddb5-231b-5f37-acef-3f3d62d1ae16'}, {'abstract': 'A new pair of all-black kicks, created exclusively for the hotel’s doormen and front-desk team, is now poised to hit the streets.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/perfect-pairing-vans-and-ace-hotel-team-up-for-a-sleek-take-on-the-skateboarding-shoe/', 'snippet': 'A new pair of all-black kicks, created exclusively for the hotel’s doormen and front-desk team, is now poised to hit the streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Ace Hotel Downtown Los Angeles, which opened earlier this year in what was once the United Artists building, the doormen and front-desk team have been outfitted with a fresh new set of kicks: a leather-and-canvas men’s lace-up designed in collaboration with Vans, the skate-shoe company which has previously teamed up with everyone from Hello Kitty to Kenzo. The black-on-black version of the classic Era model is the ultimate\xa0grown-up sneaker, equally at home in the hipster-chic, movie-set-like hotel or on the SoCal streets. Starting this weekend, the shoes are also available in limited quantities in the gift shop; next Monday, they’ll be sold online.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17vans-beddie/17vans-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17vans-beddie/17vans-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/t-magazine/17vans-beddie/17vans-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '