rticle/bdb35b16-27e6-5955-b50e-3706bca16c50'}, {'abstract': 'The Crossing the Line festvial, presented by the French Institute Alliance Française, is to open on Sept. 8.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/a-world-premiere-from-patti-smith-and-her-daughter-at-crossing-the-line-festival/', 'snippet': 'The Crossing the Line festvial, presented by the French Institute Alliance Française, is to open on Sept. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Killer Road,” a work by the rock iconoclast Patti Smith, her daughter Jesse Smith and the ambient composer-performers of Soundwalk Collective, is one of three productions that will have their world premieres as part of Crossing the Line, the multidisciplinary festival presented by the French Institute Alliance Française (FIAF).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A World Premiere From Patti Smith and Her Daughter at Crossing the Line Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World Premiere From Patti Smith', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Institute/Alliance Francaise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T17:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f7d78d-0617-5313-bf78-a4a205d2d729', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f7d78d-0617-5313-bf78-a4a205d2d729'}, {'abstract': 'The president is preparing to bar federal contractors from discriminating on the basis of sexual orientation or gender identity.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/finally-an-executive-order-on-lgbt-workplace-discrimination/', 'snippet': 'The president is preparing to bar federal contractors from discriminating on the basis of sexual orientation or gender identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workplace discrimination based on sexual orientation or gender identity “needs to stop,” President Obama said last November, “because in the United States of America, who you are and who you love should never be a fireable offense.” But November came and went, as did 2013, and the first quarter of 2014, without the president heeding the rising calls for executive action.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finally, an Executive Order on LGBT Workplace Discrimination', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T17:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c0b6376-69b1-58d3-a364-8d39052a3e53', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c0b6376-69b1-58d3-a364-8d39052a3e53'}, {'abstract': 'But there continues to be deep resistance to bioengineered products in the European Union — or to easing various other agricultural trade protections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/business/international/us-calls-on-europe-to-ease-limits-on-gene-altered-food.html', 'snippet': 'But there continues to be deep resistance to bioengineered products in the European Union — or to easing various other agricultural trade protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The top American agriculture official on Tuesday called on the European Union to do more to ease restrictions on gene-altered food and feed crops if it hoped to reach a trans-Atlantic trade pact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Calls on Europe to Ease Limits on Gene-Altered Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T17:54:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86011729-8dd5-5fc8-a73b-bebb80c78cf7', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86011729-8dd5-5fc8-a73b-bebb80c78cf7'}, {'abstract': 'The president says he will use his executive authority to create the world’s largest protected marine area to defend diverse habitats from harmful activities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/us/obama-kerry-marine-sanctuary-pacific-ocean.html', 'snippet': 'The president says he will use his executive authority to create the world’s largest protected marine area to defend diverse habitats from harmful activities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In an effort to protect diverse habitats of coral reefs, whales, dolphins, sharks, sea turtles and numerous fish species from commercial fishing and other activities, President Obama announced Tuesday that he intended to use his executive authority to create the world’s largest marine protected area in the south-central Pacific Ocean.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Plans Protected Marine Area in Pacific Ocean', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Plans Protected Marine Area in Pacific Ocean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Ocean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Remote Islands Marine National Monument', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T17:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ecc8f6a-b6fc-5ec5-aa8d-cfe04207ba00', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ecc8f6a-b6fc-5ec5-aa8d-cfe04207ba00'}, {'abstract': 'A look at Scoop, the CMS that powers NYTimes.com and its mobile apps.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/scoop-a-glimpse-into-the-nytimes-cms/', 'snippet': 'A look at Scoop, the CMS that powers NYTimes.com and its mobile apps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know the importance of technology to the future of journalism has become a widely accepted fact when a prominent editor decides to join a new company because of its content management system. That’s what Ezra Klein told The New York Times about his decision to leave The Washington Post for Vox Media, a digital publisher with a fancy, custom-built CMS. Klein couldn’t quite describe what made the Vox system so special, but the fact that a journalist said he loved, let alone even tolerated, his CMS was all you needed to know that the world has changed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scoop: A Glimpse Into the NYTimes CMS', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T18:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Vnenchak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vnenchak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d716f8f3-4b6f-5319-a842-7f7795194d42', 'word_count': 2465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d716f8f3-4b6f-5319-a842-7f7795194d42'}, {'abstract': 'Texas Tech’s Tim Tadlock, the national coach of the year, is a rarity in the college game: He trusts his young arms to pitch to a defense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/sports/defensive-shift-finds-some-believers-in-college-baseball.html', 'snippet': 'Texas Tech’s Tim Tadlock, the national coach of the year, is a rarity in the college game: He trusts his young arms to pitch to a defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — It is not that big a deal, Texas Tech Coach Tim Tadlock said. Sometimes he overshifts his infield against left-handed pull hitters, putting three players on the right side of second base like major league teams do for David Ortiz of the Boston Red Sox. Sometimes he moves defenders a few feet, subtly, all in the hope of getting an out.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/sports/18cws-1/18cws-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/sports/18cws-1/18cws-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/sports/18cws-1/18cws-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/sports/18cws-1/18cws-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1547, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/sports/18cws-1/18cws-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thum