 for a 1-1 draw with South Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Belgium as the favorite to win this group and Algeria a longshot to advance, the winner of this match should be in good position to qualify for the knockout round. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia vs. South Korea: World Cup 2014 Live Blog', 'kicker': 'Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T20:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duncan Irving', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duncan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irving', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/382cecdb-5348-5d8c-bd0e-4dfd2d23945d', 'word_count': 1868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/382cecdb-5348-5d8c-bd0e-4dfd2d23945d'}, {'abstract': 'The South Korean-born, Japan-based artist has installed a series of large-scale sculptures and land art pieces that create a dialogue with the palace’s legendary gardens.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/on-view-lee-ufans-contemplative-sculptural-installations-at-versailles/', 'snippet': 'The South Korean-born, Japan-based artist has installed a series of large-scale sculptures and land art pieces that create a dialogue with the palace’s legendary gardens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past several years, the Chateau de Versailles has invited different contemporary artists to exhibit works on its grounds, including Takashi Murakami and, controversially, Jeff Koons. Starting today, the palace will be hosting 10 new pieces by the South Korean-born, Japan-based artist Lee Ufan, nine of which have been installed outdoors in the vast gardens designed by André Le Nôtre for Louis XIV.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On View | Lee Ufan’s Contemplative Sculptural Installations at Versailles', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Versailles (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T21:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b097672-8de4-51c1-a935-971604f5a992', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b097672-8de4-51c1-a935-971604f5a992'}, {'abstract': 'The collapse of Iraq reveals some ugly truths about the real emotional stakes the United States had in the wars there and in Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/torn-between-competing-perspectives-on-iraq/', 'snippet': 'The collapse of Iraq reveals some ugly truths about the real emotional stakes the United States had in the wars there and in Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is this what 1975 felt like?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/world/atwar_castern/atwar_castern-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 381, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/1