c51881b-1002-5f65-8e24-877515a8ea13', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c51881b-1002-5f65-8e24-877515a8ea13'}, {'abstract': 'A judge’s ruling harshly rejected arguments from the estate of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/conan-doyle-estate-loses-sherlock-holmes-copyright-appeal/', 'snippet': 'A judge’s ruling harshly rejected arguments from the estate of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge has rejected a copyright appeal brought by the estate of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle, opening the way for writers, filmmakers and other creators to make free use of Sherlock Holmes, his sidekick Watson and any elements of their story that appeared in Conan Doyle works published prior to Jan. 1, 1923.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appeals Court Affirms Sherlock Holmes Is in Public Domain', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holmes, Sherlock (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T21:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e513521-5533-5149-9319-ba52d59e161a', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e513521-5533-5149-9319-ba52d59e161a'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Beason, who became one of the Giants’ defensive leaders late last season, will not need surgery to correct the ligament tear and small fracture in his right foot sustained last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/sports/football/giants-beason-avoids-surgery-but-status-for-opener-is-in-doubt.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Beason, who became one of the Giants’ defensive leaders late last season, will not need surgery to correct the ligament tear and small fracture in his right foot sustained last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Giants middle linebacker Jon Beason will not need surgery to correct the ligament tear and small fracture in his right foot sustained last week in an off-season practice, the team announced Tuesday. But Beason’s foot will be immobilized for six weeks, which will precede an additional, undetermined period of recovery. His availability for the season opener Sept. 8 in Detroit remains in doubt.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants’ Beason Avoids Surgery, but Status for Opener Is in Doubt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants’ Beason Avoids Surgery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beason, Jon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T21:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15e3877-b68c-56e0-9c73-39f04aba0706', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15e3877-b68c-56e0-9c73-39f04aba0706'}, {'abstract': 'The bands Poor Rich Boy and DakhaBrakha performed at the Global Beat Festival on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/arts/music/dakhabrakha-plays-at-the-global-beat-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The bands Poor Rich Boy and DakhaBrakha performed at the Global Beat Festival on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nina Garenetska makes an unlikely rapper. Along with the two other women in the Ukrainian band DakhaBrakha, which performed on Monday night at Brookfield Place’s Winter Garden, she was wearing a white lace wedding dress, a tall black lamb-fur hat and half a dozen beaded necklaces. Ms. Garenetska was also holding her cello, painted with bright geometric designs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Put Language Aside, Then Let the Music Take Time to Speak', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Put Language Aside, Then Let the Music Take Time to Speak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DakhaBrakha (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Place (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Poor Rich Boy (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-17T21:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/090c20ef-f63b-5f4c-a268-41e06fddd567', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/090c20ef-f63b-5f4c-a268-41e06fddd567'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Patrick J. Leahy and Representative Doris Matsui, both Democrats, filed bills that would ban deals similar to the recent agreement that allows Netflix to connect directly to Comcast’s system to avoid network congestion.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/17/lawmakers-introduce-bill-to-ban-paid-prioritization/', 'snippet': 'Senator Patrick J. Leahy and Representative Doris Matsui, both Democrats, filed bills that would ban deals similar to the recent agreement that allows Netflix to connect directly to Comcast’s system to avoid network congestion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – Democratic members of both houses of Congress introduced legislation Tuesday that would ban Internet service providers from charging content companies for faster or more direct connections to Internet service subscribers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/business/17bits-net/17bits-net-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank