m industry pioneers in the United States, Europe and Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUANGZHOU, China — A year ago, China’s light-emitting diode industry seemed like a case study of industrial policy gone awry. Hundreds of factories built all over eastern China, often with lavish clean energy subsidies from state-owned banks and local governments, were operating at half capacity. The share prices of LED manufacturers were plunging.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/LIGHTS1/LIGHTS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As LED Industry Evolves, China Elbows Ahead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As LED Industry Evolves, China Elbows Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T00:38:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a875975-1b91-5d79-96c1-9aa667523fdd', 'word_count': 1314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a875975-1b91-5d79-96c1-9aa667523fdd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Koenig, who developed the original campaign for the Volkswagen Beetle, is widely regarded as one of the 20th century’s most innovative advertising writers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/business/julian-koenig-who-sold-americans-on-beetles-and-earth-day-dies-at-93.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Koenig, who developed the original campaign for the Volkswagen Beetle, is widely regarded as one of the 20th century’s most innovative advertising writers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julian Koenig, who is widely regarded as one of the 20th century’s most innovative advertising writers — a creative force behind an array of memorable campaigns, including for the original Volkswagen Beetle and the enduring environmental brand Earth Day — died on Thursday in Manhattan. He was 93.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 761}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 808, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1605, 'width': 1266, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/KOENIG-1-obit/KOENIG-1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Julian Koenig, Who Sold Americans on Beetles and Earth Day, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Julian Koenig, Who Sold Americans on Beetles and