iew', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7ab28ae-9504-5a4b-acaa-e5937429f9eb', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7ab28ae-9504-5a4b-acaa-e5937429f9eb'}, {'abstract': 'Sprinklers, perhaps more ubiquitous in New York than in any other city, are often gussied up in fanciful designs: a sea turtle, a ship, even a subway token.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/nyregion/citys-love-affair-with-the-summer-sprinkler-bursts-forth.html', 'snippet': 'Sprinklers, perhaps more ubiquitous in New York than in any other city, are often gussied up in fanciful designs: a sea turtle, a ship, even a subway token.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just after 2 p.m. Tuesday, with the temperature bursting 90 degrees, Sariya Rodriguez, age 20 months, stepped into the sprinkler section of Printer’s Park in the Longwood section of the Bronx. The water jets — set in the ground in a circle — were resting at the moment, but there were ample puddles for her to stamp with her pink plastic sandals. Suddenly, the water sprung from the jets. Sariya, who had never been in that part of the playground before, now was encircled with dancing streams of water. Her eyes and mouth opened in surprise. She looked up at her mother, Yajaira Rodriguez. Then they both laughed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/nyregion/sub-y-ABOUT/sub-y-ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/nyregion/sub-y-ABOUT/sub-y-ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/nyregion/sub-y-ABOUT/sub-y-ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': 