dofan region, the group said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/world/africa/sudan-attack-ravages-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'A hospital run by the humanitarian group Doctors Without Borders was heavily damaged by the Sudanese Air Force in an attack on the village of Farandalla in the South Kordofan region, the group said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A hospital run by the humanitarian group Doctors Without Borders was heavily damaged by the Sudanese Air Force in an attack on the village of Farandalla in the South Kordofan region, the group said Tuesday. The group’s head of mission, Brian Moller, expressed shock, “especially since it was clearly identified with a flag and a cross on the roof.” One hospital staff member was hurt, as were five villagers, the group said. Rebels in the region have been fighting the government in Khartoum since 2011.\xa0 In recent weeks, the Sudanese government has stepped up its offensive in the region. The Sudanese Army’s press officer could not be reached for comment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan: Attack Ravages Hospital', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan: Attack Ravages Hospital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Khartoum (Sudan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Kushkush, Isma'il", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': "By Isma'il Kushkush", 'person': [{'firstname': "Isma'il", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kushkush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5ac7c3-7a45-5f46-b3d1-1b87d5faab06', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5ac7c3-7a45-5f46-b3d1-1b87d5faab06'}, {'abstract': 'Frequent exercise may influence our weight and overall health by altering the kinds of organisms that live inside of us, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/exercise-and-the-good-bugs-in-our-gut/', 'snippet': 'Frequent exercise may influence our weight and overall health by altering the kinds of organisms that live inside of us, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being physically active may encourage beneficial germs to thrive in your gut, while inactivity could do the reverse, according to an innovative new study. The findings suggest that, in addition to its other health benefits, frequent exercise may influence our weight and overall health by altering the kinds of organisms that live inside of us. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/science/18wellphysed/18wellphysed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/science/18wellphysed/18wellphysed-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/science/18wellphysed/18wellphysed-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/science/18wellphysed/18wellphysed-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048