en-yə-re\\• noun ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | penury', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7a8fbea-76ca-5c33-b60d-b8b5cd7b2353', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7a8fbea-76ca-5c33-b60d-b8b5cd7b2353'}, {'abstract': 'President Dilma Rousseff met Tuesday with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. as Brazil and the United States moved to improve relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/world/americas/brazil-biden-and-rousseff-meet.html', 'snippet': 'President Dilma Rousseff met Tuesday with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. as Brazil and the United States moved to improve relations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Dilma Rousseff met Tuesday with Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. as Brazil and the United States moved to improve relations. Ties were strained last year by revelations of surveillance of Ms. Rousseff and other Brazilian officials by the National Security Agency. Mr. Biden told reporters in Brasília that their conversation about the spying was “candid,” while emphasizing the potential for improving ties. He also handed over to Ms. Rousseff declassified documents related to Brazil’s military dictatorship, which seized power in a 1964 coup supported by the United States. Ms. Rousseff is a former Marxist guerrilla who was tortured by agents of the dictatorship. She said this month in an\xa0interview that she was prepared for a thaw in ties with Washington. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Biden and Rousseff Meet', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: Biden and Rousseff Meet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/161e44f7-e44b-5df2-a8a5-fd13bd8081a3', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/161e44f7-e44b-5df2-a8a5-fd13bd8081a3'}, {'abstract': 'About 70 children and 10 adults were overcome by carbon monoxide at a day care northwest of Montreal on Tuesday and were rushed to the hospital by ambulances and school buses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/world/americas/canada-carbon-monoxide-affects-scores-at-day-care.html', 'snippet': 'About 70 children and 10 adults were overcome by carbon monoxide at a day care northwest of Montreal on Tuesday and were rushed to the hospital by ambulances and school buses.', 'lead_paragraph': ' About 70 children and 10 adults were overcome by carbon monoxide at a day care northwest of Montreal on Tuesday and were rushed to the hospital by ambulances and school buses. Health and fire officials said at a news conference that no one had lost consciousness during the episode in St.-Eustache, Quebec. But the five children with the most severe symptoms were transferred to a larger hospital for further examination. The source of the gas was unclear, but fire officials are investigating the cleaning machinery used in the day care center the previous night. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Carbon Monoxide Affects Scores at Day Care', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Carbon Monoxide Affects Scores at Day Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Care Centers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Monoxide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f1026b2-d4ce-5162-81e1-6a8fc6549ae9', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f1026b2-d4ce-5162-81e1-6a8fc6549ae9'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, June 18, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-wednesday-june-18-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, June 18, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There really isn’t much better dietary advice than eating your veggies, exercising and limiting calories. People just seem to like making eating difficult for themselves.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, June 18, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ee85d7-18f5-5f32-b768-e15b90adf550', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ee85d7-18f5-5f32-b768-e15b90adf550'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:05 P.M. (Cinemax) SAVAGES (2012) Two Southern California marijuana dealers — Chon (Taylor Kitsch), a cynical combat veteran, and Ben (Aaron Johnson, above right, with Mr. Kitsch and Blake Lively), a soulful Berkeley graduate — and their gorgeous significant other, O (Ms. Lively), take on Mexican traffickers in what A. O. Scott, writing in The New York Times, called “Oliver Stone’s feverish, fully baked, half-great adaptation of Don Winslow’s ferocious and funny drug-war novel of the same name.” The film, he added, “is a daylight noir, a western, a stoner buddy movie and a love story, which is to say that it is a bit of a mess. But also a lot of fun, especially as its pulp elements rub up against some gritty geopolitical and economic themes.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/051e8059-6985-588b-8775-0a5a7b3cb9d1', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/051e8059-6985-588b-8775-0a5a7b3cb9d1'}, {'abstract': 'The director of women’s athletics at the University of Texas testified that paying athletes for the use of their likenesses or allowing them to share in revenue was “incongruous” with the university’s approach to amateur sports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/sports/ncaabasketball/ncaa-begins-its-turn-in-ed-o-bannon-antitrust-case.html', 'snippet': 'The director of women’s athletics at the University of Texas testified that paying athletes for the use of their likenesses or allowing them to share in revenue was “incongruous” with the university’s approach to amateur sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAKLAND, Calif. — Christine Plonsky, the director of women’s athletics at the University of Texas, took the stand\xa0Tuesday morning in federal court here in an effort to persuade a judge that the N.C.A.A. and its biggest athletics programs are not the commercialized profit centers they have been accused of being by a string of witnesses during the past week and a half.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.C.A.A. Begins Its Turn in Antitrust Case Brought by Athletes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.C.A.A. Begins Its Turn in Antitrust Case Brought by Athletes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plonsky, Christine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Myles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beebe, Dan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ed6e00-c073-589b-b965-63a6c00e517c', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ed6e00-c073-589b-b965-63a6c00e517c'}, {'abstract': 'Marcus A. Wellons, convicted in the 1989 rape and murder of a teenage girl, was the first inmate put to death in the United States since a botched execution in Oklahoma seven weeks ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/us/georgia-inmate-is-put-to-death-in-first-us-execution-since-botched-procedure.html', 'snippet': 'Marcus A. Wellons, convicted in the 1989 rape and murder of a teenage girl, was the first inmate put to death in the United States since a botched execution in Oklahoma seven weeks ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSON, Ga. — Marcus A. Wellons, who was convicted in the 1989 rape and murder of a teenage girl, was executed at a Georgia prison on Tuesday, becoming the first inmate put to death in the United States since a botched execution in Oklahoma seven weeks ago prompted renewed questions about capital punishment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia Inmate Is Put to Death in First U.S. Execution Since Botched Procedure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia Inmate Is Put to Death in First U.S. Execution Since Botched Procedure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wellons, Marcus A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lockett, Clayton Darrell', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T04:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b328d432-2333-5aeb-aa3d-a5da836a5c3c', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b328d432-2333-5aeb-aa3d-a5da836a5c3c'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Niese allowed three earned runs or fewer for an 18th consecutive start, but a struggling Mets offense and two questionable plays in the field by Daniel Murphy m