Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darren Sands', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sands', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f49d873a-b2d0-57b9-8cd9-5c23f5a1b5c2', 'word_count': 4204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f49d873a-b2d0-57b9-8cd9-5c23f5a1b5c2'}, {'abstract': 'A Hong Kong nanny adept at street photography prompts comparisons to Vivian Maier. But Xyza Cruz Bacani wants to be known on her own merits.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/taking-care-of-people-and-pictures-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'A Hong Kong nanny adept at street photography prompts comparisons to Vivian Maier. But Xyza Cruz Bacani wants to be known on her own merits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A stream of images from Hong Kong caught Rick Rocamora’s attention on Facebook: black and white street scenes, with dramatic light and compositions that ranged from kinetic to serene. The fact that the photographer, Xyza Cruz Bacani, was from the Philippines — like Mr. Rocamora — intrigued him, though he was reluctant to contact her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/blogs/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/blogs/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/blogs/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0/20140617-lens-xyza-slide-KNW0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup