902-f0a2414ec508'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on ocean conservation, the Brownback amendment, Middle East cooperation, public records and digital dispatch markets.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/morning-views-17/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on ocean conservation, the Brownback amendment, Middle East cooperation, public records and digital dispatch markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times welcomes the news that President Obama will double the area of protected waters in the Pacific Ocean. “The United States does not have an Amazon basin,” the editorial board writes, “but it has the watery equivalent, a paradise of turtles and sharks, seals and dolphins, coral reefs and giant clams, frigate birds and boobies.” Mr. Obama is expanding on the legacy of his predecessor, George W. Bush — a fact The Times finds heartening: “Environmental conservation has a long bipartisan history in this country. These remote waters are a part of America most citizens may never see, but they should be thankful that presidents, of both parties, had the foresight to protect them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T10:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dbbd39f-5504-5fca-ae17-215982234040', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dbbd39f-5504-5fca-ae17-215982234040'}, {'abstract': 'Witnesses said the refinery in Baiji had fallen to attackers from the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, but some Iraqi officials asserted that fighting was still going on in the facility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/world/middleeast/iraqi-oil-refinery-ablaze-as-army-and-militants-clash.html', 'snippet': 'Witnesses said the refinery in Baiji had fallen to attackers from the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, but some Iraqi officials asserted that fighting was still going on in the facility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Refinery workers, witnesses and an Iraqi Army officer reported the seizure of Iraq’s biggest oil refinery by Sunni extremists on Wednesday after army helicopter gunships failed to repel their attack. But other Iraqi officials, including the commander of the garrison defending the refinery in Baiji, asserted that fighting was still going on inside the extensive facility, shut down by the violence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/19/world/IRAQ-1/IRAQ-1-thumbS