The real problem, according to the man in charge of thinking about these problems, is an ongoing “think big” approach.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/g-a-o-tech-director-says-washington-needs-to-think-smaller/', 'snippet': 'The Government Accountability Office says many U.S. IT projects are nearing failure, costing taxpayers maybe $10 billion. The real problem, according to the man in charge of thinking about these problems, is an ongoing “think big” approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to technology, Washington needs to learn how to fail smaller.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/business/18bits-gao1/18bits-gao1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.A.O. Tech Chief Says Washington Should Start Small on Big Projects', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T11:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a1086a3-53c6-5e46-8f2a-2c9e80a75294', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a1086a3-53c6-5e46-8f2a-2c9e80a75294'}, {'abstract': 'Asking negative questions about an issue or candidate does not, in itself, make it a push poll.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/upshot/push-polls-defined.html', 'snippet': 'Asking negative questions about an issue or candidate does not, in itself, make it a push poll.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Push polls” — which are not really polls at all — are often criticized as a particularly sleazy form of negative political campaigning. Voters pick up the phone to hear what sounds like a research poll. But there is no effort to collect information, which is what a legitimate poll does.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capt