ate': '2014-06-18T14:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic and Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a1aaa93-7982-5340-ba93-b6968414b88d', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a1aaa93-7982-5340-ba93-b6968414b88d'}, {'abstract': 'The June 15 Look features children from 4 months to 22 months during infant survival swim training in Kissimmee, Fla. They were photographed by Seth Casteel, who specializes in animal photography and is publishing a book called “Underwater Puppies” in September.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/just-how-were-those-underwater-babies-photographed/', 'snippet': 'The June 15 Look features children from 4 months to 22 months during infant survival swim training in Kissimmee, Fla. They were photographed by Seth Casteel, who specializes in animal photography and is publishing a book called “Underwater Puppies...', 'lead_paragraph': 'What better way to welcome summer’s arrival than with pictures of happy babies underwater? The June 15 Look features children from 4 months to 22 months during infant survival swim training in Kissimmee, Fla. They were photographed by Seth Casteel, who specializes in animal photography and is publishing a book called “Underwater Puppies” in September. Here, Casteel talks about what babies and dogs have in common when they’re all wet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-articleLarge.png', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-jumbo.png', 'height': 669, 'width': 944, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-superJumbo.png', 'height': 669, 'width': 944, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/17/magazine/BabiesID/BabiesID-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just How Were Those Underwater Babies Photographed?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T14:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannie Choi', 'person': [{'firstna