homs-syria-civil-war-bashar-assad.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Times bureau chief in Beirut, Anne Barnard, shared some of her experiences during a recent visit to Homs, Syria, via Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anne Barnard, the Beirut bureau chief for The New York Times, traveled to Syria recently and reported her experiences in Damascus and Homs via Twitter. Her social media dispatches provided a rare view into the dire circumstances in Syria where the three-year conflict has killed an estimated 160,000 Syrians and left millions displaced. And she shared some poignant reactions to the devastation there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Glimpse of Syrian Lives Ravaged by War in Homs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T14:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f0a55b-b28e-5b5e-8b9c-9cdbe2bc2297', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f0a55b-b28e-5b5e-8b9c-9cdbe2bc2297'}, {'abstract': 'The actor Richard Beymer campaigned for civil rights and shot film in Mississippi in 1964 that appears in the documentary “Freedom Summer.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/arts/television/right-out-of-hollywood-a-witness-to-history.html', 'snippet': 'The actor Richard Beymer campaigned for civil rights and shot film in Mississippi in 1964 that appears in the documentary “Freedom Summer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 1964, Richard Beymer — the actor who a few years earlier had made a splash playing Tony in the film of “West Side Story” — furiously drove his Austin-Healy from Los Angeles to rural Mississippi. He was going to join the hundreds of young people heading there, mostly white students from the North, who would become part of the audacious civil-rights campaign known as Freedom Summer.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 711}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 865, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1729, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22WESTSIDE1/22WESTSIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Right Out of Hollywood, a Witness to History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Right Out of Hollywood, A Witness to History ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Felicia R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Stanley', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Freedom Summer (TV Program)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T14:38:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc69732f-aaad-5293-936c-bc61b94b557b', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc69732f-aaad-5293-936c-bc61b94b557b'}, {'abstract': 'The historic neighborhood of St. George, Staten Island, offers a wide variety of homes and views of New York Harbor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/realestate/living-in-st-george-staten-island.html', 'snippet': 'The historic neighborhood of St. George, Staten Island, offers a wide variety of homes and views of New York Harbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In praise of St. George, a historic neighborhood on Staten Island that gazes on New York Harbor, residents invariably mention the free ferry to Manhattan. They often cite the affordability of a place where one-bedroom apartments can cost less than half of what they go for in pricier parts of the city. And they might even point out the wondrously out-of-place look of some blocks, with fanciful Victorians on steep hills that can feel cut-and-pasted from San Francisco.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'St. George, S.I.: Framed by the Harbor', 'kicker': 'Living in', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Framed by the Harbor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, C J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe6ea3b-0118-50b6-a44d-bc32f1bda60d', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe6ea3b-0118-50b6-a44d-bc32f1bda60d'}, {'abstract': 'The former “Tonight” show host is the 17th recipient of the annual prize.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/jay-leno-to-receive-mark-twain-prize-for-humor/', 'snippet': 'The former “Tonight” show host is the 17th recipient of the annual prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you heard about this? Have you seen this? Jay Leno, the doggedly populist comedy monologist and former host of the “Tonight” show, will be the next recipient of the Mark Twain Prize for American Humor, the prize’s organizers said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jay Leno to Receive Mark Twain Prize for Humor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jay Leno to Receive Mark Twain Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T15:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f20938cd-00e5-5835-aab7-6b60f1dc985b', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f20938cd-00e5-5835-aab7-6b60f1dc985b'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Bertozzi’s graphic novel “Shackleton” follows the explorer and his crew on his third attempt to reach the South Pole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/books/nick-bertozzis-shackleton.html', 'snippet': 'Nick Bertozzi’s graphic novel “Shackleton” follows the explorer and his crew on his third attempt to reach the South Pole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Nick Bertozzi’s graphic novel “Shackleton,” the great man who between 1901 and 1921 embarked on four attempts to reach the South Pole is first depicted in a moment of total failure. So sick with scurvy that he can scarcely lift his head from his pillow — let alone pull a loaded sledge — Shackleton is ordered back to England, forced to abandon Robert Falcon Scott’s Discovery expedition. But he is determined to return to the Antarctic, despite his wife’s entreaties (“The children are growing so quickly”!) and the claims of common sense. Though it’s easy to miss in Bertozzi’s telling, Shackleton went back about 5 years later, leading the Nimrod expedition, which came within 97 miles of reaching the South Pole. He managed to secure funding for a third attempt in August 1914, on the eve of the First World War. It is this famed adventure that is the focus of “Shackleton.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/18/books/18childrens-1/18childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':