8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a8c3d0-9483-5fe4-88bf-48e25c6e4483'}, {'abstract': 'The incursion of militants into Northern Iraq has instigated arguments on military action and governance in Washington and the Middle East, JAKE FLANAGIN writes.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/the-isis-advance-provokes-the-west-and-arab-states/', 'snippet': 'The incursion of militants into Northern Iraq has instigated arguments on military action and governance in Washington and the Middle East, JAKE FLANAGIN writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Islamic State of Syria and Iraq, or ISIS, advances in Iraq, many eyes are trained on Washington and on the governments of Mesopotamia. Two questions are being hotly debated: First, will the United States take military action to prop up a fragile government it left in place after a decade of battle and more than 4,000 casualties? And, at a higher level, what does ISIS’s rise say about the prospects of an effective governance ever being established in the region?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ISIS Advance Provokes the West and Arab States', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T15:44:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60abfebb-c20a-5448-991a-481540028398', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60abfebb-c20a-5448-991a-481540028398'}, {'abstract': 'Several factors push up prices in the Stockholm area, from low interest rates to a strong job market and limited housing stock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/greathomesanddestinatio