 world, has been like a gospel for Silicon Valley. But suddenly, writes ANNA NORTH, critics divided over whether the business theory holds up at all.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/arguing-about-the-truth-of-disruption/', 'snippet': '“Disruption,” a shorthand that supposedly explains technology’s cheaper, faster, downmarket effect on our world, has been like a gospel for Silicon Valley. But suddenly, writes ANNA NORTH, critics divided over whether the business theory holds up ...', 'lead_paragraph': '“Most big ideas have loud critics,” writes Jill Lepore in The New Yorker. “Not disruption.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arguing About the Truth of Disruption', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T15:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/450bc1f9-9637-54f9-b18a-fbad1a8fdaf1', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450bc1f9-9637-54f9-b18a-fbad1a8fdaf1'}, {'abstract': 'Abdullah Abdullah, a candidate for Afghanistan’s presidency, said he suspended work with the country’s electoral bodies and asked officials to stop counting votes because of widespread fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000002947861/abdullah-halts-work-on-afghan-vote-count.html', 'snippet': 'Abdullah Abdullah, a candidate for Afghanistan’s presidency, said he suspended work with the country’s electoral bodies and asked officials to stop counting votes because of widespread fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abdullah Abdullah, a candidate for Afghanistan’s presidency, said he suspended w