difference in the current mess —\xa0constraining the Maliki government’s sectarian impulses, stiffening up the Iraqi Army’s backbone, giving us better intelligence about ISIS’s development. But that’s pure hindsight, and looking forward most of the strategic options being discussed look somewhat fantastical, from the invasion 2.0 favored by the editors of The Weekly Standard (in which\xa0“special operators, and perhaps regular U.S. military units” would rout ISIS, and then somehow re-join together what Maliki has very deliberately put asunder) to the ally-with-Tehran option advanced as the thinking internationalist’s alternative\xa0(which even its advocates acknowledge requires lending U.S. resources to the cause of\xa0a “strengthened expansionary Iran”), to the “targeted” air strikes reportedly being contemplated by the administration (which, as a certain general with some in-theater experience just pointed out, would risk turning the U.S. military into “the air force for Shia militias”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq Under a Colder Eye', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filkins, Dexter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'FRUM, DAVID', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weekly Standard', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 