tion, has been sanctioned by the Association of Art Museum Directors, which said the museum’s actions “violated one of the most basic and important” principles of a collecting institution.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delaware Museum Faces Sanctions From Directors’ Group', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delaware Museum Faces Sanctions for Art Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Art Museum Directors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delaware Art Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T17:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b459f527-9b1b-5de4-b19c-7e52416b9399', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b459f527-9b1b-5de4-b19c-7e52416b9399'}, {'abstract': 'London has been gradually moving to restore full diplomatic relations with Iran, whose role in the region is crucial amid the violence in Iraq and Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/world/europe/thaw-in-relations-between-britain-iran-critical-for-syria-iraq-and-isis.html', 'snippet': 'London has been gradually moving to restore full diplomatic relations with Iran, whose role in the region is crucial amid the violence in Iraq and Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — With the election of a relatively moderate president in Iran and the rise of radical Sunni fighters in Syria and Iraq, Britain is pressing ahead to improve relations with Iran and reopen its embassy in Tehran.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Thaw With Iran, Coming at a Crucial Juncture, Could Be Useful to Allies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain’s Thaw With Iran, Coming at a Crucial Juncture, Could Be Useful to Allies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T17:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4afcc43a-fff1-501d-afdb-f46c4f471234', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4afcc43a-fff1-501d-afdb-f46c4f471234'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s chief executive has been rethinking his business model. Entering 2014, he believed he had three options.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/how-should-select-home-care-adjust-to-new-wage-and-labor-regulations/', 'snippet': 'The company’s chief executive has been rethinking his business model. Entering 2014, he believed he had three options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve just published a case study about Select Home Care, based in Westlake Village, Calif., which offers 24-hour nonmedical care to elderly clients in California, Nevada, Utah, Colorado, Oregon and Texas. As the article explains, Select is confronting an array of regulatory changes that will necessitate shorter shifts, more employees and higher wages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Should Select Home Care Adjust to New Wage and Labor Regulations?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T17:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9afd009-638d-575a-b8f2-7ac946130709', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9afd009-638d-575a-b8f2-7ac946130709'}, {'abstract': 'John S. Chen, BlackBerry’s chairman and chief executive, has repeatedly acknowledged that an absence of popular apps has hampered the BlackBerry 10 line of phones.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/18/blackberry-to-add-amazon-app-store-to-phones/', 'snippet': 'John S. Chen, BlackBerry’s chairman and chief executive, has repeatedly acknowledged that an absence of popular apps has hampered the BlackBerry 10 line of phones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — In a side story to Amazon’s expected move into the smartphone business, the ailing handset maker BlackBerry said on Wednesday that it would include Amazon’s app store on its phones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/18/technology/18bits-bberry/18bits-bberry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnai