ion_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e78c6a98-14ff-5190-a7e7-837735b3a962', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e78c6a98-14ff-5190-a7e7-837735b3a962'}, {'abstract': 'The adventure writer and novelist Peter Heller discovers happiness in his Colorado dirt-brick cabin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/garden/he-found-his-corner-of-the-sky.html', 'snippet': 'The adventure writer and novelist Peter Heller discovers happiness in his Colorado dirt-brick cabin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a boy growing up in Brooklyn Heights, Peter Heller was fascinated by the mythic West, in particular the cowboy novels of Louis L’Amour. “I remember the cover of this one L’Amour book showed a guy on horseback, leading a pack horse across a creek in the snow,” Mr. Heller, 55, said. “Something about that cover — all I wanted to do was drift the high lonesome on horseback.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Found His Corner of the Sky', 'kicker': 'At Home With Peter Heller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Found His Corner of the Sky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paonia (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T22:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2198aaf-3c59-5e88-9c78-cb4a417ea1d3', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2198aaf-3c59-5e88-9c78-cb4a417ea1d3'}, {'abstract': 'By the time her son was nine months old, the writer Nicole C. Kear had baby-proofed her apartment. Blind-proofing it proved more difficult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/garden/mastering-a-collision-course-called-home.html', 'snippet': 'By the time her son was nine months old, the writer Nicole C. Kear had baby-proofed her apartment. Blind-proofing it proved more difficult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time my son was 9 months old, I had fully baby-proofed our tiny Brooklyn walk-up. Cabinets containing toxic chemicals were locked. Doorknobs and stove dials had been disabled. All four corners of the coffee table were padded. Easy. Effective. The process of blind-proofing the apartment, for myself, was far more complicated.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19DOMESTIC3/19DOMESTIC3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mastering a Collision Course Called Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mastering a Collision Course Called Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T22:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole C. Kear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Kear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51655992-503a-51f4-9439-2987a4aae51c', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51655992-503a-51f4-9439-2987a4aae51c'}, {'abstract': 'How does a Brazilian family satisfy a longing for the outdoors? With a giant Manhattan terrace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/greathomesanddestinations/bringing-rio-a-bit-closer.html', 'snippet': 'How does a Brazilian family satisfy a longing for the outdoors? With a giant Manhattan terrace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cristiane Peixoto, a floral designer, and her husband, Marcus Silberman, an investment banker, are from Rio de Janeiro, and as Ms. Peixoto said, “Life in Rio is all about being on the beach and outdoors.” So when the couple bought an apartment for their family in Manhattan, they chose one with as much space outdoors as there is indoors.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing Rio a Bit Closer', 'kicker': 'On Location: Upper East Side', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing Rio a Bit Closer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Balconies and Terraces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T22:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80bb7fda-c681-5f92-a659-f61e76662bd4', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80bb7fda-c681-5f92-a659-f61e76662bd4'}, {'abstract': 'Carsten Höller’s latest slide is on the campus of the furniture company Vitra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/garden/descend-into-giddiness.html', 'snippet': 'Carsten Höller’s latest slide is on the campus of the furniture company Vitra.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I think it would change our lives if we could slide more,” said the Belgian artist Carsten Höller, who has been building slides on and off since 1998. The structures not only carry you efficiently from place to place, he believes, but they also create a special state of mind that, borrowing a phrase from the French sociologist Roger Caillois, he likes to describe as “voluptuous panic.” On Wednesday, Mr. Holler unveiled his first free-standing slide on the campus of the furniture company Vitra in Weil am Rhein, Germany. It is a steel spiral descending from a 100-foot-high tower with a platform that offers a rare elevated view of the architectural masterworks around it. (Among the neighbors are buildings by Álvaro Siza, Tadao Ando and Zaha Hadid.) Topping the structure is a large, numberless clock that is positioned askew so that viewers must tilt their heads and guess the correct time. Mr. Holler prefers that idea to consulting a cellphone, a gesture that can be construed as rude. “People think you could be checking your email,” he said. Information: vitra.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 540}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1844, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/19OUTSIDE/19OUTSIDE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Descend Into Giddiness', 'kicker': 'Currents: Outdoors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Descend Into Giddiness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vitra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holler, Carsten', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T22:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed864d94-7efe-5586-a31c-8d8d5617b2f7', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed864d94-7efe-5586-a31c-8d8d5617b2f7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s no longer enough to look nice. A well-designed interior now needs an interesting scent built into it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/garden/what-good-taste-smells-like.html', 'snippet': 'It’s no longer enough to look nice. A well-designed interior now needs an interesting scent built into it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meredith Melling’s duplex loft in NoHo features the polished decorating of Ariel Ashe — lots of neutrals with some standout pieces like a tufted royal-blue velvet sofa and a burl-wood-and-chrome dining table — set against its bleached wood floors and gutsy exposed beams and columns. Tying it all together is an invisible, but palpable, element: a sandalwood, vanilla and pepper fragrance, designed especially for Ms. Melling and her apartment, wafting from a sleek metal machine the size of a tablet hidden behind the blue sofa.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/19/garden/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy/20140619-SCENT-slide-7OSH-copy-thum