Trial and Appeal Board ruled that the word was “disparaging.” But many came to that conclusion — and stopped using the name — a long time ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Blow to the ‘Redskins’ Name', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T22:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92f32cf0-9f18-5694-a912-0c1f6543e410', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92f32cf0-9f18-5694-a912-0c1f6543e410'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers now can turn to the Container Store for help in organizing their belongings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/garden/assembly-is-not-required.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers now can turn to the Container Store for help in organizing their belongings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Instead of trying to make sense of the dizzying array of boxes and shelving options at the Container Store, you can now hire somebody to figure it out for you. After successful runs in Texas, the company just started At Home in its two Manhattan locations. Twelve orderly professionals are ready to lend a hand, said Eva Gordon, vice president for stores. “They’ll come to your home, look at your space to understand your style, assess your needs and come back with an organizational plan.” The cost to get started is $50, which covers the visit and creation of the plan. The organizer recommends Container Store products to carry it out, and returns — at $50 an hour — to oversee the installation of shelving systems and the like, help with staging and styling, and even paint the space. Information: 