t scores. Robert Schaeffer, public education director of FairTest, said Hampshire would be the only test-blind college: Sarah Lawrence College was test-blind for several years, but it reverted to test-optional two years ago after U.S. News and World Report stopped ranking it because of the lack of test scores. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College to No Longer Consider Test Scores in Its Decisions', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'College to No Longer Consider Test Scores in Its Decisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hampshire College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACT (Examination)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMHERST (MASS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T23:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcbc2b1f-855a-52be-bad1-610e30a9b794', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcbc2b1f-855a-52be-bad1-610e30a9b794'}, {'abstract': 'The former secretary of state, who is promoting her new memoir, gave a boost of 23 percent to the usual audience on the network.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/business/media/2-million-tune-in-to-see-hillary-rodham-clinton-on-fox-news.html', 'snippet': 'The former secretary of 