sensus on how to define the region denoted by the classical Arabic term “al-Sham,” which is part of the name of the group called the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria by many news outlets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone seems to agree that the Sunni extremists who are striving to carve out a caliphate in Syria and Iraq have upended the region, but there is no consensus on what to call the militant group, in English at least.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Call Iraq Fighters? Experts Vary on S’s and L’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What to Call Iraq Fighters? Experts Vary on S’s and L’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Naggar, Mona el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T23:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick J. Lyons and Mona El-Naggar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'El-Naggar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8905bc57-38a8-51c6-a1f1-495cea4af401', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8905bc57-38a8-51c6-a1f1-495cea4af401'}, {'abstract': 'Fafsa’s complicated application form discourages many from going to college. Our bill proposes replacing it with just two simple questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/opinion/simplifying-fafsa-will-get-more-kids-into-college.html', 'snippet': 'Fafsa’s complicated application form discourages many from going to college. Our bill proposes replacing it with just two simple questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — THIS year, more than 20 million college students will complete the dreaded 108-question Free Application for Federal Student Aid, commonly known as the Fafsa. Most do it again every year they’re in school. Some pay someone to help them. Colleges hire thousands of staff members to assist. Too many students are so intimidated by the form that they don’t bother to apply.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Answer on a Postcard', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Answer on a Postcard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alexander, Lamar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennet, Michael Farrand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-18T23:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lamar Alexander and Michael Bennet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alexander', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d103e875-759b-5079-9a13-89720ad2a790', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d103e875-759b-5079-9a13-89720ad2a790'}, {'abstract': 'As it becomes trendy, soccer is losing its old frisson of hooliganism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/opinion/world-cup-reflections-on-soccer-of-old.html', 'snippet': 'As it becomes trendy, soccer is losing its old frisson of hooliganism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S wonderful that America has fallen in love with World Cup soccer, as it plays out across the greenswards of Brazilian host cities like Natal, Manaus and Curitiba. To walk through New York City on Monday night and hear the restaurant crowds’ whooping at John Brooks’s late-game goal, which propelled the United States over Ghana, was to experience soccer as it is experienced in the rest of the world: collective, noisy and cathartic.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/opinion/0619OPEDhornschemeier/0619OPEDhornschemeier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 509, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/opinion/0619OPEDhornschemeier/0619OPEDhornschemeier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 509}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/opinion/0619OPEDhornschemeier/0619OPEDhornschemeier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/opinion/0619OPEDhornschemeier/0619OPEDhornschemeier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1715, 'width': 2021, 'subType': 