nk': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Voice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Esquire (Magazine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T00:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c3eae3b-9a99-53cc-9542-809bd63b42e7', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c3eae3b-9a99-53cc-9542-809bd63b42e7'}, {'abstract': 'Dubai’s rise as a modern crossroads connecting East and West is a tale of globalization, ambition, and an audacious bet on the future of air travel that proved prescient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/business/international/once-a-humble-refueling-stop-dubai-is-crossroad-to-the-globe.html', 'snippet': 'Dubai’s rise as a modern crossroads connecting East and West is a tale of globalization, ambition, and an audacious bet on the future of air travel that proved prescient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBAI, United Arab Emirates — The gimmicks to attract attention and passengers — a $1 million raffle, a chance to win a Porsche 911, or a monthlong shopping festival — are still there but are hardly needed anymore. Travelers from around the world no longer need to be lured to this parched former trading post on the edge of the Persian Gulf.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/business/international/DUBAI/DUBAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/business/international/DUBAI/DUBAI-artic