estion, or many.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — I’m not sure if I’ve ever seen a 15 x 16 crossword puzzle with 20-plus theme entries, but we have one today, and you really have to admire the sneaky way Timothy Polin got them in there. Instead of a set of a few long entries, he and Will Shortz have clued many of the shorter entries as trivia questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mentally Pooped', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T02:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d1a327-976f-586d-bf11-b357134f4063', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d1a327-976f-586d-bf11-b357134f4063'}, {'abstract': 'Elected Islamists have been shoved to the margins, and they are debating how to revive the Arab Spring’s dream of synthesizing Islam and democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/world/middleeast/as-moderate-islamists-retreat-extremists-surge-unchecked.html', 'snippet': 'Elected Islamists have been shoved to the margins, and they are debating how to revive the Arab Spring’s dream of synthesizing Islam and democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNIS — Islamist politicians swept elections across the region in the aftermath of the Arab Spring, stepping close to power in Tunisia, Egypt, Libya and Morocco and undermining the thesis of Qaeda-style militants that violence offered the only hope for change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':