phisticated and accessible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/arts/music/horace-silver-85-master-of-earthy-jazz-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Silver, a pianist, composer and bandleader, wrote and performed music that was both sophisticated and accessible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Horace Silver, a pianist, composer and bandleader who was one of the most popular and influential jazz musicians of the 1950s and ’60s, died on Wednesday at his home in New Rochelle, N.Y. He was 85.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 889}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1383, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/SILVER-1-obit/SILVER-1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Horace Silver, 85, Master of Earthy Jazz, Is Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Horace Silver, 85,Master of Earthy Jazz, Is Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Horace (1928-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keepnews, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Note Jazz Club (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Note Records', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T02:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Keepnews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keepnews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3942cd7f-9da1-51cd-937d-67a1a089b9c7', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3942cd7f-9da1-51cd-937d-67a1a089b9c7'}, {'abstract': 'A ruling to cancel the trademark registration of the name of the Washington Redskins because it is disparaging to American Indians was right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/opinion/slurs-dont-deserve-trademark-protection.html', 'snippet': 'A ruling to cancel the trademark registration of the name of the Washington Redskins because it is disparaging to American Indians was right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no question that the term “redskin” has been used as a racial slur for American Indians for hundreds of years and is on par with offensive terms used to denigrate blacks and Hispanics. And it is also clear that federal law prohibits the Patent and Trademark Office from registering trademarks that disparage people or bring them “into contempt, or disrepute.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slurs Don’t Deserve Trademark Protection', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slurs Don’t Deserve Trademark Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trademark Trial and Appeal Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Patent and Trademark Office (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Daniel M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T02:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/303d8adf-4dcf-5fe3-af3c-b8c486686533', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/303d8adf-4dcf-5fe3-af3c-b8c486686533'}, {'abstract': 'China’s mounting campaign to control the South China Sea has generated fear and anger among its neighbors, and tensions with Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/opinion/china-roaring-on-the-seas.html', 'snippet': 'China’s mounting campaign to control the South China Sea has generated fear and anger among its neighbors, and tensions with Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few aspects of China’s dynamic emergence as a global power have generated as much insecurity and danger in its neighborhood as its mounting campaign to control the South China Sea, a vital waterway for international commerce. On Wednesday, at a high-level meeting in Hanoi, China’s top diplomat scolded his Vietnamese hosts for complaining about an oil rig that Beijing planted in early May in waters that Vietnam claims, as its own. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roaring on the Seas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roaring on the Seas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spratly Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T02:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9358bfd9-5a27-5273-afb5-47b1b59862a6', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9358bfd9-5a27-5273-afb5-47b1b59862a6'}, {'abstract': 'The governor of Michoacán, one of the country’s most violent states, where people have taken up arms to fight drug and organized crime gangs, has resigned because of poor health', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/world/americas/mexico-governor-of-michoacan-resigns.html', 'snippet': 'The governor of Michoacán, one of the country’s most violent states, where people have taken up arms to fight drug and organized crime gangs, has resigned because of poor health', 'lead_paragraph': ' The governor of Michoacán, one of the country’s most violent states, where people have taken up arms to fight drug and organized crime gangs, has resigned because of poor health. The resignation on Wednesday of the governor, Fausto Vallejo, 65, injects political uncertainty in a state where officials’ failure to quell surging violence, giving rise to vigilante groups, led the federal government to take over security this year. Mr. Vallejo, whose four-year term expires in 2016, did not disclose his health problem, but he underwent a liver transplant last year. He returned Tuesday night from a checkup in the United States and informed President Enrique Peña Nieto of his decision Wednesday morning. The State Legislature will choose a successor to serve the remainder of the term. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Governor of Michoacán Resigns', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Governor of Michoacán Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michoacan (Mexico)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vallejo, Fausto', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T02:34:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a25335-7225-5472-8211-e47027fdf7e2', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a25335-7225-5472-8211-e47027fdf7e2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Vaughan, who got his start directing the first productions of the New York Shakespeare Festival in 1956, professed a loyalty to the text and an aversion to “revisionist approaches.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/theater/stuart-vaughan-director-and-shakespeare-expert-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Vaughan, who got his start directing the first productions of the New York Shakespeare Festival in 1956, professed a loyalty to the text and an aversion to “revisionist approaches.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stuart Vaughan, who directed the first productions of the New York Shakespeare Festival and later seeded several regions of the country with classic works, starting repertory theaters in Seattle and New Orleans and another that toured community centers and colleges, died on June 10 at his home in High Bridge, N.J. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/VAUGHAN-obit/VAUGHAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/VAUGHAN-obit/VAUGHAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 712}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/VAUGHAN-obit/VAUGHAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/arts/VAUGHAN-obit/VAUGHAN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1727, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0