cost-cutting hybrid pension plan. | Markit shares are set begin trading. | A British hedge funds is breaking ties with its charitable arm. | The Justice Department’s cases against two European banks have ra...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the face of Detroit’s tumultuous bankruptcy proceedings, the city and its unions have quietly negotiated a scaled-back pension plan that could serve as a model for other troubled governments, Mary Williams Walsh writes in DealBook. One of the most closely watched issues of the case is whether government pensions can be legally cut in bankruptcy. Now, Detroit has introduced a new plan with the cooperation of its unions, which have been among the most vocal opponents of cutbacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Detroit’s New Pension Plan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T11:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46cddda3-6fd3-5ee3-b040-b7719d25b89f', 'word_count': 2074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46cddda3-6fd3-5ee3-b040-b7719d25b89f'}, {'abstract': 'The troubled smartphone maker, in the middle of a turnaround push, reported a narrower-than-expected adjusted loss and a rise in phone sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/technology/blackberry-earnings-report.html', 'snippet': 'The troubled smartphone maker, in the middle of a turnaround push, reported a narrower-than-expected adjusted loss and a rise in phone sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — For BlackBerry, the smartphone company recently known for producing relentlessly 