d States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the 43 teenage musicians of the National Youth Orchestra of Iraq, it was a dream about to come true: the ensemble, formed by the Iraqi pianist Zuhal Sultan in 2008, was planning to visit the United States this summer to work a similarly constituted American group, the Elgin Youth Symphony Orchestra, of Elgin, Ill., and then to perform in Elgin, Washington, D.C., Chicago and possibly New York (a concert was in the planning stages).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraqi Youth Orchestra Cancels American Trip', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraqi Youth Orchestra Cancels Visit to U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T20:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a5ce290-4f56-5d98-bbcb-cf9db2559908', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a5ce290-4f56-5d98-bbcb-cf9db2559908'}, {'abstract': 'Shop for handmade shoes and edible souvenirs, sample cocktails and cuisine and go on a cultural crawl during a weekend in the Spanish capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/travel/36-hours-in-madrid.html', 'snippet': 'Shop for handmade shoes and edible souvenirs, sample cocktails and cuisine and go on a cultural crawl during a weekend in the Spanish capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the five years since Spain’s economy took a nose-dive, madrileños never stopped going out, but they did become more judicious in their spending. While not easy on businesses, this has ultimately been good for consumers, as retailers and restaurateurs dug deep in the treasure chest of Spanish talents and traditions — not to mention agricultural bounty — to weather the economic storm. Before that storm, Madrid seemed frantic to become a copy of any other European metropolis, but now the city feels more Spanish again. Resourcefulness, creativity and reinvention are bubbling up in art galleries, designer ateliers and restaurants. The city’s symbol may be a bear, but for style, culture, history and sybaritic delights, there are plenty of reasons to be bullish on Madrid.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 918, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1836, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/travel/22-hours-combo/22-hours-combo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Madrid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T20:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ferren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ferren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a81d622-1f70-59c5-be22-4e59261a1256', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a81d622-1f70-59c5-be22-4e59261a1256'}, {'abstract': 'In recent years, a whole new music scene has developed in this Spanish city, merging local musicians with students from all over the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/travel/valencias-newest-sounds-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'In recent years, a whole new music scene has developed in this Spanish city, merging local musicians with students from all over the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Music is at the heart of Valencia, Spain’s third largest city. For hundreds of years, people in and around the city have formed symphonic brass bands. Children grow up learning to dance the jota and boleros and to play works by Mozart and Stravinsky, with flamenco coursing through their veins as well. Bordering the Mediterranean on Spain’s east coast, Valencia has long been the nexus o