tates, focuses on a young man vacationing in Brittany who feels torn among three women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/movies/a-summers-tale-from-eric-rohmers-seasons-cycle.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Rohmer’s languid 1996 film, “A Summer’s Tale,” finally released in the United States, focuses on a young man vacationing in Brittany who feels torn among three women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Rohmer, the French New Wave master, was in his mid-70s when “A Summer’s Tale,” the third installment of his “Tales of the Four Seasons” cycle, was released abroad in 1996. The only one of the cycle’s four films not distributed in the United States, it is finally having an American release, and it was worth the wait. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMMERTALE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMMERTALE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMMERTALE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMMERTALE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMMERTALE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20SUMMERTALE/20SUMME