rs his wife, Emmanuelle Seigner.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Venus in Fur,” Roman Polanski’s nimble film adaptation of the play by David Ives, might provoke a lively post-viewing argument. Is it about sex or power? Art or life? The nature of theater or the logic of desire?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sadist and a Masochist Walk Into a Theater', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sadist and a Masochist Walk Into a Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polanski, Roman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seigner, Emmanuelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMALRIC, MATHIEU', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Venus in Fur (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ives, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T21:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72dd2c52-136a-5189-b279-8caf6f560e86', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72dd2c52-136a-5189-b279-8caf6f560e86'}, {'abstract': 'The General Assembly of the Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.) voted to change the definition of marriage from “a man and a woman” to “two people,” and to allow ministers to perform same-sex marriages where it is legal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/us/presbyterians-vote-to-change-definition-of-marriage-to-two-people.html', 'snippet': 'The General Assembly of the Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.) voted to change the definition of marriage from “a man and a woman” to “two people,” and to allow ministers to perform same-sex marriages where it is legal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The Presbyterian Church (U.S.A.) voted at its General Assembly on Thursday to change its constitution’s definition of marriage from “a man and a woman” to “two people,” and to allow its ministers to perform same-sex marriages where it is legal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1410, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/us/SUB-PRESBY-1/SUB-PRESBY-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}