: 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dexter Ford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dexter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8d77167-106b-5d9b-a9e8-96cf9e7eb577', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8d77167-106b-5d9b-a9e8-96cf9e7eb577'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors in Ohio have developed a simple four-page quiz that can help reveal dementia early on, allowing patients to get their lives in order.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/your-money/a-test-for-the-early-detection-of-alzheimers-disease.html', 'snippet': 'Doctors in Ohio have developed a simple four-page quiz that can help reveal dementia early on, allowing patients to get their lives in order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liz Arledge is all too familiar with the ravages of dementia. Her mother died of Alzheimer’s, and one of her brothers has been found to have the progressive brain disease as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Test for the Early Detection of Alzheimer’s Disease', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T22:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27345cc4-7995-5c0c-986a-0e73935931c4', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27345cc4-7995-5c0c-986a-0e73935931c4'}, {'abstract': 'The law professor explains what is at stake for Hong Kong as the Chinese Communist Party attempts to consolidate its influence over the city. “The coming few months could be very rough,” Mr. Davis says.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/q-and-a-michael-c-davis-on-the-battle-over-hong-kongs-future/', 'snippet': 'The law professor explains what is at stake for Hong Kong as the Chinese Communist Party attempts to consolidate its influence over the city. “The coming few months could be very rough,” Mr. Davis says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hong Kong is undergoing deepening tensions over its political future as a self-governed territory under Chinese sovereignty. Democratic activists have demanded that residents win the right to elect Hong Kong’s top leader, called the chief executive, without procedures that would ensure that only candidates approved by Beijing appear on the ballot. Many of the activists have endorsed Occupy Central with Love and Peace, a movement whose members have said they will stage civil disobedience protests in the city’s financial heart if electoral reform plans proposed by the Hong Kong government and Beijing, possibly later this year, do not meet their criteria for universal suffrage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/19sino-QNA1/19sino-QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/19/world/19sino-QNA1/19sino-QNA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/19/world/19sino-QNA1/19sino-QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':