elings.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/19/good-feelings-about-mccarthy-and-scalise-elections-on-twitter/', 'snippet': 'If any Republicans were disappointed with the leadership elections in the House, they weren’t taking to Twitter to express their feelings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans elected two members of their caucus to the No. 2 and No. 3 leadership positions in the House of Representatives today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Feelings About McCarthy and Scalise Elections on Twitter', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Kevin (1965- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalise, Steve', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T22:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d345bb7e-7946-575a-825c-4522cbe8042a', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d345bb7e-7946-575a-825c-4522cbe8042a'}, {'abstract': 'R. C. Sherriff’s 1928 play “Journey’s End,” based on his memories of life in the trenches, anticipates the absurdism and existentialism of Beckett.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/theater/r-c-sherriffs-journeys-end-a-remembrance-of-war.html', 'snippet': 'R. C. Sherriff’s 1928 play “Journey’s End,” based on his memories of life in the trenches, anticipates the absurdism and existentialism of Beckett.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many and contradictory are the claims that have been made for “Journey’s End,” the British playwright R. C. Sherriff’s 1928 portrait of life in the trenches and probably still the greatest of 20th-century English-language war dramas. It has been extolled and reviled as an impassioned plea for pacifism, a jingoistic celebration of homegrown heroes and an indictment of shortsighted military blundering.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-t