enus in Fur’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T22:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Sony Pictures Classics', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sony', 'middlename': 'Pictures', 'lastname': 'Classics', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/9cc7b4aa-b6b3-550a-a7a9-460d7facadb7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9cc7b4aa-b6b3-550a-a7a9-460d7facadb7'}, {'abstract': 'At Yevma Authentic Greek Cuisine in East Meadow, a chef tested in Athens and New York City presides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/nyregion/a-review-of-yevma-authentic-greek-cuisine-in-east-meadow.html', 'snippet': 'At Yevma Authentic Greek Cuisine in East Meadow, a chef tested in Athens and New York City presides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Tuesday night at Yevma Authentic Greek Cuisine in East Meadow, a young man approached the takeout counter and complained that the gyro he had just purchased lacked lettuce and was studded with French fries. Peter Messaris, 48, the owner and chef, offered to add lettuce but also explained to the customer that gyros in Greece sometimes have French fries — not lettuce — tucked into the pita. The patron left with a smile on his face and we (seated nearby) learned why “authentic” is part of the restaurant’s name. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlar