s lashed together, stretching out to infinity.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Luxury Apartments? Later. For Now, They Burn Sage.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Condos? Later. For Now, Sage.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Sara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Two Trees Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tepees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cermanski, Denise', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-19T23:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8924e6cd-e1eb-5eac-b154-9c8e552cc056', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8924e6cd-e1eb-5eac-b154-9c8e552cc056'}, {'abstract': 'The real star of “Exhibition,” the third feature by the British filmmaker Joanna Hogg, is an austere but elegant, ultramodern townhouse in West London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/movies/exhibition-by-joanna-hogg-looks-at-a-long-term-relationship.html', 'snippet': 'The real star of “Exhibition,” the third feature by the British filmmaker Joanna Hogg, is an austere but elegant, ultramodern townhouse in West London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The real star of “Exhibition,” the third feature by the British filmmaker Joanna Hogg, is an austere but elegant, ultramodern townhouse in West London. Within its chilly spaces, the principal characters have lived and worked for 20 years. Married, childless artists in their 50s, the couple — identified only as D (Viv Albertine, an alumna of the rock group the Slits) and H (Liam Gillick, a well-regarded Conceptual artist) — work on separate floors connected by an elevator and a spiral staircase, and communicate via intercom. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/EXHIBITION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/EXHIBITION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/EXHIBITION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/EXHIBITION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/20EXHIBITION-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/20EXHIBITION-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20EXHIBITION/20EXHIBITION-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thum