l.html', 'snippet': 'The lawyer for a 14-year-old boy charged with killing another student said the boy suffered months of antagonism and bullying before the deadly fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Noel Estevez and Timothy Crump were friends, they did the things that 14-year-old boys everywhere like to do. They played video games, shared dirty jokes on Facebook and had at least one sleepover.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/nyregion/20boys-01/20boys-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs of Trouble Preceded Fatal Stabbing at Bronx School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Signs of Trouble Preceded Fatal Stabbing at Bronx School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crump, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Estevez, Noel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Administration for Children's Services (NYC)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intermediate School 117 (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T01:43:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/750ec93f-cfd0-5cdf-8909-4bd9a76c8c0c', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/750ec93f-cfd0-5cdf-8909-4bd9a76c8c0c'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Treasury on Thursday removed 308 names from a sanctions blacklist that helped cripple the Cali drug gang in Colombia, once considered the most powerful drug trafficking organization in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/world/americas/colombia-us-ends-cali-gang-blacklist.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Treasury on Thursday removed 308 names from a sanctions blacklist that helped cripple the Cali drug gang in Colombia, once considered the most powerful drug trafficking organization in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Treasury on Thursday removed 308 names from a sanctions blacklist that helped cripple the Cali drug gang in Colombia, once considered the most powerful drug trafficking organization in the world. The delisting, the largest in the history of the Treasury’s economic sanctions operations, lifted penalties against 78 individuals and 230 entities, mostly based in Colombia. The move left only the two leaders of the organization, which has collapsed financially, on the list. The leaders — the brothers Miguel and Gilberto Rodríguez Orejuela — were sentenced to 30-year prison terms in the United States after their capture and extradition in 2006. The brothers also agreed to forfeit $2.1 billion in assets worldwide, which the Colombian authorities are in the process of collecting. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colombia: U.S. Ends Cali Gang Blacklist', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colombia: U.S. Ends Cali Gang Blacklist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T01:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/958373bb-3839-591d-993b-67b24a574cc2', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958373bb-3839-591d-993b-67b24a574cc2'}, {'abstract': 'In “Fonzy,” a French film directed by Isabelle Doval, a man who donated sperm for a research project discovers that he fathered 533 children — 142 of whom want to meet him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/movies/fonzy-about-a-sperm-donor-tracked-by-dozens-of-progeny.html', 'snippet': 'In “Fonzy,” a French film directed by Isabelle Doval, a man who donated sperm for a research project discovers that he fathered 533 children — 142 of whom want to meet him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diego Costa (José Garcia) is a feckless if amiable 42-year-old who regularly donated his sperm for research purposes 20 years ago, using the name Fonzy (no relation to Fonzie, Henry Winkler’s “Happy Days” character). A pothead with a vintage pinball machine at home, he is a variation on the movies’ overfamiliar man-child template. Now Diego learns he has sired 533 children, 142 of whom are looking for him. Oh, and his no-nonsense girlfriend (Audrey Fleurot) is pregnant by him, too. But by customary means.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20FONZY/20FONZY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20FONZY/20FONZY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20FONZY/20FONZY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20FONZY/20FONZY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1211, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/arts/20FONZY/20