lly dominant ethnic minority and a historically oppressed majority, as in Iraq. Yet, today, Rwanda is a relatively successful country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Land of Mass Graves', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Land of Mass Graves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kagame, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:04:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/da507e8e-44ba-5156-998c-a208b5128713', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da507e8e-44ba-5156-998c-a208b5128713'}, {'abstract': 'The health care scandal at Veterans Affairs is real, but it’s being hyped out of proportion in an attempt to block reform of the larger national system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/opinion/the-hype-behind-the-health-care-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'The health care scandal at Veterans Affairs is real, but it’s being hyped out of proportion in an attempt to block reform of the larger national system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ve surely heard about the scandal at the Department of Veterans Affairs. A number of veterans found themselves waiting a long time for care, some of them died before they were seen, and some of the agency’s employees falsified records to cover up the extent of the problem. It’s a real scandal; some heads have already rolled, but there’s surely more to clean up.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1881, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Veterans and Zombies', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veterans and Zombies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf07d9e-3a67-563c-b34f-a047c6b86013', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf07d9e-3a67-563c-b34f-a047c6b86013'}, {'abstract': 'An Egyptian court on Thursday began the process of imposing death sentences on the top leader and other members of the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/world/middleeast/egypt-court-calls-for-death-sentences-for-top-muslim-brotherhood-members.html', 'snippet': 'An Egyptian court on Thursday began the process of imposing death sentences on the top leader and other members of the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Egyptian court on Thursday began the process of imposing death sentences on the top leader and other members of the Muslim Brotherhood, the Islamist political movement swept from power by the military nearly a year ago, in the latest sign of judicial support for the government’s crackdown on the Brotherhood. In the past few months, Egyptian courts have drawn international condemnation by issuing hundreds of death sentences against Brotherhood members and supporters after rushed trials that have relied on questionable evidence. On Thursday, the court referred the cases of Mohamed Badie, above, the Brotherhood’s spiritual leader, and 13 other people to Egypt’s highest religious authority, in what is seen as the first step in confirming the death sentences. Mr. Badie was also sentenced to death in April, in an unrelated case, but he is entitled to a retrial because the sentence was passed in absentia. In the latest trial, Mr. Badie and other senior leaders, including Essam el-Erian and Mohamed el-Beltagy, faced charges that included inciting murder during violence in Cairo last August. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Court Calls for Death Sentences for Top Muslim Brotherhood Members', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Court Calls for Death Sentences for Top Muslim Brotherhood Members', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:07:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdc7b843-9843-5c39-8fe4-20029a5306fd', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdc7b843-9843-5c39-8fe4-20029a5306fd'}, {'abstract': 'The decision to cancel plans to broadcast the opera in movie theaters because of pressure from critics is an artistic step backward for the Met.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/opinion/the-metropolitan-operas-backward-move.html', 'snippet': 'The decision to cancel plans to broadcast the opera in movie theaters because of pressure from critics is an artistic step backward for the Met.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera, which has scheduled “The Death of Klinghoffer” in the next season, has canceled plans to broadcast the opera live in movie theaters around the world. Peter Gelb, the Met’s general manager, defended the decision this week, saying that the broadcasts “would be inappropriate at this time of rising anti-Semitism, particularly in Europe.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Klinghoffer Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Klinghoffer Tragedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death of Klinghoffer (Opera)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, John (1947- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinghoffer, Leon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3a82f3-134d-5a7f-b91b-d464ae37d013', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3a82f3-134d-5a7f-b91b-d464ae37d013'}, {'abstract': 'Two new reports suggest that Americans are finding bargains and a wide choice of insurance plans thanks to the Affordable Care Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/opinion/good-progress-on-affordable-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Two new reports suggest that Americans are finding bargains and a wide choice of insurance plans thanks to the Affordable Care Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are finding very affordable health insurance and a wide choice of plans on the exchanges operated by the federal government, according to a report issued Wednesday by the Department of Health and Human Services. The report was based on data from the 36 states in which the federal government is operating health insurance exchanges this year. Comparable data from states operating their own exchanges is not yet available. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Progress on Affordable Health Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Progress on Affordable Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10e54a5-235b-506a-9700-7913ccb37229', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10e54a5-235b-506a-9700-7913ccb37229'}, {'abstract': 'The presidential election is in crisis with accusations of balloting-box stuffing and one candidate withdrawing from the process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/opinion/playing-with-fire-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The presidential election is in crisis with accusations of balloting-box stuffing and one candidate withdrawing from the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At this pivotal moment for Afghanistan, one of the two candidates for president, Abdullah Abdullah, is creating a political crisis by trying to interrupt the vote-counting in Saturday’s runoff. On Wednesday, he demanded that the election commission stop counting ballots and withdrew his election observers from the process.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Playing With Fire in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playing With Fire in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH, ABDULLAH', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghani, Ashraf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Independent Election Commission (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:08:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea869444-e5f0-5bc7-a28e-72fcfcdd2307', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea869444-e5f0-5bc7-a28e-72fcfcdd2307'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration announced additional punitive steps against Uganda on Thursday in response to the country’s new law criminalizing homosexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/world/africa/uganda-anti-gay-law-draws-sanctions.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration announced additional punitive steps against Uganda on Thursday in response to the country’s new law criminalizing homosexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Obama administration announced additional punitive steps against Uganda on Thursday in response to the country’s new law criminalizing homosexuality. Certain Ugandan officials will be barred from entering the United States, and some aid money for Ugandan police and health agencies will be cut off or redirected, the administration said. In addition, the Obama administration canceled plans to hold a military aviation exercise in Uganda. But administration officials said the moves would not diminish the American partnership with Uganda against the Lord’s Resistance Army, a rebel force known for its brutality. And the new travel ban is not expected to prevent Uganda’s foreign minister, Sam Kutesa, from traveling to New York, where he has just been elected president of the United Nations General Assembly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda: Anti-Gay Law Draws Sanctions', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uganda: Anti-Gay Law Draws Sanctions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T02:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/86afb919-5c86-509b-bccc-c4e65565389c', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86afb919-5c86-509b-bccc-c4e65565389c'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Morrison’s wordless film “The Great Flood” depicts the Mississippi River flood of 1927; Godfrey Reggio’s “Visitors” presents portraits of the human animal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/movies/homevideo/nonnarrative-cinema-great-flood-and-visitors-on-dvd.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Morrison’s wordless film “The Great Flood” depicts the Mississippi River flood of 1927; Godfrey Reggio’s “Visitors” presents portraits of the human animal.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Great Flood” and “Visitors,” two monochromatic, wordless, nonnarrative features that opened theatrically this year and are now available for home viewing, aren’t so much avant-garde as anachronistic — although it is that anachronism, the notion of a silent cinematic symphony, that makes them seem avant-garde.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22HOBERMAN1/22HOBERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22HOBERMAN1/22HOBERMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22HOBERMAN1/22HOBERMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22HOBERMAN1/22HOBERMAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 1439, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22HOBERMAN1/22HOBERMAN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 's