at the School of American Ballet, Ms. Le Clercq (above, with Edward Bigalow) appeared in “Resurgence,” a short piece created by George Balanchine for a March of Dimes benefit. Portraying the evil Polio, Balanchine enveloped Ms. Le Clercq in a black cape, rendering her character paralyzed. After children tossed dimes at her character, she arose. In 1956, by then the wife of Balanchine and a muse to Jerome Robbins, Ms. Le Clercq, 27, contracted polio while touring with the New York City Ballet in Copenhagen. Paralyzed from the waist down, she never danced again. Through interviews with her colleagues Jacques d’Amboise and Arthur Mitchell and others, this “American Masters” documentary, directed by Nancy Buirski, chronicles the life of Ms. Le Clercq (1929-2000), the inspiration behind Balanchine’s “Symphonie Concertante,” “Symphony in C,” “Bourrée Fantasque” and “La Valse” and Robbins’s “Afternoon of a Faun.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T05:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c832045-0d14-5313-a16b-3e7fdbac8746', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c832045-0d14-5313-a16b-3e7fdbac8746'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, June 20, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-june-20-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, June 20, 2014.', 'lead_paragrap