{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Jane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T12:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7989a91-e493-529f-a62c-c1cc026da738', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7989a91-e493-529f-a62c-c1cc026da738'}, {'abstract': 'A committee representing the Met’s orchestra joins its union in telling the opera’s board that the struggles of recent revivals were “evidence of a failed artistic vision.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/arts/music/facing-cuts-musicians-criticize-mets-leadership.html', 'snippet': 'A committee representing the Met’s orchestra joins its union in telling the opera’s board that the struggles of recent revivals were “evidence of a failed artistic vision.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bitter labor talks at the Metropolitan Opera took a new turn this week with a blast from the pit: Musicians in the orchestra, who are being asked to accept pay and benefit cuts, sent letters to the company’s board questioning the Met’s artistic and financial stewardship.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing Cuts, Musicians Criticize Met’s Leadership', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facing Cuts, Musicians Criticize Met’s Leadership', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF MUSICIANS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T12:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc643ac5-a297-572c-85f9-59655bcc2a4c', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc643ac5-a297-572c-85f9-59655bcc2a4c'}, {'abstract': 'Yefim Bronfman set fire to the Third Concerto in the Beethoven Festival of the New York Philharmonic on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/arts/music/a-festival-of-concertos-at-the-new-york-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'Yefim Bronfman set fire to the Third Concerto in the Beethoven Festival of the New York Philharmonic on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice now, in the course of a week, a New York Philharmonic concert has begun, uninspiringly, with a Beethoven piano concerto and has ended, powerfully, with a Beethoven piano concerto.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beethoven, Bronfman and Soaring Sparks', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beethoven, Bronfman and Soaring Sparks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronfman, Yefim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major'