ld’s novel, a sick and aging man in Jerusalem hires a young caretaker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/books/review/suddenly-love-by-aharon-appelfeld.html', 'snippet': 'In Aharon Appelfeld’s novel, a sick and aging man in Jerusalem hires a young caretaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the many challenges confronting the contemporary writer of fiction, among the most vexing is the problem of goodness. How does one convincingly portray goodness in an age when the twin presiding deities are irony and violence, when the most feared transgression is the sin of sentimentality? Can there be a place for a character who seems genuinely selfless, motivated by benevolence, decency, the desire to be of help?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1408, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/books/review/22GORDON/22GORDON-thu