ld Place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bang on a Can Marathon has been one of the central events of the new-music calendar since 1987, when the composers who founded the organization – Michael Gordon, Julia Wolfe and David Lang – invited composers and performers to present the first of them at a SoHo gallery. In recent years, the marathon has been part of the River to River Festival, and has been held in the vast Winter Garden at Brookfield Place (formerly the World Financial Center), where listeners can take it in with varying degrees of casualness, coming and going as they see fit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/20artsbeat-bang/20artsbeat-bang-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Hours of Free Music at Sunday’s Bang on a Can Marathon', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bang on a Can Marathon To Be Shown Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'River to River Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bang on a Can', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T15:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/502a7dca-b5b6-5d3b-a942-50e5b0eb8116', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/502a7dca-b5b6-5d3b-a942-50e5b0eb8116'}, {'abstract': 'In London, the spring/summer 2015 men’s shows favored this throwback silhouette in a series of minimal looks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/london-fashion-week-trend-wide-legged-jeans/', 'snippet': 'In London, the spring/summer 2015 men’s shows favored this throwback silhouette in a series of minimal looks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tight-fitting denim will always have its place on the runway, thanks to designers like Hedi Slimane for Saint Laurent. But in the spring/summer 2015 collections so far, looser, longer jeans silhouettes are on the rise. Unlike the baggy low-riders of the hip-hop ’90’s, the new crop of wide-legged jeans is surprisingly understated. At the E.Tautz show in London, the designer Patrick Grant offered a version that was dark-washed, cuffed and slightly high waisted. (He sported a pair for his bow.) Worn monochromatically with a tucked shirt and long mac coat, the runway look was put-together but relaxed. Margaret Howell, who continues to show strong collections of covetable basics, also introduced a loose-fitting pair of jeans, which was topped with a simple shirt and coat. And Marta Marques and Paulo Almeida, the duo behind Marques’Almeida, took a more youthful approach, fraying the pants’ hems and pairing them with an equally frayed top and coat that evoked a similarly laid-back minimalism, but with an edge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/t-magazine/20trend-jeans/20trend-jeans-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | The Return of Wide-Legged Jeans', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almeida, Paulo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marques, Marta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slimane, Hedi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T15:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17d4377a-2c0f-588b-ac52-49c2acaf02f4', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17d4377a-2c0f-588b-ac52-49c2acaf02f4'}, {'abstract': 'When my son first asked me a question about sex, I was surprised by how fundamentally unembarrassed I was, because it didn’t occur to him that it was something to be embarrassed about.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/surprisingly-good-at-talking-about-sex/', 'snippet': 'When my son first asked me a question about sex, I was surprised by how fundamentally unembarrassed I was, because it didn’t occur to him that it was something to be embarrassed about.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I hate the word ‘moist.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/02/26/style/motherlode-body-books/motherlode-body-books-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_nam