name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH, ABDULLAH', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghani, Ashraf', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T16:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e75b7a8-c8c1-571f-ab4f-64bfa2f5feb0', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e75b7a8-c8c1-571f-ab4f-64bfa2f5feb0'}, {'abstract': 'The complicated college financing process is discouraging people from applying for aid and going to college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/upshot/a-simple-way-to-help-financial-aid-do-its-job.html', 'snippet': 'The complicated college financing process is discouraging people from applying for aid and going to college.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any college student who wants a federal loan or Pell grant has to file a Free Application for Federal Student Aid. With well over 100 questions about income, assets and expenses, the Fafsa approaches the IRS Form 1040 in length, and is longer and more complicated than the 1040A and 1040EZ, the tax forms filed by a majority of taxpayers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/upshot/21up-aid/21up-aid-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There Is a Simpler Way for Students to Apply for Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'When Complexity Is the Enemy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T16:37:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dynarski and Judith Scott-Clayton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dynarski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott-Clayton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc1b2c11-c018-5eba-80bb-fe3f02d34bda', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc1b2c11-c018-5eba-80bb-fe3f02d34bda'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a reason the Chinese authorities are not known for their sense of humor. They even stopped the artist Han Bing when he went to Tiananmen Square with the latest trendy object in the Chinese art world — a pet cabbage.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/20/the-latest-icon-in-artistic-rebellion-a-cabbage/', 'snippet': 'There’s a reason the Chinese authorities are not known for their sense of humor. They even stopped the artist Han Bing when he went to Tiananmen Square with the latest trendy object in the Chinese art world — a pet cabbage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every so often, the artist Han Bing likes to play a little prank with a white cabbage — that iconic, rectangular vegetable synonymous in China with full bellies and good fortune. Impaled on a wheeled frame and tied to a length of rope, the cabbage resembles a miniature parade float trailing along behind him through streets around the globe. In Beijing, Los Angeles, New York, Tokyo and other cities, the spectacle has triggered laughter, finger-pointing and questions from bemused passersby. But Mr. Han, 40, gives no answers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest Icon in Artistic Rebellion: A Cabbage', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cabbage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Han Bing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T16:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2671f72d-b4b3-536a-8047-be417197462c', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2671f72d-b4b3-536a-8047-be417197462c'}, {'abstract': 'The Times critic Manohla Dargis reviews “Jersey Boys.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002952554/movie-review-jersey-boys.html', 'snippet': 'The Times critic Manohla Dargis reviews “Jersey Boys.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times critic Manohla Dargis reviews “Jersey Boys.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/multimedia/movies-jerseyboys-062014/movies-jerseyboys-062014-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/20/multimedia/movies-jerseyboys-062014/movies-jerseyboys-062014-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/20/multimedia/movies-jerseyboys-062014/movies-jerseyboys-062014-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url