, 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T17:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f5bafc1-b8ed-53f9-9d1b-a997697cdf08', 'word_count': 1390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f5bafc1-b8ed-53f9-9d1b-a997697cdf08'}, {'abstract': 'The number of French émigrés was four times higher in the first three months of the year than in the same period a year earlier, in part because of a weak economy and anti-Semitism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/world/europe/number-of-french-jews-emigrating-to-israel-rises-sharply.html', 'snippet': 'The number of French émigrés was four times higher in the first three months of the year than in the same period a year earlier, in part because of a weak economy and anti-Semitism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — For Tiffany Taieb Nizard, the decision to abandon France for Israel came this month when a French-born man was accused of gunning down four people at the Jewish Museum in Brussels in an anti-Semitic attack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/world/alt-21-france-1/alt-21-france-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/21/world/alt-21-france-1/alt-21-france-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/world/alt-21-france-1/alt-21-fran