'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c51f08-ef0d-5087-9e4d-11bebd43787f', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c51f08-ef0d-5087-9e4d-11bebd43787f'}, {'abstract': 'On the edge of a highway, the Jamaica Bay Riding Academy sits on 500 surprisingly peaceful acres of rugged coastline and unspoiled forest paths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/nyregion/jamaica-bay-riding-academy-in-bergen-beach.html', 'snippet': 'On the edge of a highway, the Jamaica Bay Riding Academy sits on 500 surprisingly peaceful acres of rugged coastline and unspoiled forest paths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a city where dogs are carried around in purses, it seems amazing to find that Susan Gallahue, 64, keeps a horse. Not in her apartment on the Upper West Side, of course, but at the bucolic Jamaica Bay Riding Academy in Bergen Beach, Brooklyn, where she visits Silver Palace, her Thoroughbred-warmblood mix, about four times a week. Ms. Gallahue, a full-time psychiatric nurse, looks forward to every visit with Silver, a retired show-jumping mare she says has “the best personality.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoofbeats and Ocean Views in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoofbeats and Ocean Views in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay Riding Academy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danza, Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T17:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ilise S. Carter', 'person': [{'firstn