ce lumped with Oldsmobile and Mercury as retiree-friendly brands, Buick may be shedding that long-held stigma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/automobiles/autoreviews/video-the-2014-buick-regal-turbo-is-fun-for-all-ages.html', 'snippet': 'Once lumped with Oldsmobile and Mercury as retiree-friendly brands, Buick may be shedding that long-held stigma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baby boomers know Buick as an automotive brand favored by their parents (or grandparents). Jingles that purred “Wouldn’t you really rather have a Buick?” during “The Ed Sullivan Show” didn’t work on the generation raised on Barbie, Hot Wheels and the Beatles. They ended up preferring to have a Lexus. Or an Audi. Or a BMW.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: The 2014 Buick Regal Turbo Is Fun for All Ages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buick Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opel, Adam, AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T18:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f64ebb0-e5e8-5739-9295-bee52230ad90', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f64ebb0-e5e8-5739-9295-bee52230ad90'}, {'abstract': 'John Koskinen, the Internal Revenue Service commissioner, clashed with lawmakers over missing emails during a heated House hearing on the tax agency’s scrutiny of Tea Party-aligned political groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www