favorites from among 100 works posted on the ArtEverywhereUS.org website. Voting was closed in early May, and the museums announced the 58 winning works on Friday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America, Online: Love for Hopper’s ‘Nighthawks’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winning Artworks Named in Billboard Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-20T18:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2639c06-9912-5b98-803e-1f829a8a1463', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2639c06-9912-5b98-803e-1f829a8a1463'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is expected to sign the bill, which would be effective immediately, though the bill’s regulations and implementation could take up to 18 months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/nyregion/new-york-senate-passes-bill-on-medical-marijuana.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is expected to sign the bill, which would be effective immediately, though the bill’s regulations and implementation could take up to 18 months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The New York Senate passed a bill legalizing access to medical marijuana on Friday, a day after Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and legislative leaders announced the agreement on a seven-year pilot program to provide the drug to sick New Yorkers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Senate Passes Bill on Medical Marijuana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'nam