on-from-the-vault.html', 'snippet': 'The life of Yves Saint Laurent, the subject of a biopic by Jalil Lespert, can be traced through the narrative of the clothes he designed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tormented yet indissoluble relationship between Yves Saint Laurent and his life and business partner, Pierre Bergé, is the governing narrative of Jalil Lespert’s “Yves Saint Laurent,” a biopic about that French fashion designer that opens in New York on June 25. But the life of Saint Laurent, who died in 2008, can also be traced through a parallel narrative: that of the clothes he designed. Between his first collection in 1957 and his retirement in 2002, he changed the way modern women dressed, often prefiguring social change by bringing street and exotic influences to conventional wear, and showing women as newly powerful figures in trousers, trench coats and tuxedos.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22YVES1/22YVES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22YVES1/22YVES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22YVES1/22YVES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22YVES1/22YVES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22YVES1/22YVES1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbna