tion, hypnotic repetition and ecstatic drive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Swedish band Goat calls its concerts rituals, and that’s how it performed on Wednesday night at Webster Hall: as a psychedelic rock ritual of rhythm, motion, hypnotic repetition and ecstatic drive. The men in the band were masked or hooded, in a mélange of ethnic clothes. The two female singers up front, dancing and shaking assorted percussion instruments, were post-hippie celebrants in colorful dresses, wearing feathered headdresses above their own glittery masks. No one spoke to the audience: The songs arrived on their own, droning and pounding, wailing with guitar solos and churning with funk.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/21/arts/21GOAT/21GOAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capt