1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41bf60c8-4c5e-5968-8ed3-4557bd68f20e', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41bf60c8-4c5e-5968-8ed3-4557bd68f20e'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary General Ban Ki-moon’s spokesman denied that the official had been served.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/world/americas/un-chief-served-papers-in-suit-by-haitian-cholera-victims-lawyers-say.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary General Ban Ki-moon’s spokesman denied that the official had been served.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations has been resisting, successfully so far, lawsuits from Haiti cholera victims who assert that United Nations peacekeepers caused the 2010 epidemic still ravaging the country. But on Friday, lawyers for the plaintiffs said, something new happened: Secretary General Ban Ki-moon was personally served with court papers ordering him to appear, an assertion that his spokesman denied.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Chief Served Papers in Suit by Haitian Victims, Lawyers Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Chief Served Papers in Suit by Haitian Victims, Lawyers Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T00:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dd3d482-db13-54e1-9184-f43d551ca903', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dd3d482-db13-54e1-9184-f43d551ca903'}, {'abstract': 'The White House announced new initiatives on Friday to promote the health of honeybees and other pollinators, which have suffered enormous losses in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/us/administration-takes-steps-to-aid-bees.html', 'snippet': 'The White House announced new initiatives on Friday to promote the health of honeybees and other pollinators, which have suffered enormous losses in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House announced new initiatives on Friday to promote the health of honeybees and other pollinators, which have suffered enormous losses in recent years. The memorandum, signed by President Obama, called for research into the causes of the severe decline and the role of pesticides, and formed a “pollinator health task force” of more than 14 federal agencies, saying, “It is critical to expand federal efforts and take new steps to reverse pollinator losses and help restore populations to healthy levels.” Erich Pica, president of the environmental group Friends of the Earth, said the administration “does not go far enough” to address pesticide issues. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Administration Takes Steps to Aid Bees', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Administration Takes Steps to Aid Bees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Friends of the Earth', 'ran