'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/automobiles/21WEEKEND-image/21WEEKEND-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/automobiles/21WEEKEND-image/21WEEKEND-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/21/automobiles/21WEEKEND-image/21WEEKEND-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/21/automobiles/21WEEKEND-image/21WEEKEND-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Auto Calendar: Camaros of the World Unite, in Maryland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T00:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/831bfad8-0576-5f3d-b8c2-398d5f59dd3b', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831bfad8-0576-5f3d-b8c2-398d5f59dd3b'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense and the Veterans Affairs Department should track their efforts to treat post-traumatic stress more carefully, to see how effective those efforts are, a report released Friday said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/us/report-calls-for-tracking-data-on-stress-disorder.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense and the Veterans Affairs Department should track their efforts to treat post-traumatic stress more carefully, to see how effective those efforts are, a report released Friday said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense and the Veterans Affairs Department should track their efforts to treat post-traumatic stress more carefully, to see how effective those efforts are, a government-sponsored report released Friday said. The report, from an expert panel assembled by the Institute of Medicine, noted that the agencies spend more than $3.3 billion annually on treatment of the disorder, which affects more than 500,000 veterans, including 8 percent of those who served in Iraq or Afghanistan — who are twice as likely to seek help as veterans of previous wars. It affirms the findings of a report published in 2012 that called for more careful tracking. The V.A. has tracked symptoms in some members given treatment, but it is not clear how many and whether those veterans are in fact improving, experts said. “Given that the D.O.D. and V.A. are responsible for serving millions of service members, families and veterans, we found it surprising that no PTSD outcome measures are used consistently to know if these treatments are working or not,” the chairman of the panel, Sandro Galea of Columbia University, said in a statement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Calls for Tracking Data on Stress Disorder', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Calls for Tracking Data on Stress Disorder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Benedict', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T00:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf06963-a307-5c27-ad01-02cee02b0eea', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf06963-a307-5c27-ad01-02cee02b0eea'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Charles B. Rangel, State Senator Adriano D. Espaillat and a third candidate, the Rev. Michael A. Walrond, debated whether to send forces to Iraq and the Dominican Republic’s denial of citizenship to children born to undocumented Haitian immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/nyregion/rangel-and-espaillat-discuss-foreign-affairs-as-house-primary-nears.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Charles B. Rangel, State Senator Adriano D. Espaillat and a third candidate, the Rev. Michael A. Walrond, debated whether to send forces to Iraq and the Dominican Republic’s denial of citizenship to children born to undocumented Hai...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Charles B. Rangel and his top challenger, State Senator Adriano D. Espaillat, debated international issues on Friday in one of the final pushes for votes in the Democratic primary for the 13th Congressional District seat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 's