nal Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T04:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/55451a62-e588-58cf-8af7-eb9ed03a0dda', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/55451a62-e588-58cf-8af7-eb9ed03a0dda'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) THE WOLVERINE (2013) This sixth installment in the X-Men film franchise finds Logan (Hugh Jackman) living as a hermit in the great white north and tormented by the memory of being forced to kill Jean Grey (Famke Janssen). Then the warrior pixie Yukio (Rila Fukushima) spirits him back to Tokyo to meet with Yashida (Haruhiko Yamanouchi), who is intent on repaying his life debt to Logan, who saved him during the bombing of Nagasaki — and alleviate Logan of his immortality, which he now considers a curse. “Mr. Jackman, for all his growling, flexing and macho wisecracking, keeps our attention focused on Logan’s feelings,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. So does the director James Mangold, he said, adding, “A modest superhero picture may sound like a contradiction in terms, but really it is a welcome respite.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T05:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/777ea8a4-2a1c-5055-9eb1-87c0142306ff', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/777ea8a4-2a1c-5055-9eb1-87c0142306ff'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 21, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/21/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-saturday-june-21-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 21, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We no longer have to imagine a terror state. We have one.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 21, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T05:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb4d48a-dae3-5015-b6d5-f54e87731e45', 'word_count': 28, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb4d48a-dae3-5015-b6d5-f54e87731e45'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin accepted the premise of a peace plan proposed by Ukraine’s president, but put Russian troops on combat alert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/world/europe/ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin accepted the premise of a peace plan proposed by Ukraine’s president, but put Russian troops on combat alert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia proffered both a carrot and a stick to Ukraine on Saturday, issuing a qualified acceptance of a peace plan proposed by the Ukrainian leadership to quell a separatist uprising in the southeast, but simultaneously putting troops across central Russia on combat alert and mo