organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af820db6-c5e9-5679-a2f8-17c6c71cb6a4', 'word_count': 1677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af820db6-c5e9-5679-a2f8-17c6c71cb6a4'}, {'abstract': 'The great street photographer Garry Winogrand once said, “I photograph to find out what something will look like photographed.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/arts/design/urban-hurly-burly-of-a-bumptious-era.html', 'snippet': 'The great street photographer Garry Winogrand once said, “I photograph to find out what something will look like photographed.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great street photographer Garry Winogrand once said, “I photograph to find out what something will look like photographed.” That curiosity led him to make some of the most indelible photographs of life in the United States during one of its most turbulent decades, the Sixties, with extraordinary avidity. In crowded off-kilter pictures that seemed haphazard and badly composed to critics at the time, he captured urban pedestrian traffic, people and animals at zoos and political demonstrations and altercations.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urban Hurly-Burly of a Bumptious Era', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Urban Hurly-Burly of a Bumptious Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T14:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22a4aa1d-4012-5415-836c-85173aae0239', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22a4aa1d-4012-5415-836c-85173aae0239'}, {'abstract': 'In jazz, there are young people who sound old, old people who sound young and, very occasionally, young people who sound like old people who sound young.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/arts/music/hes-an-old-soul-in-a-young-way.html', 'snippet': 'In jazz, there are young people who sound old, old people who sound young and, very occasionally, young people who sound like old people who sound young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In jazz, there are young people who sound old, old people who sound young and, very occasionally, young people who sound like old people who sound young. Pay attention to those people. The tenor saxophonist Bill McHenry has been such a person, with a full tone, slow and songlike phrasing and a totally in-the-present disposition equally indebted to free jazz and, say, Lester Young. He’s unpredictable, open to the ideas of his band members and to creating benign mischief. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s an Old Soul, In a Young Way', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s an Old Soul, in a Young Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T14:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4822b07e-0d92-5110-b86c-2c7f9beff63e', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4822b07e-0d92-5110-b86c-2c7f9beff63e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Outlaw Prophet: Warren Jeffs,” on Saturday night at 8 on Lifetime, Tony Goldwyn channels Mr. Jeffs, of the Fundamentalist Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/arts/television/tyrannical-captor-of-under-age-wives.html', 'snippet': 'In “Outlaw Prophet: Warren Jeffs,” on Saturday night at 8 on Lifetime, Tony Goldwyn channels Mr. Jeffs, of the Fundamentalist Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talk about scandalous. In “Outlaw Prophet: Warren Jeffs,” on Saturday night at 8 on Lifetime, Tony Goldwyn channels Mr. Jeffs, the president and prophet, seer and revelator, of the Fundamentalist Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints — who in 2006 joined Osama bin Laden on the F.B.I.’s 10 Most Wanted list for having arranged illegal marriages between his adult male followers and under-age girls. “He’s a far cry worse than playing President Fitz,” Mr. Goldwyn said in a phone interview, alluding to his role in the ABC drama “Scandal.” “You have a guy who was essentially disenfranchised in this very strange community, and who usurped power and became a complete dictator in his world.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyrannical Captor of Under-Age Wives', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tyrannical Captor of Under-Age Wives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T14:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a70354-19b5-50ad-ab00-bf126f6fcf36', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a70354-19b5-50ad-ab00-bf126f6fcf36'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh air, proud history: The Naumburg Orchestral Concerts in Central Park has both.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/arts/music/a-verdant-treat-and-a-period-viola.html', 'snippet': 'Fresh air, proud history: The Naumburg Orchestral Concerts in Central Park has both.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fresh air, proud history: The Naumburg Orchestral Concerts in Central Park has both. A perfect setting, then, for the Knights, a collective that brings equal doses of meticulous musicianship and fun to its performances. In the opening concert of the series on Tuesday, the conductor Eric Jacobsen leads the Knights in a typically eclectic program, including an arrangement of Boccherini’s Quintet in C (Op. 30), set in nighttime Madrid, alongside two newer works by composers with a strong sense of place: Andrew Norman’s “Light Screens” and Ives’s “Three Places in New England.” The composer-pianist Timo Andres joins in for his own take on Mozart’s “Coronation” Concerto. (7:30 p.m.; naumburgconcerts.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Verdant Treat, and a Period Viola', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahe