 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-21T18:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Skoyles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Skoyles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/00377fd9-c107-54ae-83ae-ab2d04ca503b', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00377fd9-c107-54ae-83ae-ab2d04ca503b'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Maddux will be inducted into the Hall of Fame this year, the first longtime client of the agent Scott Boras to be enshrined in Cooperstown, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/22/sports/baseball/an-ace-agent-finally-has-a-hall-of-famer.html', 'snippet': 'Greg Maddux will be inducted into the Hall of Fame this year, the first longtime client of the agent Scott Boras to be enshrined in Cooperstown, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of the last three decades, few people have had more influence on baseball, or been more ubiquitous, than the agent Scott Boras. When you flip on a game taking place in Anaheim, Calif., chances are he is looking back at you from his suite behind home plate. When you wonder whether your team will sign, or retain, a prominent star, quite often it is Boras handling the negotiations.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/22/sports/DOG-22bases1/DOG-22bases1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/22/sports/DOG-22bases1/DOG-22bases1-articleLa