ualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e9ad80-dfb1-52f5-8101-80f1c17c6d32', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e9ad80-dfb1-52f5-8101-80f1c17c6d32'}, {'abstract': 'If the opera house is to survive, those who work onstage and off will have to take a breath and compromise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/opinion/labor-talks-turn-bitter-at-metropolitan-opera.html', 'snippet': 'If the opera house is to survive, those who work onstage and off will have to take a breath and compromise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over its 131 years, the Metropolitan Opera has drawn virtually all the major stars onto its massive stage — from the days of Enrico Caruso to the time of Anna Netrebko. The company presents more than 20 operas each season, drawing about 800,000 people to more than 200 performances. Its live broadcasts in movie theaters around the world give 2.5 million people a chance to enjoy opera up close and in real time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Drama at the Met', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Real Drama at the Met', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T01:26:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id