rdistan has lost its greatest asset, which isn’t oil, but security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems that some who support the Kurdish cause see an opportunity in the mayhem in Iraq. Commentators from abroad see the Iraqi army’s meltdown and retreat from the Sunni Arab heartland north of Baghdad as a sign that things might finally fall into place for the Kurds. Here in Erbil, people were positively elated when the Kurdish armed forces, called pesh merga (meaning “those who face death”), consolidated their grip on oil-rich Kirkuk, after the Iraqi army gave up on the region this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Iraq Crisis is Worse Than it Seems for the Kurds', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T02:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cale Salih', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Salih', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c50f0c26-d2c2-58ac-9df3-6312758021e5', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c50f0c26-d2c2-58ac-9df3-6312758021e5'}, {'abstract': 'Abdullah Abdullah accused a top election official of colluding with his rival, Ashraf Ghani, to steal the presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/world/asia/abdullah-abdullah-says-recordings-show-afghan-election-was-rigged.html', 'snippet': 'Abdullah Abdullah accused a top election official of colluding with his rival, Ashraf Ghani, to steal the presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — One of the candidates in Afghanistan’s disputed presidential election released on Sunday what his campaign said were recordings of phone calls in which a top election official, other election officials an