RATION CHANGE Former President Bill Clinton (above, in Zambia), Richard Branson, Elton John, the Dalai Lama, Harry Connick Jr. and other celebrities join Bill and Tani Austin and their son Steven Sawalich of the Starkey Hearing Foundation as they take on projects intended to improve lives in some of the world’s poorest regions. This 10-part documentary series begins in Haiti, where the fashion designer Donna Karan, the actress Maria Bello and the entrepreneur Bill Rancic work with organizations including World Wide Village, We Advance and Urban Zen to help survivors of the 2010 earthquake. (The Starkey Hearing Foundation distributes free hearing aids to people in need.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b39d6a-45a1-5b5c-90fc-5478b21ffdc6', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b39d6a-45a1-5b5c-90fc-5478b21ffdc6'}, {'abstract': 'In the 15 years since a global pact took effect, the use and production of antipersonnel mines has nearly stopped and casualties have plummeted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/world/africa/treaty-is-making-land-mines-weapon-of-past-group-says.html', 'snippet': 'In the 15 years since a global pact took effect, the use and production of antipersonnel mines has nearly stopped and casualties have plummeted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the conflicts in Syria, Iraq and Afghanistan, the armed uprising in Ukraine and turmoil in other hot spots in the Middle East and Africa, one of war’s most insidious weapons — antipersonnel land mines — have been largely outlawed and drastically reduced, a monitoring group said in a report released Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treaty Is Making Land Mines Weapon of Past, Group Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treaty Is Making Land Mines Weapon of Past, Group Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines, Explosive', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Campaign to Ban Landmines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T06:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3fbde66-89a2-5704-9e78-4ac31bb1894d', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3fbde66-89a2-5704-9e78-4ac31bb1894d'}, {'abstract': 'The Global Times editorial was one of very few online posts about the democratic movement in Hong Kong that made it past heavy censorship in China.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/china-state-media-calls-hong-kong-vote-mincing-ludicrousness/', 'snippet': 'The Global Times editorial was one of very few online posts about the democratic movement in Hong Kong that made it past heavy censorship in China.', 'lead_paragraph': '“However many people take part in Hong Kong’s illegal public vote, there will never be as many as 1.3 billion,” the headline in the state-run newspaper Global Times declared on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/23/business/23sino-vote01/23sino-vote01-