rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be43aa20-fa95-57c2-8e23-78a56b009ed7', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be43aa20-fa95-57c2-8e23-78a56b009ed7'}, {'abstract': 'It has been four years since the Little Orphan Annie comic strip ended with Annie missing in Guatemala, but Dick Tracy is now looking for her.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/annie-missing-no-worries-dick-tracy-is-on-the-case/', 'snippet': 'It has been four years since the Little Orphan Annie comic strip ended with Annie missing in Guatemala, but Dick Tracy is now looking for her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The search for Little Orphan Annie is on. Readers were left with a cliffhanger when the “Annie” newspaper strip, distributed by Tribune Media Services, ended in June 2010 with the eternal youngster left missing in Guatemala. Four years later Daddy Warbucks has got his act together and found the best man for the job of finding his ward: Dick Tracy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annie Missing? No Worries, Dick Tracy Is on the Case', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dick Tracy Is on Case Of Missing Little Orphan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Media Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T15:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83700e79-950f-54ca-b881-7910ff9bae76', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83700e79-950f-54ca-b881-791