ope/polands-prime-minister-says-he-wont-dismiss-officials-caught-on-leaked-tapes.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Donald Tusk said the government would focus on uncovering the “criminal gang” that made illegal recordings of ministers having blunt and profane conversations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW — Prime Minister Donald Tusk of Poland said Monday that he would not dismiss any of the ministers whose bluntly political and occasionally profane conversations were caught on tape in the back rooms of expensive Warsaw restaurants, unless they are caught engaging in illegal behavior.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poland’s Prime Minister Says He Won’t Dismiss Officials Caught on Leaked Tapes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poland: Premier Stands by His Ministers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyman, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tusk, Donald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Komorowski, Bronislaw', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Poland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T18:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Lyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/373df221-6998-5498-a581-c31a532f685c', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/373df221-6998-5498-a581-c31a532f685c'}, {'abstract': 'How a company of Odawa, Chippewa and Potawatomi men ended up in the horrific Andersonville prison camp.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/american-indians-in-confederate-territory/', 'snippet': 'How a company of Odawa, Chippewa and Potawatomi men ended up in the horrific Andersonville prison camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the morning of June 18, 1864, Pvt. Payson Wolf trudged through the streets of Petersburg, Va., with other battered and bloodied Union prisoners of war. The captives were herded into an old tobacco barn with hundreds of other bluecoats to await their fate in the hands of Confederate military authorities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Indians in Confederate Territory', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 4, 