 thousand likes (or in the case of Kim Kardashian and Kanye West’s wedding photo, more than two million), it’s easier than ever to peer into the lives of others, even those in the public realm. Now, Liberatum, the self-described “cultural diplomacy organization,” has invited a few big names from the world of New York nightlife to contribute exclusive personal snaps to a monthlong exhibition that opens this Thursday at the recently renovated salon at the W New York, the Living Room. Titled “Tagged,” the show “sets out to explore the new cultural etiquettes that technology has put on the New York scene,” according to Liberatum founder Pablo Ganguli. “With some venues banning photos and others encouraging it, people are still treading the water lightly to determine what is and isn’t appropriate when it comes to mixing social life, photography and technology.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gallery | An Exhibit of Instagram Photos of Kimye with LiLo, Lorde, Damien Hirst and More', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boardman, Mickey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Eva (1979- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T19:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58831f3-5af4-5a42-8ba4-6abbbf0a83b4', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58831f3-5af4-5a42-8ba4-6abbbf0a83b4'}, {'abstract': '“Midnight in Europe,” Alan Furst’s latest historical thriller, centers on a Spanish agent in Paris who is trying to route arms to Republican forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/books/midnight-in-europe-a-thriller-by-alan-furst.html', 'snippet': '“Midnight in Europe,” Alan Furst’s latest historical thriller, centers on a Spanish agent in Paris who is trying to route arms to Republican forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Alan Furst’s latest World War II novel, “Midnight in Europe,” could apply to any of them. But don’t be fooled by its generic sound: Mr. Furst, who has by now approached that era and the dread preceding it from so many different cultural and geographical perspectives, remains at the top of his game. This is another fine addition to his elegant, gripping, interwoven set of novels that will someday form a kaleidoscopic map of European powers forced into desperate alliances as they fight for their lives.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/bookfurst1/bookfurst1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 977, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/bookfurst1/bookfurst1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 977}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/bookfurst1/bookfurst1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/bookfurst1/bookfurst1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1258, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': 