d immigration policy.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/reform-conservatism-and-immigration/', 'snippet': 'A response to William Galston on the right’s reformers and immigration policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This will hopefully be the week in which I settle all family business — by which I mean that I intend to write the responses to liberal critics of “reform conservatism” than I’ve been promising since long before World Cup season. Having discussed immigration policy in yesterday’s column, I’ll start with that issue, and with William Galston’s Wall Street Journal essay from late last month, which offered praise for the recent reformocon manifesto “Room to Grow” but also suggested that reform conservatives were too often coloring “within the lines”\xa0— and in particular, that “if immigration is to today’s Republicans as welfare was to the Democrats of the early 1990s, someone will have to go further.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reform Conservatism and Immigration', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T20:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84bfa940-2de3-551f-a76f-ea6fd55ab1d2', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84bfa940-2de3-551f-a76f-ea6fd55ab1d2'}, {'abstract': 'St. Michael’s Episcopal Church in Manhattan had been working with developers since 2008 to build condominium building, but new leadership at the church decided the project was too risky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/nyregion/st-michaels-episcopal-shifts-course-on-condo-project.html', 'snippet': 'St. Michael’s Episcopal Church in Manhattan had been working with developers since 2008 to build condominium building, but new leadership at the church decided the project was too risky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven stained-glass windows more than a story high surround the apse of St. Michael’s Episcopal Church at the corner of Amsterdam Avenue and 99th Street in Manhattan. The panels, created a century ago by Louis Comfort Tiffany, depict in vivid hues the celestial triumph of the archangel for whom the 206-year-old church is named.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/APPRAISALweb1/APPRAISALweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/A