': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa01523-221c-516a-bff3-52661e84dbf6', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa01523-221c-516a-bff3-52661e84dbf6'}, {'abstract': 'Just off the Walk of Fame there’s an airy new space, conceived by the artist Piero Golia, for the L.A. art community to let its hair down.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/23/secret-art-world-gathering-los-angeles-piero-golia/', 'snippet': 'Just off the Walk of Fame there’s an airy new space, conceived by the artist Piero Golia, for the L.A. art community to let its hair down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around the corner from a blighted stretch of the Hollywood Walk of Fame, through a back entrance that opens onto a seedy parking lot, there’s a space that feels rather like an alpine chalet. Created by the artist Piero Golia, the unlikely oasis is a salon for those in the know located in the storage of L.A.C.E. (Los Angeles Contemporary Exhibitions), an artist-run space that has been operating since the late 1970s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happenings | A Secret Chalet Off Hollywood Boulevard Where the L.A. Art World Gathers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huyghe, Pierre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-23T21:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'report