ter-presents-giselle.html', 'snippet': 'Different ballerinas performed the “Giselle” title role in distinctive ways in performances last week at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater’s performances of “Giselle” at the Metropolitan Opera House last week featured several debuts in the title role and saved the best for last, with Saturday’s return of Alina Cojocaru (who stars in “Swan Lake” this week at the Met). In every case, the interpretation was simpler than the ornate, fervent, virtuosic rendition of Diana Vishneva on opening night. But there are different ways of being simple.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/24GISELLE/24GISELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None