_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/sports/tennis/in-wimbledon-lottery-lucky-losers-win-a-second-chance.html', 'snippet': 'The six highest seeds who lost in the final round of qualifying were put in a random draw for four spots that became available in men’s singles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Luck in tennis is most commonly associated with balls that hit the net cord and dribble over, or shots that hit the racket frame and land square on the line. But there is no luck in tennis quite as important as the luck of the draw. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Wimbledon Lottery, Lucky Losers Win a Second Chance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Wimbledon Lottery, Lucky Losers Win a Second Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Tennis Professionals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Tennis Assn", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T00:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1705672d-43b8-5855-8b5a-727da0e33bec', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1705672d-43b8-5855-8b5a-727da0e33bec'}, {'abstract': 'Monroe Capital claims that Warren Woo, a former executive at the company, stole sensitive information to help start Breakaway Capital, a new private investment firm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealb