raph': 'WASHINGTON — Fear of losing a seat to a Democrat because of a Tea Party upset is one reason congressional Republicans are warily watching Tuesday’s Mississippi Senate runoff and other primary challenges to incumbents. But it is not the sole reason, and perhaps not the most important one, for Republicans this election cycle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mavericks Could Fracture a G.O.P. Senate Majority', 'kicker': 'Congressional Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mavericks Could Fracture a G.O.P. Senate Majority', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hulse, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDaniel, Chris (1972- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochran, Thad', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T00:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7307111-2038-54bd-8960-98acde32a709', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7307111-2038-54bd-8960-98acde32a709'}, {'abstract': 'A roaring lover of money, women, drugs, trees, cars and later in life, poetry, Mr. Dennis built a magazine empire and fortune on being able to spot and exploit budding trends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/business/media/felix-dennis-67-flamboyant-publisher-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A roaring lover of money, women, drugs, trees, cars and later in life, poetry, Mr. Dennis built a magazine empire and fortune on being able to spot and exploit budding trends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Felix Dennis, a flamboyant, boastfully profligate, immensely successful British businessman who built a publishing empire that included Maxim, America’s most successful young men’s lifestyle magazine, died on Sunday at his home in Dorsington, Stratford-upon-Avon, England. He was 67.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/business/DENNIS-obit/DENNIS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/business/DENNIS-obit/DENNIS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/business/DENNIS-obit/DENNIS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/business/DENNIS-obit/DENNIS-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1551, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'