 trafficking sting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/us/fbi-cracks-down-on-sex-trafficking.html', 'snippet': 'The F.B.I. director, James B. Comey, said that in the past week law enforcement authorities had arrested 281 pimps and recovered 168 child prostitutes in a sex trafficking sting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I. director, James B. Comey, on Monday said that in the past week law enforcement authorities had arrested 281 pimps and recovered 168 child prostitutes in a nationwide sex trafficking sting. The arrests and recoveries were made in 106 cities, and roughly 10 percent of the prostitutes had been missing from child protective services, the authorities said. In Phoenix, 21 pimps were apprehended, and in Denver 18 prostitutes were recovered, the highest numbers in the operation. More than a dozen children were recovered in other cities, including Chicago and Cleveland. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.B.I. Cracks Down on Sex Trafficking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.B.I. Cracks Down on Sex Trafficking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T00:33:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/58aa3fc5-49f2-5d95-baff-08b02b6a282f', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58aa3fc5-49f2-5d95-baff-08b02b6a282f'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Rockefeller, who died on June 13, devoted himself to a half-dozen causes, among them healing the wounds of post-traumatic stress disorder, curing sleeping sickness in Africa and saving the seas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/nyregion/a-rockefeller-known-not-for-wealth-but-for-his-efforts-to-help.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Rockefeller, who died on June 13, devoted himself to a half-dozen causes, among them healing the wounds of post-traumatic stress disorder, curing sleeping sickness in Africa and saving the seas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POCANTICO HILLS, N.Y. — As a late afternoon sun tinted the room in gold, the children and grandchildren of David Rockefeller, the banker and philanthropist, gathered around a long table this month for a dinner of scallops and vegetables and toasted his 99th birthday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1066, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/nyregion/ROCKEFELLER/ROCKEFELLER-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rockefeller Known Not for Wealth but for His Efforts to Help', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rockefeller Known Not for Wealth but for His Efforts to Help', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller, Richard (1949-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T00:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cbb9754-f05b-53fe-a300-083d491741e7', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cbb9754-f05b-53fe-a300-083d491741e7'}, {'abstract': 'Two brothers convicted of filing a false $2 million claim to the Boston Marathon victims’ compensation fund using the name of a long-dead aunt were sentenced Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/us/massachusetts-men-get-3-years-for-theft-from-marathon-fund.html', 'snippet': 'Two brothers convicted of filing a false $2 million claim to the Boston Marathon victims’ compensation fund using the name of a long-dead aunt were sentenced Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two brothers convicted of filing a false $2 million claim to the Boston Marathon victims’ compensation fund were sentenced Monday to three years in jail plus 468 hours of community service to help amputees and people with brain injuries. Judge Jeffrey A. Locke of Suffolk County Superior Court gave Branden Mattier, 23, and Domunique Grice, 28, a choice of six years in jail or three years in jail, after which they would serve six hours of community service every other Saturday for three years. The judge said the service could include building ramps for people who are handicapped, serving as an aide in a rehabilitation facility or changing bedpans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Men Get 3 Years for Theft From Marathon Fund', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Men Get 3 Years for Theft From Marathon Fund', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'One Fund Boston', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Locke, Jeffrey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattier, Branden', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grice, Domunique', 'rank': 10, 'majo