', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/24/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blue Jays’ Big Inning Helps Keep Yankees at a Distance', 'kicker': 'Blue Jays 8, Yankees 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blue Jays’ Big Inning Helps Keep Yankees at a Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitley, Chase', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stroman, Marcus (1991- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T02:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f462c6a5-b178-5acf-b9b0-6d4fabe39269', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f462c6a5-b178-5acf-b9b0-6d4fabe39269'}, {'abstract': 'On a police wiretap in Italy, a mafia suspect was heard bragging that his great-uncle murdered Giuseppe Petrosino, a New York police lieutenant investigating organized crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/nyregion/new-lead-in-1909-killing-of-a-star-officer.html', 'snippet': 'On a police wiretap in Italy, a mafia suspect was heard bragging that his great-uncle murdered Giuseppe Petrosino, a New York police lieutenant investigating organized crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was not long after the turn of the 20th century when Giuseppe Petrosino, the New York Police Department’s most effective weapon against organized crime, was sent to Italy to attack the problem’s roots.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Lead in 1909 Killing of a Star Officer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Lead in 1909 Killing of a Star Officer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palermo (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petrosino, Giuseppe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palazzotto, Domenico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T03:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9bce8a9-f643-50de-a581-8ac21308af1c', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9bce8a9-f643-50de-a581-8ac21308af1c'}, {'abstract': 'The geneticist Svante Paabo created his own research field by sequencing the genomes of ancient humans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/science/searching-for-answers-in-very-old-dna.html', 'snippet': 'The geneticist Svante Paabo created his own research field by sequencing the genomes of ancient humans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As he puts it in the subtitle of his memoir, “Neanderthal Man,” Svante Paabo goes in search of lost genomes. Dr. Paabo, a 59-year-old Swede who leads his own laboratory at the Max Planck Institute for Evolutionary Anthropology in Leipzig, Germany, was the first to extract and sequence the genomes of the ancient humans called Neanderthals and Denisovans, and to compare them with those of modern humans. Genes, and the stories they tell, are texts he reads.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24CONV/24CONV-thumbStandard.jpg'