when-advance-directives-are-ignored/', 'snippet': 'Medical personnel are more likely to pay attention to one type of advance directive, a study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final two years of her mother’s life, Lisa McAllister started carrying copies of her mother’s do-not-resuscitate and power-of-attorney forms in her purse and her car. Her mother was cycling between the hospital, assisted living and rehab — “a round robin of craziness,” said Ms. McAllister, a retired copy editor — and was clear about not wanting to be kept alive with substantially diminished quality of life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Advance Directives Are Ignored', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f2bbf5-56ba-5620-b94f-8197ae53b7f3', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f2bbf5-56ba-5620-b94f-8197ae53b7f3'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/us/your-morning-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the Morning Briefing on NYT Now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':