ritish and Israeli law — that was clearly tailored to the desired result.” The board remains unpersuaded that Mr. Awlaki’s due-process rights were given proper consideration. “More documents must be made public. The public is still in the dark on too many vital questions.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T10:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a34cab8-d980-5983-be78-b629a2fcf72e', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a34cab8-d980-5983-be78-b629a2fcf72e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: King Peter transfers power to Crown Prince Alexander in 1914; the U.S. Army completes a topographic study of the moon in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/in-our-pages-june-25/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: King Peter transfers power to Crown Prince Alexander in 1914; the U.S. Army completes a topographic study of the moon in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/25iht-oldjune25/25iht-oldjune25-articleLarge.png', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/25iht-oldjune25/25iht-oldjune25-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre