 and delivered Senator Thad Cochran a hard-fought victory over his Tea Party challenger, Chris McDaniel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HATTIESBURG, Miss. — With an unusual assist from African-American voters and other Democrats who feared his opponent, Senator Thad Cochran on Tuesday beat back a spirited challenge from State Senator Chris McDaniel, triumphing in a Republican runoff and defeating the Tea Party in the state where the movement’s hopes were bright.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/politics/cochran-hp-1/cochran-hp-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cochran Holds Off Tea Party Challenger in Mississippi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cochran Holds Off Tea Party Challenger in Mississippi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochran, Thad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDaniel, Chris (1972- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T14:35:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0360e3b6-9fb8-5dca-9fae-138b08a420d1', 'word_count': 1290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0360e3b6-9fb8-5dca-9fae-138b08a420d1'}, {'abstract': 'Love is not for the meek.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/orange-is-the-new-black-recap-its-valentines-day-at-the-litch/', 'snippet': 'Love is not for the meek.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Season 2, Episode 6 It’s Valentine’s Day, and love is in the air at the Litch. Crazy, complicated prison love, making it not so much different from love everywhere else. This episode has an almost giddy looseness to it, with dialogue and scenes bleeding into one another – from prison staff into inmates, from Litchfield into Larry’s Brooklyn (Larry – “my sweet, kind, unfocused fiancé,” as Piper describes him). The looseness conveys the messiness of the business at hand – as do the closeups of inmates giving their definitions of love to an off-camera interviewer. (Who turns out to be Piper, with an interest in interviewing that is somewhat duplicitous. More on that below, and while it’s not really much of a spoiler, this is probably a good place to issue the standard spoiler alert.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/24/arts/television/ORANGE/ORANGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge