, 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T16:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b62abc-9b68-54fb-9a38-3f5968d6c056', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b62abc-9b68-54fb-9a38-3f5968d6c056'}, {'abstract': 'Will Torres talks T through an at-home summer training session based on basic gym-class moves and amped up with a weighted bag of sand.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/workout-advice-from-calvin-klein-personal-trainer-will-torres/', 'snippet': 'Will Torres talks T through an at-home summer training session based on basic gym-class moves and amped up with a weighted bag of sand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Squats, push-ups, lunges, sit-ups: these are the physical drills most of us have been familiar with since elementary school gym class. And according to Will Torres — the personal trainer behind Willspace whose clientele includes Calvin Klein, Julia Restoin-Roitfeld, Andy Cohen and the model Ashley Smith — they’re the basis to achieving your ideal body. That may sound like an overly simplistic notion, especially in this era of hybridized fitness routines, but at Torres’s intimate West Village studio, it’s the focus on precision and consistency that render these timeless workouts effective. “There’s no point in progressing to a new exercise if you haven’t perfected fundamental movements like hinging and torque,” Torres says. “And you don’t need a lot of equipment.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Wellness | A Summer Workout From a Personal Trainer to the Fashion Set', 