 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T22:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfcfa2a5-ef94-51db-98fd-1a4619de36c1', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfcfa2a5-ef94-51db-98fd-1a4619de36c1'}, {'abstract': 'It seemed like many voters on social media were more concerned with today’s weather than with the state’s political climate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/24/no-matter-the-political-climate-the-conversation-on-twitter-turns-to-the-weather/', 'snippet': 'It seemed like many voters on social media were more concerned with today’s weather than with the state’s political climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters headed back to polling places in Mississippi on Tuesday to cast ballots in the runoff between Senator Thad Cochran and his Tea Party-backed challenger, State Senator Chris McDaniel. In keeping with a race that has generated its share of political conflict, Mr. Cochran’s and Mr. McDaniel’s partisans were active on Twitter describing Mississippi’s second day at the polls this month in a way that was helpful to their candidates. But it seemed like many voters on social media were more concerned with today’s weather than with the state’s political climate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Matter the Political Climate, the Conversation on Twitter Turns to the Weather', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochran, Thad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDaniel, Chris (1972- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-24T22:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Roston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30eb2723-a46b-50d6-9c4e-8ee8fb488acc', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30eb2723-a46b-50d6-9c4e-8ee8fb488acc'}, {'abstract': 'The World Cup — a.k.a. one of the largest sports fashion catwalks in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2014/06/24/fashion/world-cup-brazil-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'The World Cup — a.k.a. one of the largest sports fashion catwalks in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Cup — a.k.a. one of the largest sports fashion catwalks in the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/fashion/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/fashion/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/fashion/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS/world-cup-brazil-fashion-slide-KCRS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo',