 special treatment in federal tobacco regulations proposed recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Documents released by the federal government\xa0on Tuesday\xa0provided clues about how premium cigars got special treatment in federal tobacco regulations proposed recently. The rules, written by the Food and Drug Administration, originally subjected all cigars to federal regulation. But a proposal to exempt premium cigars surfaced after the rules were submitted to the White House for editing last year, the documents show. Matthew L. Myers, president of the Campaign for Tobacco Free Kids, an advocacy group, said an exemption, if made final, would set a troubling precedent for the future of tobacco regulation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Premium-Cigar Exemption Traced', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Premium-Cigar Exemption Traced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cigars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T00:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/96d02183-a7f4-529a-86a7-b13955e87aa5', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96d02183-a7f4-529a-86a7-b13955e87aa5'}, {'abstract': 'Why two Arab gover