ance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T00:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/541c5eea-26b8-542e-9973-8f1d60f37f92', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541c5eea-26b8-542e-9973-8f1d60f37f92'}, {'abstract': 'A Federal District Court judge on Tuesday rejected a request by a high-profile detainee at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/us/guantanamo-detainee-rebuffed.html', 'snippet': 'A Federal District Court judge on Tuesday rejected a request by a high-profile detainee at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Federal District Court judge on Tuesday rejected a request by a high-profile detainee at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, that the judge order his release because he is suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder and other mental and physical ailments. The habeas corpus challenge was brought in April on behalf of Shaker Aamer, 45, a Saudi citizen and former British resident. Judge Rosemary M. Collyer gave her rejection in a terse one-page order; an accompanying memorandum opinion explaining her reasoning was sealed. The Justice Department’s filings in the case were also sealed, but Judge Collyer ordered it to file a public version of her order and its documents by July 9. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guantánamo Detainee Rebuffed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guantánamo Detainee Rebuffed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aamer, Shaker', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T00:58:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/65e33eb5-3f20-586e-8c26-019d4e4f4a82', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65e33eb5-3f20-586e-8c26-019d4e4f4a82'}, {'abstract': 'A new campaign, aimed at mothers between 25 to 45, plays off the fact that the snack is known for the prize inside its box.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/business/media/cracker-jack-wants-to-break-out-of-the-ballpark.html', 'snippet': 'A new campaign, aimed at mothers between 25 to 45, plays off the fact that the snack is known for the prize inside its box.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT would be impossible to put a dollar value on how much “Take Me Out to the Ball Game,” the 1908 song ritually sung by baseball fans during the seventh-inning stretch, has had for the 121-year-old snack named in the refrain, “Buy me some peanuts and Cracker Jack.” But in a segment for “On the Media,” the syndicated public radio show produced by WNYC, Mike Pesca once tried to assess the value, equating it with Cracker Jack placing an advertisement along outfield walls of all of the major league’s 30 stadiums, a marketing campaign that would cost the brand about $25 million a year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1007}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 611, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1221, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/business/Adco/Adco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracker Jack Wants to Break Out of the Ballpark', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Familiar Snack Wants to Break Out of the Ballpark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Andrew Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pepsico Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T00:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb6dd78b-462d-5bb9-987a-43362884d38b', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb6dd78b-462d-5bb9-987a-43362884d38b'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s highest court ruled Tuesday that a proposal to repeal the state’s expanded casino gambling law can appear on the ballot this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/us/massachusetts-court-allows-public-to-vote-on-repealing-casino-law.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s highest court ruled Tuesday that a proposal to repeal the state’s expanded casino gambling law can appear on the ballot this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state’s highest court ruled Tuesday that a proposal to repeal the state’s expanded casino gambling law can appear on the ballot this fall. The ruling by the Supreme Judicial Court overturned a decision by Attorney General Martha Coakley, setting the stage for what is likely to be a closely watched and expensive campaign. The 2011 law allows for up to three resort-style casinos and one slots parlor to be built in the state. Casino opponents say they have more than twice as many signatures than required to get the question on the ballot; those signatures are being certified. One license has been provisionally awarded in Springfield, pending the outcome of the repeal effort; the slots parlor is under construction in Plainville. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Court Allows Publ