: 'New York Today: Reading Room Refugees', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T09:59:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal and Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d35c10d-a8df-5162-9bac-d99b045d1331', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d35c10d-a8df-5162-9bac-d99b045d1331'}, {'abstract': 'A vertical map representing China’s claims in the South China Sea shows two disputed clusters of islands entirely within Chinese territory.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/china-unveils-new-map-of-south-china-sea/', 'snippet': 'A vertical map representing China’s claims in the South China Sea shows two disputed clusters of islands entirely within Chinese territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China is standing tall over its expansive claims to territory in the South China Sea. This week, Hunan Map Publishing House unveiled a new map of China — a vertical representation of the country that includes the vast body of water south of Hainan Island. China’s assertions of ownership in the South China Sea have put it at odds with at least four Southeast Asian nations, which have competing claims, and with the United States, which has said that China’s actions in the region — including having a state-owned oil company place an exploratory oil rig near the Vietnamese coast in May — are creating instability.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Unveils New Map of South China Sea', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Nationalist Party (Taiwan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hainan Island (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paracel Islands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spratly Islands', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T10:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e168de-d9b3-5687-b761-598402dcb8dc', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e168de-d9b3-5687-b761-598402dcb8dc'}, {'abstract': 'A ship has begun mapping the Indian Ocean floor in preparation for a renewed search for Malaysia Airlines Flight 370, though the effort has been complicated by a lack of satellite images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/world/asia/malaysia-airlines-plane-search.html', 'snippet': 'A ship has begun mapping the Indian Ocean floor in preparation for a renewed search for Malaysia Airlines Flight 370, though the effort has been complicated by a lack of satellite images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANBERRA, Australia — A commercial vessel under contract from the Australian government has begun mapping the floor of the southern Indian Ocean in preparation for a renewed search for Malaysia Airlines’ missing Flight 370, but that search has been complicated by a complete lack of satellite images of the new search area from the week after the plane disappeared.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Area of Seafloor Is Mapped in Jet Search', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Area of Seafloor Is Mapped in Jet Search', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 370', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hishammuddin Hussein', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indian Ocean', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T10:36:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba3788e4-b977-5694-b1c7-63ecafc034f9', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba3788e4-b977-5694-b1c7-63ecafc034f9'}, {'abstract': 'The British prime minister’s case against Jean-Claude Juncker could well boomerang and feed anti-E.U. sentiments in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/opinion/mr-camerons-losing-battle.html', 'snippet': 'The British prime minister’s case against Jean-Claude Juncker could well boomerang and feed anti-E.U. sentiments in Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Selecting the president of the European Commission, the powerful executive branch of the European Union, has always entailed a lot of politicking and bluster, and there’s been no shortage of that in advance of a meeting of European leaders later this week. The difference this time is that Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain is staunchly opposed to the likely pick, Jean-Claude Juncker of Luxembourg, and that is shaping into a potential turning point for the entire European project. Mr. Cameron has a good case, but he should make sure that his looming defeat does not turn into an irrevocable march toward the “Brexit,” a British exit from the European Union.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Cameron’s Losing Battle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Mr. Cameron's Losing Battle", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juncker, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luxembourg', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T10:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7394b22e-1823-5b75-b9cf-d16ea9112a98', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7394b22e-1823-5b75-b9cf-d16ea9112a98'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: France orders the closing of a refugee camp in the south in 1939; Robert F. Kennedy visits Berlin in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/in-our-pages-june-26/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: France orders the closing of a refugee camp in the south in 1939; Robert F. Kennedy visits Berlin in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': '1939: Camp Ordered Abandoned', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Our Pages: June 26', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Civil War (1936-39)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Robert Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T10:42:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9572c973-a3e0-5ee3-958a-85401b5bc466', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9572c973-a3e0-5ee3-958a-85401b5bc466'}, {'abstract': 'The steady decline in interest rates has pushed pension funds away from bonds and toward riskier investments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/upshot/why-government-pension-funds-became-addicted-to-risk.html', 'snippet': 'The steady decline in interest rates has pushed pension funds away from bonds and toward riskier investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A public pension fund works like this: The government promises to make payments to its employees after they retire; it invests money now and uses those investments, and the returns on them, to make those promised payments later.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/upshot/00up-pension/00up-pension-articleLarge.png', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/upshot/00up-pension/00up-pension-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/upshot/00up-pension/00up-pension-jumbo.png', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/upshot/00up-pension/00up-pension-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/upshot/00up-pension/00up-pension-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', '