 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a4da04b-cb51-5ac8-ae03-19a62406594f', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a4da04b-cb51-5ac8-ae03-19a62406594f'}, {'abstract': 'The “uterus-space-groove-rock” quartet Wannabe Jalva is set to go global with their new single, “Mainline,” which debuts exclusively here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/wannabe-jalva-brazilian-rock-band-to-get-you-into-the-world-cup-groove/', 'snippet': 'The “uterus-space-groove-rock” quartet Wannabe Jalva is set to go global with their new single, “Mainline,” which debuts exclusively here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s World Cup season, and native Brazilians can’t get enough of the attention. “My country is living and breathing soccer more than usual,” says Rafael Rocha, the frontman for the band Wannabe Jalva, which is based in Porto Alegre in the south of the country. “Brazil has kind of stopped for a bit.” Rocha and his bandmates Felipe Puperi, Fernando Paulista and Tiago Abrahão are in an especially celebratory mood these days: they’ve just finished their upcoming, as-yet-untitled EP, and are planning to take their sound — which they’ve curiously taken to calling “uterus-space-groove-rock” — global. “That’s a term we put together only because everybody needs a label,” Rocha explains. “We have so many influences, from newer acts like Queens of the Stone Age to older ones like the Doors. We also have a funk and soul vibe going on. Our music somehow links all of that together … we try not to place any boundaries on ourselves.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/t-magazine/25wannabe-ledonne/25wannabe-ledonne-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | A Brazilian Rock Band to Get You Into the World Cup Groove', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T13: