://article/7bf78a00-d283-5738-ad92-1ffe8024929f', 'word_count': 1313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf78a00-d283-5738-ad92-1ffe8024929f'}, {'abstract': 'Here, the annual fine art and antique fair’s chairman joins the director of the Victoria and Albert Museum, Elizabeth Hurley and Sir Paul Smith in discussing their favorite finds at this year’s event.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/masterpiece-london-2014-finest-offerings/', 'snippet': 'Here, the annual fine art and antique fair’s chairman joins the director of the Victoria and Albert Museum, Elizabeth Hurley and Sir Paul Smith in discussing their favorite finds at this year’s event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sandwiched between Royal Ascot and the Henley Royal Regatta, the fifth edition of Masterpiece London, the annual fine art and antiques fair, opens its doors tomorrow. For one week, everything from 19th-century Italian paintings to a 2013 Italian Maserati will be up for sale on the South Grounds of the historic Royal Hospital Chelsea.“The London Season has made its return,” says the event’s chairman, Philip Hewat-Jaboor, “and I see Masterpiece very much as the glue that cements the astonishing array of activities in these summer months.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closer Look at 10 of Masterpiece London’s Finest Offerings', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurley, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T15:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gay Gassmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gassmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b6ba91-13c6-526e-abaa-92ab426296a5', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b6ba91-13c6-526e-abaa-92ab426296a5'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to give visitors an “elevated experience,” and better manage tourist traffic, NBCUniversal has plans to reconstruct a mezzanine lounge for visitors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/nyregion/at-30-rock-recreating-a-rotunda-with-a-nod-to-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking to give visitors an “elevated experience,” and better manage tourist traffic, NBCUniversal has plans to reconstruct a mezzanine lounge for visitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time in the 1930s and ’40s when the excitement of attending an NBC broadcast at Rockefeller Center began long before you were ushered into Studio 6B, where Bob Hope held forth, or the astonishing 1,500-seat Studio 8H, home of Arturo Toscanini and the NBC Symphony Orchestra.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/nyregion/BLOCKSweb1/BLOCKSweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/nyregion/BLOCKSweb1/BLOCKSweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 552, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/nyregion/BLOCKSweb1/BLOCKSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnai