 down, and there it stays, until you are ready to pick it up again. But in two new picture books, “My Pet Book,” written and illustrated by Bob Staake (“The Red Lemon,” “Bluebird,” “The Donut Chef”) and “Brother Hugo and the Bear,” written by Katy Beebe and illustrated by S.D. Schindler, precious books go missing, and have to be found — or recreated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/books/25childrens/25childrens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Budding Book Lovers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staake, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beebe, Katy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schindler, S D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T15:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Harrison Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/12435c00-6cb9-5035-973e-94f547165613', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12435c00-6cb9-5035-973e-94f547165613'}, {'abstract': 'As Canada reconsiders its prostitution laws, the debate around sex work has spread to related issues of women’s rights, JAKE FLANAGIN writes.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/what-it-takes-to-legalize-sex-work/', 'snippet': 'As Canada reconsiders its prostitution laws, the debate around sex work has spread to related issues of women’s rights, JAKE FLANAGIN writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill introduced in Canada by Prime Minister Stephen Harper’s Conservative government would criminalize buying sexual services but would not necessarily make selling them illegal. It follows a Canadian Supreme Court ruling last year that overturned most laws governing the sex trade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/opinion/nyto-sexwork/nyto-sexwork-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/opinion/nyto-sexwork/nyto-sexwork-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargew