a0Posted a little over a week ago on the website of Amnesty International’s French-speaking division in Belgium, it\xa0showed the rock star Iggy Pop, his face battered and bruised, saying, “Justin Bieber is the future of rock ’n’ roll.” Underneath was the slogan: “Torture a man and he will tell you anything.” In smaller letters it continued: “Besides being inhumane, torture doesn’t work. Let’s stop it.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Much Creative License: Amnesty International Withdraws Iggy Pop Ad', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights Group Pulls Ad Featuring Iggy Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pop, Iggy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T16:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c90b92f-1db5-5dac-b51f-4850abf3bd5b', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c90b92f-1db5-5dac-b51f-4850abf3bd5b'}, {'abstract': 'A new app from 2wice Arts Foundation is based on choreography by Justin Peck of New York City Ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/arts/dance/youre-the-choreographer-an-ipads-your-stage.html', 'snippet': 'A new app from 2wice Arts Foundation is based on choreography by Justin Peck of New York City Ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There I was, riding the subway over the Williamsburg Bridge, making a dance. The stage was my iPad. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You’re the Choreographer, an iPad’s Your Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mobile Choreography, at Your Fingertips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '2wice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Justin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarr, Patsy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ulbricht, Daniel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T16:40:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca8a2131-636b-5ecd-8a43-7320589ace3b', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca8a2131-636b-5ecd-8a43-7320589ace3b'}, {'abstract': 'A three-judge panel deemed the ban unconstitutional in the first ruling on same-sex marriage at the appellate level since the Supreme Court struck down the Defense of Marriage Act in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/us/us-appeals-court-rejects-utahs-ban-on-gay-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'A three-judge panel deemed the ban unconstitutional in the first ruling on same-sex marriage at the appellate level since the Supreme Court struck down the Defense of Marriage Act in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — Expanding a streak of legal victories for same-sex marriage, a federal appeals court ruled on Wednesday that states may not deny same-sex couples their “fundamental right” to marry, overturning Utah’s voter-approved ban on such unions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Appeals Court Rejects Utah’s Ban on Gay Marriage, Prodding Supreme Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appeals Court Rejects Utah’s Ban on Gay Marriage, Prodding Supreme Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T16:47:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdeea1bd-da14-515f-8a47-fc6106000860', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdeea1bd-da14-515f-8a47-fc6106000860'}, {'abstract': 'Watching a recent ISIS video of militants forcing Iraqi soldiers to switch allegiance, a former Marine wonders what happened to the Iraqi soldiers he helped train in Anbar Province, some of them Sunnis with little chance for promotion in the Shiite-led army.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/swearing-allegiance-iraq/', 'snippet': 'Watching a recent ISIS video of militants forcing Iraqi soldiers to switch allegiance, a former Marine wonders what happened to the Iraqi soldiers he helped train in Anbar Province, some of them Sunnis with little chance for promotion in the Shiit...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a few days last week before YouTube pulled the video, “Clanging of the Swords IV” gave a graphic visual account of the violence unfolding in Iraq. The hourlong reel is a mash-up of attacks, allegedly by militants with the Sunni extremist group Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, against Iraqi security forces: drive-by shootings; roadside bombings; a beheading. Like most jihadi videos, it has a soundtrack of atonal religious chanting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Iraq, Switching Allegiance Once Again', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANBAR PROVINCE (IRAQ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T16:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Blake J. Rice', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Blake', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rice', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7a7ee0-1aad-5fca-b9e5-61e0f360ce6c', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7a7ee0-1aad-5fca-b9e5-61e0f360ce6c'}, {'abstract': 'Jill Sigman’s "(Perma)Culture” examines how dance movements alter the perception of space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/arts/dance/jill-sigmans-perma-culture-at-danspace-project.html', 'snippet': 'Jill Sigman’s "(Perma)Culture” examines how dance movements alter the perception of space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Jill Sigman, it’s safe to say, is fueled by a sensitivity for perceiving the movement in nature and the nature in movement. Her latest work, “(Perma)Culture,” performed last Thursday at Danspace Project, gather