rning a profit when it lost half its space in Hong Kong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ask most winemakers about the pitfalls of harvest, and they talk about excessive rain or pesky bugs. Lysanne Tusar, owner of the 8th Estate Winery, has a more unusual problem: the rising cost of rent in the city.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Challenges of Starting an Urban Winery', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Urban Winery in Hong Kong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T18:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colleen DeBaise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeBaise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1591c4a0-51a7-5166-943e-9bc375356a11', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1591c4a0-51a7-5166-943e-9bc375356a11'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the men’s fashion week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/the-scene-paris-mens-fashion-week-haider-ackermann-springsummer-2015/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the men’s fashion week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the men’s fashion week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Scene | Paris Men’s Fashion Week: Haider Ackermann Spring/Summer 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Men's Fashion Week", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackermann, Haider', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T18:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerio Mezzanotti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerio', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mezzanotti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e89dec37-c8c5-55cf-affc-d314c9166877', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e89dec37-c8c5-55cf-affc-d314c9166877'}, {'abstract': 'A portrait of a homeless man, “Man With a Plaid Blanket,” by Thomas Ganter, won the award for $50,922.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/25/german-artist-wins-the-bp-portrait-award-with-depiction-of-homeless-man/', 'snippet': 'A portrait of a homeless man, “Man With a Plaid Blanket,” by Thomas Ganter, won the award for $50,922.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A portrait of a homeless man, “Man With a Plaid Blanket,” by Thomas Ganter, has won the BP Portrait Award, the National Portrait Gallery announced here on Tuesday. Mr. Ganter, who is the first German artist to win the prize, an annual award aimed at encouraging artists to focus on portrait-painting, received £30,000 or roughly $50,922 at an award ceremony hosted by the actor Nigel Havers. The prize, which is sponsored by BP, also includes a commission to paint a portrait for the National Portrait Gallery’s permanent collection. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Artist Wins the BP Portrait Award With Depiction of Homeless Man', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Portrait Gallery (London)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T18:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e1f0551-439a-5fe9-80fd-1faf4b302f93', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e1f0551-439a-5fe9-80fd-1faf4b302f93'}, {'abstract': 'Tech companies are poised to compete in selling services to businesses and gathering information on who does what within them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/technology/google-microsoft-and-others-delve-deeper-into-cloud-storage-for-businesses.html', 'snippet': 'Tech companies are poised to compete in selling services to businesses and gathering information on who does what within them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — File cabinets — the digital kind — may be the technology industry’s next big battleground.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google, Microsoft and Others Delve Deeper Into Cloud Storage for Businesses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'majo