 Haley Barbour political machine\xa0—\xa0pulling out an unlikely comeback in the Mississippi Senate run-off by persuading African-American Democrats to turn out in a G.O.P. primary is such an occasion: A time to savor some of the historical ironies at work, to appreciate the establishment’s back-to-the-wall strategery, and to let the Penn Warren-ish phrase “Barbour brothers” roll over and over on your tongue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Machiavelli in Mississippi', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbour, Haley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochran, Thad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T19:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b74b5bff-f4b7-56cc-adc4-3d9cdb7aa482', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b74b5bff-f4b7-56cc-adc4-3d9cdb7aa482'}, {'abstract': 'Kristin Newman, a comedy writer, talks about finding romance while on vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/travel/the-art-of-the-vacationship.html', 'snippet': 'Kristin Newman, a comedy writer,