nd-off-the-runways.html', 'snippet': 'In London, Milan and Paris, journalists and models prefer leather lace-ups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is the runway a two-way street? The thought occurred to one observer as he wended his way through the men’s fashion weeks. One particular style of shoe — the white sneaker, low-topped, often in leather — recurred again and again, on the runway and in the front rows. It raised the question: Do trends trickle down, or do they trickle up?', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1539, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZSNEAKERA/26ZSNEAKERA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Way Do the Sneaker Prints Lead?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Which Way Do the Sneaker Prints Lead?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sneakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Stan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Common Projects (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T21:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d2eabea-4a70-5089-9f04-44e15bd28d12', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d2eabea-4a70-5089-9f04-44e15bd28d12'}, {'abstract': 'A first look at Loewe’s men’s line under the creative direction of Jonathan Anderson, and its new advertising campaign', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/fashion/first-look-at-jonathan-andersons-mens-line-for-loewe.html', 'snippet': 'A first look at Loewe’s men’s line under the creative direction of Jonathan Anderson, and its new advertising campaign', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two days before his men’s wear presentation for Loewe, the first since his appointment as creative director last September, Jonathan Anderson was standing at the company’s soon-to-be-former headquarters on the Rue François Ier in Paris. It would be a goodbye of sorts to the place where he has spent much of his time these last eight months. The presentation will be held at the new offices, on St.-Sulpice. The space will be not only an office and headquarters, but for the first time, the home of the design team, which Mr. Anderson has imported from the label’s native Madrid.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26ZROW1/26ZROW1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Provocateur Prepares to Show His Quiet Side', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Provocateur Prepares to Sho