rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcfacd80-f45d-5b83-9bb6-53078de8a9d3', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcfacd80-f45d-5b83-9bb6-53078de8a9d3'}, {'abstract': 'Borrowing flourishes from recent fall runways; Versace and Superga team up on a sneaker and more shopping news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/fashion/Furry-Fringes-a-Look-for-Summer-Versace-and-Superga-Team-Up-on-a-Sneaker-Cotton-Bag-Replaces-Plastic.html', 'snippet': 'Borrowing flourishes from recent fall runways; Versace and Superga team up on a sneaker and more shopping news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Texture was big on the fall runways, which were a frenzy of fur and feathers in artful assemblages and rainbows of colors. No need, though, to wait to try out an artsy-craftsy look for yourself. For summer, think fur-like. Ryan Roche, who works in upstate New York, uses crocheted cashmere for her lovely furry fringe sweaters. Maria Cornejo used a synthetic feather effect for a shrug and as trim on a silk dress. Other labels, like Chloé and Samuji, a young Finnish line to watch, have affixed fringe all over lightweight sweaters and linen dresses. At a recent Acria event to raise money for H.I.V. research and education, the fashionable art director Sofía Sanchez Barrenechea wore an ostrich feather and faille tulip dress from Jason Wu’s spring 2010 collection, proving that not every soiree calls for a brand-new frock, just one you want to reach out and touch.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26BROWSING_COMBO/26ZBROWSING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/fashion/26BROWSING_COMBO/26ZBROWSING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 's