27213-27a9-5b0e-bdd4-c38f5f56550d'}, {'abstract': 'A diagramed deal from the first round of the European Championships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/senior-teams-at-european-championships-in-croatia.html', 'snippet': 'A diagramed deal from the first round of the European Championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1960s and ’70s, the battle for the medals at the European Bridge Championship was among just a few countries. Back then, it was vital for the contenders to score as many victory points as possible against the weaker nations. In particular, the strong teams gained many points from superior declarer play and defense. Today, bidding has assumed a more important role. Also, competitive bidding has become much more aggressive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 561, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1053, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/crosswords/bridge/26card/26card-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senior Teams at European Championships in Croatia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senior Teams at European Championships in Croatia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T22:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a75ec78f-a491-5361-bb8d-1a416a073f1e', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a75ec78f-a491-5361-bb8d-1a416a073f1e'}, {'abstract': 'The 2014 River to River Festival includes performances at Governors Island, Pier 15 and a South Street Seaport bar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/arts/dance/river-to-river-festival-embraces-ambiguity.html', 'snippet': 'The 2014 River to River Festival includes performances at Governors Island, Pier 15 and a South Street Seaport bar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weather is always a collaborator in River to River, the Lower Manhattan Cultural Council’s annual festival of site-specific performance, and last weekend it was in peak form. The festival’s organizer, Sam Miller, deserved nothing less; his lineup this year is stellar. Lucid skies, light breezes and just-right temperatures made a dancegoer rejoice in the concept of piers, lawns and seaside cafes as theatrical spaces, as did the stealthy use of those spaces by the artists who occupied them. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/arts/LMCC1/LMCC1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Loneliness or Something Like It', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing Loneliness or Something Like It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'River to River Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T22:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/461c1a4d-a275-5fce-bd13-c6754bd6e02f', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/461c1a4d-a275-5fce-bd13-c6754bd6e02f'}, {'abstract': 'The Knights chamber orchestra and the pianist Timo Andres presented Mr. Andres’s revision of Mozart’s unfinished “Coronation” Concerto in Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/arts/music/the-knights-and-timo-andres-fill-out-mozarts-coronation.html', 'snippet': 'The Knights chamber orchestra and the pianist Timo Andres presented Mr. Andres’s revision of Mozart’s unfinished “Coronation” Concerto in Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a time that has brought us renovations and revisions of Vivaldi’s “Four Seasons,” Beethoven’s Seventh Symphony and Stravinsky’s “Rite of Spring,” among other overhauls, do we really need a recomposition of Mozart’s “Coronation” Concerto?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lending Mozart a Left Hand', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lending Mozart a Left Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andres, Timo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knights, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Naumburg Bandshell (Central Park)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T22:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'last