 in Paris is the epicenter of bohemian bourgeois French style. “What I like about this neighborhood is that it is romantic and fashionable,” said Johanna Lebrun, who was in the area riding her Peugeot bike from the 1950s. “The idea is not necessarily to show off wealth, but to show a cool attitude.” Wearing a floral, flowing Vanessa Bruno dress (which she said was like wearing a painting) and carrying a 50-year-old Hermès bag, Ms. Lebrun was channeling just that attitude. This interview has been edited and condensed.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Teeth in Her Look', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting Teeth in Her Look', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-25T22:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefania Rousselle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rousselle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ee628df-6e36-500e-8420-8fad747dd589', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ee628df-6e36-500e-8420-8fad747dd589'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors can get details on attractions, animals, camps, parking, the weather and more on their mobile devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/technology/personaltech/navigating-national-parks-with-rich-digital-guides.html', 'snippet': 'Visitors can get details on attractions, animals, camps, parking, the weather and more on their mobile devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT wasn’t long ago that a trip to a national park meant packing books, paper maps, a guide