1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eff5d32b-2041-5526-ba4c-8ddff7ae97f5', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eff5d32b-2041-5526-ba4c-8ddff7ae97f5'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations named three international experts on Wednesday to be advisers on an inquiry into human rights abuses in the final months of Sri Lanka’s war against ethnic Tamil insurgents in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/world/asia/sri-lanka-advisers-set-for-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations named three international experts on Wednesday to be advisers on an inquiry into human rights abuses in the final months of Sri Lanka’s war against ethnic Tamil insurgents in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations named three international experts on Wednesday to be advisers on an inquiry into human rights abuses in the final months of Sri Lanka’s war against ethnic Tamil insurgents in 2009. The three are Martti Ahtisaari, a former president of Finland and Nobel Peace Prize-winning diplomat; Silvia Cartwright, who served as a judge on the war crimes tribunal in Cambodia; and Asma Jahangir, a veteran human rights defender from Pakistan. The United Nations Human Rights Council voted in March to authorize the inquiry. Its 12-member team of investigators is supposed to present preliminary findings as early as September. Whether the experts will be allowed entry into Sri Lanka, which has resisted such an inquiry, remains unclear. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sri Lanka: Advisers Set for Inquiry', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sri Lanka: Advisers Set for Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons',