alia — Nearly four months after Malaysia Airlines Flight 370 vanished into the night, Australian transportation officials said in a report on Thursday that the plane kept flying until it ran out of fuel, most likely because the cockpit crew had become unresponsive, perhaps because of oxygen deprivation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressure Loss Is Explored in Vanishing of Jetliner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressure Loss Is Explored in Vanishing of Jetliner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 370', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indian Ocean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houston, Angus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T08:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/321d9d0b-ffeb-5617-9b35-4a51a612d15c', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/321d9d0b-ffeb-5617-9b35-4a51a612d15c'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation into sexual abuse by the disgraced television host Jimmy Savile at state-funded medical institutions in Britain revealed episodes involving patients ages 5 to 75.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/world/europe/britain-jimmy-savile-sexual-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation into sexual abuse by the disgraced television host Jimmy Savile at state-funded medical institutions in Britain revealed episodes involving patients ages 5 to 75.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British health authorities said on Thursday that inquiries into sexual abuse by the disgraced television host Jimmy Savile at state-funded medical facilities had revealed “truly awful” episodes involving patients ages 5 to 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.K. Inquiry Finds ‘Truly Awful’ Sexual Abuse by TV Host at Medical Facilities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savile Inquiry Finds ‘Truly Awful’ Abuse at Medical Units', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savile, Jimmy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Health Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T08:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a74607-63ef-58b7-8013-59c6ad53f25c', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a74607-63ef-58b7-8013-59c6ad53f25c'}, {'abstract': 'Under British takeover rules, AMS has until July 24 to make a firm offer for Dialog Semiconductor, which is based in London and listed in Frankfurt. The combined company would have a market capitalization of nearly $5 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/semiconductor-makers-ams-and-dialog-in-early-talks/', 'snippet': 'Under British takeover rules, AMS has until July 24 to make a firm offer for Dialog Semiconductor, which is based in London and listed in Frankfurt. The combined company would have a market capitalization of nearly $5 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The Austrian semiconductor company AMS confirmed on Thursday that it was in preliminary talks about a “possible merger of equals” with the London-based Dialog Semiconductor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Semiconductor Makers AMS and Dialog in Early Talks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T08:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d25cd1-d0a3-55d6-b964-70ebe4d1ebe3', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d25cd1-d0a3-55d6-b964-70ebe4d1ebe3'}, {'abstract': 'The L.S.E., which already owns the operator of the FTSE 100, said it was “a rare opportunity” to acquire a high quality American business with a leading global brand.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/london-stock-exchange-to-buy-russell-investments-for-2-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'The L.S.E., which already owns the operator of the FTSE 100, said it was “a rare opportunity” to acquire a high quality American business with a leading global brand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The London Stock Exchange said on Thursday that it had agreed to pay $2.7 billion in cash for Russell Investments, the owner of the Russell 2000 stock market index.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Stock Exchange to Buy Russell Investments for $2.7 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expanding a Platform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russell 2,000 Stock Index', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rolet, Xavier', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northwestern Mutual Life Insurance Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russell Investments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T08:53:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a02f0b15-4364-58b2-aa3a-49eb547b8ab5', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a02f0b15-4364-58b2-aa3a-49eb547b8ab5'}, {'abstract': 'The South Carolina governor went from potential presidential contender to late-night punch line. Now he’s just a junior congressman trying to find his way in a divided G.O.P.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/magazine/mark-sanfords-path-of-most-resistance.html', 'snippet': 'The South Carolina governor went from potential presidential contender to late-night punch line. Now he’s just a junior congressman trying to find his way in a divided G.O.P.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It had been a 14-hour day of campaign-style barnstorming, but at nearly 11 p.m. there was something Mark Sanford felt compelled to show me. We were hiking across the Coosaw Plantation, an enviable slice of Southern landscape that Sanford’s family owns. Nestled in the marshy South Carolina coastline, it has ancient live oaks and twisting palmettos, cascading Spanish moss and views of the Coosaw River and the Atlantic beyond. But I could see none of it as we walked in the pitch black.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29sanford1/mag-29sanford-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29sanford1/mag-29sanford-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29sanford1/mag-29sanford-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29sanford1/mag-29sanford-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty