The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/202f0bf3-5644-59e1-bd93-296a364a5ff9', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202f0bf3-5644-59e1-bd93-296a364a5ff9'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Berger has relied on his knowledge of Yiddish throughout 30 years as a reporter at The Times, including at a state senator’s trial that ultimately hinged on Yiddish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/06/26/no-order-in-the-court-without-yiddish/', 'snippet': 'Joseph Berger has relied on his knowledge of Yiddish throughout 30 years as a reporter at The Times, including at a state senator’s trial that ultimately hinged on Yiddish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once the sounds of Yiddish filled the streets of New York. Not so much anymore. But a Times reporter, Joseph Berger, grew up with Yiddish. His knowledge of the language helped him cover a recent corruption trial in which a key government informer was a Hasidic developer who employed Yiddish in many of his recorded conversations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/berger/berger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/berger/berger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/berger/berger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/25/blogs/berger/berger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio