st year to a disappointing 1.5 percent. Yet the labor market continues to deliver good news, and over the same period, the unemployment rate fell by more than a full percentage point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Growth Is Up, Production Down', 'kicker': 'Mixed Signals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross National Product (GNP)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T13:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a7c5e1c-b5ee-5f35-b7c6-08d7a97ef238', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a7c5e1c-b5ee-5f35-b7c6-08d7a97ef238'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “The Two Hotel Francforts” was struck reading “Middlemarch” in Rome at age 20. “That feeling of being unequal to antiquity — no one has ever described it so well as Eliot.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/books/review/david-leavitt-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “The Two Hotel Francforts” was struck reading “Middlemarch” in Rome at age 20. “That feeling of being unequal to antiquity — no one has ever described it so well as Eliot.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author of “The Two Hotel Francforts” was struck reading “Middlemarch” in Rome at age 20. “That feeling of being unequal to antiquity — no one has ever described it so well as Eliot.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page':