 threat, but the size of the mission will drop to a dozen or so advisers from its current 320 service members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/world/asia/us-will-disband-terrorism-task-force-in-philippines.html', 'snippet': 'American Special Forces will continue to help Philippine security forces counter a smaller, lingering Islamist threat, but the size of the mission will drop to a dozen or so advisers from its current 320 service members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — An elite American military counterterrorism unit that has been operating in the southern Philippines for more than a decade is being phased out, the Pentagon’s Pacific Command said Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Phasing Out Its Counterterrorism Unit in Philippines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Phasing Out Its Counterterrorism Unit in Philippines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABU SAYYAF', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T14:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Whaley and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whaley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf9b477-c4b0-50dd-8808-3363d8ceefdf', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf9b477-c4b0-50dd-8808-3363d8ceefdf'}, {'abstract': 'Germany has advanced and must draw to win the group. The U.S. tops the group with a win, but candidly will be happy with a draw and advancement.', 'web_url': 'https://sports.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/u-s-vs-germany-world-cup-2014-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'Germany has advanced and must draw to win the group. The U.S. tops the group with a win, but candidly will be happy with a draw and advancement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Germany has scored six goals in two games, it has done so with a deliberate passing style, rather than a frenzied attack. Look for more of the same, especially since a draw is good enough for Germany to win the group. The United States may look for a slow pace too, especially after having played its previous game in the steamy rain forest. The U.S. tops the group with a win, but candidly will be happy with a draw and advancement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. vs. Germany: World Cup 2014 Live Blog', 'kicker': 'Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T14:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '