ader and composer, known for her big and small bands and ambitious collaborations with Charlie Haden and Gary Burton, among others; George Coleman, the saxophonist and bandleader, who first became a standard-bearer through his work with Miles Davis and Herbie Hancock in the mid-’60s; Charles Lloyd, the saxophonist, flutist and bandleader, who made popular jazz records in the late 1960s, largely dropped out of jazz for a decade afterward, and has been on a consistent climb since; and Joe Segal, owner of the Jazz Showcase in Chicago since 1947. Each of the recipients, announced on Wednesday, will receive $25,000. They will be honored at an awards ceremony and concert at Jazz at Lincoln Center on April 20, 2015. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NEA Names 4 New Jazz Masters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Crop of Jazz Masters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bley, Carla', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T15:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e96109e-9bfc-542d-a0cf-f3147c75e547', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e96109e-9bfc-542d-a0cf-f3147c75e547'}, {'abstract': 'Ghana atta