0b2b0505-d3fe-5c52-b09c-4db62e904c3c'}, {'abstract': 'Over the weekend, Akiko Thurnauer closed the doors to Family Recipe with a celebratory meal.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/family-recipe-closes-sunday-night-beloved-lower-east-side-nook/', 'snippet': 'Over the weekend, Akiko Thurnauer closed the doors to Family Recipe with a celebratory meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Charlotte Druckman and the photographer Melanie Dunea spend Sunday evenings at New York City dining establishments to find out what’s new with the people behind them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Night Dinner | Closing Time at a Beloved Lower East Side Nook', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Family Recipe (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T17:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlotte Druckman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlotte', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Druckman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/455401a3-b6d5-5912-8792-3c358217b104', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/455401a3-b6d5-5912-8792-3c358217b104'}, {'abstract': 'In the 1970s, the first polling partnership between two major national news organizations in the United States created a collaboration that became the blueprint for rival alliances between television networks and newspapers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/06/26/times-polling-a-history/', 'snippet': 'In the 1970s, the first polling partnership between two major national news organizations in the United States created a collaboration that became the blueprint for rival alliances between television networks and newspapers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, The Times released a poll on a variety of subjects from approval ratings for President Obama’s foreign policy to support for the Tea Party. Polling will increase as the midterm elections draw near. Marjorie Connelly, editor of news surveys, shared some of the history of the Times polling department. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading Minds: A History of Times Polling', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connelly, Marjorie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Gerald Rudolph Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitofsky, Warren J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T17:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None