s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Checks and Checking Accounts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T20:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58259438-8eb8-516c-9f1b-f6cbc588ec4f', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58259438-8eb8-516c-9f1b-f6cbc588ec4f'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday handed down a major decision concerning a president’s power to appoint executive branch officials when the Senate is in recess without going through the confirmation process. The court rejected the validity of four appointments President Obama made in January 2012, when the question of whether the Senate was in recess was in dispute. While on the surface the ruling was a blow to executive power, on a deeper level it was also a victory for executive power because it rolled back an appeals court ruling that had gone much further in restricting such authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/06/25/us/annotated-supreme-court-recess-decision.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday handed down a major decision concerning a president’s power to appoint executive branch officials when the Senate is in recess without going through the confirmation process. The court rejected the validity of four ap...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday handed down a major decision concerning a president’s power to appoint executive branch officials when the Senate is in recess without going through the confirmation process. The court rejected the validity of four appointments President Obama made in January 2012, when the question of whether the Senate was in recess was in dispute. While on the surface the ruling was a blow to executive power, on a deeper level it was also a victory for executive power because it rolled back an appeals court ruling that had gone much further in restricting such authority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/25/us/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 762}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 741, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/25/us/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176/annotated-supreme-court-cellphone-privacy-decision-1403716252176-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 741, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail