id prosecutors had to provide defense attorneys with never-revealed information about his years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defense lawyers for terrorism suspects at Guantanamo Bay have long complained — and with good reason — that ongoing government resistance to sharing details about mistreatment while in U.S. custody makes it hard, if not impossible to provide adequate legal representation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Torture Details for U.S.S. Cole Bombing Suspect', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cole (USS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nashiri, Abd al-Rahim al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pohl, James L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ae6214-3dea-549a-a967-137f43b1e0b0', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ae6214-3dea-549a-a967-137f43b1e0b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Museum has a new leader for its board, Elizabeth A. Sackler.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/elizabeth-a-sackler-to-lead-brooklyn-museum-board/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Museum has a new leader for its board, Elizabeth A. Sackler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth A. Sackler has been named chairwoman of the Brooklyn Museum, the first woman in the museum’s nearly 200-year history to serve in that position.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth A. Sackler to Lead Brooklyn Museum Board', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Chairwoman for Brooklyn Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chicago, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d3b4289-5729-5671-a903-b28aed055005', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3b4289-5729-5671-a903-b28aed055005'}, {'abstract': 'The conservative commentator blasts the sport, and its defenders blast back.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/world-cup-captivates-america-except-for-ann-coulter/', 'snippet': 'The conservative commentator blasts the sport, and its defenders blast back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many Americans were excited to learn on Thursday that the United States would advance to the next round of World Cup competition. One who probably was not: Ann Coulter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Cup Captivates America, Except for Ann Coulter', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68828bc6-b31b-5301-9be5-6d67ec427930', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68828bc6-b31b-5301-9be5-6d67ec427930'}, {'abstract': 'For decades the Gang of Four’s influence went virtually unchallenged, and for now Rangel seems to be holding on. Here’s a selection of what has been said over the years about the Gang of Four and their influence in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/with-rangels-win-another-chapter-in-the-gang-of-four/', 'snippet': 'For decades the Gang of Four’s influence went virtually unchallenged, and for now Rangel seems to be holding on. Here’s a selection of what has been said over the years about the Gang of Four and their influence in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, Representative Charles B. Rangel won the primary election contest to represent New York’s 13th District in Congress. Darren Sands wrote about the campaign in last Sunday’s magazine, noting that Rangel’s political strength in the community began in the 1980s, when the Coalition for a Just New York ‘‘rallied minority voters and African-American and Latino candidates.’’ The most prominent among the coalition was the ‘‘Gang of Four,’’ which included Charles Rangel, David N. Dinkins, Basil Paterson and Percy Sutton. Sands says that for decades the Gang of Four’s influence went virtually unchallenged, and for now Rangel seems to be holding on. Here’s a selection of what has been said over the years about the Gang of Four and their influence in Harlem:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Rangel’s Win, Another Chapter in the Gang of Four', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dinkins, David N', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterson, Basil A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rangel, Charles B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sutton, Percy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walrond, Michael A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Torres', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Torres', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba0a33f-90bf-5252-841a-0a60444af873', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba0a33f-90bf-5252-841a-0a60444af873'}, {'abstract': '“Begin Again,” starring Keira Knightley, Mark Ruffalo and Adam Levine, is the director John Carney’s follow-up to “Once.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/movies/begin-again-from-the-once-director-john-carney.html', 'snippet': '“Begin Again,” starring Keira Knightley, Mark Ruffalo and Adam Levine, is the director John Carney’s follow-up to “Once.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before it was a Tony Award-winning Broadway musical, “Once” was a scruffy and charming movie, written and directed by John Carney, about a man and a woman united by their love of music and their unstated but obvious attraction to each other. Filmed at street level in the lived-in parts of a picturesque city, it managed to be touristic and authentic at the same time, partly because the central pair consisted of a native and an outsider. Mr. Carney pulled off the enviable trick of dressing unabashed romantic sentiment in a style that felt rough and real, so that every cliché he touched felt shiny and new.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/BEGIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/BEGIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 860}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/BEGIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/BEGIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1430, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/27BEGIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/27BEGIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27BEGIN/27BEGIN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Genre, if Not the Song, Remains the Same', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Genre, if Not the Song, Remains the Same', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knightley, Keira', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruffalo, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keener, Catherine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Begin Again (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eafa2180-3d35-5720-b4ff-6c3aa7229d52', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eafa2180-3d35-5720-b4ff-6c3aa7229d52'}, {'abstract': 'How did we ever manage without Baggies?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/fashion/fear-of-packing.html', 'snippet': 'How did we ever manage without Baggies?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We all have our favorites when it comes to the life-changing inventions of the 20th century, and mine is the Baggie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29Misinformed-web/29Misinformed-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29Misinformed-web/29Misinformed-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29Misinformed-web/29Misinformed-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1015, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N