d City, Queens, offer refreshingly un-Koonsian ideas about sculpture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/arts/design/three-solo-shows-at-sculpturecenter-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'Solo shows by Katrin Sigurdardottir, Liz Glynn and Jory Rabinovitz at SculptureCenter in Long Island City, Queens, offer refreshingly un-Koonsian ideas about sculpture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For refreshingly un-Koonsian ideas about sculpture, look no further than the three solo exhibitions now at SculptureCenter. One is a large-scale installation by the midcareer Icelandic artist Katrin Sigurdardottir; the other two are smaller projects by the emerging American artists Liz Glynn and Jory Rabinovitz. Shiny objects and artisanal craftsmanship play a role here, as they do in Jeff Koons’s survey at the Whitney, but so do imperfection, evanescence and parsimoniousness.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SCULPTURE1/27SCULPTURE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SCULPTURE1/27SCULPTURE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SCULPTURE1/27SCULPTURE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SCULPTURE1/27SCULPTURE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SCULPTURE1/27SCULPTURE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height