f5789-5bbe-5bef-9253-37f609bcb777', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aff5789-5bbe-5bef-9253-37f609bcb777'}, {'abstract': 'Spain, Italy, England – all gone home. With the U.S. team reaching the next stage of competition, some predictions are due.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/26/a-shift-in-the-beautiful-game/', 'snippet': 'Spain, Italy, England – all gone home. With the U.S. team reaching the next stage of competition, some predictions are due.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Spain, Italy and England have all gone home, and the United States is through to the Round of 16 of the World Cup, something has shifted in the beautiful game. Jurgen Klinsmann’s U.S. team has been gritty, cohesive and occasionally explosive, as when Jermaine Jones almost burst the net with his equalizing rocket against Portugal. America, less naïve with each recent World Cup, deserves its place in the knock-out phase.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shift in the Beautiful Game', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81aab261-ebce-564c-8244-b0f819f992ea', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81aab261-ebce-564c-8244-b0f819f992ea'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/arts/music/jazz-listings-for-june-27-july-3.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Full reviews of recent jazz performances: nytimes.com/jazz. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Listings for June 27-July 3', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:32:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/871caeb6-e259-545d-8947-948c91863f2b', 'word_count': 1786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/871caeb6-e259-545d-8947-948c91863f2b'}, {'abstract': 'Bong Joon-ho’s “Snowpiercer” envisions a postapocalyptic world on a train, where first class is fabulous and the economy cars are a lot like hell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/movies/in-snowpiercer-the-train-trip-to-end-all-train-trips.html', 'snippet': 'Bong Joon-ho’s “Snowpiercer” envisions a postapocalyptic world on a train, where first class is fabulous and the economy cars are a lot like hell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mood for allegory? Have a look at Bong Joon-ho’s “Snowpiercer,” which proceeds from a fantastical premise rich with real-world relevance. After a human-engineered planetary catastrophe (trying to arrest the planet’s warming, we accidentally froze it solid), the remaining people are stuck on a train that never stops moving. A few thousand survivors live in railway cars, sorted into a rigid and ruthlessly enforced social order. In the back are huddled masses fed on gelatinous, insect-based black protein bars and kept in line by a combination of propaganda and brute force. Toward the front, the more fortunate enjoy access to schools, nightclubs, fresh food and the reassurance that they deserve everything they have. An unseen, quasi-mythical entrepreneur is in charge, and a group of rebels have decided to challenge his power and the extreme inequality he represents.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/SNOWPIERCER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/SNOWPIERCER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/SNOWPIERCER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/SNOWPIERCER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 2030, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/27SNOWPIERCER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/27/arts/27SNOWPIERCER1/27SNOWPIERCER1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27