e3b6-bf5f-521b-991b-8edea41b963e', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b547e3b6-bf5f-521b-991b-8edea41b963e'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to fairs and cultural festivals, literary events, walking tours and more in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/arts/spare-times-for-june-27-july-4.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to fairs and cultural festivals, literary events, walking tours and more in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYC Pride Events (Friday through Sunday) The monthlong celebration of lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender diversity concludes this weekend with something for everyone. A free rally with performances will kick things off on Friday, from 6 to 9:30 p.m., at Pier 26, in Hudson River Park, at North Moore Street, TriBeCa. It will be followed by a dance party for men, starting at 11 p.m. at BPM, 516 West 42nd Street, Clinton. Women will get their own party at Pier 26 on Saturday, from 4 to 10 p.m.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for June 27-July 4', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-26T22:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joumana Khatib, Anne Mancuso and Andrew Boryga', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joumana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khatib', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boryga', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materi