 'snippet': 'The police appeared to have lost track of Matias Reyes after the jogger attack, even though he had been identified as a suspect in the rape two days before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the man was finished raping the 20-year-old college student and searching her apartment for money, he announced that he had to kill or blind her. He held an ice pick to her eyes, then found a blade. Already he had bound her with telephone wire ripped from the wall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Botched Case of Park Jogger, an Altered Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Botched Case of Park Jogger, an Altered Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Matias', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Central Park Five (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central Park Jogger Case (1989)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T01:50:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c849bd6-698b-50b9-8571-01e6eb989305', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c849bd6-698b-50b9-8571-01e6eb989305'}, {'abstract': 'World War I demolished empires and destroyed kings, kaisers and sultans. It introduced chemical weapons and aerial bombing. It brought women into the work force and hastened their legal right to vote