im, a sunny weekend, and a misbehaving actor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning to you on this summer-break Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: Pick Your Pool', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T09:43:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal and Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/404a9b8f-8238-50c5-8258-b8bd401206b1', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/404a9b8f-8238-50c5-8258-b8bd401206b1'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrators haven’t been alone in advocating democracy during a trip to Taiwan by Zhang Zhijun, the mainland’s highest-ranking official to visit the island. Some local leaders have also been raising the issue.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/in-taiwan-chinese-official-confronted-with-voices-of-democracy/', 'snippet': 'Demonstrators haven’t been alone in advocating democracy during a trip to Taiwan by Zhang Zhijun, the mainland’s highest-ranking official to visit the island. Some local leaders have also been raising the issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zhang Zhijun, the highest-ranking Chinese official to visit Taiwan, has said he wanted to hear the voices of its people during his four-day trip to the self-governed island. Demonstrators in Taiwan have tried to meet that request, following him since the start of his visit on Wednesday. And while the official meetings have been less confrontational, with talk of increasing trade and travel across the Taiwan Strait, some local leaders have also talked up Taiwan’s democratic values, a sharp contrast with Communist-ruled China, which considers Taiwan as part of its territory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/world/28sino-TAIWAN1/28sino-TAIWAN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Taiwan, Chinese Official Confronted With Voices of Democracy', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 