, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29opm-promo/29opm-promo-jumbo.png', 'height': 306, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29opm-promo/29opm-promo-superJumbo.png', 'height': 306, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29opm-promo/29opm-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29opm-promo/29opm-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29opm-promo/29opm-promo-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Anaerobic Driving', 'kicker': 'The One-Page Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T14:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/99c2aa11-1902-5a62-afbe-4780b9735e2b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/99c2aa11-1902-5a62-afbe-4780b9735e2b'}, {'abstract': 'Burlesque boys around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/magazine/the-real-hedwigs.html', 'snippet': 'Burlesque boys around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway success of “Hedwig and the Angry Inch” suggests that gender-bending male performance has moved closer to the American mainstream, but it has also been flourishing in clubs around the world. The photographer Magnus Arrevad spent close to five years in several countries, documenting men applying makeup, dressing in elaborate costumes and performing. One of them, Eric Gorsuch, who goes by Mr. Gorgeous, says he has witnessed the transformation of the art form in real time. “I’m superlucky in that I feel like, even looking five years ago till now, so many people today are aware of and acknowledge different kinds of sexuality — gay, straight, bisexual, whatever,” he says. “When society becomes a little more aware of other people’s lifestyles, it allows people to make decisions artistically. For me, if it was 10 years ago, I don’t think I would feel as confident being a male performer doing a parody of a stocking peel in high heels.” Julie Bosman', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Hedwigs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Real Hedwigs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hedwig and the Angry Inch (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T14:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Photographs by Magnus Arrevad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Photographs', 'middlename': 'Magnus', 'lastname': 'Arrevad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b5e115-aaab-5ea2-a276-6b2b10d934fb', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b5e115-aaab-5ea2-a276-6b2b10d934fb'}, {'abstract': 'Revisiting a snowy night in 1926 that changed the life of E.E. Cummings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/magazine/how-to-solve-an-88-year-old-literary-mystery.html', 'snippet': 'Revisiting a snowy night in 1926 that changed the life of E.E. Cummings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Edward and Rebecca Cummings passed the town of Center Ossipee, N.H., in their new 1926 Franklin sedan, it began to snow. They left their home in Cambridge, Mass., hours before, driving a car with high seats, no defroster and a top speed of about 50. Rebecca took over the driving for the last part of the trip to their summer place at Silver Lake.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 91, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 91}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 155, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29riff/mag-29Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg