me, it had changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/magazine/looking-for-the-russia-i-once-knew.html', 'snippet': 'Two decades later, the country was still inside me. But all around me, it had changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On my last night in Petrozavodsk, in the last months of the Soviet Union, I stood in an unlit back alley buying boots off a soldier from the nearby army base. They were knee-high, and black, and illegal. It was midnight. I was 14. For about a month, I’d lived with a host family as part of a student exchange. In a week, leaving the country, I would wait, sweating, at Sheremetyevo airport while security rummaged through random suitcases, hoping they wouldn’t choose mine. Soviet Army surplus is ubiquitous now, but in 1991, you had to buy it on the black market and smuggle it out. If you got caught, I figured, you probably stayed in Moscow while the rest of your exchange group flew home.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29lives/mag-29Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29lives/mag-29Lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 713}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29lives/mag-29Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 862, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/magazine/29lives/mag-29Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1940, 'width': 1633, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'