ytimes.com/2014/06/29/books/review/the-fever-by-megan-abbott.html', 'snippet': 'Megan Abbott’s novel centers on teenage desire and the outbreak of a mysterious illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Le Roy, N.Y., a former factory town \xadbetween Rochester and Buffalo, became famous three years ago when 14 girls and one boy were afflicted with undiagnosed verbal and physical tics. Cheerleaders writhing and snarling on the “Today” show: It’s not hard to understand why Megan Abbott, a reliable producer of noir page turners, based her seventh novel, “The Fever,” on the Le Roy outbreak. In real life, the underpinnings of the \xadteenagers’ outbursts turned out to be psychological. But in “The Fever,” Abbott attributes the epidemic to a curious brand of black magic.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/0629TENNANT-MOORE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/0629TENNANT-MOORE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/0629TENNANT-MOORE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/0629TENNANT-MOORE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1524, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/29TENNANTMOORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/29TENNANTMOORE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/29TENNANTMOORE/29TENNANTMOORE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Awakening', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Awakening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Fever (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abbott, Megan (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T14:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Tennant-Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tennant-Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3360068-bdc6-5353-9fc2-778dfe1e0e05', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3360068-bdc6-5353-9fc2-778dfe1e0e05'}, {'abstract': 'In Mark Billingham’s “The Bones Beneath,” Inspector Tom Thorne is part of a group stranded on an island off the coast of Wales with two murderers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/books/review/the-bones-beneath-by-mark-billingham-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'In Mark Billingham’s “The Bones Beneath,” Inspector Tom Thorne is part of a group stranded on an island off the coast of Wales with two murderers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To quote a line that’s sure to make hearts flutter: “We’re almost completely cut off here.” In THE BONES BENEATH (Atlantic Monthly, $25), “we” is a party composed of Mark Billingham’s supersleuth, Inspector Tom Thorne; a skeleton staff of police officers and crime scene investigators; and two murderers. “Here” is a mountainous island off the coast of Wales, said to be the resting place of 20,000 saints. And being “cut off” from civilization is fair warning that the characters in this thriller are likely to revert to savagery.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 765}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 804, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1607, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/books/review/0629CRIMESUB/0629CRIMESUB-thumb