me': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T15:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b2b4cad-5897-5a9e-a76c-22d3b9811316', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b2b4cad-5897-5a9e-a76c-22d3b9811316'}, {'abstract': 'Is the little-known Export-Import Bank under Congressional scrutiny because of crony capitalism?', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-7/', 'snippet': 'Is the little-known Export-Import Bank under Congressional scrutiny because of crony capitalism?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a government agency that’s flown under the radar for most of its 80-year history, the Export-Import Bank of the United States is getting a lot of attention recently: It’s now at the center of a fight in Congress over the role of government in business. This week on Money Talking, Joe Nocera and Rana Foroohar look at why the Export-Import Bank is under such scrutiny, and what it means for business in general.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s Money Talking', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T15:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b3451e9-3d00-53dd-b5cd-528aec2badcd', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b3451e9-3d00-53dd-b5cd-528aec2badcd'}, {'abstract': 'I continue to find new uses for quinoa, which keeps well in the refrigerator after it’s cooked and adds protein and textures to these easy salads, including some inspired by the ideas of the vegetarian cookbook author Deborah Madison.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/50-ways-to-love-your-quinoa/', 'snippet': 'I continue to find new uses for quinoa, which keeps well in the refrigerator after it’s cooked and adds protein and textures to these easy salads, including some inspired by the ideas of the vegetarian cookbook author Deborah Madison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’d think I would eventually run out of ideas for quinoa. I’ve posted over 50 recipes on this page over the years. But ideas keep coming and I keep loving this grain (O.K., Paleos, I know, it’s a seed, not a grain. But we use it on the plate like a grain, so that’s what I’ll continue to call it.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24recipehealth/24recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24recipehealth/24recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24recipehealth/24recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/24/science/24recipehealth/24recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu