'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Fernanda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T17:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'World Cup', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/610d6c65-3ee8-54e9-aa59-ef57b776c00e', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/610d6c65-3ee8-54e9-aa59-ef57b776c00e'}, {'abstract': 'These summer cocktail recipes err on the side of easy-to-drink and favor sake, wine and vermouth over the harder stuff.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/cocktail-culture-inventive-low-proof-cocktails-sake-wine-vermouth/', 'snippet': 'These summer cocktail recipes err on the side of easy-to-drink and favor sake, wine and vermouth over the harder stuff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the many virtues of a potent Manhattan, Martini or Sazerac, the all-spirit cocktail doesn’t lend itself well to, say, postwork happy hours or, for that matter, pleasant mornings-after. Happily for the congenitally thirsty, a new wave of complex and inventive low-proof cocktails is popping up, and they’re a far cry from that less-potent fallback drink, the white-wine spritzer. Coming on the heels of the relentless rise of the Aperol Spritz,\xa0these new, lighter drinks appeal as much to those with an aversion to strong liquors as they do to the heartiest of drinkers after one dirty martini too many. And as Dinah Sanders, author of “The Art of the Shim: Low-Alcohol Cocktails to Keep you Level,” says, “The more subtle ingredients these drinks often feature don’t overwhelm the palate, so they are generally more food-friendly.” Thanks to exotic sakes, a variety of vermouths, a growing range of bitters, flavorful teas, infused syrups, fresh herbs and wines of all colors and ranges of effervescence, the sky’s the limit in creating easier-to-drink concoctions, as evidenced in the following five recipes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27cocktail-rowan/27cocktail-rowan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inventive Cocktails That Pack a Low-Proof Punch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Absinthe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citrus Fruits', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prosecco (Wine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sake', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T17:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rowan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rowan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/958cc3b1-2958-564a-b307-983a35bbd2dc', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958cc3b1-2958-564a-b307-983a35bbd2dc'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement by Richard W. Dreiling, the chairman and chief executive of the discount retailer, comes as a smaller competitor, Family Dollar, is under pressure from the activist investor Carl C. Icahn.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/head-of-dollar-general-to-retire/', 'snippet': 'The announcement by Richard W. Dreiling, the chairman and chief executive of the discount retailer, comes as a smaller competitor, Family Dollar, is under pressure from the activist investor Carl C. Icahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard W. Dreiling, the chairman and chief executive of the discount retailer Dollar General, said on Friday that he was retiring. The move is effective May 30, 2015, or until the company names a successor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/dbpix-store/dbpix-store-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Head of Dollar General to Retire', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoppi