d after disrupting a performance of the musical “Cabaret.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shia LaBeouf Arraigned on Disorderly Conduct Charge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaBeouf, Shia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio 54', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T18:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62bb4960-144b-5baf-8540-bb6269bc9e74', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62bb4960-144b-5baf-8540-bb6269bc9e74'}, {'abstract': 'Esther Bejarano, 89, who had to perform in the Auschwitz Girls’ Orchestra, joined the German duo Microphone Mafia five years ago to further her musical activism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/world/europe/auschwitz-orchestra-survivor-sings-anew-in-rap-group.html', 'snippet': 'Esther Bejarano, 89, who had to perform in the Auschwitz Girls’ Orchestra, joined the German duo Microphone Mafia five years ago to further her musical activism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — AT various points during shows, the German rapper Kutlu Yurtseven gestures to a bandmate sitting demurely off to the side. That’s the cue for 89-year-old Esther Bejarano, a diminutive woman with a snow-white pixie cut, to jump in with a song. “When will the heavens open up, again, for me?” is one favorite, the refrain of a local carnival tune. “When will they open up?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid the Rap Music, Echoes of an Orchestra Playing in a Dark Past', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid the Rap Music, Echoes of an Orchestra Playing in a Dark Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bejarano, Esther', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auschwitz Concentration Camp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microphone Mafia (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Women's Orchestra of Auschwitz", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T18:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally McGrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6dd5787-0312-55d9-8c1c-5c39845d3add', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6dd5787-0312-55d9-8c1c-5c39845d3add'}, {'abstract': 'His lawsuit is utterly frivolous.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/john-boehner-deflects-attention-by-suing-the-president/', 'snippet': 'His lawsuit is utterly frivolous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama was generous on Thursday in referring to Speaker John Boehner’s proposed lawsuit against him as a “stunt,” a word generally used to mean a playful attempt to get attention. In fact, the suit is a mean-spirited attempt to deflect attention — specifically from the House’s refusal to engage in the act of governing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Boehner Deflects Attention by Suing the President', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T18:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c492d71-1e3a-5afa-9498-11446114df86', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c492d71-1e3a-5afa-9498-11446114df86'}, {'abstract': 'An upper Fifth Avenue duplex, with 12 rooms and 5,400 square feet of space, is the sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/big-ticket-a-grand-gothic-duplex-for-16-5-million/', 'snippet': 'An upper Fifth Avenue duplex, with 12 rooms and 5,400 square feet of space, is the sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 12-room duplex on upper Fifth Avenue, with a Gothic decorating theme but no Central Park views from its grand primary rooms, sold for $16.5 million and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. The monthly maintenance is $11,048.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/realestate/29TICKETSUB/29TICKETSUB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/realesta