'GQ', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Selfridges', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T19:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gregory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6d6df48-2699-5ec9-ab0c-a86efc8dfd26', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d6df48-2699-5ec9-ab0c-a86efc8dfd26'}, {'abstract': 'The main challenge at Book Review this week was to have an illustrator create a cover image for a review of “The Silkworm” by Robert Galbraith (a.k.a. J.K. Rowling) with very little to go on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/06/27/the-book-reviews-killer-cover/', 'snippet': 'The main challenge at Book Review this week was to have an illustrator create a cover image for a review of “The Silkworm” by Robert Galbraith (a.k.a. J.K. Rowling) with very little to go on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no question that this week’s cover was going to be Harlan Coben on “The Silkworm” by Robert Galbraith (a.k.a. J.K. Rowling). This is Coben’s first review for us, and we’ve had our eye on him as a reviewer for years. And of course, like most media outlets, we missed the first Robert Galbraith novel, before J.K. Rowling was unmasked as the true author. We weren’t going to lose that opportunity again.When the review came in, it more than lived up to our expectations. Here was one of the masters of literary genre fiction writing on someone who is relatively new to the genre, though of course a gigantic success elsewhere in the book world. It was a strong and logical, yet also slightly unexpected match between book and reviewer.'