 went into the meeting in which he demoted Martin Vasquez, his longtime assistant, he asked a staff member with U.S. Soccer to knock on the door and interrupt after about five minutes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 912, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 912}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1347, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/sports/CITY-JP-USSOCCER/CITY-JP-USSOCCER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coach Boldly Moves U.S. Forward', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boldly Moving Toward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beasley, DaMarcus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T20:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'World Cup', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5eab210-ce54-50e1-b198-460c76475f54', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5eab210-ce54-50e1-b198-460c76475f54'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of the social media reaction to the United States-Germany soccer match details the hope, angst and relief experienced during the game.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/the-u-s-germany-match-through-a-social-media-lens/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of the social media reaction to the United States-Germany soccer match details the hope, angst and relief experienced during the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States-Germany soccer match on Thursday was a roller coaster of emotions. And an analysis of the social media communications before, during and after the match shows the minute-by-minute shifts in sentiment and in subjects discussed, as the American team lost to Germany but moved on in the World Cup competition.', 'sou