content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T21:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/52495320-2541-57a8-8b3e-587bf30ad818', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/52495320-2541-57a8-8b3e-587bf30ad818'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Saudi Arabia, Sudan, India and China.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/27/pictures-of-the-day-saudi-arabia-and-elsewhere/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Saudi Arabia, Sudan, India and China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Saudi Arabia, Sudan, India and China. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Saudi Arabia and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T21:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/586baa6f-9da6-57e0-9c6f-01d52fc7e774', 'word_count': 14, 'uri': 'nyt://article/586baa6f-9da6-57e0-9c6f-01d52fc7e774'}, {'abstract': 'In Arthur Nazaryan’s photographs of a hospice nurse and her patients, death shapes the scene by its absence, not its presence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/nyregion/before-night-falls.html', 'snippet': 'In Arthur Nazaryan’s photographs of a hospice nurse and her patients, death shapes the scene by its absence, not its presence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Death typically appears in photographs as an intruder: an unbidden force that sweeps down on a battlefield or leaves survivors pained and bereft. We see the images and know that just hours or moments earlier, the subjects’ lives were intact, the world complete and in order. In Arthur Nazaryan’s photographs of a hospice nurse and her patients, death plays a different role, shaping the scene by its absence, not its presence. It is the reason the characters are assembled, the order toward which the chaos of life is resolving itself; not just their lives, but ours as well.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Night Falls', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before Night Falls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazaryan, Arthur', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvary Hospital', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T21:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8988bc0e-dd75-57df-8972-9c1f3e81fb8b', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8988bc0e-dd75-57df-8972-9c1f3e81fb8b'}, {'abstract': 'The big surprise at Bartaco in Westport is how good so many of the nibbles are and how easily you can make a full meal of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/nyregion/a-review-of-bartaco-in-westport.html', 'snippet': 'The big surprise at Bartaco in Westport is how good so many of the nibbles are and how easily you can make a full meal of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They say there is nothing new under the sun, but the Bartaco concept may be an exception. Bartaco in Westport, an indoor-outdoor locale, offers a limited menu, more snacklike than full service, in a noisy, lively atmosphere, with seating for 110 inside, and for 25 more outside, facing the Saugatuck River. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/nyregion/29DINECT2/29DINECT2-thumbStand