 woman who was detained at the airport in Khartoum with her family by Sudanese authorities after an appeals court overturned her conviction and death sentence for abandoning Islam and ordered her set free is now in the protection of the United States Embassy here, her lawyer said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christian Sudanese Woman and Her Family in Protection of U.S. Embassy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan: Christian Woman Granted Temporary Refuge at U.S. Embassy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Kushkush, Isma'il", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Khartoum (Sudan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ishag, Mariam Ibraheem', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T21:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': "By Isma'il Kushkush", 'person': [{'firstname': "Isma'il", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kushkush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/01d5643a-33d6-5ce9-a98d-0e7921524511', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01d5643a-33d6-5ce9-a98d-0e7921524511'}, {'abstract': 'Kay-Wolff celebrated her 80th birthday this month.', 'web_url': 'https://ww