ps://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/arts/dance/a-new-iteration-of-reggie-wilsons-moses-es.html', 'snippet': 'Reggie Wilson’s “ ... Moses(es)” returned to the stage on Wednesday, this time at the St. Cornelius Chapel on Governors Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the stage version of “ ... Moses(es),” performed at the Brooklyn Academy of Music last December, the choreographer Reggie Wilson began by introducing himself to the assembled crowd. His dancers followed suit, adding how long they’d spent as members of his Fist & Heel Performance Group. Mr. Wilson then stuffed armloads of silver tinsel into a suitcase. He packs a lot into his dances.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1226, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28REGGIE/28REGGIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prophet Goes to Church', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prophet Goes to Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Reggie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'River to River Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Governors Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bcad8a-b227-511e-831b-9ee682aa0c89', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bcad8a-b227-511e-831b-9ee682aa0c89'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Wolfgang Tillmans has long been occupied with what he has called the “objectness” of a photograph.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/arts/design/disparate-but-connected.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Wolfgang Tillmans has long been occupied with what he has called the “objectness” of a photograph.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Wolfgang Tillmans has long been occupied with what he has called the “objectness” of a photograph, its role as a thing in the world and not just as “a conduit of information,” and this has often led to explorations of the relationship between painting and photography in the digital age. A tightly focused exhibition opening Tuesday at the Philadelphia Museum of Art takes Mr. Tillmans’s fascinations and runs with them. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE3/29GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disparate but Connected', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disparate but Connected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed8f66e-aa14-5d39-8e14-de2153b0eb05', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed8f66e-aa14-5d39-8e14-de2153b0eb05'}, {'abstract': 'Art can start relationships, and end them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/arts/music/marathon-tribute-to-philip-guston.html', 'snippet': 'Art can start relationships, and end them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art can start relationships, and end them. The composer Morton Feldman and the painter Philip Guston had been close for years when Feldman attended an opening of Guston’s in 1970. The work on display was figurative, an abrupt turn from the abstraction Guston had been known for. Feldman was stunned silent. Telling the story much later, he said that the episode ended their decades-long friendship. The two men never saw each other again.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marathon Tribute to Philip Guston', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marathon Tribute to Philip Guston', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0371e17-77c8-5337-b326-0643fef57c62', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0371e17-77c8-5337-b326-0643fef57c62'}, {'abstract': 'The name Urban Bush Women suggests a fierce and perhaps frightening tribe — something