ad to Broadway.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 689, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1377, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE4/29GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Damned People Got No Reason to Live', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Damned People Got No Reason to Live', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd0ef6c-e9cd-532e-b5ff-17952bd01a04', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd0ef6c-e9cd-532e-b5ff-17952bd01a04'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years ago Doug Block began shooting wedding videos to support his true passion, documentary filmmaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/arts/television/following-9-trips-from-i-do-to-i-did.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years ago Doug Block began shooting wedding videos to support his true passion, documentary filmmaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago Doug Block began shooting wedding videos to support his true passion, documentary filmmaking. Sure, the money was good. But he soon discovered a far more intriguing aspect. “I could stand just feet away,” he says, “as two ordinary people experience one of the most extraordinary days of their lives.” But after the vows had been uttered and the videos sent on their way, he couldn’t help but wonder what happened next. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 1919, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/arts/29GUIDE6/29GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following 9 Trips From ‘I Do’ to ‘I Did’', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following 9 Trips From ‘I Do’ to ‘I Did’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:19:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15516f3f-e423-57df-9849-a78ba4f9b522', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15516f3f-e423-57df-9849-a78ba4f9b522'}, {'abstract': 'At Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola, the Azar Lawrence Quintet is focusing on music from Mr. Lawrence’s new album, “The Seeker.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/arts/music/azar-lawrence-quintet-focuses-on-the-seeker.html', 'snippet': 'At Dizzy’s Club Coca-Cola, the Azar Lawrence Quintet is focusing on music from Mr. Lawrence’s new album, “The Seeker.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With improvised music, you get used to seeing a band warm up by degrees. It comes with the aesthetic form, and also with the business model, if it’s a band performing sporadic multiple-night stands. Jazz is full of groups reconvening, recohering, then pacing themselves across a few nights and days. The quintet led by the saxophonist Azar Lawrence, from Los Angeles, is of that form and that model. For the last three years or so, it’s been playing gigs in clubs — often on the East Coast, where all its other members are based — and then everyone scatters and does different things.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/28DIZZY/28DIZZY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 