adline': {'main': 'Scenes from San Francisco', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:36:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1428c5ee-69a1-5506-9331-faeaa3518538', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1428c5ee-69a1-5506-9331-faeaa3518538'}, {'abstract': 'The last big week of the social season held one final grand surprise: the Jeff Koons retrospective at the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/fashion/bill-cunningham-big-bloom.html', 'snippet': 'The last big week of the social season held one final grand surprise: the Jeff Koons retrospective at the Whitney Museum of American Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIG BLOOM The last big week of the social season held one final grand surprise: the Jeff Koons retrospective at the Whitney Museum of American Art that occupies the entire museum, including the front moat. On the top floor is Mr. Koons’s latest work, “Play-Doh,” a monumental pile of color. The owners of the work are Maria and Bill Bell. Many of the women’s dresses at the opening Tuesday echoed the colors of the sculpture and recalled the colors of the Fauve painters of early-20th-century Paris and the smaller “Split-Rocker,” left. It contrasts with the colossal “Split-Rocker,” below, covered in over 50,000 dwarf marigolds, zinnias, petunias, wax begonias, impatiens and geraniums, installed above the statue of Prometheus in Rockefeller Center. The sculpture, which exploded to 37 feet tall, was unveiled at a luncheon.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Big Bloom', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Bloom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1e2aa9d-4ef7-50c4-bc47-a9fd18c327ba', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1e2aa9d-4ef7-50c4-bc47-a9fd18c327ba'}, {'abstract': 'Warpaint, a four-woman Los Angeles band, appeared as part of the Celebrate Brooklyn! concert series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/arts/music/warpaint-plays-celebrate-brooklyn-in-park-slope.html', 'snippet': 'Warpaint, a four-woman Los Angeles band, appeared as part of the Celebrate Brooklyn! concert series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Musical patterns are neat, stable, definite, predictable. Feelings and relationships — well, they aren’t. But they can all be hypnotic, compelling, even obsessive. Warpaint, the four-woman Los Angeles band that headlined Celebrate Brooklyn! on Thursday night, places its songs at that complicated intersection: where a grid of repetition meets the amorphous crosscurrents of emotion and desire. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulletins From the Gut, From a Quartet at Work in the Park', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bulletins From the Gut, From a Quartet at Work in the Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warpaint (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrate Brooklyn (Festival)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-27T22:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9c201c4-2b25-5833-a7a4-d990c91f80af', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9c201c4-2b25-5833-a7a4-d990c91f80af'}, {'abstract': 'Music, art and dancing to start the summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/02/28/fashion/29-bill-cunningham-evening-hours.html', 'snippet': 'Music, art and dancing to start the summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Music, art and dancing to start the summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29PARTY/29PARTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29PARTY/29PARTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 677}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/fashion/29PARTY/29PARTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 