ni militants, Iraq’s future as a unified state is becoming less and less likely. As the Sunni militants take hold of a large swath of northwest Iraq, the Kurds, who operate a semiautonomous province in northeast Iraq, are edging toward independence, leaving Shiites controlling Baghdad and regions in the south. Yet Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki seems to have no interest in finding a new way forward from a catastrophe his policies ignited. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'While Iraq Burns', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Iraq Burns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T00:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f66351bf-ebf4-5810-949e-9c94cf882d36', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f66351bf-ebf4-5810-949e-9c94cf882d36'}, {'abstract': 'A study finds that states reduce recidivism rates when they commit to measures that help ex-prisoners to transition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/opinion/committed-states-have-reduced-recidivism-rates.html', 'snippet': 'A study finds that states reduce recidivism rates when they commit to measures that help ex-prisoners to transition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With corrections costs exceeding $60 billion a year, state and local governments are rightly focused on making sure that newly released prisoners stay out of jail instead of coming back in through a revolving door. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Second Chance Act Proves Its Worth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Second Chance Act Proves Its Worth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Second Chance Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Reentry Resource Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T00:53:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f17e10a-bffc-5d87-91ce-351c73023490', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f17e10a-bffc-5d87-91ce-351c73023490'}, {'abstract': 'G.M. said it was recalling more than half a million more vehicles, including full-size pickup trucks and sport utility vehicles that can suddenly switch into neutral.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/business/new-general-motors-recall-includes-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'G.M. said it was recalling more than half a million more vehicles, including full-size pickup trucks and sport utility vehicles that can suddenly switch into neutral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding to the mounting toll of its safety crisis, General Motors said on Friday that it was recalling more than half a million more vehicles, including full-size pickup trucks and sport utility vehicles that can suddenly switch into neutral.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1507, 'width': 1085, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/business/Motors/Motors-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New General Motors Recall Includes Best Sellers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Recall Includes Best Sellers at G.M.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jensen, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T00:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen and Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c90ad282-5340-5aa9-b2d5-8e68eb4e3134', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c90ad282-5340-5aa9-b2d5-8e68eb4e3134'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Womack was nicknamed the Preacher for his authoritative, church-trained voice and the way he introduced songs with long discourses on life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/arts/music/bobby-womack-songwriter-and-musician-dies-at-70.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Womack was nicknamed the Preacher for his authoritative, church-trained voice and the way he introduced songs with long discourses on life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bobby Womack, who spanned the American soul music era, touring as a gospel singer in the 1950s, playing guitar in Sam Cooke’s backup band in the early ’60s, writing hit songs recorded by Wilson Pickett and the Rolling Stones and composing music that broke onto the pop charts, died on June 27 at his home in Tarzana, Calif. He was 70.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 691}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 890, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1779, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/womack-obit-1/womack-obit-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bobby Womack, Royalty of the Soul Era, Dies at 70', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bobby Womack, Royalty of the Soul Era, Dies at 70', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitel