nant’s uniform on its hanger and grabbed a pair of black Crocs. The choice seemed logical enough. Where she was going, she would need some kind of waterproof footwear to get from her cabin to the shower room.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Women Who Saw Combat, a Place to Find Inner Peace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Women Who Saw Combat, a Place to Find Inner Peace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedman, Samuel G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T01:34:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e93f9ab-1668-504f-907f-3bd53012903f', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e93f9ab-1668-504f-907f-3bd53012903f'}, {'abstract': 'Forward Jozy Altidore, who left early in the United States’ opening match of the World Cup with a strained hamstring, should be available to face Belgium in the second round, Coach Jurgen Klinsmann said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/sports/worldcup/altidore-may-return-for-us-in-match-aga