xas lawyer who gets in over his head in a drug deal with Reiner (Javier Bardem), a nightclub owner involved with a Mexican cartel promising a 4,000 percent return — in this thriller directed by Ridley Scott from a screenplay by Cormac McCarthy. Mr. Pitt is the Counselor’s wary business associate, Cameron Diaz is Reiner’s predatory girlfriend and Penélope Cruz is the woman the Counselor intends to marry. “From all the ellipses, as well as the eccentric, mesmerizing poetry of his dialogue, Mr. McCarthy appears to have never read a screenwriting manual in his life. (That’s a compliment; this is his first produced film script.),” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about what she called a “terrifying, implacable new movie.” In Mr. McCarthy, she added, Mr. Scott “has found a partner with convictions about good and evil rather than canned formula.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa2b006-0770-5193-b35d-9fc97fe67715', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa2b006-0770-5193-b35d-9fc97fe67715'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 28, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/pageoneplus/corrections-june-28-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 28, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'Th