': 'There may be a link between your Internet use and how often you end up in the emergency room.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 1866, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-TECHNO/29-TECHNO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Health Plan Knows How You Shop', 'kicker': 'Technophoria', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Health Plan Knows How You Shop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pittsburgh Medical Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACXIOM CORP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T14:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NODESK', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e35813d-ccbe-5518-afb7-366d432875b6', 'word_count': 1396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e35813d-ccbe-5518-afb7-366d432875b6'}, {'abstract': 'Lucy Liu writes about directing a film about a woman’s tireless efforts to rescue her daughter, who was forced into prostitution.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/28/lucy-lius-directorial-debut-on-human-trafficking/', 'snippet': 'Lucy Liu writes about directing a film about a woman’s tireless efforts to rescue her daughter, who was forced into prostitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I traveled to Mumbai in 2010 to direct my first film “MEENA,” based on the first chapter of Nick and Sheryl’s book Half The Sky: Turning Oppression Into Opportunity for Women Worldwide. Even though MEENA is only a 20 minute film and took 5 days to shoot, it has taken nearly four years for it to finally be seen by an audience. The earlier feedback we received was that the content was too strong and that viewers would feel uncomfortable with the aggressive nature of violence in conjunction with children. The premiere of Meena this week was truly transformative. I felt excited and reinvigorated to be surrounded by an audience who were not only engaged by the film’s message, but also curious about how they can become more actively involved in learning about child protection. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lucy Liu’s Directorial Debut on Human Trafficking', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-28T14:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucy Liu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c5ec4be-0fbe-51d7-b482-9813a97fc189', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c5ec4be-0fbe-51d7-b482-9813a97fc189'}, {'abstract': '“You’ve got to get in and take risks, but you also have to get out, reassess and modify,” a chief executive says. “That, in my opinion, is how you get ahead.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/business/corner-office-joanne-rohde-on-knowing-when-to-get-in-and-to-get-out.html', 'snippet': '“You’ve got to get in and take risks, but you also have to get out, reassess and modify,” a chief executive says. “That, in my opinion, is how you get ahead.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This interview with  Joanne Rohde, C.E.O. of Axial Exchange, a developer of mobile health care applications, was conducted and condensed by  Adam Bryant.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-CORNER/29-CORNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 916, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/business/29-CORNER/29-CORNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 916}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi