ds vs. Mexico and Costa Rica vs. Greece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What to watch for in today’s World Cup matches, two elimination games in the knockout phase of the tournament. (Times are Eastern.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1088, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/29/sports/29wcdaily1/29wcdaily1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s World Cup Matches: June 29, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Rica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marquez, Rafael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robben, Arjen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Persie, Robin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c11f8cca-e6b6-5d58-944d-221331d9c44b', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c11f8cca-e6b6-5d58-944d-221331d9c44b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1914, the assassination of Archduke Francis Ferdinand was the outcome of a conspiracy; Dublin elects its first woman Lord Mayor in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/1914-assassination-of-the-archduke-francis-ferdinand-was-a-conspiracy/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1914, the assassination of Archduke Francis Ferdinand was the outcome of a conspiracy; Dublin elects its first woman Lord Mayor in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': ' VIENNA —\xa0That the assassination of Archduke Francis Ferdinand, the heir to the thrones of Austria and Hungary, and of the Duchess of Hohenberg, his consort, was the result of a widespread plot, the extent of which the actual actors were perhaps unaware of, now appears to be beyond doubt.\xa0In case the attempt on the Archduke’s life in Sarajevo failed, other bombs, it is stated, were to have been exploded on the railway as the Royal train was on its return journey from the Bosnian capital. Serious disturbances have taken place in Sarajevo and other towns in Bosnia and Herzegovina. Yesterday, another bomb was thrown at a street corner in Sarajevo by a young man, a Mussulman being wounded by the explosion. Martial law has been proclaimed in the town.\xa0The bodies of Archduke Francis Ferdinand and the Duchess of Hohenberg were embalmed during Sunday night, and were removed yesterday by special train to Metkovich, Dalmatia, on their way to Vienna. The funeral will take place on Friday, the interment being in the mausoleum on the Archduke’s estate at Artstetten. Emperor Francis Joseph will not be present at this ceremony, but will attend a requiem mass on the following day.\xa0A representative of a Prague bank in which Archduke Francis Ferdinand’s will had been deposited has arrived in Vienna with the document. It is stated that certain questions of State in which the Archduke was interested will be confided by the Emperor to the new heir to the throne. — From The New York Herald, European Edition, June 30, 1914.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Assassination of the Archduke Francis Ferdinand was a conspiracy', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sarajevo (Bosnia and Herzegovina)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T10:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd6aad5d-8bb0-5009-b3e8-0a6ca20a8a87', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd6aad5d-8bb0-5009-b3e8-0a6ca20a8a87'}, {'abstract': 'An unofficial referendum on democratic changes in Hong Kong attracted votes equal to more than a fifth of the city’s electorate, organizers said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/world/asia/turnout-for-unofficial-vote-in-hong-kong-cheers-democracy-advocates.html', 'snippet': 'An unofficial referendum on democratic changes in Hong Kong attracted votes equal to more than a fifth of the city’s electorate, organizers said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — An unofficial referendum on making the selection of Hong Kong’s chief executive more democratic has attracted votes equal to more than a fifth of the city’s electorate, organizers said Sunday, the referendum’s final day. They voiced hopes that the higher-than-anticipated participation would, along with a protest march scheduled for Tuesday, increase the pressure on the mainland Chinese government to give ground on the issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Poll Turnout Buoys Democracy Activists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hong Kong Poll Turnout Buoys Democracy Activists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Central', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T11:07:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f8b09eb-5add-5046-954d-35b1c86fd347', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f8b09eb-5add-5046-954d-35b1c86fd347'}, {'abstract': 'The experts’ arrival was seen as an implicit rebuke to the United States, where concerns in Congress about the political viability of Iraq’s government have stalled aircraft sales to Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/world/middleeast/iraq.html', 'snippet': 'The experts’ arrival was seen as an implicit rebuke to the United States, where concerns in Congress about the political viability of Iraq’s government have stalled aircraft sales to Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Iraqi government officials said Sunday that Russian experts had arrived in Iraq to help the army get 12 new Russian warplanes into the fight against Sunni extremists, while the extremists declared their leader the caliph, or absolute ruler, of all jihadi organizations worldwide.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/world/JP-IRAQ/JP-IRAQ-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/world/JP-IRAQ/JP-IRAQ-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/world/JP-IRAQ/JP-IRAQ-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'supe