alk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/assisting-life-and-death/', 'snippet': 'Patients’ rights advocates are making swift strides toward the decriminalization of assisted death, writes JAKE FLANAGIN. But others are hesitant to give governments a say on such a delicate issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saturday was a watershed moment for the American suicide-prevention effort. In response to decades of public advocacy, San Francisco transit authorities unanimously approved a $76 million plan to construct suicide barriers on the Golden Gate Bridge — where 46 people jumped to their death last year alone. “The time of healing can only begin when the drip-drip-drip of bodies into the raging waters has stopped,” a mother of one jumper told\xa0Michael Cabanatuan of The San Francisco Chronicle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/weekinreview/nyto-suicide/nyto-suicide-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/weekinreview/nyto-suicide/nyto-suicide-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/weekinreview/nyto-suicide/nyto-suicide-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/weekinreview/nyto-suicide/nyto-suicide-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/weekinreview/nyto-suicide/nyto-suicide-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {