i Poppea” for the Paris Opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Nero and Poppea never touch in Robert Wilson’s new production of Monteverdi’s “L’Incoronazione di Poppea” for the Paris Opera, which ends its run at the Palais Garnier on Monday. Their love affair, which drives anyone who gets in its way to death or exile, is one of the most violent portrayed in opera. Yet even during their final, rapturous duet, “Pur ti miro,” on Saturday, the tenor Jeremy Ovenden and the mezzo-soprano Karine Deshayes maintained a sliver of space between their outstretched hands.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1278, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/POPPEA/POPPEA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Passion Rules, Morality Stands Little Chance', 'kicker': 'Opera Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Passion Rules, Morality Stands Little Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Robert (1941- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovenden, Jeremy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deshayes, Karine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "L'Incoronazione di Poppea (Opera)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monteverdi, Claudio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T21:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/48e117fc-e947-54d6-8b75-2644068d514c', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48e117fc-e947-54d6-8b75-2644068d514c'}, {'abstract': '“Redeeming the Dream” centers on the lawyers Theodore B. Olson and David Boies and their fight to end California’s law against same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/books/redeeming-the-dream-by-theodore-b-olson-and-david-boies.html', 'snippet': '“Redeeming the Dream” centers on the lawyers Theodore B. Olson and David Boies and their fight to end California’s law against same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than four years a group of prominent lawyers led by Theodore B. Olson and David Boies, along with political consultants and Hollywood celebrities, campaigned against Proposition 8, the ban on same-sex marriages approved by California voters in 2008. The group, the American Foundation for Equal Rights, had two primary goals: to secure a judicial victory in the Supreme Court extending marriage to gay couples nationwide and to increase support for the cause through a public-relations blitz.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Legal Front Lines of Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Legal Front Lines of Same-Sex Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Theodore B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boies, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T21:53:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dale Carpenter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carpenter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f505ec2f-778f-5d16-916e-759e852e765d', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f505ec2f-778f-5d16-916e-759e852e765d'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater’s “Swan Lake,” as seen through three casts at the Metropolitan Opera House last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/arts/dance/american-ballet-theaters-swan-lake-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater’s “Swan Lake,” as seen through three casts at the Metropolitan Opera House last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Siegfried, the prince in “Swan Lake,” spends a lot of time surrounded by women who don’t seem to interest him. In American Ballet Theater’s production, he invariably appears more excited by the arrival of a maypole at his birthday party (Act I) than by the young ladies lining up to dance with him. In Act III, when princesses of the world parade through his court, enticing him with their national dances — Hungarian, Spanish, Italian, Polish — he wants none of them for his bride. “No,” he mimes to the Queen Mother, who has urged him to choose one, causing a flurry of disbelief among his courtiers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1213, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/LAKE/LAKE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ooh, a Maypole! And Love Interests, With Feathers', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ooh, a Maypole! And Love Interests, With Feathers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Swan Lake (Ballet)',