', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5921d5b8-e995-589d-8557-e3bdf7ae7215', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5921d5b8-e995-589d-8557-e3bdf7ae7215'}, {'abstract': 'Start out your solving week with a puzzle by Ed Sessa.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/one-who-plays-for-pay/', 'snippet': 'Start out your solving week with a puzzle by Ed Sessa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Happy Monday, everyone! It’s a vowel run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Who Plays For Pay', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T22:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84cc7f69-8d51-5ead-8344-81bfdb01d870', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84cc7f69-8d51-5ead-8344-81bfdb01d870'}, {'abstract': 'A witch’s curse, embattled lovers and a gondolier with royal blood will be part of the 2014-15 lineup for the New York Gilbert & Sullivan Players, the organizers have announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/arts/music/gilbert-sullivan-announces-season.html', 'snippet': 'A witch’s curse, embattled lovers and a gondolier with royal blood will be part of the 2014-15 lineup for the New York Gilbert & Sullivan Players, the organizers have announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A witch’s curse, embattled lovers and a gondolier with royal blood will be part of the 2014-15 lineup for the New York Gilbert & Sullivan Players, the organizers have announced. The season, which will take place at New York University’s Skirball Center for the Performing Arts, is to begin on Oct. 12 with a benefit gala celebrating the group’s 40th anniversary. That will be followed on Nov. 1 and 2 by “Ruddigore,” in which the Baronet of Ruddigore tries to escape a curse that forces him to commit a daily crime. “H.M.S. Pinafore,” Dec. 26-31, tells the comedic story of a lowly sailor’s plan to elope with the captain’s daughter before finding out that he isn’t as lowly as everyone — including himself — thinks he is. The theme of mistaken identity continues with the season’s final production, “The Gondoliers,” May 15-17. More information is at nygasp.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gilbert & Sullivan Announces Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gilbert & Sullivan Announces Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gilbert & Sullivan Players', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T22:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b2e9bfd-af0a-56f3-936e-5d43bf657ced', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b2e9bfd-af0a-56f3-936e-5d43bf657ced'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Dublin elects its first woman Lord Mayor in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/29/1939-first-woman-elected-mayor-of-dublin/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Dublin elects its first woman Lord Mayor in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — The first woman Lord Mayor of Dublin in history was elected last night. She was Mrs. Tom Clarkes, widow of Fenian leader executed after the 1916 Easter uprising, who herself has been an active Nationalist. The decisive vote which put her into office was cast by the outgoing Lord Mayor, Alderman Alfred Byrne, whom she has previously tried to oust from office on six different occasions. Byrne had been Lord Mayor for nine years. — From The New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, June 30, 1939. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: First Woman Elected Mayor of Dublin', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-29T22:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/175d152b-9450-5d66-9641-d2ec1d8306c6', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/175d152b-9450-5d66-9641-d2ec1d8306c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Vienna Philharmonic chose its material carefully for a concert held in Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina, that remembered World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/arts/music/the-vienna-philharmonic-recalls-world-war-i-in-sarajevo.html', 'snippet': 'The Vienna Philharmonic chose its material carefully for a concert held in Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina, that remembered World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARAJEVO, Bosnia and Herzegovina — If there was a moment that captured better than any other the light and the dark in Sarajevo’s centenary weekend, marking 100 years since the events here that unleashed the demons of World War I, it came with the opening bars of Beethoven’s “Ode to Joy.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/arts/jpsarajevomusic/jpsarajevomusic-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbna