n a 72-year-old codfish schooner, but rather where to put it. Now, his vision has become reality in the form of Grand Banks, which will begin serving food and drinks Thursday afternoon on a boat docked off Hudson River Park in TriBeCa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30boat-wharton/30boat-wharton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Docking Downtown: An Oyster Bar on a Boat', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Wharton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wharton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad80658d-c7b6-5f9d-bac5-7eea18d6523c', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad80658d-c7b6-5f9d-bac5-7eea18d6523c'}, {'abstract': 'Colony, a new exhibition space and collective for emerging and midcareer designers in New York, offers its members a mutually beneficial business model.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/t-magazine/reclaim-nyc-a-cooperative-hub-for-emerging-talent-opens-in-tribeca.html', 'snippet': 'Colony, a new exhibition space and collective for emerging and midcareer designers in New York, offers its members a mutually beneficial business model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s often said that good design solves a problem. And a year and a half ago, Jean Lin learned that some New York designers had problems of their own. “They had nowhere to show their work in Manhattan,” says Lin, the co-founder of the charitable design organization Reclaim NYC. “They’re not in a showroom like Ralph Pucci, but they’ve grown out of their 450-square-foot bay in Red Hook.” So Lin, along with the marketing consultant Michael Maloney, created Colony, a multipurpose design exhibition space on New York’s Canal Street, which opened to the public last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/27/t-magazine/27colony-hruska/27colony-hruska-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cooperative Hub for Emerging Talent Opens in TriBeCa', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Hruska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hruska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0a83d2b-c01e-5703-b679-d7ddf79dc88a', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0a83d2b-c01e-5703-b679-d7ddf79dc88a'}, {'abstract': 'Summer heat waves are becoming more frequent and increasingly intense. They put both young and old, the physically active and the sedentary, at risk of a heat-related illness and death.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/keeping-your-cool/', 'snippet': 'Summer heat waves are becoming more frequent and increasingly intense. They put both young and old, the physically active and the sedentary, at risk of a heat-related illness and death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, New York’s first documented heat-related death occurred on July 8, after three consecutive days with temperatures at 90 degrees or above. The victim was a 57-year-old man on Staten Island. The summer before, a record-breaking eight-day heat wave killed four people, three of them with health problems.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 972, 'width': 1211, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/science/01brody/01brody-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Your Cool', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooler Heads Will Prevail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T04:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d084cb0-14d5-512b-96d4-3882421bfff9', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d084cb0-14d5-512b-96d4-3882421bfff9'}, {'abstract': 'The British-born Mrs. McLellan, who wrote for three Washington papers, gained a devoted readership by skewering the powerful in the nation’s capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/business/media/diana-mclellan-gossip-columnist-with-an-ear-to-washington-dies-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'The British-born Mrs. McLellan, who wrote for three Washington papers, gained a devoted readership by skewering the powerful in the nation’s capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diana McLellan, a grande dame of Washington gossip who perforated the pretentious, skewered the powerful and sometimes felt honor-bound to keep fact-checkers from coming between her bons mots and her “darlings,” as she called the devoted readers of her syndicated newspaper column, died on Thursday in Easton, Md. She was 76.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 931, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 931}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1320, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/business/30mclellan/30mclellan-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diana McLellan, Gossip Columnist With an Ear to Washington, Dies at 76', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diana McLellan, 76, the Capital’s Gossip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '