 Tuesday at 98, through five of his performances, starting with Curtis Bernhardt’s “Kisses for My President” (1964), with Polly Bergen as the first female president, Fred MacMurray as her ego-bruised husband and Mr. Wallach as a rowdy Latin American dictator. Dore Schary’s “Act One” (1963), in which George Hamilton channels the playwright Moss Hart and Mr. Wallach the producer Warren Stone, follows at 11; “How the West Was Won” (1963), John Ford’s epic about three generations of pioneers, with Mr. Wallach as a train robber, at 1 p.m.; John Huston’s “The Misfits” (1961), starring Marilyn Monroe as a newly divorced showgirl, Clark Gable as an aging cowboy and Mr. Wallach as the ranch hand who devises a plan to round up wild mustangs and sell them to a dog food manufacturer, at 3:45; and Elia Kazan’s “Baby Doll” (1956), Mr. Wallach’s first film — and reportedly his favorite — in which he starred alongside Carroll Baker (above with Mr. Wallach) and Karl Malden as a Sicilian cotton-gin owner who seduces the child bride of his rival, at 6.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T04:16:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9afd2f-850f-5588-992d-072c94ce5c76', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9afd2f-850f-5588-992d-072c94ce5c76'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: Almost 50 years after trading Dublin’s lilts for a Manhattan commute, a man made the change official, and then wondered how people would know he was an American.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/her-father-becomes-a-citizen/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: Almost 50 years after trading Dublin’s lilts for a Manhattan commute, a man made the change official, and then wondered how people would know he was an American.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-articleLarge.png', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-jumbo.png', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-superJumbo.png', 'height': 900, 'width': 1425, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/nyregion/30diary-illo-cityroom/30diary-illo-cityroom-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Father Becomes a Citizen', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River Valley (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T04:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Coughlan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coughlan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08e65c59-9710-5b52-9646-3fe2f77dd498', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08e65c59-9710-5b52-9646-3fe2f77dd498'}, {'abstract': 'A lot happened, but the outcomes were more or less as expected.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/penny-dreadful-recap-did-the-finale-surprise/', 'snippet': 'A lot happened, but the outcomes were more or less as expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Season 1, Episode 8 Before I begin unpacking everything – and I mean everything – that went down in the Season 1 finale, “Grand Guignol,” a brief clarification/apology: I’m afraid I misinterpreted a fairly central aspect of Vanessa’s two demonic visitors in recent episodes of “Penny Dreadful.” In both instances – explicitly the first time (in all senses of the word) and more obliquely the second time – the encounter is meant to be a figment of Vanessa’s imagination. I spoke of first Sir Malcolm and then Ethan being possessed by this force; this is inaccurate. The reason why she (or whoever) conjured these two particular men was and is a topic worthy of discussion, but only once the facts are straight. I hope they are now, and I’m sorry it took me so long to get there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/28/arts/PENNY/PENNY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Penny Dreadful’ Recap: Did the Finale Surprise?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T05:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Grode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69e292c8-c167-5d3f-8cbb-17e8f056e4ad', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69e292c8-c167-5d3f-8cbb-17e8f056e4ad'}, {'abstract': 'Zhang Zhijun, the head of China’s Taiwan Affairs Office, cut short meetings on his final day on the island after protesters hit his bodyguards with paint.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/despite-protests-china-official-calls-taiwan-trip-a-success/', 'snippet': 'Zhang Zhijun, the head of China’s Taiwan Affairs Office, cut short meetings on his final day on the island after protesters hit his bodyguards with paint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The highest-level Chinese official to visit Taiwan since the two sides split at the end of the Chinese civil war in 1949 described his trip as a success even as he had to cut short his final day of appearances because of aggressive protests.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Protests, China Official Calls Taiwan Trip a Success', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin Fei-fan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma Ying-jeou', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang Yu-chi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Zhijun', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Nationalist Party (Taiwan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocat