': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/SUB2-01UP-Email/SUB2-01UP-Email-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lost Emails of the I.R.S. Point to a Wider Problem', 'kicker': 'Technical Difficulties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lost Emails of the I.R.S. Point to a Wider Dysfunction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Willis, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T11:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ed995ee-c65c-571c-9467-19d4c29b91cb', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ed995ee-c65c-571c-9467-19d4c29b91cb'}, {'abstract': 'In the most far-reaching public move so far in President Xi Jinping’s drive against corruption, the Communist Party leadership expelled a retired military commander.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/world/asia/china-moves-against-one-of-its-top-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'In the most far-reaching public move so far in President Xi Jinping’s drive against corruption, the Communist Party leadership expelled a retired military commander.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — In the most far-reaching public move so far in President Xi Jinping’s drive against corruption in China, the Communist Party on Monday expelled a retired military commander, Xu Caihou, and handed him over for an investigation into accusations that he took huge bribes in return for military promotions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Antigraft Push Snares an Ex-General', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Antigraft Push Snares an Ex-General', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Caihou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T11:42:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b70b336-5265-55b8-a937-510f292435a5', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b70b336-5265-55b8-a937-510f292435a5'}, {'abstract': 'Bulk investors in foreclosed homes are looking to sell. | Morgan Stanley’s chief has focused on safer ways of making money. | A settlement is expected with BNP Paribas over sanctions violations. | Prosecutors seek a stiff sentence for Mathew Martoma for insider trading.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/morning-agenda-a-shift-on-foreclosed-homes/', 'snippet': 'Bulk investors in foreclosed homes are looking to sell. | Morgan Stanley’s chief has focused on safer ways of making money. | A settlement is expected with BNP Paribas over sanctions violations. | Prosecutors seek a stiff sentence for Mathew Marto...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, buying foreclosed homes to rent out was the sure-thing trade for investment firms backed by money from private equity companies, hedge funds and pension systems, Matthew Goldstein writes in DealBook. But now, with the supply of cheap foreclosed homes dwindling, some early investors are looking to cash out a bit by flipping homes to competitors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Shift on Foreclosed Homes', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T11:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/588e6c1a-35ad-521a-84e3-b2246a8b0b1e', 'word_count': 2057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/588e6c1a-35ad-521a-84e3-b2246a8b0b1e'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The French government wants to hold down the cost of a vacation in France in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/1964-france-to-curb-vacation-costs/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The French government wants to hold down the cost of a vacation in France in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The French Finance Ministry\xa0launched a campaign today [June 30] to hold down the cost of vacation in France. “Operation Vacation,” which begins tomorrow and ends Sept. 15, involves a program of vigilance over the cost of hotels, restaurants, tours, amusements and retail shops in 20 of France’s 90 departments most frequented by vacationers and tourists. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 1, 1964.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: France to Curb Vacation Costs', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T12:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03481832-6db8-571f-bd88-02e4bd8bc435', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03481832-6db8-571f-bd88-02e4bd8bc435'}, {'abstract': 'Strict guidelines for how to treat certain conditions in certain patients, and allowing physicians to use their judgment, both have a role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/upshot/what-the-reduction-in-tonsillectomies-teaches-us-about-medicine.html', 'snippet': 'Strict guidelines for how to treat certain conditions in certain patients, and allowing physicians to use their judgment, both have a role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a child, one of my favorite books was “Curious George Goes to the Hospital.” It told the story of a little monkey who swallowed a puzzle piece, needed an operation to get it out, and got ice cream to soothe his sore throat afterward. It seemed at the time to be a thinly veiled story about tonsillectomy. One of the driving forces behind the publication, I’m sure, was that so many children had their tonsils removed that it wa