erties of Spain Slips in Trading Debut', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bankia SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T13:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7733b789-907b-5462-a264-917689e55600', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7733b789-907b-5462-a264-917689e55600'}, {'abstract': 'After years of delay, the automaker is moving rapidly to try to handle death and injury claims from accidents caused by a faulty ignition switch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/business/gms-payout-formula-for-the-dead-1-million-and-up.html', 'snippet': 'After years of delay, the automaker is moving rapidly to try to handle death and injury claims from accidents caused by a faulty ignition switch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — General Motors on Monday became consumed once again by the safety crisis it cannot seem to shake, announcing the recall of 8.4 million more vehicles worldwide — most of them for an ignition defect similar to the flaw that the company failed to disclose in other models for more than a decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Recalls Expand, G.M. Offers Plan for Victims of Faulty Ignition Switch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As G.M. Unveils Its Payout Plan, Recalls Expand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T14:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Stout', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stout', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82aae68-9244-5728-ac23-a4346d933fcd', 'word_count': 1494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82aae68-9244-5728-ac23-a4346d933fcd'}, {'abstract': 'Bell & Ross has created a timepiece inspired by the legacy of Georges Guynemer, complete with the emblem of the French aviator’s squadron.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/bell-ross-watch-this-vintage-style-model-designed-in-honor-of-a-fallen-wwi-hero/', 'snippet': 'Bell & Ross has created a timepiece inspired by the legacy of Georges Guynemer, complete with the emblem of the French aviator’s squadron.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekly series, the men’s fashion editors of T invite creative personalities to put their own aesthetic spin on a new watch. Here, the photographer Rob Kulisek captures a timepiece from Bell & Ross.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 855}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1438, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/t-magazine/30watch-tudela/30watch-tudela-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vintage-Style Model Designed in Honor of a Fallen WWI Hero', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T14:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be12592f-299a-5cb4-9652-e7c322ee2103', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be12592f-299a-5cb4-9652-e7c322ee2103'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A correspondent argues Germany hasn’t enough raw materials to wage war in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/1939-reporter-doesnt-expect-war/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A correspondent argues Germany hasn’t enough raw materials to wage war in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cornelius Vanderbilt Jr., Liberty magazine’s roving correspondent, returned to Paris from Rome yesterday after a month’s flying survey of Poland, Germany, Czecho-Slovakia, Hungary and other European trouble zones. “I’ll bet my shirt there’ll be no war,” said Mr. Vanderbilt, on his arrival last night at the Hotel Crillon. “Germany hasn’t enough wheat, oil, steel and other raw materials to wage a war successfully.” Mr. Vanderbilt said Germany “is in for a partial, if not a total crop failure in its bread basket.” As for the raw material situation, Mr. Vanderbilt said German economists estimate the Reich needs 20,000,000 tons of steel annually, but can count on only 7,000,000 tons. — New York Herald Tribune, July 1, 1939. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/blogs/01iht-old01/01iht-old01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 409, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N