'abstract': 'The Lincoln Center Theater production, which would be Mr. Watanabe’s American stage debut, is scheduled to open April 16 at the Vivian Beaumont Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/ken-watanabe-will-star-opposite-kelli-ohara-in-the-king-and-i/', 'snippet': 'The Lincoln Center Theater production, which would be Mr. Watanabe’s American stage debut, is scheduled to open April 16 at the Vivian Beaumont Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five-time Tony nominee Kelli O’Hara (“The Bridges of Madison County”) and the Japanese film star Ken Watanabe (an Oscar nominee for “The Last Samurai”) will play Anna and the King of Siam in the Lincoln Center Theater production of the Rodgers and Hammerstein classic, “The King and I.” The theater on Monday announced those and other details on the revival, which is scheduled to begin previews March 12, 2015, and opens April 16, 2015, at the Vivian Beaumont Theater. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/30artsbeat-kelli/30artsbeat-kelli-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/30artsbeat-kelli/30artsbeat-kelli-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/30artsbeat-kelli/30artsbeat-kelli-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/30artsbeat-kelli/30artsbeat-kelli-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':