imes, including organizing and taking part in terrorist organizations, state media reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Courts in the Kashgar area of the western Chinese region of Xinjiang have sentenced 113 people to prison terms for a wide range of crimes, including organizing and taking part in terrorist organizations, according to a state media report from Xinjiang.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Sentences 113 to Prison in Xinjiang Region', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: 113 Sentenced in Xinjiang Region', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashgar (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T17:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2740d793-012c-5808-99b8-2b83a5829388', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2740d793-012c-5808-99b8-2b83a5829388'}, {'abstract': 'A study compared how two species in different mediums, air and water, reacted to apparent obstacles as they were moving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/science/how-bumblebees-and-zebra-fish-navigate-their-worlds.html', 'snippet': 'A study compared how two species in different mediums, air and water, reacted to apparent obstacles as they were moving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All moving animals do their best to avoid running into things. And most living things follow a tried and true strategy — Watch where you’re going!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Bumblebees and Zebra Fish Navigate Their Worlds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T17:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf11f052-4b38-5444-81ef-20c0e64ffca3', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf11f052-4b38-5444-81ef-20c0e64ffca3'}, {'abstract': 'This was a political decision and it is proper for Democrats to use it as a weapon in the midterm election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/the-political-repercussions-of-the-hobby-lobby-decision/', 'snippet': 'This was a political decision and it is proper for Democrats to use it as a weapon in the midterm election campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Normally it’s not a good idea to jump right into the political implications of a major Supreme Court decision like Hobby Lobby, but in this case there’s no point in waiting. This was a political decision and it is absolutely proper for Democrats to use it as a weapon in the midterm election campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Political Repercussions of the Hobby Lobby Decision', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hobby Lobby Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d39e709-a7b9-592a-ac62-849b29109e49', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d39e709-a7b9-592a-ac62-849b29109e49'}, {'abstract': 'The group will tour the British Isles in the fall, with future dates to be announced.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/the-who-to-tour-for-50th-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'The group will tour the British Isles in the fall, with future dates to be announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ve heard this before: the Who’s next tour, which will begin in December and stretch into 2015, will definitely, absolutely, positively be the band’s last. Pete Townshend, the band’s guitarist and composer, said as much in interviews last October, although only a few days later, his colleague Roger Daltrey – the group’s singer and only other surviving original member – told Rolling Stone that after the 2015 tour, the Who might record some new music and perhaps play occasional concerts, maybe in the context of a theater residency.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/