roduced-with-slave-labor/', 'snippet': 'It’s hard for consumers to know whether a seafood supplier in Thailand or a clothes manufacturer in Bangladesh built its business on the backs of indentured or otherwise abused workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All consumers should be outraged by the idea that they’ve bought something – from shrimp to shirts – produced with slave labor. Yet as numerous reports have documented, that is a serious and growing possibility, particularly in the United States, the world’s biggest importer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Your Food and Clothes Produced With Slave Labor?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maloney, Carolyn B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T19:14:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ef66ec-b5e8-5e60-aeb2-b8485e15e908', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ef66ec-b5e8-5e60-aeb2-b8485e15e908'}, {'abstract': 'The French Senate has passed legislation, nicknamed the anti-Amazon law, designed to protect local bookstores.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/france-gives-cold-shoulder-to-amazon/', 'snippet': 'The French Senate has passed legislation, nicknamed the anti-Amazon law, designed to protect local bookstores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a backlash against the retail giant Amazon, France is preparing to impose new restrictions this summer that would bar online merchants from offering free shipments of discounted bo