: '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42a35387-3c9a-57db-9c41-1d07a6af0ed3', 'word_count': 14, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42a35387-3c9a-57db-9c41-1d07a6af0ed3'}, {'abstract': 'As part of his spiritual convalescence after his 2009 political scandal, Mark Sanford built a single-room cabin with his sons, on the eastern edge of his family’s 3,000-acre plantation in the South Carolinian coastal county of Beaufort. He offered us a look inside.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/inside-mark-sanfords-man-cave/', 'snippet': 'As part of his spiritual convalescence after his 2009 political scandal, Mark Sanford built a single-room cabin with his sons, on the eastern edge of his family’s 3,000-acre plantation in the South Carolinian coastal county of Beaufort. He offered...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Sanford finished out the two years of his governor’s term after news broke in 2009 that he left his state for five days for an assignation with his mistress, Maria Belen Chapur — not for a hike of the Appalachian Trail, as he initially said. With his political career practically dead when he left office, he retreated to his family’s 3,000-acre plantation in the South Carolinian coastal county of Beaufort. As part of a spiritual convalescence there, he built a single-room cabin with his sons, on the eastern edge of the property. He took me on a late-night tour there in March, while I was interviewing him for my article about his political recovery in last Sunday’s magazine. ‘‘It doesn’t look like much, but it was pretty hard,’’ Sanford told me. ‘‘It’s not an advanced building by any stretch of the imagination.’’ Inside, the cabin is packed with items from Sanford’s political rise and fall and his family life. I asked him about some of the items.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/30/magazine/Sanfordblog1/Sanfordblog1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Mark Sanford’s Man Cave', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chapur, Maria Belen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanford, Jenny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanford, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T20:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'new