tails of their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRAVELING is just part of the deal if you’re running a business. I’m C.E.O. and founder of Rosenzweig and Company, a global executive search firm, and I have to travel a lot. I don’t like airports, and I don’t really like flying, so I try to be as efficient as possible with scheduling.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/business/Flier/Flier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unwitting Father Confessor in Flight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unwitting Father Confessor in Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenzweig, Jay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rosenzweig & Company Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T21:22:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Rosenzweig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenzweig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7d0a3ac-0bb4-54f8-9af6-fd14f5430c74', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7d0a3ac-0bb4-54f8-9af6-fd14f5430c74'}, {'abstract': 'In a YouTube video, Mr. Jagger chides the members of Monty Python for being over the hill: “Who wants to see that again?”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/mick-jagger-teases-monty-python-wrinkly-old-men-trying-to-relive-their-youth/', 'snippet': 'In a YouTube video, Mr. Jagger chides the members of Monty Python for being over the hill: “Who wants to see that again?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Monty Python about to begin its run of reunion (and farewell) shows at the 02 Arena in London on Tuesday, Mick Jagger and Charlie Watts of the Rolling Stones have made a video clip – commissioned by the Pythons, and shown at the troupe’s news conference about the shows on Monday – in which they tease the comedians as being past their sell-by date.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1074, 'width': 1470, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01artsbeat-mick/01artsbeat-mick-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mick Jagger Teases Monty Python: ‘Wrinkly Old Men Trying to Relive Their Youth’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jagger for Monty Python: Oldies but Goodies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monty Python', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T21:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f20dccd9-6c03-50fc-ac73-1a5f85f6696c', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f20dccd9-6c03-50fc-ac73-1a5f85f6696c'}, {'abstract': 'During the MAN trade show, the two cooks behind Meteor served up decadent dishes from their mobile kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/06/30/man-trade-show-belgian-food-truck-meteor-feeds-the-hungry-fashion-set-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'During the MAN trade show, the two cooks behind Meteor served up decadent dishes from their mobile kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend in Paris, fashion editors and buyers took breaks from the back-to-back spring/summer 2015 men’s runways to stretch their legs at the MAN trade show, where a diverting lineup included more than just gazing at clothes. The show’s three-day run kicked off with an exhibition of Mote Sinabel Aoki’s photographs; eased into a friendly tournament of petanque, a French ball game; and culminated with a garden party at l’Institut Suédois à Paris. Throughout it all, MAN’s guests noshed on decadent dishes — crispy-skinned roasted chicken over greens, salted mackerel with juniper-roasted cauliflower cream, aged rib-eye, gazpacho, a green pea salad\xa0— served out of the Meteor food truck. The photographer Adrian Crispin was on the scene to capture the delicious offerings of Maarten van Essche and Floris Van Looy — and their stylish customers — before the two cooks drove their fine mobile eatery off to their next destination: a seashore in their hometown of Belgium (Ostend, Zeedijk 10), where they’ll be parked this Friday, Saturday and Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Belgian Food Truck Feeds the Hungry Fashion Set in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Trucks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T21:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adrian Crispin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adrian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crispin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21f2890-9230-5b6e-95f7-52924ed07a9d', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21f2890-9230-5b6e-95f7-52924ed07a9d'}, {'abstract': 'TruTV’s “Motor City Masters” and History’s “Biker Battleground Phoenix” feature competitions to design vehicles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/arts/television/motor-city-masters-begins-on-trutv.html', 'snippet': 'TruTV’s “Motor City Masters” and History’s “Biker Battleground Phoenix” feature competitions to design vehicles.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Project Runway” — yes, it’s still on — begins a new season on July 24 on Lifetime, but perhaps you can’t wait that long to watch high-strung contestants bitch at one another as they design something utterly frivolous, while all over the world people are confronting real problems that have life-or-death consequences. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making It Work, but on Wheels', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making It Work, but on Wheels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Biker Battleground Phoenix (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Motor City Masters (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TruTV', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T21:32:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/319cdbac-ba55-57c8-9242-32cab1a3883c', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319cdbac-ba55-57c8-9242-32cab1a3883c'}, {'abstract': 'Powdered eggshells can be a useful source of dietary calcium, comparable to a supplement, but crunching on coarse bits will probably not have much nutritional effect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/science/eating-the-shell-along-with-the-egg.html', 'snippet': 'Powdered eggshells can be a useful source of dietary calcium, comparable to a supplement, but crunching on coarse bits will probably not have much nutritional effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I often include about half of one eggshell in the cup with my soft-boiled breakfast egg. Is eating it good for my health or bad?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/science/01QA/01QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/01/science/01QA/01QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 612}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 