he process will free up its staff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/business/media/the-ap-plans-for-computers-to-write-corporate-earnings-news.html', 'snippet': 'Articles based on companies’ quarterly reports are quite formulaic, and The Associated Press says that automating the process will free up its staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Associated Press announced Monday that it would use computer automation to perform one of the most formulaic tasks for business reporters — writing articles about the quarterly earnings of companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The A.P. Plans to Automate Quarterly Earnings Articles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The A.P. Plans to Automate Some Writing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zacks Investment Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-06-30T21:46:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00b2486f-a78b-5524-856e-2f269a519d42', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00b2486f-a78b-5524-856e-2f269a519d42'}, {'abstract': 'Boston Ballet’s season at the Koch Theater included works that show the troupe’s strengths and weaknesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/07/01/arts/dance/boston-ballet-visits-new-york-with-a-bulging-suitcase.html', 'snippet': 'Boston Ballet’s season at the Koch Theater included works that show the troupe’s strengths and weaknesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All ballet companies have their self-contradictions. Boston Ballet is both a much better company than it allowed New York to see last week in its season at the David H. Koch Theater and, occasionally, a more dismaying one. The troupe has the world’s finest current production of “The Sleeping Beauty,” at least two of America’s best classical ballerinas (Kathleen Breen Combes and Misa Kuranaga, wholly unalike), a staging of Balanchine’s “Jewels” with (as seen in 2009) several exhilarating points of text and style absent from New York City Ballet’s, and many other productions that make me wish I had time to visit Boston more often. Its choice of ballets by living choreographers is, however, much more problematic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01BOSTONBALLET1/01BOSTONBALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01BOSTONBALLET1/01BOSTONBALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01BOSTONBALLET1/01BOSTONBALLET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/01/arts/01BOSTONBALLET1/01BOSTONBALLET1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':